(612, 'Poster Presentation Competition on Pi Approximation Day', 'The students showcased their understanding of Pi through informative and visually appealing posters. The themes of student presentations covered a wide range of topics, including the history of &pi;, information about Pi Day as well as Pi Approximation Da', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-07-22', '2026-07-22', '11:30', '01:30', '', '', 'Smt A. A. Namjoshi', 38, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 376, '2026-08-05', 'Room No. 8', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p>The students showcased their understanding of Pi through informative and visually appealing posters. The themes of student presentations covered a wide range of topics, including the history of &pi;, information about Pi Day as well as Pi Approximation Day and its significance, interesting facts about Pi, the role of Pi in scientific and mathematical advancements, graphical interpretation of differentiation using Pi, role of Pi in understanding topological holonomy, etc. The event provided an excellent platform for students to explore the historical, mathematical, and practical importance of Pi while enhancing their creativity and presentation skills.</p>', 'uploads/Events/1000136097.jpg', 'uploads/Poster-Presentation-competition-.pdf', '', '', '', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-05', 1, ''),
(613, 'Prize Distribution Ceremony of Poster Presentation Competition', 'The prizes and certificates for the Poster Presentation Competition, held on 22nd July 2026, on the occasion of Pi Approximation Day, were awarded to the participants.', '2026', '', '2026-07-29', '2026-07-29', '11:30', '01:00', '', '', 'Smt A. A. Namjoshi', 38, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 376, '2026-08-05', 'Room no. 8', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p>The prizes and certificates for the Poster Presentation Competition, held on 22nd July 2026, on the occasion of Pi Approximation Day, were awarded to the participants.</p>', 'uploads/Events/1000138098.jpg', 'uploads/Report-on-Prize-Distribution-Ceremony-of-Poster-Presentation-Competition.pdf', '', '', '', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-05', 1, ''),
(614, 'Gurupournima Celebration 2026', '', '2026', '', '2026-07-29', '2026-07-29', '10:00', '12:30', '', '', 'Department of Education', 20, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 254, '2026-08-13', 'Room No. 217', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '', 'uploads/Events/GURUPOURNIMA.jpg', 'uploads/GURUPOURNIMA-REPORT-2026.pdf', NULL, NULL, 'NaN', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-12', 1, ''),
(615, 'Movie Screeing', '', '2026', '', '2026-08-19', '2026-08-19', '10:00', '12:00', '', '', 'Department of Education', 20, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 253, '2026-10-21', 'Ground Floor Auditorium', 'Past Event', 'Upcoming Event', '<p>The Department of Education, in collaboration with the Department of Sociology, organised a movie screening of I Am Kalam under the Social Science Association on 19th August 2026. The screening provided students with an experiential learning opportunity to reflect on education, aspirations, social inequality, determination and the power of dreams. The movie highlighted the transformative role of education and the importance of perseverance in overcoming social and economic challenges.</p>', 'uploads/Events/I-AM-KALAM-PIC.jpg', 'uploads/EVENT-PROPOSAL-&-REPORT.pdf', 'Department of Sociology', 'Students and Teachers', '44', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-12', 1, ''),
(616, 'Educational Activities- Learning Beyond the Classroom', '', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-08-19', '2026-08-19', '12:00', '15:30', '', '', 'Department of Education', 20, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 253, '2026-10-21', 'Ground Floor Foyer', 'Past Event', 'Upcoming Event', '<p>The Department of Education, Sathaye College (Autonomous), organised EDUQUEST 2026 &ndash; Learn &bull; Play &bull; Achieve on 19th August 2026 at 12:00 p.m. onwards at the Ground Floor Foyer. The event included eight fun and educational games such as Riddles, Word Search, Puzzle Station, Find the Difference, Mystery Box and Blindfold Cup Stack. The main aim was to make learning enjoyable and interactive.</p>', 'uploads/Events/FLYER-EDUQUEST.jpg', 'uploads/Education-Activity-Report.pdf', 'NIL', 'Degree and Junior College Students and Teachers', '120', '[{\"name\":\"NIL\",\"designation\":\"NIL\",\"affiliation\":\"NIL\"}]', 1, '2026-08-12', 1, ''),
(617, 'Workshop: Suicide Prevention – Myths and Basics of Being a First Responder', 'The workshop aimed to create awareness among students about suicide prevention and to help them develop a better understanding of the realities surrounding suicidal thoughts and behaviours. The session addressed several common myths and misconceptions sur', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-08-10', '2026-08-10', '11:30', '13:00', '', '', 'Dept of Psychology', 28, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 265, '2026-08-13', 'Room number: 108', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j9DNhfByykeHM1h8GjWNM7WLXCxagKBSOran_QaJCz8/edit?usp=sharing\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j9DNhfByykeHM1h8GjWNM7WLXCxagKBSOran_QaJCz8/edit?usp=sharing</a></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', 'uploads/Events/IMG-20260813-WA0010.jpg', '', 'Department of Psychology, Counseling Cell', 'Junior and Degree College Students', '50', '[{\"name\":\"Ms. Sanhita Ethape\",\"designation\":\"Counseling Psychologist\",\"affiliation\":\"NGO\"},{\"name\":\"Cassandra Hetraj\",\"designation\":\"Counseling Psychologist\",\"affiliation\":\"NGO\"}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 1, ''),
(618, 'Workshop on Herbal Cosmetology', 'The Department of Botany, successfully organized a One-Day Workshop titled &ldquo;Herbal Cosmetology&rdquo; on 8 th August 2026 for students of Botany (UG &amp; PG). It witnessed the enthusiastic participation of over 60 students.Purpose/Objectives of the', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-08-08', '2026-08-08', '09:30', '00:30', '', '', 'Dr. Jayashree Gaikwad', 49, 0, '', 'AQAR', 0, NULL, NULL, 334, '2026-08-13', 'Biology Lab', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p>The Department of Botany, successfully organized a One-Day Workshop titled &ldquo;Herbal Cosmetology&rdquo; on 8 th August 2026 for students of Botany (UG &amp; PG). It witnessed the enthusiastic participation of over 60 students.<br />Purpose/Objectives of the workshop:<br />&bull; To give students the practical exposure to herbal cosmetic formulation using medicinal plants<br />&bull; To create awareness about quality control, safety, standardization of herbal cosmetics.<br />&bull; To promote entrepreneurship and self- employment opportunities in the herbal cosmetic sector.</p>\r\n<p>Outcome of the workshop:<br />&bull; Increased awareness of the herbal cosmetics formulation from raw materials to packaging<br />&bull; Practical training delivered to students to formulate herbal cosmetics on their own<br />&bull; Inspiration to explore herbal cosmetics as a mini start-up idea or part of eco entrepreneurship<br />&bull; Seeding the idea of research &amp; development in the sector of<', 'uploads/Events/1000211378.jpg', 'uploads/Report-of-herbal-cosmetics-workshop-8-Aug.-2026.pdf', 'Moroccan Earth India under Synk Enterprises', 'Students of Botany (UG & PG)', '65', '[{\"name\":\"Dr. Saif Khan\",\"designation\":\"Assistant Professor\",\"affiliation\":\"St. Xavier\'s College\"}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 1, ''),
(619, 'Excursion to Matheran', 'A one-day educational excursion to Matheran, located in Neral, Raigad District, was organised on July 11, 2026, to provide students with practical exposure to plant diversity, different types of vegetation etc. The excursion was organized for SYBSc, TYBSc', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-07-11', '2026-07-11', '08:00', '16:00', '', '', 'Dr. Jayashree Gaikwad', 49, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 334, '2026-08-13', 'Matheran', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A one-day educational excursion to Matheran, located in Neral, Raigad District, was organised on July 11, 2026, to provide students with practical exposure to plant diversity, different types of vegetation etc. The excursion was organized for SYBSc, TYBSc. and M.Sc. students. Matheran is a partially automobile-free hill station and a municipal council in the Karjat taluka of the Raigad district located in the Indian state of Maharashtra. Matheran is part of the Mumbai Metropolitan Region, and one of the smallest hill stations in India. It is located in the Western Ghats, at an elevation of around 800 m (2,625 feet) above sea level. It is about 90 km from Mumbai, and 120 km from Pune. This proximity to these urban areas makes it a weekend getaway for many. Matheran, which means \"forest on the forehead\" (of the mountains) in Marathi, is an eco-sensitive region as declared by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change, Government of India.</p>', 'uploads/Events/IMG-20260727-WA0033.jpg', 'uploads/Report-of-Excursion-to-Matheran.pdf', NULL, 'UG & PG students of Botany', '28', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 1, ''),
(620, 'Guest lecture on Stress Management', 'A lecture on &ldquo;Stress Management&rdquo; was organized for the undergraduate (UG) and postgraduate (PG) students of the Department of Botany on 29th July 2026 from 11:30 a.m. to 12.30 pm. The session was conducted with the objective of creating awaren', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-07-29', '2026-07-29', '11:30', '12:30', '', '', 'Dr. Jayashree Gaikwad', 49, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 334, '2026-08-13', 'Biology lab (Room no. 110)', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A lecture on &ldquo;Stress Management&rdquo; was organized for the undergraduate (UG) and postgraduate (PG) students of the Department of Botany on 29th July 2026 from 11:30 a.m. to 12.30 pm. The session was conducted with the objective of creating awareness among students about stress, its effects on physical and mental well-being, and the importance of adopting healthy strategies to manage stress effectively. The interactive nature of the lecture provided students with an opportunity to reflect on their own stress levels and learn practical ways of dealing with challenging situations. The session also highlighted the importance of balancing academic responsibilities with physical activity, relaxation, and emotional well-being.</p>', 'uploads/Events/20260729_120519PMByGPSMapCamera.jpg', 'uploads/Report-on-lecture-on-stress-management.pdf', 'Dept. of Psychology, Sathaye college (Autonomous)', 'UG & PG students', '85', '[{\"name\":\"Smt. Anuja Pingle\",\"designation\":\"Asst. Prof.\"}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 1, ''),
(621, 'Literary Competitive Events for Youth Festival 2026-2027', '', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-07-18', '2026-07-18', '10:00', '14:00', '', '', 'Dr. (Smt.) Panchshiela Mahale', 0, 34, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 257, '2026-08-13', 'Ground Floor Auditorium', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '', 'uploads/Events/1000107132.jpg', 'uploads/Literary_Competitive_Events_Report_18072026.pdf', '', 'Sathaye College', '45', '[{\"name\":\"Shri. Rishabh Upadhyay\",\"designation\":\"Judge\"}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 1, ''),
(622, 'National Reading Day 2026', '&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;On the occasion of National Reading Day, the Library Department of Sathaye College organized&nbsp;a special program me on 19th June 2026 to promote reading habits and create awareness about&nbsp;library resources among students.&nbsp;&', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-06-19', '2026-06-19', '10:30', '16:30', '', '', 'Smt. Swapna S Gawde', 64, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 446, '2026-08-13', 'Reading Hall library', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;On the occasion of National Reading Day, the Library Department of Sathaye College organized&nbsp;<br />a special program me on 19th June 2026 to promote reading habits and create awareness about&nbsp;<br />library resources among students.&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The program was graced by Vice Principal Prof. Dr. Suraj Pandit, who guided and motivated the&nbsp;<br />students about the importance of reading in academic and personal development. He emphasized&nbsp;<br />that reading is a lifelong habit that enriches knowledge, enhances critical thinking, and contributes&nbsp;<br />to overall personality development.&nbsp;<br />As part of the celebration, the Library Department organized a Book Exhibition featuring more&nbsp;<br />than 200 books from various subjects and genres. Students actively visited the exhibition and&nbsp;<br />explored the collection. They were encouraged to write their feedback and reviews about the&nbsp;', 'uploads/Events/National-Reading-Day-(6).jpeg', 'uploads/National-Reading-Day.pdf', '', '200', '', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-13', 0, ''),
(623, 'Study Trip to Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaja Vastu Sangrahalaya organised by Department of Ancient Indian Culture & Archaeology', 'The Department of Ancient Indian Culture &amp; Archaeology organised a Study trip to Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Vastu Sangrahalaya, for the FYBA (Major 1 &amp; 2), SY, TY (Major/Minor) and PG (Part I &amp; II) students of the department on Tuesday, 11th ', '2026', 'Intra-College', '2026-08-11', '2026-08-11', '10:00', '14:00', '', '', 'Department of Ancient Indian Culture & Archaeology', 15, 0, '', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, 245, '2026-08-14', 'Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Vastu Sangrahalaya', 'Past Event', 'Past Event', '<p>The Department of Ancient Indian Culture &amp; Archaeology organised a Study trip to Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Vastu Sangrahalaya, for the FYBA (Major 1 &amp; 2), SY, TY (Major/Minor) and PG (Part I &amp; II) students of the department on Tuesday, 11<sup>th</sup> August 2026.</p>', 'uploads/Events/WhatsApp-Image-2026-07-31-at-12.39.45-(2).jpeg', '', '', 'UG and PG Students', '', '[{}]', 1, '2026-08-14', 1, ''),
