INSERT INTO `tbl_faq` (`tf_id`, `tf_category`, `tf_question`, `tf_answer`, `tf_updated_date`) VALUES
(7, 'admission', 'How to Apply?', 'After selecting the course and fulfilling the eligibility criteria, you can apply by paying required registration amount for reserving the seat, which will be adjusted with the Tuition Fees while completing the Admission Process.', '2023-03-14 00:28:50'),
(8, 'admission', 'How does the admission process work?', 'Our counselor guides the candidate for the selection of right course and career, placement opportunities, etc. The eligibility of the candidate for the opted course is checked and confirmed by the respective authorities at Indian Academy. Candidate may take provisional \nadmission in the opted course by paying the Registration Fee along with submission of necessary supporting documents & testimonials and filled application form. The final admission process takes place once the candidate brings along all the original documents required \nfor admission and approval, pay the necessary fees and complete all the necessary formalities.', '2023-03-14 21:52:21'),
(9, 'admission', 'Are all the courses affiliated?', 'All our Undergraduate and Post Graduate courses are affiliated to Bangalore University and are NAAC Accredited – Grade A with CGPA 3.9. MBA is approved by All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) and is Recognised as a Top B-School in India – \nAll India Management Association, Dalal Investment Journal, THE WEEK and Business India, 2010.\n\nPre University Courses are approved by Pre University Board of Karnataka and our college is granted Grade A by the Board.\n\nNursing Courses are affiliated to Rajiv Gandhi University of Health Sciences and are approved by Indian Nursing Council, Karnataka Nursing Council and Government of Karnataka.', '2023-03-14 21:52:32'),
(10, 'admission', 'English coaching program?', 'Yes. We do have a full fledged English laboratory with instructor. Candidates those who are weak in English language are trained by our dedicated instructor using sophisticated technology and the performance of the candidates \nare monitored periodically.', '2023-03-14 21:53:18'),
(11, 'admission', 'Arrange for a campus visit?', 'Thirty-minute walking tours of campus, including laboratories, research centre, library, language laboratory, cafeteria, are accessible throughout the calendar year with a prior appointment from the Admissions unit. The tour is held \non the hour, Monday through Saturday, from 9.30 a.m. to 4.30 p.m.', '2023-03-14 21:53:50'),
(12, 'bonafide', 'What is a Bonafide Certificate?', 'It is an official document that acts as proof that an individual belongs to a particular educational institute or an organisation. \nFor students, it mainly specifies that an individual belongs to a specific class and course at an institution for a particular time period. \nWhile for employees, this document elucidates that the concerned person is a part of a certain company/organisation working under a specific job profile.', '2023-03-14 21:54:23'),
(13, 'bonafide', 'Use of a Bonafide Certificate?', 'This certificate can be asked for multifarious purposes, which can vary for students as well as employees.\n\n-As a student, you might need one while applying for educational loans, attending seminars or workshops at academic institutions, visiting any organisation for project work, availing of travel concessions or joining a public library.\n-As an employee, you might require bonafide certification in order to open a bank account, to attend an official conference or seminar or for any other company-related activities.', '2023-03-14 21:54:51'),
(14, 'bonafide', 'Bonafide Certificate valid till?', 'It is generally valid for a duration of three months and is issued on a letterhead of the educational institution or the company with a duly signature and official seal.', '2023-03-14 21:55:22'),
(15, 'bonafide', 'Who issues a Bonafide Certificate?', 'Mainly, for a student, the head of the administrative department/the academic institution issues this certificate while for an employee, the manager of their concerned department/organisation gives their final seal of approval.', '2023-03-14 21:55:38'),
(16, 'campus', 'What kinds of food options are available on campus?', 'A sprawling dining hall serves students and staff with healthy vegetarian meals. The food services that are already paid for in the fees; the dining provides breakfast, lunch, evening snacks, and dinner at fixed timings. The range in these meals includes:\nBreakfast: We serve South Indian, North Indian, Maharashtrian and Continental cuisine dishes (Bread, Butter, Jam, Varieties of Flakes, Cold Milk etc.) Lunch: We serve North Indian, different state themed foods, Chinese, Thai, Continental foods and live counters.\nEvening Snacks: We serve different types of Indian snacks like chat items, varieties of pakodas, dhokla, and bakery savouries.', '2023-03-14 21:56:14'),
(17, 'campus', 'What sort of medical facilities are available on campus?', '24 hour doctor availability with 2 residential doctors\n2 female doctors and one male doctor. Patient has a choice to choose female doctor if not comfortable to consult with male doctor.\n24 hour ambulance service with pick-up and drop services.\nAll basic treatment, vaccination, minor procedures (dressing, stitches) all major medicines including antibiotics, skin related creams, eye ear drops\nIn case of a serious health issue, 24 hour ambulance service to higher centre like Chellaram hospital.', '2023-03-14 21:56:46'),
(18, 'campus', 'What is your policy for substance abuse?', 'FLAME University maintains a zero-tolerance policy on drug abuse by students. FLAME University prohibits the unlawful manufacture, sale, distribution, possession, or use of illegal drugs, or unauthorized use of prescription drugs.\nIt is mandatory for a student to provide, if required, samples of urine, blood, and breath or to allow officers to medically examine them.', '2023-03-14 21:57:14'),
(19, 'college hostel', 'When can we start staying in our hostel rooms?', 'You can start staying in the hostel rooms just after you report to the institute on the&nbsp;reporting date.', '2023-03-14 21:57:40'),
(20, 'college hostel', 'Are there AC room for students?', 'No', '2023-03-14 21:57:52'),
(21, 'college hostel', 'Are the hostel accommodation rooms with attached washrooms ?', 'Yes . Each room has its own attached washroom.', '2023-03-14 21:58:06'),
(22, 'college hostel', 'How many meals are provided?', 'Four Meal. Breakfast, Lunch, Snacks and Dinner.', '2023-03-14 21:58:17'),
(23, 'college hostel', 'Do you provide laundry facility?', 'Yes. It is a paid facility. The charges are per cloth per student basis.', '2023-03-14 21:58:29'),
(24, 'college hostel', 'Can hostel students bring in their friends into their rooms ?', 'NO. Hostel students are not allowed to bring in non-hostel student friends inside the hostel building. It is strictly prohibited.', '2023-03-14 21:59:12'),
(25, 'exam', 'What are supplementary exams?', 'Supplementary exams are conducted in the same format as the in-session exams.\n\nNote: Taking a supplementary exam may impact the units you can enrol into in future study periods. You will need to submit a special consideration application and will be contacted about your supplementary exam details.', '2023-03-14 21:59:42'),
(26, 'exam', 'I have two exams on the same day – Can I move one of these exams?', 'No. If you have two exams scheduled on the same day at different start times (for example, at 9.00am and 1.30pm), you cannot move these exams and you are expected to sit both.', '2023-03-14 22:00:06'),
(27, 'exam', 'I\'m not feeling well – What should I do?', 'On campus exam: If you are unwell or become unwell during a final exam, you will need to speak to the exam supervisor as soon as you feel unable to continue.  You will also need to apply for special consideration - you will need to submit the form as soon as possible after the exam.\n\nOnline exam: If you are unwell or become unwell during the final exam, you will need to apply for special consideration. Note you\'ll need to submit the form as soon as possible.\n\nMacquarie operates under a ‘Fit to Sit’ model, where, in sitting an examination, you are declaring yourself fit to do so.', '2023-03-14 22:00:24'),
(28, 'exam', 'Who can I talk to about what’s in my exam?', 'Your lecturer is the best person to tell you what to expect in the exam and what materials you can bring into the exam.\n\nThe University has general rules that will apply to you in every exam you sit. Find out more about the Assessment Policy, Assessment Procedures, Section E Final Examination Requirements', '2023-03-14 22:00:39'),
(29, 'exam', 'My exam is offered at different times – Can I sit it twice?', 'No, you can only sit your exam once and there are only a handful of exams with multiple offerings. Find out more information on iLearn.', '2023-03-14 22:00:52'),
(30, 'exam', 'Where is my exam/room?', 'The exam room listed in your individual exam timetable is shown using the street name followed by the room number. For example, an exam held in room 11WW 130 means the building is 11 Wally’s Walk and the room number is 130.\n\nIf you have trouble finding your exam room, you can visit Service Connect on the Ground Floor, 18 Wally’s Walk or use the campus map.', '2023-03-14 22:01:14'),
(31, 'exam', 'I\'m late for my exam – Will they still let me in?', 'If you’re late for an exam, you are not permitted to enter the exam venue after one hour from the start (excluding reading time). We have a ‘Fit to Sit’ policy for exams, so you must sit your exam unless you have serious and unavoidable circumstances that may be considered in an application for special consideration.', '2023-03-14 22:01:52'),
(32, 'infrastructure', 'What are the infrastructural assets of  University?', 'University’s expansive campus spreads over 1300,000 sq. ft, replete with world-class academic, administrative, residential, sports and convention space. It holds state-of-the-art computer centers, \ndesign studios, labs, and lecture theatres. Students can expect high speed digital connectivity and make use of online libraries, interactive classrooms, and data centers.', '2023-03-14 22:02:16'),
(33, 'infrastructure', 'Is there Hostel facility available in campus?', 'Yes', '2023-03-14 22:02:30'),
(34, 'infrastructure', 'Is there a medical center in campus?', 'Yes, there is a medical center and 24*7 ambulance available in campus.', '2023-03-14 22:02:39'),
(35, 'infrastructure', 'What are the assets of the Computer Lab?', 'Turing - the computer lab, has 60 Intel windows based i7 high-end systems with fully loaded Academic software, 20 Apple iMacs, multi-function SHARP-color printer and 44-inch HP Design jet pro postscript printer (plotter).', '2023-03-14 22:02:50'),
(36, 'infrastructure', 'Is there a Fabrication lab available in campus?', 'Yes, the FabLab at college is equipped with hi-tech machinery like Laser Cutting Machine, Milling Machine, Thermocol Cutting Machine, Vinyl Plotter, Router Machine, 3D Printers and other tools required for fabrication.', '2023-03-14 22:05:13'),
(37, 'infrastructure', 'What are the banking facilities available in the campus?', 'Bank of India mobile ATM van visits the campus ones every week and their banking personnel is available twice a week in the academic complex for all banking transactions.', '2023-03-14 22:05:25'),
(38, 'infrastructure', 'Are there any tuck shops on campus?', 'A tuck shop is available on campus for students to purchase both fresh and packaged food, and other general provisions.', '2023-03-14 22:05:34'),
(39, 'infrastructure', 'Is there stationery available in the campus?', 'Yes, basic stationary material is available in the Student Union Complex.', '2023-03-14 22:05:49'),
(40, 'infrastructure', 'Is there any system of feedback available at the university?', 'Yes, the university has feedback boxes available at various locations on campus. Anyone who wants to suggest and give anonymous feedback can write to us and leave their message in the feedback box.', '2023-03-14 22:06:00'),
(41, 'placement cell', 'Is there a cut off of marks to be eligible for placement?', 'It depends on the company’s screening criteria; some companies have strict cut offs ranging from 60% to 75% while some do not have any marks cut off criteria. \nIf there is any cut off criteria it will be communicated to you by the Placement Cell.', '2023-03-14 22:07:05'),
(42, 'placement cell', 'Are students prepared to appear for aptitude and GD PI?', 'The Placement Cell conducts interactive workshops before the commencement of the Placement Drives to prepare the students for these screening rounds. \nThe students are offered workshops on various topics such as GD PI and aptitude tests so that students are well prepared in advance for them.', '2023-03-14 22:07:21'),
(43, 'placement cell', 'What activities are conducted by the Placement Cell?', 'The Placement Cell conducts a host of activities for the batch namely,\ni) Conducting several interactive workshops for the students to prepare them for Placement Drives.\nii) Organising Pre-Placement Talks for the Placement Drive so that the students get a clear picture of the job as well as the company.\niii) Inviting companies to conduct Placement Drives for the students.\niv) Acting as an intermediary between the company and students to facilitate a smooth selection process for the students from beginning to end.', '2023-03-14 22:07:42'),
(44, 'placement cell', 'How can I be a part of the Placement Cell?', 'The Placement Cell offers the position of Placement Cell Coordinators to students after completing their 4th semester. \nAll students are eligible to sit for the screening process and the screening is performed by the Placement Cell on the basis of a personal questionnaire and PI.', '2023-03-14 22:07:54'),
(45, 'placement cell', 'How will I get to know that a company is coming for placement?', 'All the details related to the upcoming placement drive are notified on the official WhatsApp class group.', '2023-03-14 22:08:11'),
(46, 'placement cell', 'How can I apply for a Campus Placement Drive?', 'Students can apply using the google form registration link shared on their WhatsApp class group.', '2023-03-14 22:08:27'),
(47, 'placement cell', 'Can I sit for more than one placement?', 'You can sit for every placement drive until you get placed. However, once you are placed in any company, you\'ll not be allowed to sit for any further placement drives under any circumstances.', '2023-03-14 22:08:45'),
(48, 'scholarship', 'What are my chances of receiving a scholarship?', 'This depends largely upon the scholarship, how well you meet qualifications and the level of effort that you exert in your search. \nTypically, if you can find scholarships that are limited to students within a state, city, sport or academic area, you have a better chance of winning. \nThe more applicants there are for a particular offer, the less chance you have of winning. \nChoose scholarships that give you an opportunity to exercise your skills in an area of interest to you —this should increase your chance of winning. \nAlso, keep in mind that to find money for college, you have to create your own success by committing the time and brain power necessary to achieve your goal.', '2023-03-14 22:09:12'),
(49, 'scholarship', 'How does community service increase my chances for receiving a scholarship?', 'Not only is community service experience a common essay topic but your involvement in community service can distinguish you from other applicants. \nScholarship providers often look for this quality because they are looking to assist in funding the education of someone who gives back to their community and values \nmaking contributions of time and service for its benefit.', '2023-03-14 22:09:28'),
(50, 'scholarship', 'If the required G.P.A. is 3.8 and I have a 3.7, should I still apply?', 'No. If you don\'t meet the criteria exactly you shouldn\'t apply. Scholarship offers typically receive thousands of applications. Anyone who doesn\'t meet the requirements is typically disqualified.', '2023-03-14 22:09:40'),
(51, 'scholarship', 'How quickly will I be notified?', 'You will typically be notified within a few weeks of the deadline, though this varies with each scholarship provider.', '2023-03-14 22:09:53'),
(52, 'other', 'how to test cms', 'By Manual test', '2023-04-13 03:27:43'),
(53, 'admission', 'when our admission will be start', 'from 15 june', '2023-05-15 01:31:51'),
(54, 'admission', 'New Admission', 'New AdmissionNew AdmissionNew AdmissionNew Admission', '2025-09-22 01:45:06');
