(249, 'Sanskrit Story Telling Competition (संस्कृत कथाकथन स्पर्धा)', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/image.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/image_.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '4', '', 512, '•	Ms. Tirtha Upendra Pandit, our student from F.Y.B.A. secured 2nd Prize in Group 4 (Junior College and Degree College category), showcasing her outstanding storytelling skills in Sanskrit.', 1, ''),
(250, 'Teacher’s Day Celebration', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/09_04_2025_10_07_16_AM.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/Img_03092025_113950.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG_20250904_095405.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG_20250904_095600.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20250906-WA0013.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '7', '', 513, 'This year, the students expressed their gratitude by gifting Handmade Pocket Diaries to the teachers. These diaries were lovingly crafted, with thoughtful designs and personalized messages, reflecting the students’ deep respect and admiration for their mentors.', 1, ''),
(251, 'Guest Lecture on “Artificial Intelligence and Indian Languages: Role and Opportunities”', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/20250910_115153.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20250910_120309.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20250910_121032.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20250910_121538.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', '', 514, 'The theme of his lecture, “Artificial Intelligence and Indian Languages: Role and Opportunities,” was both contemporary and thought-provoking. Dr. Joshi highlighted how Artificial Intelligence (AI) is transforming the linguistic world and emphasized the importance of adapting traditional Indian languages to this new technological era.', 1, ''),
(252, 'Online Intercollegiate Sanskrit Story Telling Competition', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/IMG-20250920-WA0009.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20250920-WA0011.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '4', '', 515, 'Ms. Tirtha Upendra Pandit, our student from F.Y.B.A. secured the 1st Prize.', 1, ''),
(253, '७०वा व्यसनमुक्ती तथा अंमली पदार्थ सेवन विरोधी सप्ताह (चर्चासत्र)', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/20251007_113206AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20251007_114552AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20251007_114605AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', '', 516, 'प्रमुख पाहुणे व्याख्याते डॉ. सत्यजीत कोसंबी यांनी या विषयावर विद्यार्थ्यांशी संवाद साधला. त्यांनी व्यसनाचे दुष्परिणाम सांगत वैज्ञानिक दृष्टिकोनातून त्याचे शरीर आणि मनावर होणारे परिणाम स्पष्ट केले.', 1, ''),
(254, 'Sanskrit Movie Screening & Reviewing Activity', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/20251208_110659AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20251208_114216AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '7', '', 517, 'The movie Punyakoti, screened with English subtitles, enabled even non-Sanskrit learners to understand and appreciate the story.', 1, ''),
(255, 'Sanskrit Olympiad', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/Prerana-Mestry-2nd-Rank_page-0001.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/Prerana-Mestry_page-0001.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/Rugved-Neman_page-0001.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/Tirtha-Pandit_page-0001.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '7', '', 518, 'Ms. Tirtha Pandit secured 86 out of 100 marks, while Mr. Rugved Neman scored 66 out of 100. Notably, Ms. Prerana Mestry achieved an outstanding score of 94 out of 100 and secured the 2nd position in the Maharashtra State in the Samajik category.', 1, ''),
(256, 'Intercollegiate Geeta Jayanti Competition, Somaiya College', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/IMG-20260119-WA0016.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260119-WA0019.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260119-WA0020.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260119-WA0021.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260120-WA0022.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '4', '', 519, 'The students of the department delivered an excellent performance and won a total of 6 prizes.  •	Ms. Mukta Kolhapure (TYBA) secured the First Prize in Sanskrit Story Writing.  •	Ms. Tirtha Pandit (FYBA) and Ms. Dhanishtha Haldankar (TYBA) won the Second Prize in Debate •	Ms. Dnyanada Gurav (SYBA) and Ms. Bhargavi Kamat (SYBA) secured the Third Prize in Debate.  •	Ms. Dnyanada Gurav (SYBA) won the Third Prize in Sanskrit Essay Writing. •	Ms. Dnyanada Gurav (SYBA) and Ms. Bhargavi Kamat (SYBA) also won the Third Prize in Quiz. •	Ms. Tirtha Pandit (FYBA) secured the Third Prize in Shlok Pathan.', 1, ''),
(257, 'Fledgling Research -  Poster Presentation', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/copy-1776338843-20260221_10117PMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260221_10119PMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260221_95931AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260221_122631PMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '7', '', 520, 'SYBA students Mr. Rugved Neman and Ms. Janhavi Ranade, who actively contributed to the academic spirit of the conclave. The poster presented by the students demonstrated a thoughtful understanding of scriptural concepts alongside modern social concerns.', 1, ''),
(258, 'Interactive Session with Alumni', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/20260228_104913AMByGPSMapCamera-(1).jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260228_104934AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260301-WA0075.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260301-WA0080.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', '', 521, 'The resource person for the session was Ms. Pranjali Sathe, an esteemed alumna of the department. She shared her academic journey and professional experiences with the students, offering clear insights into the various paths available after completing a degree in Sanskrit. She specifically guided students about competitive examinations such as NET and SET, explaining their structure, eligibility criteria, preparation strategies, and long-term benefits.', 1, ''),
(259, 'Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-02-163948.png~%~Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions~^~uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-02-160436.png~%~Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions~^~uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-02-164337.png~%~Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions~^~uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-02-165731.png~%~Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions~^~uploads/Screenshot-2026-03-02-165739.png~%~Interdisciplinary Online Lecture on Inscriptions', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', 'NULL', 522, 'During the lecture, Smt. Sabnis explained the importance of inscriptions as valuable historical sources. She highlighted how inscriptions help historians understand political history, social life, language, and cultural traditions of ancient and medieval India.', 1, ''),
(260, 'Launch of “सुभाषितस्रग्धरा”', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/No.-29-Notice.jpg~%~Launch of “सुभाषितस्रग्धरा”', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '8', 'NULL', 523, 'Under this initiative, selected Subhāṣitas (wise sayings from Sanskrit literature) are being presented every week through the department’s official Instagram page “संस्कृतपर्णिका”. Each weekly presentation includes: •	The original Sanskrit Subhāṣita •	Meaning and explanation •	Relevance in the contemporary context', 1, ''),
(261, 'Interdisciplinary Lecture on Women Empowerment & Social Awareness', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/20260307_103733AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260307_103736AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/20260307_103808AMByGPSMapCamera.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260307-WA0016.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', '', 524, 'The lecture was delivered by Dr. Sarita Kadam, Assistant Professor, Department of Sociology, Sathaye College (Autonomous). The programme aimed to create awareness among students about the importance of women’s empowerment and the role of society in promoting equality and respect for women.', 1, ''),
(262, 'Spoken Sanskrit Workshop', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/IMG_20260406_084802.jpg~%~Spoken Sanskrit Workshop~^~uploads/IMG_20260406_084735.jpg~%~Spoken Sanskrit Workshop~^~uploads/IMG_20260406_084709.jpg~%~Spoken Sanskrit Workshop~^~uploads/IMG_20260406_084652.jpg~%~Spoken Sanskrit Workshop', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '11', 'NULL', 525, 'The sessions were conducted by Ms. Nidhi Karlekar, who served as the resource person for the programme. She introduced participants to simple Sanskrit vocabulary, sentence formation, common conversational expressions, and practical usage of Sanskrit in everyday situations. Interactive activities and speaking exercises were included to help participants gain confidence in speaking Sanskrit.', 1, ''),
(263, 'Career Conclave – Guidance Lecture', '2025-26', 1, '2026-04-16', 'uploads/IMG-20260328-WA0008.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260331-WA0053.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260331-WA0124.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260331-WA0137.jpg~%~image~^~uploads/IMG-20260331-WA0151.jpg~%~image', 0, 0, 266, '', '', 1, '29', '2', '', 526, 'As part of the conclave, the Department organized an engaging and informative session titled “Career in Sanskrit.” The session focused on highlighting diverse academic pathways and professional avenues available to students, including teaching, research, translation, linguistics, archaeology, manuscriptology, civil services, and emerging interdisciplinary fields.', 1, ''),
