(106, 'Arts', '<div id=\"pills-tabContent\" class=\"tab-content\">\n<div id=\"pills-first\" class=\"tab-pane fade show active\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"pills-first-tab\">\n<div class=\"vtabs admissionsTabs\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-3  tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-1\" aria-controls=\"first1-1\" aria-selected=\"true\">First Year</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1\" aria-controls=\"first1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Second Year</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"second-tab3\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#second3\" aria-controls=\"second3\" aria-selected=\"false\">Third Year</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-9  tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\">\n<div id=\"first1-1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item active show\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\">First Year B. A. (Sem I &amp; Sem II)</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1-1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1-1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">First Year B. A. (Sem I &amp; Sem II)</h2>\n<section>\n<p>In take Capacity - 360</p>\n<p>(Each paper of 100 marks)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Subject I - Foundation Course - I / N.C.C. Studies (Only available to NCC Cadets)Theory + Project (75 + 25)</li>\n<li>Subject II - Communication Skills in English</li>\n<li>Subject III - Marathi or Hindi (Compulsory) N.B.: Before selecting Subjects IV, V and VI students should note that at present, the college does not have Sociology, Psychology and Sanskrit at the T.Y.B.A. level.</li>\n<li>Subject IV: Select any one subject from the following: Economics, History, English, Hindi, Sanskrit</li>\n<li>Subject V: Select any one subject from the following: Political Science, Ancient Indian Culture (A.I.C.), Geography, Philosophy.</li>\n<li>Subject VI: Select any one subject from the following: Marathi, Education, Psychology, Sociology, Gujarati</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\">Second Year B. A. (Sem III &amp; Sem IV)</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Second Year B. A. (Sem III &amp; Sem IV)</h2>\n<section>\n<p>(Each paper of 100 marks)</p>\n<p>A student is required to select five subjects as given below:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Foundation course - II / N.C.C. Studies (only available to NCC cadets) Theory + Project (75 + 25)</li>\n<li>Two papers in each of the three optional subjects offered at F.Y.B.A. (as per the scheme available in this college)</li>\n<li>General Applied component (one paper) Mass Communication OR Advertising</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"second3\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#fee-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"fee-article1\">Third Year B. A. (Sem V &amp; Sem VI)</button></div>\n<article id=\"fee-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"second-tab3\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Third Year B. A. (Sem V &amp; Sem VI)</h2>\n<section>\n<p>(Each paper of 100 marks)</p>\n<p>A student is required to select five subjects as given below:</p>\n<p>A student is required to select one Major subject with 6 papers or two Major subjects with 3 papers each. The Major subject should be one/two of the optional subjects offered by the student at S.Y.B.A.</p>\n<p>Each paper will carry 100 marks. Total marks 600.</p>\n<p>The subjects offered are</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>6 - paper Major Subjects:</strong> English, Marathi, Hindi, Economics, Philosophy, History, Political Science, Geography, Ancient Indian Culture (A.I.C.), and Education</li>\n<li><strong>3 - paper Major Subjects: </strong>a) History and A. I. C. b) Political Science and Education c) Philosophy and Education d) A. I. C. and Education e) History and Education</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '', 'same_window', 'page/106/arts', 'user_defined', 0, 'Arts', 'Explore the Arts faculty at Sathaye College offering diverse subjects, experienced faculty, and a holistic approach to humanities and social science education.', '', 'Arts', 1, NULL, 0, '1970-01-02', 1, ''),
