(244, 'Junior College', '<div class=\"script-holder\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div id=\"pills-tabContent\" class=\"tab-content\">\n<div id=\"pills-first\" class=\"tab-pane fade show active\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"pills-first-tab\">\n<div class=\"vtabs admissionsTabs\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-3  tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-1\" aria-controls=\"first1-1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Prospectus</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab2\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first2\" aria-controls=\"first2\" aria-selected=\"false\">Admission (Junior College)</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"second-tab3\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#second3\" aria-controls=\"second3\" aria-selected=\"false\">Examination Results</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab7\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first7\" aria-controls=\"first7\" aria-selected=\"false\">Add-On Courses</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab9\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first9\" aria-controls=\"first9\" aria-selected=\"false\">Refund of Fees (Junior)&nbsp;</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcoming23-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming23-left\" aria-controls=\"upcoming23-left\" aria-selected=\"true\">Examination Pattern (Junior College)</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"tab-arts-btn\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable \" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#tab-arts\" aria-controls=\"tab-arts\" aria-selected=\"true\">Arts</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"tab-science-btn\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#tab-science\" aria-controls=\"tab-science\" aria-selected=\"false\">Science</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"tab-commerce-btn\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#tab-commerce\" aria-controls=\"tab-commerce\" aria-selected=\"false\">Commerce</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"tab-vocational-btn\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#tab-vocational\" aria-controls=\"tab-vocational\" aria-selected=\"false\">+2 Vocational Course</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-9  tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\">\n<div id=\"first1-1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item active show\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\"> Prospectus</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1-1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1-1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Prospectus</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Sathaye-College-Junior-College-Prospectus-2024-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Junior College</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first2\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#policy-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"policy-article1\"> Admission (Junior College) </button></div>\n<article id=\"policy-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab2\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Admission (Junior College)</h2>\n<section>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Rules Concerning Admission:</strong></p>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\">Admission to F.Y.J.C. Arts (Std. XI), F.Y.J.C. Science (Std. XI) (including Vocational Course under Technical Group), F.Y.J.C. Commerce (Std. XI) and MCVC (Std. XI) will start after the declaration of the S.S.C. result by the Mumbai Divisional Board of the Maharashtra State Board of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education, Pune, during the hours to be notified for the purpose.</p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A student who has passed at one and the same attempt, the 10-year S.S.C. Examination conducted by the Maharashtra State Board of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education, Pune (hereinafter called &ldquo;the Board&rdquo;), or any other examination recognised as equivalent there to by the Board is eligible for admission to the F.Y.J.C. (Std. XI) class in Arts or Science or Commerce or +2VOC Course.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Admission for those, passing an Examination other than that conducted by the Board is provisional as long as the Final Eligibility Certificate issued by the Mumbai Divisional Board is not submitted to the college. The student should apply for Eligibility Certificate to the Mumbai Divisonal Board through the college along with his/her necessary documents before the notified date, failing which his/her admission is liable to be cancelled.</li>\n<li>For admission to the F.Y.J.C. class, it is necessary to produce the following documents together with an attested copy of each of the following:</li>\n<li>S.S.C. Exam. Passing Certificate.</li>\n<li>Statement of Marks of the examination mentioned above.</li>\n<li>School Leaving Certificate.</li>\n<li>Eligibility Certifi cate in the case of those passing an examination other than that conducted by the Maharashtra State Board</li>\n<li>Aadhar Card</li>\n<li>The students are hereby informed that the original School Leaving Certificate will be kept by the College as a Permanent Record and in any case, will not be returned to the student. The students are advised to keep with them sufficient number of attested copies for future use, if necessary. It is said that the original School Leaving Certificate is required to be produced at the time of getting a Domicile Certificate. The students are advised to take due care in this regard and make necessary arrangement in such cases. (The School Leaving Certificate once submitted to the college will NOT be returned in any case.)</li>\n<li>A student who has passed the F.Y.J.C. (Std. XI) Exam. from a recognised institution in Maharashtra, or any other examination recognised as equivalent thereto by the Board is eligible for admission to the S.Y.J.C. (Std. XII) class.</li>\n<li>A student who has passed the F.Y.J.C. Exam. in Science or Commerce is permitted to join the S.Y.J.C. class in Arts. A student who has passed the F.Y.J.C. Exam. in Science is permitted to join the S.Y.J.C. class in Commerce.</li>\n<li>A student seeking admission to the college shall have to present himself along with an application in the prescribed form duly filled in and signed by him and endorsed by his parent/guardian, for an interview by the Principal. No admission shall be regarded as duly granted unless it is granted by the authority of the Principal and the necessary fees have been received by the college.</li>\n<li>All admissions are valid only for one academic year and are required to be renewed by a fresh application in the prescribed form for every subsequent year of study in the college.</li>\n<li>Normally, a student of this college, who has qualified himself for admission to a higher class, will be admitted to such a class, provided application for the purpose in the prescribed form, duly filled in, has been received with the necessary fees within the notified period.</li>\n<li>Seats are reserved for Backward Class Students as per Govt. Rules. Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit Caste Certificates issued by the competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Instructions:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Those who have opted for General Mathematics at S.S.C. Examination cannot opt for Mathematics &amp; Statistics in any stream.</li>\n<li>Students should note that they will not be permitted to change subjects once offered.</li>\n<li>The Medium of instruction in the college is English. However, Sanskrit is taught in English, Marathi &amp; Hindi.</li>\n<li>A student will not be held eligible to appear for F.Y.J.C./S.Y.J.C. Exam. unless he produces a certificate of having satisfactorily completed the course in the subject &lsquo;Physical Education&rsquo;.<br />Physical Education Examination for all the students (Boys &amp; Girls) will be held in the college every year.<br />The F.Y.J.C. Arts / Science / Commerce students who fail to appear for the Physical Education Examination are liable to be treated to have failed in the Examination.<br />The S.Y.J.C. Arts / Science / Commerce students who fail to appear for the Physical Education Examination will not be allowed to appear for the H.S.C. Examination.<br />A physically disabled candidate, who on the advice of a Registered Medical Practitioner, is unable to complete the course in Physical Education will have to apply with Medical Certificate to the Divisional Secretary, Mumbai Divisional Board, Mumbai through the Principal well in advance.</li>\n<li>As per the Board&rsquo;s rule, students of F.Y.J.C. Arts / Science / Commerce and + 2 VOC should note that they should pass in their Environment Education Examination. Separate passing in theory &amp; project work of EVS is essential. If they fail to do so they are liable to be treated as failed in the F.Y.J.C. Annual Examination.</li>\n<li>The S.Y.J.C. Science / Arts / Commerce + 2 VOC students should note that they should pass in their Environment Education Examination. Separate passing in theory &amp; project work of EVS is essential. If they fail to do so they are liable to be treated as failed in the H.S.C. Examination.</li>\n<li>Students will have to pay additional fees if they select Psychology, French or German.</li>\n<li>Students should regularly read the Notices displayed on the Notice Boards &amp; on the website.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"second3\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#fee-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"fee-article1\">Examination Results</button></div>\n<article id=\"fee-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"second-tab3\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Examination Results</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.sathayecollege.edu.in/index.php/sathayecollege.edu.in/OnlineAdmission/ResultJunior.aspx.html?College=02&amp;ComingFrom=JrResult\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Junior College</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first7\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Achievements\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#procedure-article1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"procedure-article1\">ADD-ON Courses</button></div>\n<article id=\"procedure-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#cancellation-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"procedure-article1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Add-On Courses</h2>\n<section>\n<div class=\"row online-forms-page\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-oncourses/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ADD-ON Courses</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/math-1123/home\">Mathematics for Competitive Examination</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/add-on-course-mathematics-for-/home\">Foundations for Undergraduate Mathematics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/film-and-philosophy/home\">Film &amp; Philosophy</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncourserm/home\">Research Methodology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/add-on-phy-dept-sathayecollege\">Laboratory Equipment Repairs</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/horticulture-and-gardening/home\">Horticulture and Gardening</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-course-in-commerce/home\">Share Market- Technical and Fundamental Analysis</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/bengalilanguage/home\">Certificate Course in Bengali Language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/statistics-add-on-course-1/home\">Statistical Data Analysis using MS Excel-Basic</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/exploring-mind-through-dance/home\">Exploring Mind through Dance and Movement</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/basic-data-science/home\">Basic Data Science</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/modicourse/home\">Diploma in the proficiency of Modi Transliteration-Translation, <br />Calligraphy, Research and Teaching techniques</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/diploma-in-indian-archaeology/home\">Diploma in Indian Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/introduction-to-intangible-her/home\">Certificate Course in Introduction to Intangible Heritage</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-german/home\">Certificate Course In German</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/sathaye-ipr-add-on-course/home\">Introduction to Intellectual Property Rights</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-coursesbms/home\">Office Application And Advanced Excel</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/sathayecollegedeptofenglish/home\">Public Speaking And Communication</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncoursebasiceconometrics/home\">Basic Econometrics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/digitalcartographyandsurvey/home\">Modern Surveying Techniques And Advanced Digital Cartography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/botany-mushroom-cultivation-/home\">Mushroom cultivation</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/entrepreneurship-in-education/home\">Entrepreneurship in Education</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/descriptive-statistics-using-p/home\">Descriptive Statistics Using Python</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-course-ii-statistics/home\">Statistical Data Analysis Using MS Excel - Advanced</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/adoncourse/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Film Appreciation</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/massmediaaddoncourse/home\">Mass Media Add-on Courses</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificatecourseinportuguesel/home\">Certificate course in Portuguese language, history and <br />Lusophone studies</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/jainartarchitecture/home\">Certificate Course in Jain Art and Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/buddhistrock-cutmonasteriesinm/home\">Certificate Course in Buddhist Rock-cut Monasteries in Maharashtra</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-french/home\">Certificate Course In French</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/zoologyaddoncourse/home\">Fish Rearing and Care</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/professional-ethics/home\">Professional Ethics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/certificate-course-ps/home\">Preparatory course in Competitive Examinations</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncoursebasicmathematicsand/home\">Basic Mathematics and Statistics for Economic Analysis</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/geospatial-technology/home\">Geospatial Technology - GIS, GPS and RST</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/botany-herbarium/home\">Plant Identification And Herbarium Techniques: Preparation, <br />Plant identification</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-courses-for-sanskrit/home?authuser=5\">Learning Sanskrit as a second language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/tally-erp-/home\">Basic Accounting through Tally ERP.9 / Tally Prime</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/genderandlaw/home\">Gender and Law</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-hindi/home\">Career in Hindi language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/archives-management/home\">Diploma in Archives Management: Theory and Practice</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/ancient-indian-culture/home\">Certificate Course In Ancient Indian Culture</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/buddhiststudies/home\">Certificate Course in Buddhist Art &amp; Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-spanish/home\">Certificate Course In Spanish</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/food-nutrition-and-dietetics/home\">Food Nutrition and Dietetics</a></p>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first9\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Achievements\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#attendance1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"attendance1\"> Refund of Fees (Junior)</button></div>\n<article id=\"attendance1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#attendance-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"attendance1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Refund of Fees (Junior)</h2>\n<section>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">If a student informs the college, in writing before the commencement of the academic year that he wants to withdraw and he cannot continue his education in the college for any reason, the college will refund, in full, the tuition fee, term fee, laboratory fee, library deposit and laboratory deposit actually charged from the student. The admission fee will not be refunded. As far as the F.Y.J.C. classes are concerned, the academic year shall be deemed to have commenced from the eighth working day (i.e. excluding Sunday and Public Holidays) from and including the day of declaration of S.S.C. results.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">If a student desires to withdraw and applies for a refund of fees after the commencement of the academic year, the college will retain the admission fee. Term fee and laboratory deposits will, however, be refunded. As for the tuition fee is concerned, the college will retain the tuition fee only for the month(s) beginning from the month in which the academic year had commenced and ended with the month in which the student had applied for withdrawal and refund of fees. The tuition fee for the remaining months of the terms will be refunded.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A student applying for discontinuation and refund of fees shall surrender the Identity Card and the Reader\'s Ticket if issued to him and the fee receipt along with his application.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"upcoming23-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item \" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming23-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"upcoming23-left-article\"> Examination Pattern (Junior College) </button></div>\n<article id=\"upcoming23-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming23-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Examination Pattern (Junior College)</h2>\n<section>\n<p class=\"text-theme-colored\"><strong>Four examinations will be held for the students during the course of the academic year:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mid-term Test No. 1 for F.Y.J.C. Classes only. The portion for this examination will be the portion taught upto the last working day before this examination.</li>\n<li>The First Terminal Examination for both F.Y.J.C. and S.Y.J.C. classes. The portion for this examinaion will be the entire portion taught upto the last working day before this examination.</li>\n<li>Mid-term Test No. 2 for F.Y.J.C. classes only will be held in the Second Term. The portion for the examination will be the portion taught from the first working day of the Second Term to the last working day before the examination.</li>\n<li>The Preliminary Examination for S.Y.J.C. Classes only will be held in the month of January. The portion for the examination will be the entire portion taught during both the terms of the academic year. The pattern and duration of the examination will be the same as prescribed by the Board for the H.S.C.Examination.</li>\n<li>The Second Terminal Examination for the F.Y.J.C. classes only will be held in the month of February/March. The \'Portion\' for the examination will be the portion taught during the Second Term and 20% questions on the 1st Term syllabus.</li>\n<li>Supplementary First Terminal / Second Terminal Examination is arranged only for those students who inform the Principal, In writing, their inability to appear for the First Terminal / Second Terminal Examination because of ill-health or for reasons beyond their control and to the satisfaction of the Principal.</li>\n<li>The detailed programs of the respective examinations showing the duration of each question paper and the number of marks assigned will put up on the notice-board from time to time. Appearing for all the examinations is compulsory.<br />The students should note that they will be examined in Theory and Orals or Practicals or Tutorials or Seminar and their performance in each Test-Examination will be taken into consideration while promoting them to the next higher class. For this purpose, students` attendance will also be considered.<br />Assessed answer-books of all the examinations except those of the 2nd Terminal Examination are returned to the students in the classrooms from time to time.<br />Due consideration will be given to the Term-Work such as tutorials, practicals, projects, and home assignments if any.<br />The final result of the F.Y.J.C. classes will be decided on the average marks (a+b+c+d)/2 in each subject where:<br />a = the number of marks obtained at the First Terminal Exam.<br />b = the number of marks obtained at the Annual Exam.<br />c &amp; d = the number of marks obtained in the yearly work such as Mid-term tests, tutorials, practicals seminars, projects, etc.<br />If a student is found copying or using unfair means in any paper/subject at an examination, the student will be expelled from the examination and his performance in that subject will be treated as null and void. For the purpose of computation of the final result, the student will be treated to have scored \"Zero\" marks in that subject at the examination. Such students may not be eligible for admission to this college.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"tab-arts\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item \" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-arts-main\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"collapse-arts-main\">Arts</button></div>\n<article id=\"collapse-arts-main\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-arts-btn\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Arts</h2>\n<section><!-- Inner Accordion 1 -->\n<div id=\"accordion-arts-fyjc\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-arts-fyjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-arts-fyjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-arts-fyjc\">F.Y.J.C. (XI)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-arts-fyjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-arts-fyjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-arts-fyjc\">\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Compulsory Subjects</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>English</li>\n<li>Marathi or Hindi (choose any 1)</li>\n<li>History / Mathematics and Statistics ( choose any 1) (Students opted ALGEBRA at the 10th board exam are NOT eligible)</li>\n<li>Sanskrit / French/German / Geography (choose any 1)</li>\n<li>Logic / Psychology ( Psychology as per merit and availability of the seats.)</li>\n<li>Logic or Sanskrit or French or German or Maths or Hindi</li>\n<li>Economics</li>\n<li>Environment Education and Water Security Compulsory (Graded Examination)</li>\n<li>Health &amp; Physical Education Compulsory (Graded examination)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Arts students cannot opt for Logic and Maths together.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- Inner Accordion 2 -->\n<div id=\"accordion-arts-syjc\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-arts-syjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-arts-syjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-arts-syjc\">S.Y.J.C. (XII)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-arts-syjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-arts-syjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-arts-syjc\">\n<p>Students of S.Y.J.C. in Arts must offer the same subjects as F.Y.J.C.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- ===== Science ===== -->\n<div id=\"tab-science\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-science-main\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"collapse-science-main\">Science</button></div>\n<article id=\"collapse-science-main\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-science-btn\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Science</h2>\n<section><!-- Inner Accordion -->\n<div id=\"accordion-science\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-science-fyjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-science-fyjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-science-fyjc\">F.Y.J.C. (XI)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-science-fyjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-science-fyjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-science\"><!-- your science content here --></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-science-syjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-science-syjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-science-syjc\">S.Y.J.C. (XII)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-science-syjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-science-syjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-science\">\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Compulsory Subjects</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>English</li>\n<li>Marathi / Hindi / Sanskrit / French/German ( choose any 1)</li>\n<li>Physics</li>\n<li>Chemistry</li>\n<li>Mathematics &amp; Statistics / Psychology (choose any 1) - (Psychology as per merit and availability of the seats.)</li>\n<li>Biology</li>\n<li>Environment education and water security. Compulsory(Graded examination)</li>\n<li>Health &amp; Physical Education Compulsory (Graded examination)</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>F.Y.J.C. Science (+2-Vocational): [Bifocal - Vocational]</strong></p>\n<p align=\"justify\">This college conducts Vocational Courses in Electronics and Computer Science at + 2 Stage. (Electronics: 90 seats, Computer Science: 50 seats.)</p>\n<p align=\"justify\">In the case of Electronics, the first 50 students on merit (as per rules prescribed by the Government from time to time) will not have to pay any additional fees. The next 40 students will have to pay Rs. 26,220/- per annum as additional fees for this subject.</p>\n<p align=\"justify\">All students selected for Computer Science will have to pay Rs. 26,220/- as additional fees for this subject. The additional fee is to be paid only when the student is finally selected for these subjects.</p>\n<p align=\"justify\">All students selected for Electronics &amp; Computer Science need to pay Rs.1,200/- per annum as development Fees and Rs.20/- for vocational fees. Provision for teaching the vocational subjects (i) Electrical Maintenance (EM) (ii) Mechanical Maintenance (MM) (iii) Scooter and Motor Cycle Servicing (SMCS) will be made as per instructions received from the Government.</p>\n<p align=\"justify\">Students who successfully complete the Bifocal Vocational Courses are eligible for admission to the higher class F.Y.B.Sc. at the university level and also for Engineering.</p>\n<p align=\"justify\">All Science students desirous of joining Vocational Courses will apply on a separate form available at the time of admission. The list of students selected for the Course will be notified in due course.</p>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Benefits Of Bifocal Vocational Courses</strong></p>\n<p>The students who want to opt for Engineering can apply for Bifocal Vocational Courses.</p>\n<p>Vocational Course includes the following 5 Subjects:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Electronics</li>\n<li>Computer Science (C.S.)</li>\n<li>Mechanical Maintenance (M.M.)</li>\n<li>Electrical Maintenance (E.M.)</li>\n<li>Scooter Motor and Cycle Servicing (SMCS)</li>\n</ol>\n<p>All the above subjects carry 200 Marks.</p>\n<p>After opting for any of the above subjects, one language and one optional subject is exempted.</p>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Benefits Of Vocational Courses</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>One of the most and biggest advantage is that the student will get sufficient essential knowledge about the Electronics, Computer Science, E.M., M.M., SMCS around us with which we deal in our daily life.</li>\n<li>The subject is 100% beneficial for the student of B.E., Polytechnic, B.Sc in future.</li>\n<li>Whatever may be the branch 40-50% of the syllabus will reappear in the 1st year of Engineering in subjects like physics and electrical technology.</li>\n<li>As most of the basic concepts are covered, it will be helpful for constructing any module or unit related to electronics for the project in the final year of Engineering or B.Sc.</li>\n<li>As this subject is not for maintenance and repairing purpose, but students interested in this subjects may be able to detect the faults in the household or general electronics.</li>\n<li>The syllabus is structured in a way that helps learn about both the aspects - Hardware and Software. It is the first formal education course on Computers and it certainly lays the foundation for the future.</li>\n<li>The College imparts bifocal vocational courses viz. Computer Science, Electronics. The arrangement of the bifocal vocational courses viz. Electrical Maintenance, Mechanical Maintenance, and Scooter Motor Cycle Servicing are conducted jointly and are held at Govt. Technical High School, Irla, Vile Parle (West).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Subjects to be offered by a student seeking admission to Bifocal-Vocational</p>\n<ol type=\"A\">\n<li><strong>Compulsory Subjects:</strong>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>English</li>\n<li>Chemistry</li>\n<li>Physics</li>\n<li>Mathematics &amp; Statistics</li>\n<li>Electronics/Computer Science / EM / MM / SMCS - Paper I and II</li>\n<li>Environment Education and Water security. Compulsory(Graded Examination)</li>\n<li>Health &amp; Physical Education Compulsory (Graded Examination)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- ===== Commerce ===== -->\n<div id=\"tab-commerce\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-commerce-main\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"collapse-commerce-main\">Commerce</button></div>\n<article id=\"collapse-commerce-main\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-commerce-btn\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Commerce</h2>\n<section>\n<div id=\"accordion-commerce\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-commerce-fyjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-commerce-fyjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-commerce-fyjc\">F.Y.J.C. (XI)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-commerce-fyjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-commerce-fyjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-commerce\">\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Compulsory Subjects</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>English</li>\n<li>Marathi or Hindi or Sanskrit or German or French</li>\n<li>Environment Education</li>\n<li>Economics</li>\n<li>Mathematics &amp; Statistics or Secretarial Practice (S.P.)</li>\n<li>Organization of Commerce</li>\n<li>Book-keeping &amp; Accountancy</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Certificate Subjects (Anyone)&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>NCC</li>\n<li>NSS</li>\n<li>Health &amp; Physical Education</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\"><strong>Note: </strong>It Is Advisable That Students Getting Less Than 50 Marks In Mathematics In The S.S.C. Examination Do Not Opt For Subject Mathematics But Opt For Secretarial Practice</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-commerce-syjc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-commerce-syjc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-commerce-syjc\">S.Y.J.C. (XII)</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-commerce-syjc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-commerce-syjc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-commerce\">\n<p>Students of the S.Y.J.C. Class in Commerce are required to offer the same combination of subjects as offered by them in the F.Y.J.C. class. However, students may offer Secretarial Practice in place of Mathematics &amp; Statistics</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- ===== Vocational ===== -->\n<div id=\"tab-vocational\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-vocational-main\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"collapse-vocational-main\">+2 Vocational Course</button></div>\n<article id=\"collapse-vocational-main\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"tab-vocational-btn\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">+2 Vocational Course</h2>\n<section>\n<div id=\"accordion-vocational\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"heading-vocational-hsc\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#collapse-vocational-hsc\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"collapse-vocational-hsc\">H.S.C. Vocational Courses</button></h2>\n<div id=\"collapse-vocational-hsc\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"heading-vocational-hsc\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-vocational\">\n<p><strong>Aim of the Course&nbsp;</strong><br />The main aim of the course is to divert a sizeable number of students from the University Arena and Provide them with the necessary useful skills for being self-employed. The students completing these Vocational courses will also be eligible to continue their higher education beyond 12th Class ie. in the B.A. &amp; B.Com. degree course of the University. These students will be considered for F.Y.B.A./F.Y.B.Com. only if the seats are available after granting admission to H.S.C. Pass Students of this college (Arts/Com. Streams) and admission will be granted on a merit basis. It is hoped that the students successfully completing these new Vocational courses will be able to undergo apprenticeship training on a stipend in order to secure jobs. Technical group HSC pass out will get direct admission to 2nd-year Diploma Engg.</p>\n<p><strong>Courses&nbsp;</strong><br />The students are allowed to offer the following Central Government-sponsored minimum competency-based +2 vocational courses.<br />Electronics Technology(25 seats)<br />Maintenance &amp; Repairs of Electrical Domestic Appliances(25 seats)<br />Accountancy and Auditing(25 seats)<br />Banking(25 seats)<br />Office Management(25 seats)</p>\n<p><strong>Course Content : STD.XI &amp; STD.XII&nbsp;</strong><br />A student has to offer 7 papers carrying 100 marks and of 3 hours duration. The 7 papers are as follows :<br />(1) English<br />(2) Marathi/Hindi<br />(3) General Foundation Course.<br />(4) Environment Education and<br />(5),(6),(7) Vocational Papers I, II, and III including practicals.<br />Total 55 periods per week, each period being of 40 minutes, are assigned. Each paper of the vocational course carries 12 periods and each of the language papers carries 5 periods. Syllabi are prepared by the Maharashtra State Board of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education.</p>\n<p><strong>Examination: STD. XI &amp; STD. XII&nbsp;</strong><br />Examination at the end of the First Year (XI Std.) will be conducted by the College. Examination at the end of the Second Year(XII Std.)will be conducted by the Maharashtra State Board of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education. Successful candidates will be awarded a certificate showing marks obtained in each paper and practicals and the aggregate will be 600marks. These certificates, it is hoped, will enable the candidates to secure jobs or apprenticeship training.</p>\n<p><strong>Admissions:</strong> Admission will be strictly on merit decided on the aggregate marks secured by the student at the S.S.C. Examination. The student will get all the facilities available to other students of Sathaye College(Junior College). The Students shall abide by all rules and regulations of Sathaye College (Junior College).</p>\n<p><strong>College terms, Concession, Reservation of seats to B.C.Students etc. Same as for other students of Std.XI and Std. XII.</strong></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '', 'same_window', 'page/244/junior-college', 'user_defined', 0, 'Junior College', 'Find Sathaye College’s Junior College prospectus, admission details, exam results, add-on skill courses, and junior fee refund policy. Get updated academic and admission information all in one place.', '', 'Junior College', 1, NULL, 2, '1970-01-02', 1, ''),
(245, 'folk dance competition', '', '', 'new_window', 'https://sathayecollege.edu.in/event/folk-dance-competition-2021-22', 'custom_link', 0, NULL, NULL, '', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, '1970-01-02', 1, '');
INSERT INTO `tbl_master_pages` (`tmp_id`, `tmp_pane_name`, `tmp_page_content`, `tmp_new_page_content`, `tmp_menu_target`, `tmp_menu_link`, `tmp_page_type`, `page_group_id`, `tmp_meta_title`, `tmp_meta_description`, `tmp_meta_keywords`, `tmp_page_title`, `tmp_col_width`, `tmp_page_menu_type_bit`, `user_id`, `tmp_added_date`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`) VALUES
(246, 'Degree College', '<div class=\"script-holder\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div id=\"pills-tabContent\" class=\"tab-content\">\n<div id=\"pills-first\" class=\"tab-pane fade show active\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"pills-first-tab\">\n<div class=\"vtabs admissionsTabs\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-3  tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab11-1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first11-1\" aria-controls=\"first11-1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Prospectus</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1\" aria-controls=\"first1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Admission (Aided Programs)</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab18\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first18\" aria-controls=\"first18\" aria-selected=\"true\">Admission (Self Financing Programs)</div>\n</li>\n<!-- <li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"second-tab3\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#second3\" aria-controls=\"second3\" aria-selected=\"false\">Examination Results</div>\n</li> -->\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab6\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first6\" aria-controls=\"first6\" aria-selected=\"false\">Post Graduate Courses</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab7\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first7\" aria-controls=\"first7\" aria-selected=\"false\">ADD-ON Courses</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab8\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first8\" aria-controls=\"first8\" aria-selected=\"false\">Refund of Fees (Degree)</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-9  tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\">\n<div id=\"first11-1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item active show\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\"> Prospectus</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs11-1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1-1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Prospectus</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Sathaye-Prospectus-2026--6-5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Degree College</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\">Admission (Aided Programs)</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Admission (Aided Programs)</h2>\n<section>\n<p><strong>Admission To F.Y.B.A. / F.Y.B.Sc. / F.Y.B.Com. Classes :</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Admissions to F.Y.B.A. / F.Y.B.Sc. / F.Y.B.Com. classes will start after the declaration of the H.S.C. examination results. Admission to other classes will start after the declaration of the results of the respective qualifying examinations.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Student seeking admission should apply in person during the hours notified for the purpose.</li>\n<li>Every student has to affix his/her photograph on the Admission form.</li>\n<li>A student seeking admission to the college shall have to person himself/herself along with an application in the prescribed form duly filled in and signed by him/her and by his/her parent/guardian, for an interview with the Principal. No admission shall be regarded as duly granted unless it is granted by the authority of the Principal and the necessary fees have been received by the college.</li>\n<li>All admissions are valid only for one academic year and are required to be renewed by application in the prescribed form for every subsequent year of study in the college.</li>\n<li>Normally, a student of this college who has qualified himself/herself for admission to a higher class, will be admitted to such a class, provided an application for the purpose, in the prescribed form, duly filled in, has been received with the necessary fees within the notified period.</li>\n<li>Once a student is admitted to the college he shall be liable to pay full fees for the whole term.</li>\n<li>A student once admitted will be considered as duly enrolled for the academic year, unless he/she informs the Principal, in writing of his/her intention to leave the college at least a week before the commencement of the Second Term. If no such intimation is received, full fees for the Second Term will have to be paid.</li>\n<li>For admission to any class it is necessary to produce in original:</li>\n</ul>\n<p># Statement of Marks.</p>\n<p># Passing Certificate other than Maharashtra Board Students.</p>\n<p># No Objection Certificate from the Head of the institution last attended in the case of students from other colleges joining the S.Y. and T.Y. classes.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"># Eligibility Certificate from the University of Mumbai in the case of the students passing an examination other than the H.S.C. examination of the Maharashtra State Board of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education, Pune or an Examination of any University other than the University of Mumbai, as the case may be.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Admission remains provisional until Migration Certificate/Final Eligibility Certificate/Passing Certificate / Transference Certificate is submitted to the college.</li>\n<li>A student who fails to pay his/her fees and other dues on the prescribed date will have to pay the fine as decided by the Principal.</li>\n<li>Caution Money will be returned to the student, if it is not forfeited for any reason, when he/she ceases to be student, owing no money to the college and to have no library book or any other college property in his/her possession. The caution Money will be returned only on the dates notified by the college for the purpose. The prescribed form for the withdrawal of the Caution Money will be available in the college office.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a class=\"btn btn-dark btn-theme-colored btn-sm text-uppercase mt-10\" href=\"https://enrollonline.co.in/Registration/Apply/SCA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Admission Form</a></p>\n<p><strong>Instructions:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A student who has passed the Higher-Secondary Certificate Examination conducted by the Maharashtra State Board Of Secondary and Higher Secondary Education, Pune, or an Examination recognised equivalent thereto in Arts, Science or Commerce Stream or in bifocal Vocational Course, Technical Commerce Group or bifocol Vocational Course, under Technical Group/Commerce Group/or MCVC Technical Group/Commerce Group will be eligible for admission to the F.Y.B.A. class.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A student who has passed the H.S.C. Examination conducted by the said Board or an Examination recognised equivalent thereto in Science Stream or in bifocal Vocational Course under Technical Group, will be eligible for admission to the F.Y.B.Sc. class.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Student who has passed the H.S.C. Examination conducted by the said Board in subjects English, a Modern Indian Language or Modern Foreign languages and any four subjects from among the subjects Economics, Book-Keeping and Accountancy, Organisation of Commerce, Geography, Mathematics &amp; Statistics, Secretarial Practice, Cooperation or with English and any one vocational subject carrying 200 marks and three subjects from among the subjects under the Faculty of Commerce, each carrying 100 marks or who has passed the F.Y.B.Com. Examination under the \"Old course\", or an Examination recognised equivalent thereto, will be eligible for admission to the F.Y.B.Com. class.</li>\n<li>Rules for Admission to Semester III(S.Y.B.A./S.Y.B.Com.)\n<p>A student is eligible for admission to Semester III(S.Y.B.A./S.Y.B.Com.)</p>\n<p>1. If the Student passes each of Semester I and Semester II</p>\n<p>OR</p>\n<p>2. If the student fails in not more than four papers of Semester I and Semester II taken together with not more than two papers each in Semester I and Semester II.</p>\nRules for Admission to Semester III (S.Y.B.Sc.)\n<p>A student is eligible for admission to Semester III (S.Y. B.Sc.)</p>\n<p>1. If the Student passes each of Semester I and Semester II.</p>\n<p>OR</p>\n<p>2. If the student fails in not more that three papers, in each of Semester I andSemester II.</p>\n<p>Seats are reserved for Backward class Students as per Govt. Rules :</p>\n<p>Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit the Caste Certificate issued by the Competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</p>\n</li>\n<li>0.3933 : A candidate who has passed post S.S.C. (Std. X) Three Year Engineering / Technology Diploma course is eligible for direct admission to Second Year of the B.Sc. degree course.</li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">OR A candidate who has passed post H.S.C. Diploma (one year after XII Std.) of Maharashtra State Board of Technical Education or A.I.C.T.E. approved or any other recognized Government body in Information Technology / Computer Technology / Computer Engineering / Computer Science / Electrical, Electronics and Video Engineering and Allied Branches / Mechanical and Allied Branches / Production and Allied Branches / Chemical and Allied Branches is eligible for direct admission to the Second Year of the B.Sc. degree course. Further that such students of Engineering / Technology courses should offer Foundation Course II and any two of the following subject at S.Y.B.Sc. : Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics, Statistics.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility :</li>\n</ul>\nDocuments required for eligibility from students of Other State Board or University :\n<p># XIIth Marksheet (Original &amp; Photocopy)</p>\n<p># XIIth Passing certificate (Original &amp; Photocopy)</p>\n<p># Migration Certificate (Original &amp; Photocopy)</p>\n<p># Transfer Certificate or College Leaving Certificate (Original &amp; Photocopy)</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>Arts</h3>\n<div id=\"accordionFlushExample\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingOne\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseOne\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseOne\">BA NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseOne\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingOne\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>In take Capacity - 360</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BA.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BA NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr />\n<h3>Science</h3>\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingfour\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapsefour\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapsefour\">B.Sc. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapsefour\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingfour\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>In take Capacity - 360</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Structure-Dec-2025-BSC.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.Sc. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr />\n<h3>Commerce</h3>\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingseven\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseseven\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseseven\">B.Com. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseseven\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingseven\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>In take Capacity - 600</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BCom.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.Com. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr /></section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first18\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\" tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"About of Department\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"first-article1\"> Admission (Self Financing Programs)/button&gt;</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"first-tab1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Admission (Self Financing Programs)</h2>\n<section>\n<p>Self Financing Programs <strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #e91e63;\"><a class=\"read-more\" style=\"color: #e91e63; text-decoration: underline;\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/page/383/self-financing-course\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here</a></span></strong></p>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- <div id=\"second3\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Teaching Staff\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#fee-article1\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"fee-article1\">Examination Results</button></div>\n<article id=\"fee-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"second-tab3\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Examination Results</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"file:///C:/Users/LENOVO/Documents/sathayecollege.edu.in/OnlineAdmission/ResultDegree.aspx.html?College=02&amp;ComingFrom=DegResult\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Degree College</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div> -->\n<div id=\"first6\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Achievements\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#meritlist-article1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"meritlist-article1\"> Post Graduate Courses </button></div>\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Post Graduate Courses</h2>\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Information Technology):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduate in Information Technology from Any University&nbsp; recognized by UGC (UG/GEN/104 of 1989). The course has four semesters and is a credit&nbsp; based course. Students are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed&nbsp; by University from time to time. (Intake Capacity - 40)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Data Science):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Department of Information Technology is starting new course MSc Data Science from the&nbsp; academic year 2022-23. This is two years full time post graduate course with four semesters. Each semester will have four theory subjects and four practical subjects.Eligibility criteria: Any graduate from BSc Information Technology/Computer Science/ Physics/Statistics/Mathematics and other allied branches. (Intake Capacity - 40)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;<a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Msc.-DS.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Join Our M.Sc. Data Science Program : Admissions&nbsp;open&nbsp;2025</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Chemistry):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduate in Chemistry from Any University recognized by UGC (UG/ GEN/104 of 1989). The course has four semesters and is a credit based course. Students are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed by University from time&nbsp; to time. Upon completion of course students can take up production and/or research in&nbsp; chemical and pharmaceutical industries, teaching and government services. (Intake&nbsp; Capacity - 10)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Botany):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduate in Botany from Any University recognized by UGC (UG/ GEN/104 of 1989). The course has four semesters and is a credit based course. Students&nbsp; are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed by University from time&nbsp; to time. Upon completion of course, students can take up research, teaching and industry&nbsp; consultant, forestry and government services. (Intake Capacity - 10)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Microbiology):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The M.Sc. Microbiology program at Sathaye College (Autonomous), Mumbai, was established in 2024 with an intake capacity of 20 students. Aligned with the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020, the program emphasizes interdisciplinary learning, research, and skill development. It offers advanced knowledge and hands-on training in various fields of microbiology, including medical, environmental, industrial, and molecular microbiology. The department features a sophisticated laboratory infrastructure to facilitate practical learning and innovation. A team of experienced and highly qualified faculty members ensures academic excellence through interactive teaching methods, laboratory work, and project-based learning, equipping students for successful careers in research, industry, and higher education. (Intake Capacity - 20)&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Discover, Research, Innovate &ndash; Join Our M.Sc. Microbiology Program : Admissions&nbsp;open&nbsp;2025</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/7-Microbiology-At-PTVA\'s-Sathaye-College-(Autonomous)-Mumbai-2025-26.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Know Us Better: Microbiology&nbsp;Brochure</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc.(Zoology):</strong></p>\n<p>Department of Zoology was established independently in 1982. The department has rich history of creating successful UG students, many of them continue to pursue their PG and become well known researchers and academicians. Under the autonomous status, we are introducing the M.Sc. Zoology program with Molecular Biology as a specialization.</p>\n<p><strong>Features of the M.Sc. Zoology program:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>In trend Curriculum:</strong> The curriculum is designed to enable learners to get in depth knowledge of the subject by <strong>syllabi based on competitive exams like NTA CSIR-UGC NET, Mh-SET, GATE, DBT-JRF </strong></li>\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>Practical based learning: </strong>For each theory course there is associated practical course which allows leaners to apply the theoretical learning into praticals.</li>\n<li><strong>Industrial exposure through on job training. </strong>In semester II, learners will be given hands on training in various industries like healthcare, Biotechnology, Chemical etc.</li>\n<li><strong>Research exposure through research project.</strong> Learners will have to take up a research project in the semester III and IV. The research project to be carried out across various research institutes across Mumbai.</li>\n<li><strong>Holistic development of the learner:</strong> The department of Zoology has a reputation of keeping close eye on the academic development of the learners through programs like Research Journal Club, Student Guardianship Program, Field Visits, Research Internships, Flip Classroom etc. Approachable faculty makes it easier for leaners to share the difficulties in learning.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>(Intake Capacity - 40)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Sc. (Physics):</strong></p>\n<p>The Department of Physics was established in the year 1969 and has a rich heritage of over 55 years of producing the brightest talent. Many of our graduates are currently employed or doing research at renowned research institutes and universities, like TIFR, IIGM, CDAC, Nehru Science Centre, NCL, Max Plank Institute, Cardiff University and many other, contributing to the work in their respective fields.</p>\n<p>M.Sc. in Physics is initiated from the academic year 2024-25 under NEP 2020 Credit Based Grading System Framework. It<strong> </strong>is a two-year, four semesters&rsquo; postgraduate programme in Physics.(<strong>Intake Capacity 20)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The MSc Physics program at PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous) is designed to provide students with a comprehensive and in-depth understanding of the fundamental and advanced concepts in physics.</li>\n<li>The program integrates various branches of physics, including Nuclear Physics, Material Science, Quantum Mechanics, Electrodynamics, and Semiconductor Devices, providing a holistic understanding of the subject with a strong emphasis on both theoretical and practical knowledge.</li>\n<li>The curriculum is structured to foster critical thinking, problem-solving skills, and research capabilities, preparing students for diverse career opportunities in academia, industry, and research institutions.</li>\n<li>Students can choose from specialized elective threads in Material Science and Nuclear Physics, allowing them to tailor their studies to their interests and career goals.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility Criteria: </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The candidate should have passed a Bachelor Degree under 10+2+3 pattern of education in science with the subjects of Physics as the major subject for Bachelor&rsquo;s programme, from any College/ University recognized by the University of Mumbai / University Grant Commission, New Delhi.</li>\n<li>Minimum 55% marks secured in B.Sc. Physics. Students whose 6 semester results are awaited are eligible to apply but their admission will be provisional.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MSc-Physics-broucher-.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Know more about MSc Physics and admission&nbsp;details</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (Communication And Journalisum):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduate in Communication &amp; Journalism from Any University recognized by UGC (UG/GEN/104 of 1989). The course has four semesters and is a credit based course.&nbsp; Students are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed by University&nbsp; from time to time. Upon completion of course, students can take up research, teaching in&nbsp;<br />addition to these careers students can take up journalism, advertising and government&nbsp; services. (Intake Capacity - 60)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (Entertainment Media And Advertisement):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">मनोरंजन आणि जाहिरात हा पदव्त्तयुर अभ्यासक्रम विद्यापीठाची मान्यता प्राप्त असलेला दोन वर्षांचा अभ्यासक्रम आहे. हा अभ्यासक्रम क्रेडीट बेस असून यात चार सेमिस्टर आहेत. हा अभ्यासक्रम मराठीमध्ये शिकवला जातो.&nbsp;<br />तरीही विद्यार्थ्यांना मराठी आणि इंग्रजी अशा दोन्ही भाषांमध्ये परीक्षा देण्याची मुभा आहे. तसेच या दोन्ही भाषांमध्ये अभ्यास सामग्री दखील उपलब्ध आहे. मनोरजन आणि जाहिरात क्षेत्राची गरज आणि व्याप्तीला पूरक असा हा<br />अभ्यासक्रम आहे त्यामळुे प्रात्याक्षिक प्रोजेक्ट्सवर भर दणे्यात आला आहे. कोणत्याही शाखेतील पदवीधर विद्यार्थी या अभ्यासक्रमासाठी प्रवेश घेण्यास पात्र आहे.&nbsp;<br />(उपलब्ध जागा : ६०) Intake: 20 Seats</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (Hindi):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduate from Any University recognized by UGC (UG/Gen/104 of 1989).&nbsp; The course has four semesters and is a credit based course. Students are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed by University from time to time. The&nbsp; course prepares students towards advanced appreciation of Hindi literature. Upon completion of course, students can take up research, teaching in addition. (Intake Capacity - 60)</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (Buddhist Studies):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">M. A. (Buddhist Studies): Graduate from Any University recognized by UGC (UG/Gen/104 of 1989). The course has four semesters and is a credit based course. Students are expected to complete assignments or take tests as prescribed by University from time to time. This course is in a true sense an inter disciplinary course dealing with Buddhism<br />and its importance in international relations in Ancient Period, Economy, Role of Buddhism in modern society, Buddhist Philosophy, Act and Archaeology. Upon completion of course,&nbsp;<br />students can take up research or teaching. In addition to this, students can take up&nbsp; government services. (Intake Capacity - 60)</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course includes basics in Buddhism, the spread of Buddhism throughout the world and the socio-culture implication of the same.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology):</strong></p>\n<p>The Department of Ancient Indian Culture, now known as Department of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology was established in the year 1971. Since then, the aim of the Department is to impart both theoretical and applied knowledge to the learners while providing a platform for holistic approach. The Department has flourished into a centre of academic excellence in the last few decades with successful and distinguished alumni who have made a mark in various fields related to the subject and made the department and College proud of their achievements.</p>\n<p>On this prosperous background, the Department of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology is introducing M.A in Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology from the academic year 2025-26 under NEP 2020 Credit Based Grading system framework. It is a two-year postgraduate programme with four semesters each having major papers and electives wherein the learners will be obtaining a profound knowledge of the facets of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology along with experience of field visits which will enhance the theoretical knowledge with hands on training on site.</p>\n<p>The two-year course in M. A. Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology under NEP is structured to have a progressive and innovative curriculum in order to equip learners to face the future challenges in the field of higher education. The course curriculum is meticulously designed to make learners understand various phases in and the process of the evolution of Archaeology and Indian Culture.</p>\n<p>The course curriculum is learner friendly and will be focusing not only on theory but also practicals and site visits. While some Major papers like Methods &amp; Theories in Archaeology, Sciences in Archaeology, Introduction to Indian Prehistory, Introduction to Protohistory, Indian Neolithic, Art and Architecture in Ancient India, Introduction to Epigraphy and Numismatics will enable the learners in understanding vast variation in Archaeological data and its context, papers like Social organisation in Ancient India, Archaeology of Texts, Historical Archaeology, Medieval Archaeology will make learners interpret various cultures and cultural materialism. Papers like Introduction to Heritage Studies and Maritime Heritage are incorporated in the syllabi to highlight the importance of heritage studies and practical aspects of culture.</p>\n<p>The syllabi also include elective papers for every semester which includes Urban archaeology of Mumbai, Ethno Archaeology, Geo-archaeology, Indian Iconography and Jain art and archaeology which make the curriculum captivating, and the learners will get knowledge of varied aspects of the subject. The course also includes a paper on Research Methodology which will benefit the learners to encounter their skills in the field of research which will provide them the relevant experience in the field of research.</p>\n<p>The programme targets to provide in-depth knowledge to the learners in archaeology which widens the career paths in the said field which includes urban archaeology, historical archaeology, geo archaeology, medieval archaeology, ethno-archaeology, sciences in archaeology, Indology, art history, Epigraphy and Numismatics, Jain studies and heritage studies. The lectures will be conducted in blended form with a team of faculty experts in the field.</p>\n<p><strong>The objective of the course</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Holistic development of learners</li>\n<li>Preparing the learners for career opportunities in the relevant fields</li>\n<li>Exposure to research through paper on research methodology</li>\n<li>Acquaint learners with knowledge of art, archaeology and culture through theory and field work</li>\n<li>Understanding various phases in and the process of the evolution of Archaeology and Indian Culture.</li>\n<li>Learning methods of interpretation of Archaeological data and analyses</li>\n<li>Experiencing site visits</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong>: Graduation from any stream</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<strong>Intake Capacity</strong>: 20</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.A. (History):</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>M.Com. (Advanced Accountancy):</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduation in B.Com., BAF, BMS, BBI, BFM from any University recognized by UGC are eligible for admission. The course has four semesters and is a credit based&nbsp; course. It is available in two specializations. i:e M.Com in Advanced Accountancy and&nbsp; M.Com in Business Management. Students are expected to complete internal assignments&nbsp; or take up the tests and Semester End Examination as prescribed by University from time&nbsp; to time. After completion of the course, students can join in various business areas such as:&nbsp; Finance, Marketing, Human Resource etc. and are also eligible for teaching in the field of Commerce after passing NET/SET examination. Intake capacity: 120 for M.Com. (60 for Advanced Accountancy and 60 for Business Management</p>\n<hr /></div>\n<div id=\"first7\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Achievements\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#procedure-article1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"procedure-article1\">ADD-ON Courses</button></div>\n<article id=\"procedure-article1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#cancellation-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"procedure-article1\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">ADD-ON Courses</h2>\n<section>\n<div class=\"row online-forms-page\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-oncourses/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ADD-ON Courses</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/math-1123/home\">Mathematics for Competitive Examination</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/add-on-course-mathematics-for-/home\">Foundations for Undergraduate Mathematics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/film-and-philosophy/home\">Film &amp; Philosophy</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncourserm/home\">Research Methodology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/add-on-phy-dept-sathayecollege\">Laboratory Equipment Repairs</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/horticulture-and-gardening/home\">Horticulture and Gardening</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-course-in-commerce/home\">Share Market- Technical and Fundamental Analysis</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/bengalilanguage/home\">Certificate Course in Bengali Language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/statistics-add-on-course-1/home\">Statistical Data Analysis using MS Excel-Basic</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/exploring-mind-through-dance/home\">Exploring Mind through Dance and Movement</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/basic-data-science/home\">Basic Data Science</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/modicourse/home\">Diploma in the proficiency of Modi Transliteration-Translation, <br />Calligraphy, Research and Teaching techniques</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/diploma-in-indian-archaeology/home\">Diploma in Indian Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/introduction-to-intangible-her/home\">Certificate Course in Introduction to Intangible Heritage</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-german/home\">Certificate Course In German</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/sathaye-ipr-add-on-course/home\">Introduction to Intellectual Property Rights</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-coursesbms/home\">Office Application And Advanced Excel</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/sathayecollegedeptofenglish/home\">Public Speaking And Communication</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncoursebasiceconometrics/home\">Basic Econometrics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/digitalcartographyandsurvey/home\">Modern Surveying Techniques And Advanced Digital Cartography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/botany-mushroom-cultivation-/home\">Mushroom cultivation</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/entrepreneurship-in-education/home\">Entrepreneurship in Education</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/descriptive-statistics-using-p/home\">Descriptive Statistics Using Python</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-course-ii-statistics/home\">Statistical Data Analysis Using MS Excel - Advanced</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/adoncourse/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Film Appreciation</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/massmediaaddoncourse/home\">Mass Media Add-on Courses</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificatecourseinportuguesel/home\">Certificate course in Portuguese language, history and <br />Lusophone studies</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/jainartarchitecture/home\">Certificate Course in Jain Art and Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/buddhistrock-cutmonasteriesinm/home\">Certificate Course in Buddhist Rock-cut Monasteries in Maharashtra</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-french/home\">Certificate Course In French</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/zoologyaddoncourse/home\">Fish Rearing and Care</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/professional-ethics/home\">Professional Ethics</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/certificate-course-ps/home\">Preparatory course in Competitive Examinations</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/addoncoursebasicmathematicsand/home\">Basic Mathematics and Statistics for Economic Analysis</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/geospatial-technology/home\">Geospatial Technology - GIS, GPS and RST</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/botany-herbarium/home\">Plant Identification And Herbarium Techniques: Preparation, <br />Plant identification</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-courses-for-sanskrit/home?authuser=5\">Learning Sanskrit as a second language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/tally-erp-/home\">Basic Accounting through Tally ERP.9 / Tally Prime</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/genderandlaw/home\">Gender and Law</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/add-on-hindi/home\">Career in Hindi language</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/archives-management/home\">Diploma in Archives Management: Theory and Practice</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/ancient-indian-culture/home\">Certificate Course In Ancient Indian Culture</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/buddhiststudies/home\">Certificate Course in Buddhist Art &amp; Archaeology</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/certificate-course-in-spanish/home\">Certificate Course In Spanish</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/food-nutrition-and-dietetics/home\">Food Nutrition and Dietetics</a></p>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first8\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Achievements\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#prospectus-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"prospectus-article\">Refund of Fees (Degree)</button></div>\n<article id=\"prospectus-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#prospectus-left-tabs1\" aria-labelledby=\"prospectus-article\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Refund of Fees (Degree)</h2>\n<section>\n<p><strong>(Aided &amp; Unaided Courses):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Rules in respect of refund of fees as per University of Mumbai Circular No. UG/412 of 2008 dt. 11th September 2008. 0.2859: Refund of Tuition, Development and all other fees after cancellation of admissions: The candidates who have taken admission in under graduate courses in Govt. colleges, In Govt. aided and unaided courses conducted by affiliated colleges, and recognized Institutions may request for refund of fees after applying in writing for cancellation of their admission to the course. The refund of fees as applicable shall be made on or before 30th day after the date of cancellation and thereafter. The percentage of fee for the course shall be refunded to the candidate after deducting charges as follows:</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Period</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Deduction Charges</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prior to the commencement of the academic term and instruction of the course.</td>\n<td>Rs. 500/- Lumpsum</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Up to 20 days after the commencement of the academic term of the course.</td>\n<td>20% of the total amount of fees.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>From the 21st day up to 50 days after commencement of the academic term of the course.</td>\n<td>30% of the total amount of fees.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>From the 51st day up to 80 days after the commencement of the academic term of the course or August 31st whichever is earlier.</td>\n<td>50% of the total amount of fees.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>From September 1st to September 30th</td>\n<td>60% of the total amount of fees.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>After September 30th.</td>\n<td>100% of the total amount of fees.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Note:The total amount considered for the refund of fees from the commencement of academic term of the courses includes the following:- All the fee items chargeable for one year are per relevant University circulars for different Faculties (excluding the courses for which the total amount is fixed by other competent authorities). The Fee charged towards group insurance and all fee components to be paid as University share (including Vice-Chancellor fund, University fee for sports and culture activities, E-charge, disaster, management fund, exam fee and Enrollment fee) are non-refundable if payment is made by the college prior to the date of cancellation. Fee collected for Identity Card and Library Card, Admission Form and Prospectus, Enrollment and any other course specific fee are not refundable after the commencement of the academic term.</li>\n<li>All refundable deposits (Laboratory, Caution Money and Library etc.) shall be fully returned at the time of cancellation.</li>\n<li>All cases which do not fall under 1 above shall be within the discretion of the Principal.</li>\n<li>If the last day for submission of application for the refund of falls on a Sunday or a public holiday, the next day shall be deemed to be the last day for the purpose.</li>\n<li>Identity Card and the Reader&rsquo;s Tickets, if issued, and the fee Receipt shall be surrendered along with the application for discontinuation and refund of fees.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '', 'same_window', 'page/246/degree-college', 'user_defined', 0, 'Degree College', 'Find Sathaye College’s Degree College prospectus, admission details, exam results, add-on skill courses, and Degree fee refund policy. Get updated academic and admission information all in one place.', '', 'Degree College', 1, NULL, 139, '1970-01-02', 1, '');
INSERT INTO `tbl_master_pages` (`tmp_id`, `tmp_pane_name`, `tmp_page_content`, `tmp_new_page_content`, `tmp_menu_target`, `tmp_menu_link`, `tmp_page_type`, `page_group_id`, `tmp_meta_title`, `tmp_meta_description`, `tmp_meta_keywords`, `tmp_page_title`, `tmp_col_width`, `tmp_page_menu_type_bit`, `user_id`, `tmp_added_date`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`) VALUES
(247, 'Self Financing Courses', '<div id=\"pills-tabContent\" class=\"tab-content\">\n<div id=\"pills-first\" class=\"tab-pane fade show active\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"pills-first-tab\">\n<div class=\"vtabs admissionsTabs\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-3 tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-1\" aria-controls=\"first1-1\" aria-selected=\"true\">B.Sc. Information Technology</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-2\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-2\" aria-controls=\"first1-2\" aria-selected=\"false\">B.Com. Management Studies</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-3\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-3\" aria-controls=\"first1-3\" aria-selected=\"false\">B.A.M.M.C.</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-4\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-4\" aria-controls=\"first1-4\" aria-selected=\"false\">B.Com. Accounting and Finance</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-5\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-5\" aria-controls=\"first1-5\" aria-selected=\"false\">B.Com. Logistics and Supply Chain Management</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-6\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-6\" aria-controls=\"first1-6\" aria-selected=\"false\">B. Com. Sports Management</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-9 tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\"><!-- Repeat this block for each tab-pane -->\n<div id=\"first1-1\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item active show\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-1\" aria-expanded=\"true\">B.Sc. IT</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-1\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">B.Sc. Information Technology</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A Candidate for being eligible for admission to the degree course in Bachelor of Science Information Technology (B.Sc. I.T.) needs to have passed the XII standard examination of the Maharashtra Board of Higher Secondary Education or its equivalent with Mathematics as one of the subject and secured not less than 45% marks in aggregate, and 40% marks in aggregate in case of Reserved category candidate, at one and the same sitting.<br />OR<br />A candidate who has passed the Diploma in Computer Engineering/ Computer Science / Computer Technology / Electrical Electronics and Allied branches, Mechanical and Allied branches, Civil and Allied branches of Engineering are eligible the admission to the First Year of B.Sc. (I.T.) degree course. However, the Diploma should be recognized by the Board of Technical Education or any other recognized Government body. Minimum Marks required is 45% aggregate for open category candidates and 40% aggregate for reserved category candidates.<br />AND<br />Students with Post HSC-Diploma in Computer Engineering / Computer Science/ Computer Technology will be eligible for direct admission to Second year B.Sc. (I.T.). However, the Diploma should be recognized by the Board of Technical Education or any other recognized Government body. The Subject of Mathematics at Post HSC - Diploma is Compulsory.<br />No Common Entrance Test will be conducted.<br />Admission will be on the basis of merit. (Mathematics Marks)</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEATS ARE RESERVED FOR BACKWARD CLASS STUDENTS AS PER GOVERNMENT RULES:</strong><br />Of the total number of seats, 50% are reserved for Reserved Category students. Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit the Caste Certificate issued by the Competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"accordionFlushExample\" class=\"accordion accordion-flush mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingOne\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseOne\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseOne\"> B.Sc. IT NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseOne\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingOne\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 120</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1746691840-NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BScIT.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.Sc. IT NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Course 2 to 7 --> <!-- Copy-paste the structure above, just change IDs accordingly -->\n<div id=\"first1-2\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-2\">B.Com. Management Studies</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-2\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">B.Com. Management Studies</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>RULES CONCERNING ADMISSION :</strong><br /># Students who have appeared for the H.S.C. examination or its equivalent or Diploma in any Engineering branches with two years or three years or four years duration after the S.S.C. conducted by the Board of Technical Education, the Maharashtra States or equivalent examination.<br /># A Candidate for being eligible for admission to the degree course in Bachelor of Commerce Management Studies (B.Com. M.S.)needs to have passed the XII standard examination of the Maharashtra Board of Higher Secondary Education or its equivalent and secured not less than 45% marks in aggregate, and 40% marks in aggregate in case of Reserved category candidate, at one and the same sitting.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEATS ARE RESERVED FOR BACKWARD CLASS STUDENTS AS PER GOVT. RULES</strong><br />Out of total Seats, 50% of Seats are reserved for Reserved Category Students as per Govt. Rules. Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit the Caste Certificate issued by the Competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingTwo\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseTwo\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseTwo\"> B.Com. Mgt. Std. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseTwo\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingTwo\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 120</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BMS.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.Com. Management Studies NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1-3\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-3\">B.A.M.M.C.</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-3\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Bachelor Of Arts Mass Media Communication (Marathi/English)</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li>Students who have appeared for Higher Secondary School Examination (12th) or after SSC who have completed Diploma in any other Engineering Branch, two or three or four years equivalent course of Maharashtra Board of Technical Education Students can take admission in this course.</li>\n<li>Students seeking admission to the Bachelor of Mass Media course should have passed the Maharashtra Board Higher Secondary Examination, 12th.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEATS ARE RESERVED FOR BACKWARD CLASS STUDENTS AS PER GOVT. RULES</strong><br />Out of total Seats, 50% of Seats are reserved for Reserved Category Students as per Govt. Rules. Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit the Caste Certificate issued by the Competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingThree\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseThree\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseThree\"> B.A.M.M.C. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseThree\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingThree\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 60 (English Medium)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 60 (Marathi Medium)</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BAMMC.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BAMMC NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1-4\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-4\">B.Com. Acc and Fin</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-4\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">B.Com. Accounting and Finance</h2>\n<section>\n<ul class=\"list theme-colored\">\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>RULES CONCERNING ADMISSION :</strong><br /># Students who have appeared for the H.S.C. examination or its equivalent or Diploma in any Engineering branches with two years or three years or four years duration after the S.S.C. conducted by the Board of Technical Education, the Maharashtra States or equivalent examination.<br /># A Candidate for being eligible for admission to the degree course in Bachelor of Accounting and Finance (B.Com. A .&amp; F.) needs to have passed the XII standard examination of the Maharashtra Board of Higher Secondary Education or its equivalent and secured not less than 45% marks in aggregate, and 40% marks in aggregate in case of Reserved category candidate, at one and the same sitting.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEATS ARE RESERVED FOR BACKWARD CLASS STUDENTS AS PER GOVT. RULES</strong><br />Out of total Seats, 50% of Seats are reserved for Reserved Category Students as per Govt. Rules. Students belonging to the Backward Classes are required to submit the Caste Certificate issued by the Competent Authority in the State of Maharashtra.</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingFour\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseFour\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseFour\"> B.Com. Acc and Fin NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseFour\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingFour\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 120</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BAF.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BAF NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1-5\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-5\">B.Com. Logistics and Supply Chain Management</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-5\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">B.Com. Logistics and Supply Chain Management</h2>\n<section>\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingFive\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseFive\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseFive\"> BLSCM NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseFive\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingFive\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 60</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BCom(Logistics).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BLSCM NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div id=\"first1-6\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#first-article1-6\">B.Com. Sports Management</button></div>\n<article id=\"first-article1-6\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse pb-4\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">B.Com Sports Management</h2>\n<section>\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion mt-3\">\n<div class=\"accordion-item\">\n<h2 id=\"flush-headingSix\" class=\"inner-accordion-header\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#flush-collapseSix\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"flush-collapseSix\"> B.Com. Sps. Mgt. NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure </button></h2>\n<div id=\"flush-collapseSix\" class=\"accordion-collapse collapse\" aria-labelledby=\"flush-headingSix\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordionFlushExample\">\n<p><strong>Intake Capacity - 60</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structures-BCOM(Sports-Management).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">B.Com. Sports Management NEP-1.1-Course-credit-structure</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '', 'same_window', 'page/247/self-financing-courses', 'user_defined', 0, 'Self Financing Courses', 'Explore top self-financed undergraduate courses at Sathaye College including B.Sc. IT, B.Com. Management Studies, B.A.M.M.C., B.Com. Accounting & Finance, Logistics & Supply Chain Management, and Sports Management — designed for industry readiness and academic excellence.', '', 'Self Financing Courses', 1, NULL, 0, '1970-01-02', 1, ''),
(248, 'B.Sc. (I.T.)', '<div class=\"script-holder\">\n<script>\n$(\'body\').addClass(\'academics-page bscit-page\');\n</script>\n</div>\n<div id=\"pills-tabContent\" class=\"tab-content\">\n<div id=\"pills-first\" class=\"tab-pane fade show active\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"pills-first-tab\">\n<div class=\"vtabs admissionsTabs\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-3  tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1-1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1-1\" aria-controls=\"first1-1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Sem 1</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab1\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first1\" aria-controls=\"first1\" aria-selected=\"true\">Sem 2</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab2\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first2\" aria-controls=\"first2\" aria-selected=\"false\">Sem 3</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"second-tab3\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#second3\" aria-controls=\"second3\" aria-selected=\"false\">Sem 4</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"first-tab4\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first4\" aria-controls=\"first4\" aria-selected=\"false\">Sem 5</div>\n</li>\n<!-- <li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n                                    <div id=\"first-tab5\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#first5\" aria-controls=\"first5\" aria-selected=\"false\">\n                                    Music Association\n                                  