(418, 'IQAC', '<div class=\"vtabs\">\n<div class=\"row\"><!-- Left Sidebar with Tabs -->\n<div class=\"col-md-3 col-custom-20 tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs newsCustomeClass\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria1-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria1-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria1-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">About IQAC</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria2-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria2-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria2-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Academic Administrative Audit</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria3-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria3-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria3-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Action Taken Report</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria4-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria4-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria4-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Academic Calendar</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria5-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria5-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria5-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Annual Presentations</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria6-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria6-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria6-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">College Policies</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria7-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria7-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria7-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Best Practices</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria8-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria8-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria8-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Institutional Distinctiveness</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria9-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria9-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria9-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">IQAC Committee</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria10-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria10-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria10-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Minutes Of Meeting&nbsp;</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria11-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria11-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria11-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">RAR &nbsp;</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria12-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria12-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria12-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">SSS&nbsp;</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"criteria13-2020-left\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#criteria13-2020\" aria-controls=\"criteria13-2020\" aria-selected=\"false\">Institutional Development Plan</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<!-- Right Content with Tab Contents -->\n<div class=\"col-md-9 col-custom-80 tabs Content-holder\">\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><!-- Extended Profile Tab Content -->\n<div id=\"criteria1-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade active show\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria1-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">About IQAC</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<div class=\"script-holder\">&nbsp;</div>\n<p><strong>IQAC</strong></p>\n<p>In pursuance of its Action Plan for performance evaluation, assessment &amp; accreditation &amp; quality up-gradation of institutions of higher education, NAAC proposes that every accredited institution should establish an Internal Quality Assurance Cell (IQAC) as a post-accreditation quality sustenance measure. Since quality enhancement is a continuous process, the IQAC will become a part of the institution&rsquo;s system &amp; work towards realisation of the goals of quality enhancement &amp; sustenance. The prime task of the IQAC is to develop a system for conscious, consistent &amp; catalytic improvement in the overall performance of institutions. For this, during the post-accreditation period, it will channelize all efforts &amp; measures of the institution towards promoting its holistic academic excellence.</p>\n<p><strong>STRATEGIES</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>IQAC shall evolve mechanisms and procedures for:</li>\n<li>Ensuring timely, efficient and progressive performance of academic, administrative and financial tasks</li>\n<li>The relevance and quality of academic and research programmes</li>\n<li>Equitable access to and affordability of academic programmes for various sections of society</li>\n<li>Optimization and integration of modern methods of teaching and learning</li>\n<li>The credibility of evaluation procedures</li>\n<li>Ensuring the adequacy, maintenance and functioning of the support structure and services</li>\n<li>Research sharing and networking with other institutions in India and abroad</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>FUNCTIONS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Some of the functions expected of the IQAC are:</li>\n<li>Development and application of quality benchmarks/parameters for various academic and administrative activities of the institution</li>\n<li>Facilitating the creation of a learner-centric environment conducive to quality education and faculty maturation to adopt the required knowledge and technology for participatory teaching and learning process</li>\n<li>Arrangement for feedback response from students, parents and other stakeholders on quality-related institutional processes</li>\n<li>Dissemination of information on various quality parameters of higher education</li>\n<li>Organization of inter and intra institutional workshops, seminars on quality related themes and promotion of quality circles</li>\n<li>Documentation of the various programmes/activities leading to quality improvement</li>\n<li>Acting as a nodal agency of the Institution for coordinating quality-related activities, including adoption and dissemination of best practices</li>\n<li>Development and maintenance of institutional database through MIS for the purpose of maintaining/enhancing the institutional quality</li>\n<li>Development of Quality Culture in the institution</li>\n<li>Preparation of the Annual Quality Assurance Report (AQAR) as per guidelines and parameters of NAAC, to be submitted to NAAC</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>BENEFITS</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;IQAC will facilitate/contribute:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure heightened level of clarity and focus in institutional functioning towards quality enhancement</li>\n<li>Ensure internalization of the quality culture</li>\n<li>Ensure enhancement and coordination among various activities of the institution and institutionalize all good practices</li>\n<li>Provide a sound basis for decision-making to improve institutional functioning</li>\n<li>Act as a dynamic system for quality changes in HEIs</li>\n<li>Build an organised methodology of documentation and internal communication</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>COMPOSITION</strong></p>\n<p>IQAC may be constituted in every institution under the Chairmanship of the Head of the institution with heads of important academic and administrative units and a few teachers and a few distinguished educationists and representatives of local management and stakeholders</p>\n<p>The composition of the IQAC may be as follows:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Chairperson: Head of the Institution</li>\n<li>A few senior administrative officers</li>\n<li>Three to eight teachers</li>\n<li>One member from the Management</li>\n<li>One/two nominees from local society, Students and Alumni</li>\n<li>One/two nominees from Employers /Industrialists/stakeholders</li>\n<li>One of the senior teachers as the coordinator/Director of the IQAC</li>\n</ol>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria2-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria2-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Academic Administrative Audit</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/AAA-report-of-external-Committee-pdf-file-18-jan.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic and Administrative Audit Report 2020-2023</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria3-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria3-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Action Taken Report</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ATR-2021-2022.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Action Taken Report 2021-2022</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria4-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria4-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Academic Calendar</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a title=\"Academic Calendar 2026-2027\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Academic-Calendar-2026-27.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2026-2027</a></li>\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Academic-Calendar-2025-26.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2025-2026</a></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a title=\"Academic Calendar 2024-2025\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Sathaye-College-Academic-Calendar-2024-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2024-2025</a></span></li>\n<li><a title=\"Academic Calendar\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Academic-Calendar-2023-24.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2023-2024</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Academic-Calender-22-23.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2022-2023</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Academic-Calendar-21-22.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Calendar 2021-2022</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria5-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria5-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Annual Presentations</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1516.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2015-2016</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1415.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2014-2015</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1314.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2013-2014</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1213.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2012-2013</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1112.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2011-2012</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FinalPresentation1011.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annual Presentation 2010-2011</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria6-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">College Policies</h2>\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Anti-Ragging-policy.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Anti-Ragging policy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/4.-Anti-ragging-Policy.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Anti-Ragging Policy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/7.-Research-Policies.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Academic Research Policies</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/3-CODE-OF-CONDUCT-FOR-STUDENTS.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Code of Conduct for Students</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/6.-Choice-based-credit-and-grading-system.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Choice Based Credit and Grading System</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1746777687-Degree-College-Prospectus-2025-26.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Code of Conduct Handbook</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ep-amendment-4-Dt-18-Dec-2024.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ep amendment 4-Dt-18-Dec-2024</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/E-Governance-policy-of-Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">E-Governance policy of Sathaye College</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/IQAC.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IQAC</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/IT-Policy-of-Sathaye-college.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IT Policy of Sathaye college</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/8.-Maharashtra-University-Act-2016.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maharashtra Public University Act, 2016</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Policy-for-Gender-Equity,-In-clusivity-and-Sensitivty.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Policy for Gender Equity, In clusivity and Sensitivty</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Policy-of-the-Differently-abled-(Divyajan).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Policy of the Differently abled (Divyajan)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/5.-Sexual-Harassment-of-Women-at-Workplace.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal of Sexual Harassment</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Policy.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Research Policy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/1.-STUDENT-CHARTER.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Students&rsquo; Charter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2.-Students-Grievance-Redressal.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Students&rsquo; Grievance Redressal</a></li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria7-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria7-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Best Practices</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<h3 class=\"sub-head\">Fledgeling Program of 2025-26</h3>\n<p><a title=\"Report of 5th Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2025-26\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-on-5th-Fledgling-Researcher-program-2025-26.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report of 5th Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2025-26</a></p>\n<h3 class=\"sub-head\">Fledgeling Program of 2024-25</h3>\n<p><a title=\"Report of 4th Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2024-25\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-on-4th-Fledgling-Researcher-program-2024-25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report of 4th Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2024-25</a></p>\n<h3 class=\"sub-head\">Fledgeling Program of 2023-24</h3>\n<p><a title=\"Report of 3rd Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2023-24\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-on-Third-Fledgeling-Research-Poster-Presentation-Competetion-2023-24.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report of 3rd Fledgeling Researchers\' Program 2023-24</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"Abstract Booklet 2023-24\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Abstracts-Book-for-2023-24.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Abstract Booklet 2023-24</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"Final list of 3rd Fledgeling Program 2023-24\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Final-list-of-3rd-Fledgeling-Program-2023-24.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Final list of 3rd Fledgeling Program 2023-24</a></p>\n<h3 class=\"sub-head\">Fledgeling Program of 2022-23</h3>\n<p><a title=\"Report of 2nd Fledgeling Researchers\' Progarm 2022-23\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/IIRC-Report-2022-23.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report of 2nd Fledgeling Researchers\' Progarm 2022-23</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"Abstract Booklet 2022-23\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Abstract-Booklet-2022-23.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Abstract Booklet 2022-23</a></p>\n<h3 class=\"sub-head\">Fledgeling Program of 2021-22</h3>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a title=\"Report of 1st Fledgling Researchers\' Program 2021-22\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-of-1st-Fledgling-Researchers\'-Program-2021-22.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report </a><a title=\"Report of 1st Fledgling Researchers\' Program 2021-22\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-of-1st-Fledgling-Researchers\'-Program-2021-22.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">of 1st Fledgling Researchers\' Program 2021-22</a></span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria8-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria8-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Institutional Distinctiveness</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Parle Tilak Vidyalaya Association&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous), established in 1959, is one of Mumbai&rsquo;s most reputed and forward-thinking higher education institutions affiliated to the University of Mumbai. Managed by the visionary Parle Tilak Vidyalaya Association (PTVA), the college has a proud legacy of academic excellence, innovation, and holistic development. With its autonomous status, the college has the academic freedom to design flexible, interdisciplinary, and career-oriented curricula in alignment with the National Education Policy (NEP 2020), ensuring that education remains relevant, inclusive, and globally competitive. The college offers a broad spectrum of traditional degree programmes in Arts, Science, and Commerce, alongside Inter disciplinary professional courses such as B.Com (Management Studies) , B.Com (Accounting and Finance &ndash; BAF), BMM, B.Sc. IT, B.Com (Logistics &amp; Supply Chain Management), and B.Com (Sports Management). Additionally, it offers several postgraduate programmes that promote advanced academic and research engagement. Sathaye College has been recognized under the prestigious DBT Star College Scheme by the Government of India, acknowledging its outstanding contribution to science education, innovation, and research culture.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A distinctive strength of the college lies in its commitment to research, innovation, and entrepreneurship. Central Research Facility, equipped with modern analytical instruments and digital tools, is accessible to both faculty and students for experimental work, data analysis, and interdisciplinary studies. Regular workshops and seminars on Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) and innovation management help students understand the legal and practical dimensions of creativity. The Entrepreneurship Development Cell (EDC) nurtures start-up ideas, provides incubation support, and connects students with business mentors, thereby cultivating a strong entrepreneurial ecosystem on campus.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Among its unique infrastructural highlights, Sathaye College houses a museum managed by the Department of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology (AICA), which displays rare artifacts, coins, and heritage materials&mdash;offering a living classroom experience that fosters appreciation for tangible and intangible culture. The college library complements this with a rich and regularly updated collection of books, journals, and e-resources across disciplines, supporting research, academics, and competitive examinations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Career Guidance &amp; Placement Cell of Sathaye College plays a vital role in shaping student futures by actively bridging academics with industry exposure. The cell regularly conducts placement drives in collaboration with reputed banks, multinational companies, IT industries and professional recruitment agencies, ensuring diverse employment avenues for students. Campus interviews by leading organizations such as TCS have successfully created pathways for promising careers. Along with placements, the cell also provides structured counselling and training for competitive examinations, helping students develop confidence, employability skills and career readiness. Through continuous support and industry linkages, the cell prepares students to transition smoothly into the professional world.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The college has been honoured as the &ldquo;Best College&rdquo; by the University of Mumbai for its overall excellence and holistic development. Its National Cadet Corps (NCC) unit, one of the most active in Mumbai, has achieved the Vice-Chancellor&rsquo;s Banner three times for exemplary performance. The unit also maintains an operational KOTE, used for the storage and display of training weaponry and defense-related equipment. This facility, popularly known as the &ldquo;War Room&rdquo;, serves as a unique defense education hub, allowing cadets to experience the discipline, leadership, and operational aspects of national defense.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The college&rsquo;s National Service Scheme (NSS) and Rotaract Club actively engage in community-oriented projects, including cleanliness drives, social awareness campaigns, and blood donation camps, nurturing a sense of social responsibility and leadership among students. Sathaye College also takes immense pride in its illustrious alumni network, which includes achievers from politics, film and performing arts, business, social service, government administration, and academia. Their achievements across various sectors continue to inspire current students and reflect the institution&rsquo;s lasting influence on society.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sathaye College has also emerged as a model Green Campus, implementing eco-friendly practices such as solar energy usage, waste management, paper recycling, and plantation drives. Its environmental initiatives align with national sustainability goals and the Mission LiFE movement, reflecting the college&rsquo;s commitment to environmental stewardship. The college promotes an active sports and fitness culture through its state-of-the-art infrastructure. As a part of sports facility college have fully operational turf ground for outdoor sports such as football and cricket, a basketball court, and a Pickleball facility, encouraging students to explore new-age sporting activities. The college&rsquo;s Gymkhana serves as a dynamic space for indoor games such as table tennis, badminton, and chess, and also houses a well-equipped fitness gym that caters to students, faculty, and other stakeholders &mdash; promoting physical wellness alongside mental strength.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The campus thrives on cultural vibrancy and literary expression. The Marathi, Hindi, English, and Sanskrit departments organize a wide range of literary activities such as poetry recitation, debates, elocution, drama, and essay competitions, fostering linguistic appreciation and artistic growth. The annual intercollegiate cultural festival &ldquo;Astra&rdquo; stands as a hallmark of student creativity and participation, celebrating art, heritage, and innovation.&nbsp;Sathaye College hosts numerous cultural programmes throughout the year, including traditional day, music and dance competitions, folk art performances, and street plays that encourage creativity, confidence, and teamwork. Students also participate in intercollegiate cultural events, theatre workshops, and classical as well as contemporary performance platforms, bringing laurels to the institution. The college actively nurtures talent through cultural clubs, annual day celebrations, and workshops conducted by experts in fine arts, music, dramatics, and public speaking. These activities enrich campus life, promote cultural diversity, and help students develop leadership, communication, and artistic excellence.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The alumni of Sathaye College represent a proud legacy of academic excellence, professional success, and social contribution. Among the notable alumni are celebrated Bollywood icon Madhuri Dixit, distinguished leaders like Vinod Tawde and Ashish Shelar, and decorated defence officer Brig. Sangram Dalvi, who reflect the institution&rsquo;s diverse impact across fields of arts, politics, and national service. Many alumni hold esteemed positions globally in civil services, corporate sectors, law, research, media, and entrepreneurship. The college maintains strong ties with its former students through reunions, mentorship activities, talks, and collaborations, enabling them to guide and motivate the next generation. Their success continues to inspire</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Located in the educational hub of Vile Parle (East), the college features ICT-enabled classrooms, advanced laboratories, seminar halls, innovation centers, and Wi-Fi-enabled learning spaces. Accredited with an &lsquo;A&rsquo; Grade by NAAC, and guided by the progressive vision of PTVA Management, the college remains devoted to its mission of Education, Ethics, and Empowerment. With its recognition as a DBT Star College, recipient of the Best College Award, achiever of multiple NCC Vice-Chancellor&rsquo;s Banners, and pioneer in research, IPR, entrepreneurship, green initiatives, sports infrastructure, and literary excellence, PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous) stands as a beacon of holistic education, innovation, and institutional pride within the University of Mumbai.</p>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"criteria9-2020\" class=\"tab-pane fade\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"criteria9-2020-left\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">IQAC Committee</h2>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<div class=\"script-holder\">&nbsp;</div>\n<p>Internal Quality Assurance Cell</p>\n<div class=\"table-responsive\">\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 57.4534%; height: 360px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 18.043%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">Sr. No.</th>\n<th style=\"width: 41.9619%; height: 18px;\">Members Name</th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.6556%; height: 18px;\">Designation</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 18.043%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.9619%; height: 18px;\">Mr. D. M.Pethe</td>\n<td style=\"width: 45.6556%; height: 18px;\">Management Member</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 18.043%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.9619%; height: 18px;\">Shri. Bansidhar Dhurandhar</td>\n<td style=\"