(460, 'Placement', '<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<div class=\"vtabs\">\n<div class=\"row\"><!-- Tab Navigation -->\n<div class=\"col-md-3 col-custom-20 tabsName-holder\">\n<ul class=\"nav nav-tabs left-tabs\" role=\"tablist\">\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcoming1-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable active\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming1-left\" aria-controls=\"upcoming1-left\" aria-selected=\"true\">Overview</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcoming3-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming3-left\" aria-controls=\"upcoming3-left\" aria-selected=\"false\">Recruitment Policy</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcoming5-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming5-left\" aria-controls=\"upcoming5-left\" aria-selected=\"false\">Career Guidance and Placement Cell</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"teaching-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#teaching-left\" aria-controls=\"teaching-left\" aria-selected=\"false\">Gallery</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcoming4-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming4-left\" aria-controls=\"upcoming4-left\" aria-selected=\"false\">Contact Us</div>\n</li>\n<li class=\"nav-item\" role=\"presentation\">\n<div id=\"upcomings4-left-tab\" class=\"nav-link tab-clickable\" role=\"tab\" data-bs-toggle=\"tab\" data-bs-target=\"#upcomings4-left\" aria-controls=\"upcomings4-left\" aria-selected=\"false\">Past Report</div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab Contents -->\n<div class=\"col-md-9 col-custom-80 tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\"><!-- Tab 1: Overview -->\n<div id=\"upcoming1-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item active show\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming1-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Overview\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming1-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"upcoming1-left-article\"> Overview </button></div>\n<article id=\"upcoming1-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse show\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming1-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Overview</h2>\n<section>The Placement Cell of PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous) works towards facilitating campus recruitment for final-year students, with the objective that every student receives a job offer letter before obtaining their graduation certificate.</section>\n<section>We have around 1,400+ final-year students pursuing either undergraduate or postgraduate programs across various traditional and professional courses. Students plan their careers according to their interests, and we act as a catalyst in helping them achieve their career goals at an early stage.</section>\n<section>Some students plan to pursue higher studies in India or abroad, some intend to assist in their family businesses or start their own ventures, while others aim to secure jobs with reputed companies.</section>\n<section>Every year, on average, 300+ students choose to seek employment after graduation and register with the Placement Cell accordingly.</section>\n<section>Reputed companies approach us to hire our students as their employees. We also provide these companies with our best resources to ensure that the campus recruitment process takes place smoothly.</section>\n<section>The Placement Cell acts as a facilitating unit which brings recruiters and aspiring candidates together. The final decision regarding recruitment or selection lies solely with the recruiting company.</section>\n<section></section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab 2: Recruitment Policy -->\n<div id=\"upcoming3-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming3-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Recruitment Policy\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming3-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"upcoming3-left-article\"> Recruitment Policy </button></div>\n<article id=\"upcoming3-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming3-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Recruitment Policy</h2>\n<section>\n<p><strong>Policy for students</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Placement Cell &ndash; Rules and Guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students must register with the Placement Cell. Without registration, students will not be allowed to participate in the recruitment process.</li>\n<li>Mere registration with the Placement Cell does not guarantee a job. The Placement Cell acts only as a facilitator between recruiters and students (candidates).</li>\n<li>Students must respond promptly to all forms, communications, and instructions as required during the recruitment process.</li>\n<li>If a student is selected by a company in the final round, he/she will not be permitted to take part in any further recruitment processes. However, if the student wishes to apply for a more suitable opportunity than the one already offered, he/she must inform any of the Placement Committee members in person. In such cases, only two additional attempts will be granted.</li>\n<li>Once an offer letter is accepted, the student will not be allowed to participate in any further recruitment processes.</li>\n<li>Students who are not selected by any company may continue to participate in all available recruitment drives until they are selected. This facility will be available for one year after passing out from the college.</li>\n<li>It is the student&rsquo;s responsibility to impress the recruiter and secure the job.</li>\n<li>The Placement Cell allows companies to enter the campus for placement activities after verifying the necessary details of the company. However, students are advised to independently verify the company&rsquo;s details, including its reputation in the market, work culture, operations, and scope for future growth, from other reliable sources.</li>\n<li>If a student is recruited for an overseas office, the student needs to acquire and manage all necessary documents independently.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Policy for recruiters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company must have been in operation for at least five years.</li>\n<li>The company&rsquo;s website must have been active for at least three years.</li>\n<li>The company must recruit candidates as its own employees.</li>\n<li>Third-party recruitment is permitted only after internal scrutiny and approval.</li>\n<li>Only reputed multinational companies (MNCs) with a strong market reputation are allowed to recruit our students for overseas placements.</li>\n<li>Other companies are not permitted to recruit our students for cross-border or overseas offices.</li>\n<li>Students will be available to join as full-time employees after 30th April. The college does not encourage students to take up full-time employment during their study period.</li>\n<li>It is the recruiter&rsquo;s responsibility to retain and manage the selected students until their joining date.</li>\n<li>PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous) will provide basic infrastructure facilities such as interview rooms, projectors, and computer laboratories for computer-based tests (CBTs).</li>\n<li>The Computer Laboratory will be made available if intimation is received at least one week in advance.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Policy for Job fair</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Job Fair is organized in the first or second week of February.</li>\n<li>Companies that wish to recruit fewer than five candidates are advised to participate in the Job Fair, where on-the-spot offer letters to selected candidates are expected.</li>\n<li>Selected candidates are required to accept the offer letter on the same day.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Policy for venue</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If there are more than 15 students, the recruitment process will be conducted on the college campus.</li>\n<li>If there are fewer than 15 students, the interview will preferably be conducted at the company&rsquo;s office.</li>\n<li>The interview mode may be online and/or offline, depending on the company&rsquo;s preference.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Data Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College (Autonomous) will not provide any confidential or sensitive data of its students to any company for any purpose.</li>\n<li>Companies may collect necessary information directly from students in the form of CVs and related documents; however, it is the student&rsquo;s choice whether or not to share their data.</li>\n<li>The company must use the collected data strictly for recruitment purposes only.</li>\n<li>Use of the data for any purpose other than recruitment is strictly prohibited.</li>\n<li>Third-party data sharing is strictly restricted.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab 4: Career Guidance and Placement Cell -->\n<div id=\"upcoming5-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming5-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Career Guidance and Placement Cell\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming5-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"upcoming5-left-article\">Career Guidance and Placement Cell</button></div>\n<article id=\"upcoming5-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming5-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Career Guidance and Placement Cell</h2>\n<p><a title=\"Career Guidance and Placement Cell 2026-27\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/career-guidance-and-placement-cell-26-27.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Career Guidance and Placement Cell 2026-27</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"Career Guidance and Placement Cell 2025-26\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1788593023-Notice-No-136-Career-Guidance-and-Placement-Cell-2025-26.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Career Guidance and Placement Cell 2025-26</a></p>\n<p>The following teachers will constitute &ldquo;Career Guidance and Placement Cell&rdquo; for the academic year 2026-2027.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Smt. Sumedha Barve- Co-ordinator</li>\n<li>Dr. Sandeep Shinde</li>\n<li>Shri. Gautam Maske</li>\n<li>Shri. Abhijit Awhad</li>\n<li>Dr. Abhijeet Bhogale</li>\n<li>Shri. Namdev More</li>\n<li>Shri. Subhash Bansode</li>\n<li>Dr. (Capt.) Gaurang Rajwadkar</li>\n<li>Smt. Ridhisha Tarkari</li>\n<li>Shri. Samir Soni</li>\n<li>Smt. Rashmi Warang</li>\n</ol>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab 5: Gallery -->\n<div id=\"teaching-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"teaching-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Gallery\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#teaching-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"teaching-left-article\"> Gallery </button></div>\n<article id=\"teaching-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"teaching-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Gallery</h2>\n<p>Pre-Placement Talk by TCS for BPS Role</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1788600848-BSCIT-5.jpeg\" width=\"306\" height=\"172\" /> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1788600848-BSCIT-4.jpeg\" width=\"306\" height=\"172\" /> &nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1788600848-BSCIT-2.jpeg\" width=\"313\" height=\"176\" /> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1788600848-BSCIT-1.jpeg\" width=\"322\" height=\"181\" /></p>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab 6: Contact Us -->\n<div id=\"upcoming4-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming4-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Contact Us\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcoming4-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"upcoming4-left-article\"> Contact Us </button></div>\n<article id=\"upcoming4-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcoming4-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Contact Us&nbsp;</h2>\n<section>\n<p>Shri. Subhash Bansode (Placement Cell co-coordinator)</p>\n<p>+91 9224622364</p>\n<p>E-mail- placementcell@sathayecollege.edu.in</p>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n<!-- Tab 7: Past Report -->\n<div id=\"upcomings4-left\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item\" role=\"tabpanel\" aria-labelledby=\"upcomings4-left-tab\">\n<div class=\"accordion-header\" role=\"tab\"><button class=\"accordion-button collapsed\" title=\"Past Report\" role=\"button\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#upcomings4-left-article\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"upcomings4-left-article\"> Past Report </button></div>\n<article id=\"upcomings4-left-article\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"upcomings4-left-tab\">\n<h2 class=\"sub-head\">Past Report</h2>\n<section>\n<p>Career Guidance and Placement Cell<br />The Career and Placement Cell of the college has always worked towards securing Campus Recruitment &nbsp;for the &nbsp;final year students. In accordance with that , the students of &nbsp;B.Com ,B.Sc(IT), BMM &nbsp;and M.Sc IT have participated in numerous Pool &nbsp;Campus Drive programs over the years. Quite a few of our students were placed in renowned companies like TCS, Wipro, CapGemini, Infosys, L &amp; T Infotech, ICICI Prudential, HDFC securities, Axis Bank, iTech Solutions etc.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The following teachers will constitute &ldquo;Career Guidance and Placement Cell&rdquo; for the academic year 2025-2026.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shri S.S. Bansode - Co-ordinator</li>\n<li>Dr. Sandeep Shinde</li>\n<li>Shri. Abhijit Awhad</li>\n<li>Dr. (Smt.) Swati Jagtap</li>\n<li>Dr. (Capt.) Gaurang Rajwadkar</li>\n<li>Smt. Tanvi Nerurkar</li>\n<li>Dr. (Smt.) Monika Bhosale</li>\n<li>Shri. Nandkumar Haryan</li>\n<li>Smt. Rasika Sawant</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"font-18 text-theme-colored text-capitalize mb-10 mt-0\">Academic Year 2019-2020:</h2>\n<p><strong>1] CloudFronts Technologies</strong></p>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"card-img\"><img class=\"img-fluid\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/cc-e5a3ff5b-960b-4138-9fe4-c86d5b71099a.jpg\" width=\"410\" height=\"200\" /></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Career Guidance and Placement Cell successfully implemented On-Campus technical training program for T.Y.B.Sc(IT) and M.Sc(IT) students in tie-up with CloudFronts Technologies(Microsoft Partners) for the academic year 2019-20. The program was conducted between August 2019 and December 2019, consisting of hands-on training for the students. Around 40 students from T.Y.B.Sc(IT) and 2 students from M.Sc(IT) have signed up for the course .&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The course structure included technical training on the latest Microsoft Technologies like CRM(D365 sales,D365 Field Services), Finance and Operations/Business Central(D365 Finance and Operations, D365 Business Central), BI(Power BI, SCRIBE, Online Integration), SSIS using Kingswaysoft, SQL, Fetch XML and SSRS. A placement drive was conducted upon completion of the program on January 16, 2020. Around 20 students participated in the placement drive out of which three were placed.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Working with CloudFronts was a great learning experience for the IT Department as well as students.</p>\n<p><strong>2] TechnoServe</strong></p>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"card\">\n<div class=\"card-img\"><img class=\"img-fluid\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ts-6feecd37-87ed-4850-b99e-46a40cd158c4.jpg\" width=\"410\" height=\"200\" /></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Career Guidance and Placement Cell in association with TechnoServe has started the Campus to Corporate Careers (C2C) Program from the academic year 2019-2020. The program aims to provide transformative workforce skills training for youth to make better career choices and build a strong career path. It is an 80-hour program including Personal effectiveness, Communication Readiness, Career Readiness and Work Readiness. Around 30 students from B.Sc IT, B.Com and BMM were part of the training program and participated in the placement drive.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A MEGA Career fest for students trained by TechnoServe was organized in the college campus on January 17, 2020. Around 500 students from different colleges participated in the fest. The association with Technoserve continues and &nbsp; since 2019, the students\' response towards training and the placements offered has been positive.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Following is the list of students placed across several placement drives conducted from the academic year 2017-2018 to 2020-2021:</p>\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 54.3516%; height: 195px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 57px;\">\n<th style=\"height: 10px; width: 99.8988%;\" colspan=\"2\" scope=\"rowgroup\">\n<p>2017-2018 (BSc IT):</p>\n</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>Company</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">\n<p><strong>No. of students placed</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\">Capgemini</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">06</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\">Infosys</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">02</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\">Wipro</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">09</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%;\" scope=\"row\">TCS</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%;\">01</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\">Total no of students placed</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">18</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 54.3516%; height: 231px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 57px;\">\n<th style=\"height: 10px; width: 99.8988%;\" colspan=\"2\" scope=\"rowgroup\">\n<p>2018-2019 (BSc IT &amp; MSc IT):</p>\n</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>Company</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.8101%; height: 37px;\">\n<p><strong>No. of students placed</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.0887%; height: 37px;\" scope=\"row\">Capgemini</