(615, 1, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Department of Economics was established in 1959, the same year as the founding of Sathaye College.&nbsp;<strong>Professor P. M. Potdar</strong>&nbsp;was the first Head of the Department. Over the years, the department has been ably led by distinguished faculty members including&nbsp;<strong>Professors P. H. Parvatikar, A. D. Mascarenhas, Dr. S. B. Gupta, S. T. Asuti, and Dr. Sanjeevani Kawthalkar</strong>, each of whom has contributed significantly to the growth and development of the department.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At present, the department comprises five dedicated faculty members.&nbsp;<strong>Dr. Pratibha Kamble currently serves as the Head of the Department</strong>. Under her capable leadership, the department continues to uphold its legacy of academic excellence and pedagogical innovation. Economics is offered as a major subject in the Arts stream and as a minor subject in the Commerce stream. The department is particularly recognized for offering advanced subjects such as&nbsp;<strong>Econometrics, Mathematics and Statistics, and Quantitative Techniques</strong>&mdash;subjects that are seldom available at the undergraduate level in other colleges across Mumbai.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The faculty members are highly qualified and research-oriented, actively contributing to curriculum design, evaluation processes, and various academic and administrative committees. Students are encouraged from the early stages of their academic journey to engage in research activities such as surveys, data collection, and analysis, which helps in developing their analytical and critical thinking skills.The department also conducts On-the-Job Training (OJT), field projects, and community engagement activities. These initiatives provide students with practical exposure and opportunities to study real-world economic issues in both rural and urban contexts. Through these efforts, students develop practical knowledge, communication skills, social awareness, and leadership qualities, enabling them to become well-rounded and future-ready individuals.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to academic pursuits, the department places strong emphasis on co-curricular and extra-curricular engagement. Activities such as debate, essay writing, and elocution competitions, along with educational visits to esteemed institutions like the RBI Monetary Museum and the Bombay Stock Exchange, are organized regularly. Flagship events such as the Trogovina Intercollegiate Fest and the observance of important days which help foster holistic student development. Through these comprehensive efforts, the Department of Economics remains committed to nurturing well-rounded, socially responsible, and future-ready graduates.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span class=\"_aupe copyable-text xkrh14z\">The Department of Economics is introducing a Postgraduate Programme (M.A. in Economics) from the academic year 2026&ndash;27, focusing on market-oriented and applied areas. The programme includes courses such as Microeconomic Theory, Advanced Development Economics, Behavioural Economics, Advanced Econometrics Method, Contemporary Indian Economy, Environmental Economics, Advanced Macroeconomics, Advanced International Economics, Experimental Economics, Time Series Analysis using Statistical Software, Applied Data Analysis for Economics, and Health Economics</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 248, '2026-04-18', 0),
(617, 3, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/IMG-20230612.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Pratibha Kamble</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Assistant Professor &amp; HOD</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-PRATIBHA-KAMBLE---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/IMG-20230612-WA0014.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Mrs. Snehal Manduskar</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">SET, M.A, Assistant Professor</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Mrs.Snehal-Manduskar---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Mr.-Olya-Vasave.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Mr. Olya Vasave</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Assistant Professor</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Mr.-Olya-Vasave---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr />\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/person-icon.png\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dimple Mehta</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/download.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
