(630, 1, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>About the Department</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department of Education of Sathaye College (Autonomous) was established in June 1982. The Department of Education is dedicated to nurturing competent, socially responsible, and professionally skilled future educators and educational leaders. The department aims to promote quality education through academic excellence, innovative teaching practices, research orientation, and holistic student development.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The department offers a learner-centred and interdisciplinary approach to the study of Education in alignment with the vision of&nbsp;&nbsp; NEP 2020. The programme provides students with a strong foundation in educational philosophy, psychology, sociology, curriculum studies, pedagogy, educational management, guidance and counselling, and research methodology.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department emphasizes experiential learning through seminars, workshops, field visits, internships, project work, teaching practice, and interactive classroom activities. Students are encouraged to develop critical thinking, communication skills, leadership qualities, creativity, and ethical values essential for the teaching profession and related fields.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">With a team of experienced and dedicated faculty members, the department strives to create an engaging academic environment that supports intellectual growth, professional competence, and social commitment. The curriculum is designed to prepare students for diverse career opportunities in teaching, counselling, educational administration, research, curriculum design, EdTech, and the social sector.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department also promotes active student participation through academic activities, community engagement programmes, educational outreach initiatives, and skill development opportunities that contribute to the overall personality development of learners.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Key Features</strong></span></p>\n<ul style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">NEP 2020 Aligned Curriculum</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Experienced and Supportive Faculty</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Internship and Teaching Practice</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Workshops, Seminars, and Guest Lectures</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Research and Skill Development Opportunities</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Career Guidance and Mentorship</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Holistic and Value-Based Education</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Student-Centred Learning Environment</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>About the Subject</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The B.A. in Education programme is designed to help students understand the philosophical, psychological, sociological, and managerial foundations of education. The curriculum encourages critical thinking, creativity, communication skills, and professional ethics while promoting holistic development and social responsibility.</span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Students gain exposure to diverse areas such as Educational Psychology, Curriculum and Pedagogy, Guidance and Counselling, Educational Management, Teacher Education, and Research in Education and many more. The programme also emphasises experiential learning through internships, field visits, workshops, seminars, teaching practice, and project-based activities.</span><br /><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The department strives to create future educators, counsellors, curriculum designers, researchers, and educational administrators who can contribute positively to society and the evolving educational landscape.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Career Scope in Education</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">A degree in Education offers diverse and meaningful career opportunities in the academic, administrative, social, and corporate sectors. With the growing importance of quality education, skill development, counselling, educational technology, and policy implementation under NEP 2020, the field of Education has emerged as one of the most promising and socially impactful career domains.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The B.A. in Education programme at Sathaye College (Autonomous) equips students with theoretical knowledge, practical skills, communication abilities, leadership qualities, and research aptitude required for various professional roles.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Teaching and Academic Careers</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Students can pursue careers as school teachers, educators, academic coordinators, tutors, or teacher trainers after acquiring professional teaching qualifications such as B.Ed. The programme builds a strong foundation in educational psychology, pedagogy, curriculum development, and classroom management, which are essential for effective teaching.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"2\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Guidance and Counselling</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">With increasing awareness about mental health, career planning, and student well-being, there is a growing demand for educational counsellors and guidance professionals. Students can work in schools, colleges, NGOs, coaching institutes, and counselling centres after specialised training in counselling and guidance.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"3\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Educational Administration and Management</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The field of education also offers opportunities in school administration, educational planning, institutional management, and academic coordination. Graduates can work as education administrators, coordinators, admission counsellors, and programme managers in schools, colleges, educational institutions, and training organisations.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"4\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Curriculum and Content Development</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The rapid growth of digital education and online learning platforms has created opportunities in curriculum design, instructional planning, educational publishing, and content development. Graduates can work with EdTech companies, publishing houses, e-learning platforms, and educational startups as curriculum designers, academic writers, or instructional content developers.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"5\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Research and Higher Education</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Students interested in academics and research can pursue higher studies such as M.A., M.Ed., NET/SET, PhD, and research fellowships. The field offers opportunities in educational research, policy analysis, teacher education, and university-level teaching.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"6\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>NGO and Social Sector Opportunities</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Education graduates can contribute to social development by working with NGOs, community organisations, literacy missions, child welfare programmes, women empowerment initiatives, and rural education projects. These roles focus on inclusive education, awareness programmes, and educational outreach.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"7\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Educational Technology and Innovation</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The integration of technology in education has opened new career avenues in online teaching, educational software development, digital learning management, academic consulting, and training services. Graduates with creativity and technological skills can build careers in the expanding EdTech sector.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"8\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Competitive Examinations and the Government Sector</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The subject also provides a strong foundation for students preparing for competitive examinations and careers in educational departments, government projects, public service sectors, and policy-related work.</span></p>\n<ol style=\"text-align: justify;\" start=\"9\">\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong> </strong><strong>Entrepreneurship in Education</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Students can also become educational entrepreneurs by starting coaching classes, counselling centres, skill development institutes, online teaching platforms, or educational consultancy services.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The study of Education not only prepares students for employment but also develops communication skills, leadership qualities, critical thinking, social awareness, emotional intelligence, and professional ethics, making them capable of contributing positively to society.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The field of Education is therefore not limited to classroom teaching alone; it offers wide-ranging opportunities in teaching, counselling, administration, research, training, educational technology, and social development, making it a rewarding and future-oriented career choice.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p class=\"mb-50\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><code></code></span></p>\n<div id=\"section-two\" class=\"mb-50\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"></div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 254, '2026-08-13', 0),
(632, 3, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/sjagtap.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Swati M.Jagtap</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">HOD</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Swati-M.Jagtap---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ANJANA-PAUL.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Smt Anjana Paul</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Assistant Professor</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Smt-Anjana-Paul---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(633, 4, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"table-responsive\">\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 94.3321%; height: 606.6px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 37px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.0972%; height: 343.6px; text-align: center;\" scope=\"rowgroup\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>F.Y.B.A.&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"height: 343.6px; width: 83.8016%;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 40px;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #e03e2d;\">SEM I</span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>MAJOR 1: Introduction to Education</strong></span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>MAJOR 2: Introduction to Education</strong></span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>VSC (Vocational Skill Courses): Introduction To Childhood Education</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color: #ffffff; color: #e03e2d;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;SEM II</span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color: #ffffff; color: #e03e2d;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">MAJOR 1: Education for 21st Century</span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\">MAJOR 2: Education for 21st Century</span><br /><span style=\"color: #000000;\">VSC (Vocational Skill Courses): Introduction To Childhood Education</span></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px; line-heig