(720, 1, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Department of Philosophy was established on 20th June 1959. Evidently then, the department is one of the oldest and first among other departments that were established during the inception of Parle Tilak Vidyalaya association&rsquo;s then Parle college. During its infant years, it was headed and taken to a height by its first Head of department Prof. Kelshikar (1959-1979). Prof Kelshikar was succeeded by Prof. Poornima Dave (1979-2006) and then Prof. Sunita Jeswani ( 2006- to 2017). Presently the department is headed by Associate Professor Dr. Gautam Tenkale and his colleague Assistant Professor Dr. Sampada Chawan.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For nearly six decades, the Department of Philosophy has been committed to nurturing the true spirit of its discipline-the <em>love for wisdom</em>. Under the NEP curriculum, the department offers a range of papers that combine theoretical understanding with practical relevance. Courses such as Professional Ethics and Foundation of Film Philosophy, along with papers like Philosophy of Management and Administration, Living Ethical Issues, Logic, Buddhist Psychology, Philosophy of Art and Aesthetics, Philosophy of Human Resource Management, Existentialism, Philosophy of Mind, and Epistemology, introduce students to both classical and contemporary philosophical perspectives.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The department promotes learning beyond the classroom through study tours and field visits to places such as Silvassa, Daman, and the historic sites of Ajanta Caves and Ellora Caves.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Student engagement is further strengthened through Club Philosophy, which organizes exhibitions and activities, and the department&rsquo;s annual Philosophy Festival with changing themes each year. In 2024&ndash;25, the festival explored the theme &ldquo;Philosophy of Gender&rdquo; through debates, elocution, poetry, and creative activities.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Through an interdisciplinary and interactive approach, the department encourages students to engage with philosophical ideas through discussions, debates, case studies, and reflections on contemporary ethical issues, through film suggestions, helping them develop critical thinking and reasoning skills.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 262, '2026-02-23', 0),
(722, 3, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"container department-faculty\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-6 staff-wrapper\">\n<div class=\"photo-holder\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/gautamt.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">prof. Dr. Gautam Tenkale</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Professor</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Gautam-Tenkale---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/sampada-.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Sampada V. Chawan</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Assistant Professor.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Ms.-Sampada-V.-Chawan---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 262, '2026-02-23', 0),
(723, 4, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 98.5443%; height: 520px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 57px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 10px;\" scope=\"row\">Course</th>\n<th style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 10px;\">Details</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 56px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 56px;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>&nbsp;F.Y.B.A.</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 56px;\">\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\">Semester I</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Moral Philosophy</li>\n<li>MJ2 Moral Philosophy</li>\n<li>VSC1 Foundation of Film Philosophy</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%;\">\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\">Semester II</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Professional Ethics</li>\n<li>MJ2 Professional Ethics</li>\n<li>VSC1 Foundation of Film Philosophy</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 86px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 86px;\" scope=\"row\"><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\">S.Y.B.A.</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 86px;\">\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\">Semester III</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Western Philosophy</li>\n<li>MJ2 Philosophy of Religion-I</li>\n<li>MN1 Philosophy of Religion-I</li>\n<li>VSC- Philosophy of Management and Administration</li>\n<li>Field Project<br /><br /></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 86px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 86px;\" scope=\"row\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 86px;\">\n<div>\n<div>\n<p><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\"><strong>Semester IV</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Philosophy of Religion II</li>\n<li>MJ2 LIving Ethical Issues</li>\n<li>MN1 LIving Ethical Issues</li>\n<li>Community Engagement Program</li>\n<li>OE: Philosophy of Yoga (Offered to science)</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 236px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 236px;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>T.Y.B.A.</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 236px;\">\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\">Semester V</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Logic</li>\n<li>MJ2 Critical Thinking-I</li>\n<li>IKS Foundation of Buddhist Psychology</li>\n<li>Minor Critical Thinking-I</li>\n<li>Elective 1A Modern Western Philosophy</li>\n<li>VSC Philosophy in Human Resource Management</li>\n<li>Field Project in Philosophy</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%;\" scope=\"row\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%;\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #ba372a;\"><strong>Semester VI</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>MJ1 Logic</li>\n<li>MJ2 Critical Thinking-II</li>\n<li>MJ3 Existentialism</li>\n<li>MN1 Critical Thinking-II</li>\n<li>Elective 1A Epistemology</li>\n<li>On Job Training in Philosophy</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 46px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.1667%; height: 46px;\" scope=\"row\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Add-on Courses&nbsp;</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.7321%; height: 46px;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">1<a title=\"Professional Ethics\" href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/professional-ethics/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">. Professional Ethics</a></span><strong><br /><br /></strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"> <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/sathayecollege.edu.in/film-and-philosophy/home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2. Film &amp; Philosophy</a></span><strong><br /></strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>', '1', 0, 1, '', 262, '2026-02-23', 0),
(724, 5, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>FYBA Philosophy Paper I (NEP)</p>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ1-SEM-1-introduction-to-philosophy-f6c191ea-4666-4482-a2f4-9e7ff319d199.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ1 Introduction to Philosophy SEM I</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ2-SEM-1-Indian-Philosophy-7688bf49-5f74-4966-ad5f-6b37eee052cf.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ2 Indian Philosophy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ3-SEM-1-Moral-Philosophy-1099bc00-b596-44aa-9506-8da341faaab3.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ3 Moral Philosophy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ4-SEM-2-Philosophy-of-Yoga-8e3245d7-aea1-4c4f-95b3-ebd0f7f9b15e.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ4 Philosophy of Yoga</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ5-SEM-2-Feminist-Philosophy-8dda226a-0bf9-43e0-a37f-900326b56362.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ5 Feminist Philosophy sem 2</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MJ6-SEM-2-Moral-Philosophy-b331f938-68e1-493e-80f5-8157be5d067d-(2).docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MJ5 Moral Philosophy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/VSC-SEM-1-PROFESSIONAL-ETHICS-008e5959-b6b3-44ac-955d-23bf8fdb44d4.docx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">VSE Professional Ethics</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/VSC-SEM-2-FOUNDATION-OF-FILM-PHILOSOPHY-07f02e13-2eaf-46e5-b9e4-d8c3f0e59ef6-(1).pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">VSC Foundation of Film Philosophy SEM 2 </a></li>\n</ul>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/SYBA-SYLLABUS-c310c35c-2f0d-4024-afc0-5f49a68c6411.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SYBA Philosophy Paper II &amp; III</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"TYBA SYLLABUS&nbsp;\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.ed