-Image-2024-12-08-at-8.52.00-PM.jpeg\" data-title=\"Philosophy  festival\" data-lightbox=\"g3\"></a></div>\n                    <div class=\"desc pt-3\">Philosophy  festival (2023-24)\n                    </div>\n                </div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(735, 1, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Highlights of the Department</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Political Science Department, established in 1971, became a full-fledged Department with Political Science as a Major course in 1990.</li>\n<li>It is one of the most dynamic Departments, offering both Political Science Major &amp; Minor career-oriented courses to the students.</li>\n<li>Strength of the Department is experienced faculty.</li>\n<li>It helps students prepare for competitive exams &amp; careers broadly in law, media, social work &amp; number of related areas.</li>\n<li>The Department emphasises skill development through guest lectures, alumni interactions, field visits, legislative assembly visits, fellowships &amp; internships, etc.</li>\n<li>The Department fosters a fellowship/ internship culture among students in light of NEP 2020 implementation.</li>\n<li>Students of the Department have consistently excelled in academics and extracurricular activities, winning several \'&rsquo;Best Student\" awards of the College successively for many years till date.</li>\n<li>The Department has produced five University rank holders, with alumni succeeding in fields like law, social work, journalism, research, teaching, and active politics.</li>\n<li>The Department has a strong placement record of students. It offers internships and fellowships of prestigious bodies such as Praja Foundation, MBMC Internship, Piramal Foundation\'s Gandhi Fellowship, and an online NHRC internship to upskill the talent of students.</li>\n<li>The Department is successfully implementing&nbsp; NEP 2020 by offering a number of Major, Minor and VSC innovative courses to the students in tune with NEP 2020.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>University Rank Holders of the Department:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-responsive\">\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Name of the Student</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>Year of Passing</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>University Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>Percentage Secured</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Babita Bargade</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>1995</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>1<sup>st</sup> Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>71%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Prachee Phadke &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>1996</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>2<sup>nd</sup> Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>70%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Minal Mapuskar &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>1998</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>1<sup>st</sup> Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>68%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Kumkum Mishra</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>2002</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>2<sup>nd</sup> Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>70%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"169\">\n<p>Tejasi Bhandari</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"115\">\n<p>2013</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"142\">\n<p>3<sup>rd</sup> Rank</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"132\">\n<p>71%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary National Conference</strong></p>\n<p>The Department successfully organized two-day Interdisciplinary National Conference on 9th and 10th December 2022 on the theme of <strong>\'Contemporary Issues and Concerns in Globalization, Nationalism and Geo-politics\'</strong> in collaboration with ICSSR, Western Regional Centre.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Achievements of the Students</strong></p>\n<p>The students of the Department have successfully cleared competitive exams like MPSC and pursuing careers in law and teaching professions, in media, journalism and entertainment industry, in the field of social work and even active politics.&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Harshala Kawale successfully cleared MPSC exam in 2015 and presently posted as Principal Judicial Magistrate at Bhiwandi Court in Thane district.</li>\n<li>Laaghavi Sawant, presently working as News Anchor on Lokshahi Marathi News Channel.</li>\n<li>Akshit Shinde, successfully completed the prestigious Elected Representatives Fellowship of Praja Foundation in 2018-2019.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Yashashree Rane and Pravin Zore, two students of the Department have successfully completed the prestigious Elected Representatives Fellowship of Praja Foundation in 2019-2020.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Bhakti Anerao, successfully completed the prestigious Indian Political Action Committee Fellowship in 2019-2020.</li>\n<li>Snehal Jangam, successfully completed Observer Research Foundation (ORF) Fellowship in 2019-2020.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Snehal Jangam was also awarded 2nd prize in prestigious &lsquo;Speak for India&rsquo; - Maharashtra Edition, India&rsquo;s largest intercollegiate state-level debate competition organized by the Federal Bank in 2019-2020.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Shenal Jangam also secured 2nd runner-up position in Jack Pot Round of 51st youth festival organized by the Mumbai University in 2019-2020.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>For 3 consecutive years, students of the Department have won the Best Student Awards of the College.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Urvi Abhyankar Best Arts student of the College for 2017-2018.<br />Tanwee Amberkar Best Arts student of the College for 2018-2019.<br />Snehal Jangam overall Best student of the College for 2019-2020.</li>\n<li>Praja Foundation interns Yashashree Rane and Pravin Zore were appreciated by Deputy Mayor of Mumbai, Shri Suhas Wadkar for contributing to social work during the Covid-19 pandemic. Praja Foundation is a leading NGO working in Urban Governance in the city of Mumbai.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Rohit Sharma successfully completed MBMC\'s Safai Mitra Internship in 2021 and Swacch Sarvekshan Internship in 2022. He secured the Best Intern Award for his outstanding work from MBMC in 2023</li>\n<li>Swaraj Malekar successfully completed the Elected Representatives Fellowship of Praja Foundation in 2023. He also secured the Best Arts Student Award of the College in 2022-23</li>\n<li>Ruchi Yadav secured &lsquo;Best Arts Student Award&rsquo; of the College in 2023-24</li>\n<li>Amol Surve secured &lsquo;Best Arts Student Award&rsquo; of the College in 2024-25</li>\n<li>Sarthak Pednekar secured \'Best Arts Student Award\' of the college in 2025-26</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 264, '2026-04-13', 0),
(737, 3, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Beena-Madam.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Beena Khanolkar</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">HOD</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Beena-Khanolkar---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Ketan-Bhosale.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Ketan Bhosale</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Associate Professor</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Ketan-Bhosale---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(738, 4, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<table class=\"table table-bordered\" style=\"width: 98.8769%; height: 340px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 57px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 16.0972%; height: 10px;\" scope=\"row\">Course</th>\n<th style=\"width: 83.8016%; height: 10px;\">Details</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.0972%; height: 50px;\" scope=\"row\">F.Y.B.A.</td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.8016%; height: 50px;\">\n<p><strong>SEM I</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Constitutional Framework of India.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>VSC</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Introduction to Psephology</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>SEM 2</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Political Process in India.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 72px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.0972%; height: 72px;\" scope=\"row\">S.Y.B.A.</td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.8016%; height: 72px;\">\n<p><strong>Sem III </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Principles and concepts in Political Theory</li>\n<li>Public Administration</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>OE </strong></p>\n<p>Understanding Indian Polity for Competitive Exams</p>\n<p><strong>Sem IV</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Political Values and Ideologies</li>\n<li>Indian Administration</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>OE </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Understanding International Relations for Competitive Exams</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 208px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.0972%; height: 208px;\" scope=\"row\">T.Y.B.A.</td>\n<td style=\"width: 83.8016%; height: 208px;\">\n<p><strong>Sem V</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Western Political Thought</li>\n<li>World Politics</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Minor </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>World Politics</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Electives </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rural local Government</li>\n<li>American Constitution and Institutions</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>IKS </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ancient Indian Political Thought</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>VSC</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Understanding Politics Through Films</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;Sem VI</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Major </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Indian Political Thought</li>\n<li>India in World Politics</li>\n<li>Politics of Modern Maharashtra</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Minor </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>India in World Politics</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Electives </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Urban local Government</li>\n<li>Political process in United States</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>', '1', 0, 1, '', 264, '2026-04-17', 0),
(739, 5, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p class=\"text-break\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\"><a title=\" FYBA Political Science VSC Syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FYBA-VSC-FINAL-2024-25.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FYBA-VSC-FINAL-2024-25.pdf</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"FYBA Political Science Major Syllabus Latest\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776650173-FYBA-NEP-Major-Syallabus.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776650173-FYBA-NEP-Major-Syallabus.pdf</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"TYBA Political Science NEP Syllabus \" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776395852-TYBA-Syllabus-Sem-V-and-Sem-VI.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776395852-TYBA-Syllabus-Sem-V-and-Sem-VI.pdf</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"SYBA Political Sciecne Syllabus Latest\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/SYBA-Full-NEP-Syllabus-Re-edit.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/SYBA-Full-NEP-Syllabus-Re-edit.pdf</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"FYBA Political Science Syllabus Latest\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Edited-FY-NEP-Syallabus-Re-edit-1.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Edited-FY-NEP-Syallabus-Re-edit-1.pdf</a></p>\n<p><a title=\"SYBA Pol Sci OE\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776650630-SY-OE-POLSCI-Sem-III.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1776650630-SY-OE-POLSCI-Sem-III.pdf</a></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 264, '2026-04-20', 0),
