(780, 1, 30, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>The Department of Sociology was started in Sathaye (Parle) College in 1990. Only recently, i.e., in August 2015, it celebrated its completion of 25 years. The function was presided over by Dr. Prahlad Jogdand, Dean of the Arts Faculty, University of Mumbai, and was chaired by Shri Bansidhar Dhurandhar, Trustee of Parle Tilak Vidyala Association (PTVA).</p>\n<p>The Department offers undergraduate courses in sociology, designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of social structures, cultural dynamics, and contemporary societal issues. The curriculum is structured to equip students with analytical and research skills pertinent to the field of sociology. It has alumni of journalists (both print and television), Central government officers, lawyers, etc. who have done the Department proud.</p>\n<p>The Department of Sociology holds \"Welcome Parties\" for students of FYBA, the new entrants of the Department. These parties are hosted by students of SYBA and TYBA, who also introduce the subject to the newcomers. The parties help build a rapport with the teacher as well, so class interaction thereafter becomes more fruitful.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 372, '2025-09-23', 0),
(782, 3, 30, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/girija.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Ms. Girija Gupte</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">HOD.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Ms.-Girija-Gupte---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(783, 4, 30, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Courses offered under NEP 1.1 2025-2026</strong></p>\n<p><strong>FYBA (MAJOR 1)&nbsp; -Sem 1&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Foundations of Sociology</li>\n<li>Social Work (VSC-Vocational Skill Course)&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>FYBA (MAJOR 2)&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Foundations of Sociology</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>FYBA (MAJOR 1) Sem 2</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fundamentals of Sociology</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>FYBA (MAJOR 2)&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fundamentals of Sociology</li>\n<li>Social Work (VSC-Vocational Skill Course)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>FYBSC (OE-Open Elective) Sem 1 &amp; Sem 2</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Gender and Law-I</li>\n<li>Gender and Law-II</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>SYBA (MAJOR)&nbsp; Sem 3&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Indian Society: Structure and Change (Paper 1)</li>\n<li>Emerging Issues and concerns in Indian Contemporary Society.(Paper 2)</li>\n<li>Human Resource Development (VSC-Vocational Skill Course)</li>\n<li>Field Project (FP)&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>SYBA (MINOR)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Emerging Issues and concerns in Indian Contemporary Society.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>SYBA (MAJOR)&nbsp; Sem 4</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sociology of Development (Paper 1)</li>\n<li>Emerging fields in Sociological studies(Paper 2)</li>\n<li>Community Enhancement Program (CEP)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>SYBA (MINOR)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Emerging fields in Sociological studies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<p><strong>TYBA (MAJOR)&nbsp; Sem 5&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Social theory (Paper 1)</li>\n<li>Sociology of work (Paper 2)</li>\n<li>Intellectual Contribution of Women in Ancient India-(IKS-Indian Knowledge System)</li>\n<li>Sociology of Agrarian Society(Elective 1 A)</li>\n<li>Qualitative Social Research(VSC-Vocational Skill Course)</li>\n<li>Field Project in Sociology (FP-Field Project)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TYBA (MINOR)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sociology of Work&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TYBA(MAJOR) Sem 6</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Theoretical Anthropology (Paper 1)</li>\n<li>Sociology of Informal Sector (Paper 2)</li>\n<li>Sociology of Marginalized groups (Paper 3)</li>\n<li>Development and changes in Agrarian Society(Elective 1A)</li>\n<li>On Job Training in Sociology(OJT)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>TYBA(MINOR)&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sociology of Informal Sector</li>\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(784, 5, 30, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>FYBA Syllabus Sem 1 and Sem 2 (2025-2026)</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/13by5JnXqBCyd8ZDgdNaT2wPW9U6jQ7Vc/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/13by5JnXqBCyd8ZDgdNaT2wPW9U6jQ7Vc/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>SYBA Syllabus Sem 3 and Sem 4 (2025-2026)</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lfLkdM420y48F-9CBoGspVifwzSX9IZX/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lfLkdM420y48F-9CBoGspVifwzSX9IZX/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>TYBA Syllabus Sem 5 and Sem 6 (2025-2026)</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\"><a title=\"TYBA NEP SEM 5 AND SEM 6 2025-2026\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vEbPchUx6kMwdepwYyCgd0QO2S4RO8Ch/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vEbPchUx6kMwdepwYyCgd0QO2S4RO8Ch/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<p>FYBSC OE Syllabus -Sem 1 and Sem 2 (2025-2026)</p>\n<p class=\"text-break\"><a title=\"FYBSC NEP 2025-2026 SEM 1 AND SEM 2\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gOu6EG26TULwmfu_KKg-2hquuEZOxSEr/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gOu6EG26TULwmfu_KKg-2hquuEZOxSEr/view?usp=sharing</a></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 384, '2026-10-14', 0),
