(930, 1, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p data-start=\"168\" data-end=\"624\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong data-start=\"168\" data-end=\"317\">Established in 1959, the Department of Physics at Sathaye College (Autonomous), Mumbai, has a proud legacy of academic excellence and innovation.</strong> Initially offering an undergraduate program, the department has now expanded under the leadership of Smt. S. A. Pethe, with the launch of Postgraduate programs in Nuclear Physics and Materials Science from 2024&ndash;25, and the successful implementation of the National Education Policy (NEP-2020) from 2023&ndash;24.</p>\n<p data-start=\"626\" data-end=\"987\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The department houses well-equipped undergraduate, postgraduate and research laboratories and provides access to the college&rsquo;s Central Research Facility (CRF), enabling students and faculty to undertake independent research projects. Supported by the DBT Star College Grant, continuous upgrading of facilities and expansion of research capabilities are actively underway.</p>\n<p data-start=\"989\" data-end=\"1236\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to the central library, the department maintains its own rich departmental library, offering an extensive collection of physics books, including rare classics, and encourages students to explore beyond the curriculum at their own pace.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1238\" data-end=\"1472\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beyond academics, the department actively organizes workshops, research seminars, industrial visits, competitions, and collaborations with leading institutes such as TIFR and SPPU, creating a dynamic and engaging academic environment.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1474\" data-end=\"2143\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The department has also significantly contributed to the leadership of the college. It has given two Principals &mdash; Dr. S. V. Panse, who also served as Director of the Board of College and University Development (BCUD) at the University of Mumbai, and Dr. M. R. Rajwade, the current Principal, who additionally holds the positions of Associate Dean of Science and Technology and VC-nominated Senate Member at the University of Mumbai. Furthermore, three faculty members from the department have served as Vice Principals, and one has held the position of Controller of Examinations, reflecting the department&rsquo;s deep commitment to institutional development and leadership.</p>\n<p data-start=\"2145\" data-end=\"2250\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Department of Physics also takes pride in its distinguished alumni who have excelled internationally:</p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"2255\" data-end=\"2282\">Dr. Nikhil S. Malvankar</strong> &ndash; Associate Professor, Molecular Biophysics and Biochemistry, Yale University<br data-start=\"2360\" data-end=\"2363\" /><strong data-start=\"2366\" data-end=\"2386\">Dr. Pratik Wagle</strong> &ndash; Ph.D., Theoretical &amp; Computational Physicist, specializing in Astrophysics and Gravitation<br data-start=\"2479\" data-end=\"2482\" /><strong data-start=\"2485\" data-end=\"2505\">Mayuresh Kanagal</strong> &ndash; Research Scholar, Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR), Mumbai<br data-start=\"2579\" data-end=\"2582\" /><strong data-start=\"2585\" data-end=\"2605\">Dr. Trunali Shah</strong> &ndash; Ph.D. in Space Weather Studies from IIGM; selected under the NICT Japan program and SCOSTEP&ndash;NASA visiting scholar programs.</p>\n<p data-start=\"2733\" data-end=\"2909\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">With a vision rooted in both tradition and innovation, the Department of Physics at Sathaye College continues to inspire, nurture, and empower future generations of physicists.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 211, '2025-09-23', 0),
(932, 3, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Rajwade-Pricipal1.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Madhav Rajwade</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Principal</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Madhav-Rajwade---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/nerkar.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Prof. Dr. D. M. Nerkar</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">HOD</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Prof.-Dr.-D.-M.-Nerkar---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/yogeshg.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Yogesh Gulwadi</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Associate Professor&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1698641138-Dr.-Yogesh-Gulwadi---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr />\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/SP.jpeg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Dr. Sunil Patil</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Associate Professor&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Dr.-Sunil-Patil---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/sjaware.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Suryakant Jaware</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Associate Professor&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Suryakant-Jaware---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/spethe.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Smt. Sukruta Pethe</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Associate Professor&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3 \"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Smt.-Sukruta-Pethe---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<hr />\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div class=\"staff-card\"><img class=\"staff-card-img-top\" src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/bhandane.jpg\" alt=\"Card image cap\" />\n<div class=\"staff-card-body\">\n<p class=\"staff-card-title pt-3\">Jitendra Bhadane</p>\n<p class=\"staff-card-text\">Contractual</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"staff-card-footer mt-3\"><small class=\"text-muted\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1698641138-Jitendra-Bhadane---Sathaye-College.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Profile</a></small></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(933, 4, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>We offer the following programmes:</p>\n<p>1) B.Sc. Physics</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #236fa1;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-0.0-PHYSICS-STUCTURE.pdf\" title=\"Structure for NEP 0.0\" style=\"color: #236fa1;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span><span style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\">Structure under NEP 0.0&nbsp; for UG</span></span></span></strong></a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #3598db;\"><strong><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1.1-PHYSICS-STUCTURE.pdf\" title=\"Structure for NEP 1.1\" style=\"color: #3598db; text-decoration: underline;\"><span><span style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\">Structure under NEP 1.1 for UG</span></span></a></strong></span></p>\n<p data-start=\"1093\" data-end=\"1225\" class=\"\">At the undergraduate level, our curriculum, aligned with the <strong data-start=\"1154\" data-end=\"1194\">National Education Policy (NEP-2020)</strong>, offers a rich combination of:</p>\n<p data-start=\"1227\" data-end=\"2050\" class=\"\"><strong data-start=\"1230\" data-end=\"1247\">Major Courses</strong> covering core topics such as Mechanics, Electricity, Optics, Modern Physics, Quantum Mechanics, Thermodynamics, Solid State Physics, Electrodynamics, Nuclear Physics, and Special Theory of Relativity.<br data-start=\"1448\" data-end=\"1451\" /><strong data-start=\"1454\" data-end=\"1471\">Minor Courses</strong> for interdisciplinary exploration and academic flexibility.<br data-start=\"1531\" data-end=\"1534\" /><strong data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1557\">Elective Courses</strong> like Python Programming, C++ Programming, and Computational Physics, enhancing computational and technical skills.<br data-start=\"1672\" data-end=\"1675\" /><strong data-start=\"1678\" data-end=\"1700\">Vocational Courses</strong> in Electronics, Microprocessors, Solar Energy, and Measurement Techniques, bridging academics with industry-relevant skills.<br data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1828\" /><strong data-start=\"1831\" data-end=\"1856\">Open Elective Courses</strong> including Physics in Everyday Life, Toy Making, Weather Forecasting, and Observational Astronomy, offering students from diverse backgrounds a glimpse into the exciting applications of physics.</p>\n<p>2) M.Sc. Physics (wih Nuclear Physics and Material Science Streams for Elective)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MSc-Structure.pdf\" title=\"Structre for M.Sc.&nbsp;\"><strong></strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db; text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\">Structre for M.Sc.&nbsp;</span></span></span></strong></span></a></p>\n<p>In 2024&ndash;25, the department further expanded its academic offerings with the launch of postgraduate programs: <strong data-start=\"2370\" data-end=\"2390\">M.Sc. in Physics</strong> with specializations in <strong data-start=\"2415\" data-end=\"2434\">Nuclear Physics</strong> and <strong data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2460\">Materials Science</strong> &mdash; providing advanced training for students aiming to pursue research, higher studies, and careers in academia, industry, and technology sectors.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1227\" data-end=\"2050\" class=\"\"></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 211, '2025-09-23', 0),
(934, 5, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>F.Y.B.Sc. Physics</strong></p>\n<p><a title=\"2021-22 FYBSc (Autonomous College University syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2021-22-FYBSc-4.50-F.Y.B.Sc-Physics.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2021-22 FYBSc Physics (Autonomous College University syllabus)</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2022-23 FYBSc&nbsp; (Autunomous College Syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2022-23-FYBSc-Physics-Autunomous-College-Syllabus.pdf\">2022-23 FYBSc&nbsp; Physics (Autunomous College Syllabus)</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2023-24 FYBSc Physics NEP 0.0 syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2023-24-FYBSc-Physics-NEP-0.0-syllabus.pdf\">2023-24 FYBSc Physics NEP 0.0 syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 NEP1.0 FYBSc Major &amp; Minor Physics syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-NEP1.0-FYBSc-Major-&amp;-Minor-Physics-syllabus.pdf\">2024-25 FYBSc </a><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 NEP1.0 FYBSc Major &amp; Minor Physics syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-NEP1.0-FYBSc-Major-&amp;-Minor-Physics-syllabus.pdf\">NEP1.0</a><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 NEP1.0 FYBSc Major &amp; Minor Physics syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-NEP1.0-FYBSc-Major-&amp;-Minor-Physics-syllabus.pdf\"> Major &amp; Minor Physics syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-FYBSc-Physics-Syllabus-NEP-1_1-CO-PO-Question-Paper-Skeleton-Revised.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2024-25 FYBSc NEP 1_1 Major &amp; Minor&nbsp; Physics Syllabus CO-PO &amp; Question Paper Skeleton Revised</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 Physics FYBSc NEP syllabus for VSC\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-Physics-FYBSc-NEP-syllabus-for-VSC.pdf\">2024-25 Physics FYBSc NEP syllabus for VSC</a></span></p>\n<p><strong>S.Y.B.Sc. Physics</strong></p>\n<p><a title=\"2022-23 SYBSc Physics (Autunomous College University Syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2022-23-SYBSc-Physics-Autunomous-College-Syllabus-1.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2022-23 SYBSc Physics (Autunomous College University Syllabus)</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2022-23 SYBSc Physics Amended (Autunomous College University Syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2022-23-Amended-Syllabus-4.36-Edites-Physics-S.Y.BSc_.-Syllabus-sem-III-and-Sem-IV-2018-to-be-placed-before-Academic-Council.pdf\">2022-23 SYBSc Physics Amended (Autunomous College University Syllabus)</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2023-24 SYBSc Physics (Autunomous College Syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2023-24-SYBSc-Physics-Autunomous-College-Syllabus.pdf\">2023-24 SYBSc Physics (Autunomous College Syllabus)</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 NEP 0.0 SYBSc Physics Syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-NEP-0.0-Physics-SYBSc-syllabus.pdf\">2024-25 NEP 0.0 SYBSc Physics Syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 NEP 0.0 SYBSc amended syllabus for VSC&nbsp;\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-NEP-0.0-SYBSc-amended-syllabus-for-VSC.pdf\">2024-25 NEP 0.0 SYBSc amended syllabus for VSC&nbsp;</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2025-26 NEP 1.1 SYBSc Physics Syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2025-26-NEP-1.1-SYBSc-Physics-Syllabus.pdf\">2025-26 NEP 1.1 SYBSc Physics Syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><strong>T.Y.B.Sc. Physics</strong></p>\n<p><a title=\"2023-24 TYBSc Physics (Autonomous College University Syllabus for Core Course)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2023-24-TYBSc-Physics-FINAL-Syllabus-Mumbai-University.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2023-24 TYBSc Physics (Autonomous College University Syllabus for Core Course)</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2023-24 TYBSc Physics (Autonomous College University Syllabus for Applied Component)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2023-24-TYBSc.-Physics-Applied-Component-Electronic-Instrumentation-Mumbai-University.pdf\">2023-24 TYBSc Physics (Autonomous College University Syllabus for Applied Component)</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2024-25 TYBSc Physics (Autunomous College Syllabus)\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-TYBSc-Physics-Autunomous-College-Syllabus.pdf\">2024-25 TYBSc Physics (Autunomous College Syllabus)</a></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2025-26 NEP 0.0 TYBSc Physics Syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2025-26-NEP-0.0-TYBSc-Physics-Syllabus.pdf\">2025-26 NEP 0.0 TYBSc Physics Syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><a title=\"2026-27 NEP 1.1 TYBSc Physics Syllabus\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2026-27-NEP-1-1-TYBSc-Physics-Syllabus.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2026-27 NEP 1.1 TYBSc Physics Syllabus</span></a></p>\n<p><strong>M.Sc. Physics</strong></p>\n<p><a title=\"2024-25 MSc Physics Part I Syllabus \" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-MSc-Physics-Part-I-Syllabus.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2024-25 MSc Physics Part I Syllabus</span></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2024-25-MSc-Physics-Part-I-Syllabus-NEP-CO-PO-Question-Paper-Skeleton-Revised.pdf\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\">2024-25 MSc Physics Part I Syllabus NEP CO-PO &amp; Question Paper Skeleton Revised</span></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"MSc Physics Part II Syllabus 2025-26\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/MSc-Physics-Part-II-Syllabus-2025-26.pdf\">2025-26</a><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"2025-26 MSc Physics Part II Syllabus \" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/2025-26-MSc-Physics-Part-II-Syllabus.pdf\"> MSc Physics Part II Syllabus</a></span></p>\n<p><strong>Open Elective Courses from Physics</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #236fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #236fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"Open Elective Courses from Physics\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Open-Elective-From-Physics.pdf\">Open Elective Courses from Physics</a></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><a title=\"NEP 0.0 PHYSICS STUCTURE\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-0.0-PHYSICS-STUCTURE.pdf\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #843fa1;\">NEP 0.0 PHYSICS STUCTURE</span></strong></a></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #843fa1;\"><a style=\"color: #843fa1; text-decoration: underline;\" title=\"NEP 1.1 PHYSICS STUCTURE\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/NEP-1-1-PHYSICS-STUCTURE-2026.pdf\"><strong>NEP 1.1 PHYSICS STUCTURE</strong></a></span></p>', '1', 0, 1, 'Typo Error', 314, '2026-11-02', 0),
