(1122, 59, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Events held in Academic Year 2024-25</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h2 class=\"zv7tnb\" id=\"Pnsjpd\" aria-label=\"Share &quot;Field visit to Sakharwadi village in Satara, Maha&hellip;&quot;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18J9L0XoWXjjgtUIunKGIx0AqqY7U54eA/view?usp=sharing\">Field visit to Sakharwadi village in Satara, Maharashtra</a></h2>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/RBI\'s-Trends-and-progress-of-Banking-in-India-2024.pdf\">RBI\'s Report on Trends and Progress in Banking Sector of India</a></li>\n<li>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XY-dZZK1PgqA20yoYtH8BwgJ3PqSn4LJ/view?usp=sharinghttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1XY-dZZK1PgqA20yoYtH8BwgJ3PqSn4LJ/view?usp=sharinghttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1XY-dZZK1PgqA20yoYtH8BwgJ3PqSn4LJ/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Celebration of National Financial Awareness Day</a></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong></strong></span></h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1W_B9KvcanHfSzHBJhU_k5l8nuPS4f2V_/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Celebration of World Entreprenuer Day 2024</a><strong></strong></span></h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15He3S8sCIUVFmJJgbNh1B6QYnXEt5v-R/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Freshers Party&nbsp;</a></span></h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jjmN-r6dZS91Tdux9W5j5niQ2iHB1upE/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong></strong>Study Tour - Bombay Stock Exchange</a></span></h4>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZW9Tke4dYE16RsJb0Pab7e6BaL4SlJVN/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">World Population Day</a></span></h4>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Events held in Academic Year 2023-24</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vqQnNqZpq7POoeUKURYSsb-nf2UgdOXH/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Farewell Party</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/14lkCiVoehS2nfdIvPQjxs6Q8Ey2VHj2L/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Swami Vivekanand Jayanti</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RdmRb_4P-3Qgocp4BAubcasAL6-E1h9S/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Celebration of Shivaji Maharaj Jayanti</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1b_hqFNmnx8_tQV9gNbKFdu5OFi5I5m2d/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Trgovina Intercollegiate Fest</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MX4C8szxs0iZVjErjyPafl7iBLrkUcmO/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Study Tour - Maharashtra Urban Co-operation Bank Federation</a></span></li>\n<li>\n<p style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CWq-tQEb1J724AGHCkO2cta8HcnZMJ3l/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Celebration&nbsp;of Birth Anniversary of &nbsp;Savitribai Phule, Rajmata Jijabai and Swami Vivekanand</a></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1cVULBzlCpjoIss_AbJ8hqAyHW1q84SAK/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Jehangir Art Gallery Visit</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1B4HOnCbMnJ2Hx9HFmHJ3cbIsBY1viYGA/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">RBI Monetary Museum Tour</a><strong></strong><strong></strong></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JSOLHVsue7JQDDYplRKRHqYQ5ujtf-Mj/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Asiatic library Visit&nbsp;</a><strong></strong><strong></strong></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1l6rrXzcJKIJiuAiY_zsHl6GAAdreYGdu/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">National Teacher\'s Day</a></span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/International-Integration-Day..pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">International Integration Day</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Careers-ahead-and-MBA.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Careers ahead and MBA</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Parents---Teacher-Meeting.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Parents - Teacher Meeting</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1twO1PSkNH2fRnU7ingjFN1STucNRuxhe/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Freshers Party&nbsp;</a></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Events held in academic year 2022-23</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Interview-with-TYBA-students-Admitted-in-the-subject-of-Economics-20th-June.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Interview with TYBA Students Admitted in the Subject of Economics</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Add-On-Course-in-&ldquo;Basics-of-Econometrics&rdquo;-Certificate-Distribution-Program-15th-June-2022.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Basics of Econometrics&rdquo; Certificate Distribution Program</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/1-Career-Opportunities-in-Economics-and-Banking-Sector-867c23cf-472a-4904-b927-59770bed3a31.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Carrier Opportunities in Economics and Banking Sector</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Career-Opportunities-in-International-Trade-and-Supply-Chain-Management-54c5c9cf-1be7-477b-a96a-53070e8e94c3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Career Opportunities in International Trade and Supply Chain Management</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Talk-Show-on-Eradication-of-Poverty-5a0855fb-da36-4c3f-b53d-998dba0a92c9.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Talk Show on \"International Day for Eradication of Poverty</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">गावरान डाळ</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ANJANVEL-AGRO-TOURISM-30137baa-1e8b-465a-9b73-97ef0d12c4c3.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">ANJANVEL AGRO TOURISM</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline; color: #000000;\"><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000; text-decoration: underline;\">Talk Show on Union Budget, 2023 - Fundamental Facts and Future</a></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Events held in academic year 2021-22</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Formal-talk-of-TYBA-pass-out-students-of-2019-20-batch-with-current-TYBA-03092021-f19cb3cd-63e5-4f83-a6db-ca5b91a775ef.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Formal talk of TYBA Pass out students of 2019-20 batch with current TYBA students</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Formal-talk-of-2018-19-alumni-with-current-TYBA-students21082021-55bc2515-4c8d-40f4-9620-b08625e0ed6f.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Formal talk of 2018-19 alumni with current TYBA Students</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Debate-Competition-21st-December-2021-59a7c249-565a-4f9c-ab8d-44f23670f774.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Debate Competition</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Elocution-competition-18-February,-2022-0e0cb0a3-7dab-48eb-bb10-db24368b5390.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Elocution Competition</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Educational-Field-trip-16th-February-2022-cf000988-219f-408c-a3ae-6f10a2d0693d.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Educational Field Trip</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Essay-competition-18-February,-2022-554abe29-d1bc-48e5-9c75-c41b2ed3dada.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Essay Competition</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Webinar on economics</span></li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Webinar on Behavioural Economics and Policy</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/event/webinar-on-behavioural-economics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Gallery</a></span></p>\n<div><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/eco-780c207d-e990-4c9b-807f-11859e067623.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"250\" /></div>\n<p>TALK SHOW ON &ldquo;UNION BUDGET&rdquo; 2018</p>\n<p>Department has organized a Talk Show on Union Budg&hellip;</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/event/talk-show-on-%E2%80%9Cunion-budget%E2%80%9D-2018\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">View Gallery</a></span></p>\n<div><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/ts4-2a6a9c8c-14a2-407d-87eb-e950497b6443.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"250\" /></div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 182, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1123, 59, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4 col-md-4 col-sm-12\">\n<div id=\"carouselExampleCaptions\" class=\"carousel slide\" data-bs-ride=\"carousel\">\n<div class=\"carousel-indicators\"><button type=\"button\" data-bs-target=\"#carouselExampleCaptions\" data-bs-slide-to=\"0\" class=\"\" aria-label=\"Slide 1\"></button> <button type=\"button\" data-bs-target=\"#carouselExampleCaptions\" data-bs-slide-to=\"1\" aria-label=\"Slide 2\" class=\"active\" aria-current=\"true\"></button> <button type=\"button\" data-bs-target=\"#carouselExampleCaptions\" data-bs-slide-to=\"2\" aria-label=\"Slide 3\" class=\"\"></button></div>\n<div class=\"carousel-inner\">\n<div class=\"carousel-item active carousel-item-start\"><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/a1.jpg\" class=\"d-block w-100\" alt=\"...\" />\n<div class=\"carousel-caption d-none d-md-block\">\n<h5>First slide label</h5>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-img-overlay\"></div>\n<div class=\"carousel-item carousel-item-next carousel-item-start\"><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/a2.jpg\" class=\"d-block w-100\" alt=\"...\" />\n<div class=\"carousel-caption d-none d-md-block\">\n<h5>Second slide label</h5>\n<p>Some representative placeholder content for the second slide.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-img-overlay\"></div>\n<div class=\"carousel-item\"><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/a3.jpg\" class=\"d-block w-100\" alt=\"...\" />\n<div class=\"carousel-caption d-none d-md-block\">\n<h5>Third slide label</h5>\n<p>Some representative placeholder content for the third slide.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-img-overlay\"></div>\n<button class=\"carousel-control-prev\" type=\"button\" data-bs-target=\"#carouselExampleCaptions\" data-bs-slide=\"prev\"> <span class=\"carousel-control-prev-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Previous</span> </button> <button class=\"carousel-control-next\" type=\"button\" data-bs-target=\"#carouselExampleCaptions\" data-bs-slide=\"next\"> <span class=\"carousel-control-next-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Next</span> </button></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-8 col-md-8 col-sm-12\">\n<h1><strong>Department Of Education</strong></h1>\n<hr />\n<p class=\"news-text-line\">Zoological excursion of FYBSC students was arranged on 18th January 2023 to Rajiv Gandhi Zoological Park , Kartaj , Pune . Total 34 Students Participated in the excursion. 3 teachers accompanied the students during this zoological excursion.<strong> Name of the teachers</strong>: shri. Jitendra Shedge, Shri. Nikhil Yadav, Smt Amruta Pharande</p>\n</div>\n<div><hr /></div>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-4\">\n<div><strong>Quiz, Speech :</strong> Shruja, Shrusthi<br /><strong>Story telling : </strong>Isha, Harhsita, Shivani, Sakshi, Ekta<br /><strong>Cake making and Poem Writing :</strong> Harsha&nbsp;<br /><strong>Blog Writing :</strong> Aadita</div>\n<div><strong>Blackboard, Mandala art : </strong>Isha, Harshita, Aditi</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-lg-8\">\n<p>The Department of Education of Sathaye College has celebrated Gurupurnima on 3rd July 2023 at 10 am. Gurupurnima is also known as Vyasapurnima. A guru is someone who teach life lessons and led us to a path of glory. Gurupurnima is celebrated to express gratitude, respect and regard for Guru`s. The students and teachers of the department had planned and organized various activities for SYBA and TYBA students. The celebration started with speech, quiz, storytelling, blog and poem. The quiz was the blend of online and offline mode. The event was organized in such way that students may participate in extra curriculum activities and get motivated to showcase their talent.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"table-responsive\">\n<table class=\"table table-bordered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 25.1454%; height: 10px;\" scope=\"row\">Event Name</th>\n<th style=\"width: 7.72537%; height: 10px;\">Date</th>\n<th style=\"width: 150.829%; height: 10px;\">Description</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.1454%; height: 54px;\">Gurupournima Celebration</td>\n<td style=\"width: 7.72537%; height: 54px;\">13/07/2022</td>\n<td style=\"width: 150.829%; height: 54px;\">Education Department in collaboration with NSS celebrated Gurupournima Day. Speeches were given by students.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 126px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.1454%; height: 126px;\">Guest Lecture</td>\n<td style=\"width: 7.72537%; height: 126px;\">25/08/2022</td>\n<td style=\"width: 150.829%; height: 126px;\">Guest lecture was organized on \"Introduction to Mental Health and Suicide Prevention.\" Smt. Meenakshi Nagwekar, Director of SLW and Smt. Briliana Lopes, Training Manager, MSW has interacted with students on this topic.&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 162px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.1454%; height: 162px;\">Field Visit</td>\n<td style=\"width: 7.72537%; height: 162px;\">18/01/2023</td>\n<td style=\"width: 150.829%; height: 162px;\">Field Visit for TYBA Education students has organized on 18th January 2023 to \' Industrial Home for Blind Women\', Andheri (west). This visit was the part of the requirement of the semester VI syllabus in Education laid down by the University of Mumbai.<br /><br /></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 108px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25.1454%; height: 108px;\">Gurupoornima Celebration 2023</td>\n<td style=\"width: 7.72537%; height: 108px;\">03/07/2023</td>\n<td style=\"width: 150.829%; height: 108px;\">Education Department celebrated Gurupoornima event on 3rd July 2023 with various activities in blended mode. The students of TYBA and SYBA participated in online quizzes very actively.&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 208, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1124, 59, 21, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Oral-Presentations-TYBA-2022-23-cc84d840-3f12-4fb4-afec-5ac958cd39a5.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Oral Presentations</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Oral-Presentations-TYBA-2022-23-(2)-04481dd2-4c08-4fdf-a55e-38ebe3bf54a8.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Oral Presentation II</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Visit-to-Kala-Ghoda-Festival-2023-(2)-b3e77b0d-caa2-4236-83dc-e0d46a0da8d2.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Study Tour</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/jpg2pdf-c792ffa1-d375-4651-a46f-2f77d51c512c.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kala Ghoda Festival 2023</a></li>\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1125, 59, 22, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Interdisciplinary National Conference</p>\n<p>The Department of Geography, Political Science, Ph&hellip;</p>\n<p><a href=\"#\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">View Gallery</span></a></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Interdisciplinary-National-Conference-532a1003-f8d6-41ed-b70b-a1ae0fd3e69b.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"189\" /></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1129, 59, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p id=\"section-one\" class=\"text-capitalize font-weight-600 mt-0 font-28 line-bottom\"><strong>WDC And Dept OF Philosophy.</strong></p>\n<p>Activity Name: &lsquo;Let&rsquo;s Talk 2020-21&rsquo;</p>\n<p>Student&rsquo;s activity 2021-22 &lsquo;Discussion Meet&rsquo;</p>\n<p><strong>&lsquo;Debate Competition<br /></strong></p>\n<p>&lsquo;Department of Philosophy and The Extension Committee of Government Law College awareness program&nbsp;&lsquo;Right to Privacy&rsquo;&rsquo;.</p>\n<p>On the 30th of November 2021,</p>\n<ul class=\"list-items-pdf\">\n<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Philosophy Festival Report 2022-23</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">National Conference 2022-23 Report</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Study Tour To Silvassa 22-23</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Corporate Workshop 2022-23</a></li>\n<li>\n<p><a title=\"PHILOSOPHY FESTIVAL 2023-24\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Report-on-Philosophy-festival-2023-24.docx\"><strong>REPORT ON </strong><strong>PHILOSOPHY FESTIVAL</strong></a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>PHILOSOPHY FESTIVAL 2023-24 </strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Department of Philosophy organized a two-day event called Philosophy Festival under it&rsquo;s Club Philosophy on 7<sup>th</sup> and 8<sup>th</sup> December 2023 in the college premises.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n<li>Kintsugi (branch- Aesthetics)- the Japanese art of repairing broken pottery using gold. In this activity small earthern lamps were given to the visitors of the stalls and were asked to break them. The broken lamps then had to be rejoined using glue and then the broken lines were asked to be painted using paints of their choice.</li>\n<li>Animal Ethics - Various animal cutouts were kept. A cardboard was divided into three sections - Hospital, Home and Jungle. Participants were asked to place the cutouts in one of the three sections. Further, they were questioned about why they put them there and do these animals belong at those places.</li>\n<li>Dilemma (branch -Ethics)- Trolley Problem and Lifeboat Ethics: Models of these two dilemmas were shown to the participants and their decision making, perspectives and ideologies behind their decision was discussed.</li>\n<li>The Cinematic Secret (branch- Film &amp; Philosophy)- A Spinning Wheel had 12 Movies. Participants spun the wheel and got a movie for discussion. Their views on the movie were discussed upon. The participants were then told the hidden meaning in that Movie and its philosophy.</li>\n<li>Stall पे चर्चा (branch- epistemology)- Participants picked up a chit and the stall incharge initiated a discussion on it with some simple questions that further lead to a longer discussion. This activity was modelled on Socrates&rsquo; Elenchus Method.</li>\n<li>The last stall was an exhibition of reference books and other books related to Philosophy.</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e03e2d;\"><strong>Report on Study Tour To Global Vipassana Pagoda</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The Department of Philosophy organized a study tour to the Global Vipassana Pagoda on 24th February 2024 for students of the department. The purpose of the study tour was to provide students with an opportunity to explore the philosophy and practice of Vipassana meditation, understand its historical and cultural significance, and reflect on its relevance in contemporary life. A group of 21 students and 2 teachers participated in this enriching experience. The journey began in the morning, with the group arriving at the Global Vipassana Pagoda, located in Gorai, Mumbai.</p>\n</li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #e03e2d;\"><strong>Activities 2024-25</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>India Week </strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>As part of India Week 2024 organized by the Social Science Association of Sathaye College (Autonomous) from 19-24 August 2024, the Department of Philosophy conducted two activities based on the theme <strong>&ldquo;Indian Philosophy as Reflected in Indian Cinema</strong>.&rdquo; A guest lecture was held on 21 August 2024 in the college auditorium from 10:00 am to 12:00 pm, delivered by Dr. Amita Valmiki, who discussed the philosophical analysis of films and the <strong>reflection of Indian philosophical ideas in Indian cinema</strong>. The lecture was attended by 103 students from different faculties. An exhibition was organized on 23 August 2024 in the college foyer and inaugurated by Vice Principal Smt. Pramodini Sawant. TYBA Philosophy students presented posters on 20 films highlighting philosophical concepts in Indian cinema, along with handmade posters on Indian philosophical schools. Students from FYBA, SYBA, and TYBA who were part of <strong>Club Philosophy</strong> assisted in organizing the exhibition through registration, feedback collection, guiding visitors, and photography. The exhibition recorded a footfall of 152 visitors and concluded at 3:30 pm, receiving an enthusiastic response from both students and teachers.<br /><br /></p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>Philosophia- Departmental Annual Fest</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Department of Philosophy organized <strong>Philosophia- Intercollegiate Philosophy Festival</strong> on <strong>22nd and 23rd January 2025</strong> based on the theme <strong>&ldquo;Philosophy of Gender,&rdquo;</strong> exploring gender as a social construct and its intersections with identity, power, race, and class. The first day featured an exhibition in the college foyer presenting philosophical perspectives on gender along with interactive gender-sensitization activities, and alumni from the <strong>2022-23 and 2023-24 batches</strong> also attended and interacted with students. The second day, held in the auditorium, included intercollegiate competitions such as Debate (Gender Manthan), Paper Presentation, Reel Making (The Equal Lens), and Poetry (Kaavya-Sama), along with a short film screening and discussion. A special lecture on <strong>&ldquo;Understanding Gender Identity: Femininity, Masculinity and Beyond&rdquo;</strong> was delivered by <strong>Dr. Anupama Majumdar</strong>, which encouraged critical reflection on contemporary gender debates. Students presented research papers and creative works on topics such as the ideas of <strong>Simone de Beauvoir</strong>, philosophical questions around masculinity and femininity, and the intersection of gender with race and class. The festival successfully created an engaging academic platform for dialogue, creativity, and awareness, promoting philosophical thinking and gender sensitivity among students.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong> </strong><strong>Field Visit to Daman</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>The Department of Philosophy organized a <strong>field visit to Daman</strong> on <strong>15 February 2025</strong> to provide students with experiential learning beyond the classroom. A total of <strong>15 students from FYBA, SYBA, and TYBA</strong>, accompanied by faculty members Dr. <strong>Gautam Tenkale</strong> and <strong>Sampada Chawan</strong>, participated in the visit. During the trip, students explored <strong>Daman Beach</strong>, <strong>Moti Daman</strong>, <strong>Bom Jesus Church</strong>, and <strong>Moti Daman Fort</strong>, gaining exposure to the region&rsquo;s cultural heritage and Portuguese-influenced architecture. Although not directly linked to the syllabus, the visit provided valuable insights into history, culture, and community life while encouraging informal discussions on related philosophical themes. The group departed from Sathaye College at <strong>6:00 a.m.</strong> and returned at around <strong>10:00 p.m.</strong>, making the visit both educational and enriching.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e03e2d;\"><strong>Activities 2025-26</strong></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>A career-oriented guest lecture titled <strong><em>&ldquo;Philosophy for Human Resource Management: A Foundation for a Powerful Career in Corporate</em></strong><em>&rdquo;</em> was organized on 18 August 2025 in the Ground Floor Auditorium. The session was delivered by Alka Suryawanshi, an experienced HR professional with over 30 years of experience in the field. The lecture introduced students to the relevance of philosophical thinking in corporate environments and provided insights into career opportunities in Human Resource Management.<br /><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fe-PTtJjHDop5mvNdeAwnSvLTAJubd1Q/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fe-PTtJjHDop5mvNdeAwnSvLTAJubd1Q/view?usp=sharing</a></li>\n<li>During the college festival Utsav, the department organized a <strong>workshop on &ldquo;Application and Importance of Yoga in Day-to-Day Life&rdquo;</strong> on 19 December 2025. The session was conducted by S. G. Nigal, and was attended by 40 students, who learned about the practical and philosophical aspects of yoga in everyday life.<br /><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rIHihzgVTajZWc-GD8nuM1F4-_tLPXZ7/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rIHihzgVTajZWc-GD8nuM1F4-_tLPXZ7/view?usp=sharing</a></li>\n<li>The department also organized a <strong>study tour to the historic sites of Ajanta Caves and Ellora Caves</strong> from 9&ndash;11 January 2026. Students from FYBA, SYBA, and TYBA participated in the tour, which provided them with valuable exposure to India&rsquo;s rich cultural, historical, and artistic heritage. The visit encouraged students to reflect on the philosophical and cultural significance of these ancient monuments<br /><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/154excj8rDGctslw4dIOEFDxsOAeUGEOO/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/154excj8rDGctslw4dIOEFDxsOAeUGEOO/view?usp=sharing</a></li>\n<li>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-GB\">An interdisciplinary special lecture on the theme &ldquo;Gender and Environment&rdquo; was jointly organized by the Department of Philosophy and the Department of Psychology on 13th March 2026. The session was held from 8:00 am to 9:00 am in Room No. 116. The lecture was graced by Prof. Dr. Gautam Tenkale, Head of the Department of Philosophy and Ms. Anuja Pingale, Head, Department of Psychology.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The topic of the lecture was &ldquo;Ecofeminism: Bridging Gender Equality and Environmental Protection&rdquo;, delivered by Dr. Sampada Chawan, Asst. Professor, Department of Philosophy. The session aimed to provide students with an understanding of the interconnection between gender issues and environmental concerns through an interdisciplinary lens.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The program was attended by approximately 40 students of FYBA from the departments of Philosophy and Psychology.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KWa7Mi2OK1mLKe2zt-cPx1Abnku2PZa2/view?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KWa7Mi2OK1mLKe2zt-cPx1Abnku2PZa2/view?usp=drive_link</a></span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e03e2d;\"><strong><br /><br /></strong></span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 262, '2026-04-17', 0),
(1130, 59, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1131, 59, 28, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong><img src=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iBY9AC_JpTRAmgy945DhX5zVTRE09-pg/view?usp=drive_link\" alt=\"1) As a part of Utsav-22, Psychology department the event &ldquo;Magic of the Mind&rdquo; on 23rd and 24th December 2022. Seven games were arranged to be played and experienced by the visitors; games like &lsquo;card sorting&rsquo;, &lsquo;Stroop effect&rsquo;, &lsquo;9 dots&rsquo;, &lsquo;problem solving&rsquo;, &lsquo;Audios Amigos&rsquo;, &lsquo;Methods of Loci&rsquo; were a test in self-estimation and focus which encouraged out of the box thinking and exercising the command an individual has on their memory as well as their senses, attention was the key to ace these tests. The &lsquo;Illusions&rsquo; boggled the minds of the visitors as their own mind played fascinating visual tricks on them the illusions were then decoded and explained by our volunteers whereas the game of &lsquo;people in pairs&rsquo; encouraged and emphasised communication between two people.\" /></strong></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 235, '2025-09-23', 0),
