(1275, 54, 15, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<p>wdwedewdewd</p>', '<section>\n<p>The Drama Association encourages dramatic presentations by students in the form of Street Plays, Mono-acting, Mime, Mimicry, Skits, etc. The Association also hosts the Inter-collegiate Drama competition. Eminent theatre personalities are invited to give lectures on the new trends in theatre. Theatre workshops are conducted in order to explore the possibilities for interdisciplinary linkages between different forms of performing arts.</p>\n<p>The Association members are quite passionate about drama and its power to uplift society; they believe in &lsquo;art for society&rsquo;s sake.</p>\n<p>The club organizes Stage Plays and Street Plays to throw light on contemporary social problems and suggest possible remedies for the same.</p>\n<p><strong> DRAMA CLUB ACHIEVEMENT</strong></p>\n<p>Sathaye college has been instrumental in contributing skilled actors in the film, theater, and television industry. Rasika Joshi, Kadambari Kadam, Ajinkya Dev, Sachin Khedekar, Sunil Shende, Medha Manjrekar, and Madhuri Dixit Nene are just some of the luminaries who have graced the acting world in recent years. &lsquo;Natyaparv&rsquo; the theater association of Sathaye college has always been encouraging aspiring actors and providing them with a platform to hone their skills further. The students are also encouraged to participate in developing and honing their skills with regards to aspects of stagecraft, assisting in direction, scripting of scenes etc. The association has had a dream run the academic year 2015-16,2017-2018,2019 winning prizes in every competition they participated in. Following is the list of accomplishments of this year:</p>\n<p><strong>University of Mumbai&rsquo;s 48th Youth Festival (Group Prizes) </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Marathi One-Act Play: Urban- 1st prize at zonal level &amp; 3rd prize at the final round</li>\n<li>Hindi One Act Play: Tapish- 1st prize at zonal level &amp; 1st prize at the final round</li>\n<li>Marathi Skit: Gorya Sahebas Patr- 3rd prize at zonal level &amp; Consolation prize at the final round</li>\n<li>Hindi Skit: Frame Goes To- 3rd prize at zonal round &amp; Consolation prize at the final round</li>\n<li>Mime: Knock knock- 3rd place at zonal level</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>University of Mumbai&rsquo;s 48th Youth Festival (Individual Prizes) </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Manasi Prabhulkar- Best actress 1st prize for Hindi one-act play(Tapish)</li>\n<li>Manasi Prabhulkar- Best actress Consolation prize for Marathi on act play (Urban)</li>\n<li>Prajakta Naik- Best actress 2nd prize fo Marathi one-act play(Urban)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>IPTA Mumbai&rsquo;s 44th Inter College Drama Competition </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Best Production- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Writer- Hrishikesh Koli</li>\n<li>Best Director- Hrishikesh Koli</li>\n<li>Best Actress- Manasi Prabhuklar</li>\n<li>Merit Actor- Prajakta Naik</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Astitva INT Rajya Stariya Hindi Ekanki Spardha 2015 </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Best One-Act Play: Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Writer (special mention): Hrishikesh Koli- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Director: Hrishikesh Koli- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Actor 1st prize: Manasi Prabhulkar- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Actor 3rd prize: Chaitali Joshi- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best lights: Bhushan Desai- Tapish</li>\n<li>Best Set: Mukul Raj- Tapish</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Loksatta Lokankika Spardha 2015 </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Marathi One-Act Play (Urban) secured the 3rd prize at the Mumbai finals</li>\n<li>Indian National Theater Marathi One-Act Play Competition</li>\n<li>Best Actor 3rd prize: Shekhar Tiwary- Morcha</li>\n<li>Best Actor Consolation prize: Manasi Prabhulkar- Morcha</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>M.L.Dahanukar College&rsquo;s Kurukshetra 2015 </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Marathi Skit: Gorya Sahebas Patr- 1st prize</li>\n<li>Hindi Skit: Frame Goes To- prize</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Due to the overwhelming response which the plays got at various competitions, a special show of all the three plays; Morcha, Urban and Tapish was held at Dinanath Mangeshkar Natygruha on 30th November 2015 and the show too was a grand success. Thus were the achievements of the theater team this year.</p>\n</section>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1276, 64, 15, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>For Detail Reports go through the following link:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><a title=\"Event Report\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/natyaparva-Final-Report-2025-26.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/natyaparva-Final-Report-2025-26.pdf</a></p>\n<p>For Photographs of Events go through the following link:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><a title=\"Photos \" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Photos-of-events-Final.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Photos-of-events-Final.pdf</a></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Youth Festival: 2025&nbsp;\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Youth festival</strong> (marathi one act play) (final)</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :- &nbsp;<strong>साठी</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured<strong> FIRST RANK</strong> in One Act Play Group A (Marathi) competition at 58th Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival (Final Round): 2025-26 organized by the University of Mumbai at Lala Lajpatrai College&nbsp; of Commerce and Economics (Autonomous), Mahalaxmi, Mumbai on 11th September&nbsp; 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Sanket Gurav , Parin More</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Nandini Nirmal got 1<sup>st</sup> prize for best actress </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mohit Shejawale got 2<sup>nd</sup> prize for best actor </strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Youth festival</strong> (marathi skit) (zonal)</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :-<strong> &ldquo;</strong><strong>प्रश्नचिन्ह</strong><strong>&rdquo;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured <strong>FIRST RANK</strong> in Skit Group A (Marathi) competition at 58th Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival (Final Round): 2025-26 organized by the University of Mumbai at Kandivli Education Society\'s&nbsp; BK Shroff College Of Arts and MH Shroff College Of Commerce (Autonomous), Mumbai on 7 August , 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Pratikesh More</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :-&nbsp; Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Youth festival</strong> (hindi one act play) (final)</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :- <strong>&ldquo;</strong><strong>पेंडुलम</strong><strong>&rdquo;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured <strong>CONSOLATION</strong> In One Act Play Group C (Hindi) competition at 58th Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival (Final Round): 2025-26 organized by the University of Mumbai at Bhavans College, Mumbai on 15th&nbsp; September, 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Sanket Gurav</li>\n<li>Teach incharge:- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n<li><strong>Prizes: </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Nandini Nirmal got consolation for best actress </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Mohit Shejawale got 1<sup>st</sup> prize for best actor</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Youth festival Mime act </strong>(zonal)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured <strong>SECOND RANK</strong> in Mime act competition at 58th Inter-Collegiate Youth Festival (Elims Round): 2025-26 organized by the University of Mumbai at Kandivli Education Society&rsquo;s&nbsp; BK Shroff College Of Arts and MH Shroff College Of Commerce (Autonomous),Mumbai, on 7<sup>th</sup> September 2026</li>\n<li>Director:- Parin More</li>\n<li>Teacher incharge:- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>INT</strong>(marathi one act play) (finals)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :- <strong>&ldquo;</strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong>&rdquo; </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured <strong>SECOND RANK</strong> in One Act Play (Marathi) competition at 50th INT (Final Round) : 2025-26 organized by Aditya Birla Centre for performing arts at Yashwantrao Chavan Centre, Churchgate , Mumbai on 15th September,2025. The achievements of the students in the INT Competition are outlined below, highlighting their outstanding performance and commendable success in various categories:</li>\n<li><strong>Prizes:</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best Actor :- Mohit Shejawale </strong></li>\n<li><strong>2nd Best Actress :- Nandini Nirmal </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best lights :- Shyam Chavan </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best set :- Yegnesh Padave </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best Writer :- Sarika Dherange </strong></li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>आम्ही</strong><strong> </strong><strong>सारे</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></h1>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Niraj jad smurti prityarta spardha</strong> (Hindi skit)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo; </strong><strong>मै</strong><strong> </strong><strong>कलम</strong><strong> </strong><strong>हु</strong><strong> </strong><strong>मुझपे</strong><strong> </strong><strong>अन्याय</strong><strong> </strong><strong>हुआ</strong><strong> </strong><strong>है</strong><strong>।</strong><strong> &rsquo; </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong> Sathaye College (Autonomous), Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured CONSOLATION in Hindi Skit competition at Niraj jad smurti prityarta spardha organized by Annasaheb Vartak College and &lsquo;आम्ही सारे&rsquo; on 22nd August, 2025</li>\n<li>Director:- Pratikesh More</li>\n<li>Incharge Teacher :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Niraj jad smurti prityarta spardha </strong>(Marathi skit)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>प्रश्नचिन्ह</strong><strong>&rsquo; </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous), Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured <strong>FIRST RANK</strong> in Marathi Skit competition at Niraj jad smurti prityarta spardha organized by Annasaheb Vartak College and &lsquo;आम्ही सारे&rsquo; on 22nd August, 2025</li>\n<li>Director:- Pratikesh More</li>\n<li>Incharge Teacher :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>दाजीकाका</strong><strong> </strong><strong>गाडगी</strong><strong> </strong><strong>करंडक</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Name of the event :- <strong>Dajikaka Gadgi Karandak </strong>(Marathi one act play)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></li>\n<li>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle participated and got qualified for the final round in</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Marathi one act play at Dajikaka&nbsp; Gadgi Karandak&nbsp; (2025) organized by P.N.G jewellers at Anna Bhau Sathe Auditorium (Pune) on 28th September 2025. Here,</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The prize for Best Set was won by Yadnesh Padave </strong></li>\n<li><strong>The prize for Best Lights was won by Shyam Chavan </strong></li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>अलपद्मा</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name of the event :-&nbsp; <strong>Alpadma</strong>&nbsp; (Marathi one act play)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Name of the play :-<strong> &lsquo;</strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured <strong>FIRST RANK i</strong>n Marathi one act play at Alpadma (2025) organized by saiyojan committee at Yashwantrao Natyamandir (Matunga) on 10th October 2025. The achievements of the students in the Alpadma Competition are outlined below, highlighting their outstanding performance and commendable success in various categories:</li>\n<li><strong>Best director:- Mohit Shejawale, Buddhabhushan Tangde </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best writer :- Sarika Dherange </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best actor :- Mohit Shejawale </strong></li>\n<li><strong>2nd Best Actress :- Nandini Nirmal </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best lights :- Shyam Chavan </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best actress (consolation) :- Anushka Raikar </strong></li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>नवप्रभात</strong><strong> </strong><strong>नाटुकली</strong><strong> </strong><strong>स्पधा</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Name of the event :- <strong>Navprabhat krida mandal skit competition</strong></li>\n<li>Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>प्रश्नचिन्ह</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured <strong>SECOND RANK </strong>in Marathi skit at Navprabhat krida mandal skit competition held on 1st November 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Pratikesh More</li>\n<li>Incharge Teacher :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1] Name of the event :- <strong>Navprabhat krida mandal skit competition</strong> (Hindi skit)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]Name of the play :-<strong> &lsquo; </strong><strong>मैं </strong><strong>कलम</strong><strong> </strong><strong>हु</strong><strong> </strong><strong>मुझपे</strong><strong> </strong><strong>अन्याय</strong><strong> </strong><strong>हुआ</strong><strong> </strong><strong>है</strong><strong>।</strong><strong> &rsquo; </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous), Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured the prize for <strong>BEST WRITER </strong>in Hindi Skit competition at Navprabhat krida mandal skit competition on 1st November 2025</li>\n<li>Director:- Pratikesh More</li>\n<li>Incharge Teacher :- Dr.Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>अटल</strong><strong> </strong><strong>करंडक</strong><strong> </strong><strong>राज्यस्तरीय</strong><strong> </strong><strong>एकांकका</strong><strong> </strong><strong>स्पधा</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></h1>\n<p>1] Name of the event&nbsp; :-&nbsp; <strong>Atal karandak rajyastariya ekankika spardha </strong>(Marathi one act play)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]&nbsp; Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong>&rsquo;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle </strong>participated and secured <strong>SECOND RANK</strong> in set at Atal karandak rajyastariya ekankika spardha (2025) at Vasudev Balwant Phadke Auditorium (Panvel) on 6th December 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<h1><strong>लोकसा</strong><strong> </strong><strong>लोकांकका</strong><strong> </strong><strong>राज्यस्तरीय</strong><strong> </strong><strong>एकांकका</strong><strong> </strong><strong>स्पधा</strong><strong>\'</strong></h1>\n<p>1] Name of the event&nbsp; :-&nbsp; <strong>loksatta lokankika rajyastariya ekankika spardha </strong>(Marathi one act play)&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2]&nbsp; Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo;</strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong>&rsquo; </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle </strong>participated and got qualified for the finals at loksatta lokankika rajyastariya ekankika spardha(2025) at Ravindra natyamandir (Prabhadevi) on 12th December 2025.</li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>महाराष्ट्र राज्य मराठी एकांकिका स्पर्धा </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name of the event :- Maharashtra rajya marathi ekankika spardha ( marathi one act play) (zonal level)</li>\n<li>Name of the play :- <strong>&lsquo; </strong><strong>अमिग्डाला</strong><strong> \'</strong></li>\n<li><strong> Sathaye College (Autonomous) , Vile Parle</strong> participated and secured FOURTH RANK in Marathi one act play at Maharashtra rajya marathi ekankika spardha (2026) organized by Directorate of Cultural Affairs, Government of Maharashtra at Yashwantrao Natyamandir (Matunga) on 22nd January 2026. The achievements of the students in the competition are outlined below, highlighting their outstanding performance and commendable success in various categories:</li>\n<li><strong>Best Actor : Mohit Shejawale </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best Set (2nd) : Yegnesh Padave </strong></li>\n<li>Director:- Mohit , Buddhabhushan</li>\n<li>Teacher in-charge :- Dr. Sandip Kadam</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
