(1913, 90, 18, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(1914, 90, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>The Department of Economics at Sathaye College considers its alumni an integral part of its academic community. Over the years, the department has built a strong and supportive network of former students who actively engage with current learners by offering guidance, inspiration, and real-world perspectives. To bridge the gap between academic learning and professional life, the department regularly organizes alumni interaction sessions.</p>\n<p>In 2021-2022, the department conducted formal interactions with alumni from the 2018&ndash;19 and 2019&ndash;20 TYBA batches. During these sessions, former students shared their career journeys and practical experiences with current students. Additionally, an alumnus, Mr. Ishaan Upadhyay, delivered a career guidance lecture on MBA opportunities, providing valuable insights on preparation strategies and course selection.</p>\n<p>An Alumni Meet held on 11th January 2025 brought together alumni, faculty, and students. During this event, alumni shared their achievements and offered mentorship to students. The department also encouraged participation in the college&rsquo;s Alumni Carnival, where alumna Ms. Dimple Mehta showcased her entrepreneurial venture through a stall titled &ldquo;Gavaran Food.&rdquo;</p>\n<p>Recently, on 26th February 2026, the department organized another Alumni Interaction Session. Alumni from various batches participated and shared their professional experiences, career opportunities, challenges, and strategies to overcome them. This interaction provided students with valuable exposure to industry expectations, required skills, and higher education opportunities. The session proved to be highly informative and motivating.</p>\n<p>Such initiatives reflect the department&rsquo;s commitment to lifelong learning, collaboration, and strengthening the bond between alumni and current students for mutual growth and success.</p>\n<p><strong>Events organised by Department of Economics with Alumni Participation</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1g6XKcTmTLe0cpoEFmWAZ5aeKJOkAi_HI/view?usp=sharing\">ALUMNI MEET ON CUET (MASTER&rsquo;S) PREPARATION &nbsp;</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BVdU0McZfGKFb1EzlxMJCQ6hm-tkDi7K/view?usp=sharing\">ALUMNI MEET 2026&nbsp;</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1pPT8yyUU03rjHtEFvO-rB9eO6N-jQU6s/view?usp=sharing\">Alumni Engagement Meet: EcoNexus 2026&nbsp;</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1nK41Qhg51iOFvvrhZ78T1ZZYgphgJPZt/view?usp=sharing\">ALUMNI MEET 2025</a></li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 248, '2026-08-13', 0),
