(1920, 90, 28, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Department of Psychology organized an alumni interaction event on 19th September 2024, in the department room 228B, which aimed at fostering connections between the current TYBA Psychology batch (2024-25) and the previous batch (2023-24). This event provided an opportunity for students to gain insights into pursuing a Master&rsquo;s degree in Psychology and to understand various specializations available to them. A total of 15 students of the current batch and 10 alum were present today.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">During the discussion, alumni emphasized the importance of thorough college research, sharing various resources for identifying suitable institutions. They highlighted the application processes for colleges in Maharashtra as well as in other states, offering tips based on their own experiences. Additionally, the alumni elaborated on the admission processes for studying abroad, particularly in the UK, USA, and Australia, detailing necessary qualifications and standardized tests. Financial considerations were also discussed, with alumni providing information on fee structures and the importance of exploring scholarship opportunities.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The sharing of personal experiences proved particularly impactful, inspiring current students and helping them envision their future paths in psychology. Overall, the event was a valuable engagement, fostering a spirit of mentorship and community within the department. The Department of Psychology looks forward to hosting similar events in the future to continue supporting students in their academic and professional journeys.</span></p>', '0', 0, 1, '', 413, '2026-08-13', 0),
