(1937, 90, 49, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><b>&nbsp;\"<span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Career Connection: CV Writing and Job Interview\"&nbsp; November 7, 2023</span></b></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department of Botany at Sathaye College (Autonomous) organized an Alumni Interaction event titled \"Career Connection: CV Writing and Job Interview\" on 7th November 2023. The program, coordinated by Smt. Jayashree Gaikwad, targeted both undergraduate and postgraduate Botany students, with 48 students and 9 staff members participating. The event, held in the Biolab, featured Shri Milind Rane, HR Head at Columbia Pvt. Ltd., as the invited resource person. The primary objectives included raising student awareness about CV writing and preparing them for job interviews. The outcome was positive, with students actively engaging in the session and gaining a better understanding of essential skills for CV writing and building confidence to face job interviews.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b>Essay Writing Competition on gender equality </b><b>November 6, 2023</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department of Botany and Women\'s Development Cell at Sathaye College organized an impactful Essay Writing Competition on gender equality, held on 6th November 2023, in Room No. 115. Coordinated by Smt. Jayashree Gaikwad, the event drew participation from both undergraduate and postgraduate students, totaling 9 students and 2 staff members. The session, judged by Smt. Leela Chauhan, aimed to create awareness and enhance understanding of gender equality while honing writing skills. The outcome was commendable, with students producing insightful essays that addressed the contemporary challenges of gender equality and proposed effective measures to overcome such issues in the current societal context. The event successfully fulfilled its objectives of promoting awareness and fostering thoughtful discussions on this critical subject.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b>\"Indian Style Flower Arrangement and Biojewellery,\" November 6, 2024</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Department of Botany at Sathaye College organized an engaging event on 6th November 2023, titled \"Indian Style Flower Arrangement and Biojewellery,\" for undergraduate and postgraduate Botany students. With 57 students and 9 staff members participating in the Biolab, the event aimed to introduce students to Indian-style floral arrangements and biojewelry, emphasizing hands-on training for potential entrepreneurship opportunities. The session featured expert guidance from Dr. Rashmi Pandey and Smt. Chaitali Pujare. The outcome was fruitful, as students actively participated and successfully crafted Indian-style gajra, veni, and Garland Tiaras with flowers, showcasing both their creativity and practical skills in the realm of botanical artistry and biojewelry design.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b>Geo-tagging and Bio-mapping of Flora of Sathaye College Campus for Green Audit&rdquo; , 31st January 2024</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Geotagging.jpeg\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" alt=\"\" /></b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Department of Botany at Sathaye College organized a workshop \"Geo-tagging</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and Bio-mapping of Flora of Sathaye College Campus for Green Audit&rdquo; </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">on January 31, 2024, from 11:30 am to 1:30 pm in Biolab Room No. 111. This workshop, attended by 63 FYBSc and PG Botany students along with 9 staff members, aimed to train participants on the techniques of geotagging and the preparation of biomaps. The session featured Shri. D.D. Bombe, HOD of the Geography Department at Sathaye College, as the invited resource person. Throughout the event, various techniques of geotagging were demonstrated, and students actively engaged with online applications for practical geo-tagging exercises. As a result, participants gained valuable insights and skills in preparing biomaps, incorporating attributes using GPS systems and geotagging techniques. The workshop successfully achieved its objectives, providing students with practical knowledge in the intersection of botany and geography.</span></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b>&ldquo;Field Work in Botany&rdquo; , January 30th 2024</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Field-work-in-Botany.jpeg\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" alt=\"\" /></b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A workshop of </span><b>&ldquo;Field Work in Botany&rdquo; </b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">was conducted by the Botany Department on 30th January 2024 in Biolab, attended by 54 students and 9 staff members from UG and PG Botany. Shri. D.D. Bombe, HOD of the Geography Department at Sathaye College, served as the facilitator. The primary objectives were to raise awareness and provide hands-on training regarding instruments and techniques used in Botany fieldwork, including the Abney Level, pH meter, thermometer, GPS survey instruments, and soil analyzer. The workshop effectively achieved its goals, enhancing students\' understanding of these tools and methodologies.</span></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b>&ldquo;Seed Ball Making, Resin Art, and Photo Frame Making&rdquo; on February 15, 2024</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><b><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Resin-Art.jpeg\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" alt=\"\" /> &nbsp;</b></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The Botany Department at Sathaye College in collaboration with the Green Audit Committee, organized a comprehensive workshop on &ldquo;Seed Ball Making, Resin Art, and Photo Frame Making&rdquo; on&nbsp;<b> </b>February 15, 2024&nbsp; from 12:30 to 1:30 pm in the Biology Lab, Room No. 111. Coordinated by Smt. Jayashree Gaikwad, the event drew participants from UG and PG Botany, the Plant Identification Addon Course, and Green Audit, with a total of 98 students and 11 staff members. The session featured resource persons Smt. Chaitali Pujare (Botany Staff and Alumni), Shri. Pranav Jadhav (TYBSc Botany Student), and Ms. Rutuja Dhanawade (FYBSc Botany Student). The workshop aimed to raise awareness about sustainable methods of developing seed balls for tree plantations in remote areas, provide hands-on training in resin art and photo frame making using plant materials, and create awareness about entrepreneurship ideas for small-scale business development. The outcome was successful, as students learned to prepare seed balls for sustainable tree plantations and acquired skills in crafting photo frames and resin artifacts using plant materials collected from the college campus. The workshop effectively promoted sustainability, creativity, and entrepreneurial thinking among the participants.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-size: 12pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/plantae9.jpg\" alt=\"\" /></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
