"3862\">Sen Mathews, Naresh C., Sumit Kumar, A. Bhogale, D. C. Kothari</em><br data-start=\"3862\" data-end=\"3865\" /><em data-start=\"3868\" data-end=\"3936\">Advanced Nanomaterials and Emerging Engineering Technologies, IEEE</em>, ISBN: 978-1-4799-1377-0 (2013), pp. 517</li>\n<li data-start=\"3979\" data-end=\"4244\"><strong data-start=\"3982\" data-end=\"4085\">Work function measurements of copper nanoparticle intercalated polyaniline nanocomposite thin films</strong><br data-start=\"4085\" data-end=\"4088\" /><em data-start=\"4091\" data-end=\"4194\">U. V. Patil, Niranjan S. Ramgir, A. Bhogale, A. K. Debnath, K. P. Muthe, S. C. Gadkari, D. C. Kothari</em><br data-start=\"4194\" data-end=\"4197\" /><em data-start=\"4200\" data-end=\"4217\">AIP Conf. Proc.</em>&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"4218\" data-end=\"4226\">1832</strong>, 080091&ndash;93 (2017)</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 314, '2026-08-14', 0),
(2056, 94, 41, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 2, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2058, 94, 43, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Students from IT department participated in the <strong data-start=\"401\" data-end=\"441\">Fledgling Research 2025-26</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Assistive Communication for Deaf: Real TIme Sign Langiage Detection</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Devraj Pujari, Bhavesh Kerkar (TYBSc IT)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Larissa Pegado</strong></p>\n<p>Sign Language is one of the primary means of communication for the deaf and hard-of-hearing community. However, communication barriers exist between sign language users and individuals unfamiliar with sign language. This project presents an American Sign Language (ASL) Detection System that uses computer vision and deep learning techniques to recognize hand gestures and convert them into corresponding alphabets.<br />The system captures real-time hand gestures using a webcam, processes the images, and applies a trained machine learning model to classify the detected signs. Techniques such as image preprocessing, hand landmark detection, and neural network-based classification are used to improve recognition accuracy. The proposed system aims to provide an efficient and user-friendly solution for bridging the communication gap between sign language users and non-signers. The results demonstrate that the system is capable of recognizing ASL gestures with satisfactory accuracy under controlled conditions. Future improvements may include expanding the dataset, improving model robustness, and supporting full sentence recognition.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-SignLanguage.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"805\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>IOT Enabled Smart Cane</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Swayam Chougule, Jay Hatim, Prajot Kurhade (TYBSc IT)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Sumedha Barve</strong></p>\n<p>The Smart Guardian Cane for Visually Impaired with Obstacle and Water Detection is an assistive device designed to enhance safe mobility for blind individuals. At its core, the cane integrates an ultrasonic sensor to detect obstacles within a range of 20&ndash;100 cm and a water sensor to identify ground-level hazards. The system provides immediate local feedback through a buzzer and vibration motor, with intensity increasing as the user approaches an obstacle and a distinct alert for water detection. Building upon this foundation, the project introduces IoT-based enhancements to strengthen safety and caregiver support. An ESP-01 Wi-Fi module enables smart connectivity, ensuring that only deep or dangerous water triggers an internet alert to the caretaker, thereby avoiding unnecessary notifications. Additionally, an SOS button allows the user to instantly send a loud &ldquo;Help Me&rdquo; alert to the caretaker&rsquo;s phone in emergencies. A simple dashboard interface further improves usability by displaying a green indicator when the user is safe and a red indicator when danger is detected. Together, these features make the Smart Guardian Cane a reliable, low-cost, and intelligent travel companion that empowers visually impaired users while offering peace of mind to caregivers.<br />Beyond its technical design, the Smart Guardian Cane emphasizes simplicity and reliability, ensuring that visually impaired users can operate it without any additional training. The integration of IoT features transforms the cane from a basic detection tool into a connected safety device, bridging the gap between independence and caregiver support. By combining low‑cost hardware with intelligent alert systems, the project demonstrates how accessible technology can deliver meaningful impact in everyday life.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-SmartCane.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"805\" height=\"805\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Digital Lives: Real Anxiety</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Studnet Name: Vibhuti Nail, Sanika Raul (MSc DS Part I)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Sumedha Barve, Smt. Larissa Pegado</strong></p>\n<p>This study investigates the impact of digital technology usage patterns on the mental health of adolescents and young adults (primarily aged 18&ndash;25). By analyzing survey data from 95 participants, this research quantifies the relationship between usage duration, platform preference, and behavioral habits&mdash;such as checking frequency and FOMO&mdash;against a calculated \"Digital Distress Score.\" Results indicate that while total screen time is a factor, the frequency of digital interruption (phone checking) and social comparison are more potent predictors of anxiety. A Random Forest regression model was successfully trained to predict anxiety levels with high relevance to behavioral inputs.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-DigitalLives.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"803\" height=\"805\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Statistical Analysis of Unemployment Rate</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Shruti Shah, Riya Kadam (MSc DS Part I)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Sumedha Barve, Smt. Larissa Pegado</strong></p>\n<p>This project provides a comprehensive analysis of unemployment trends through an interactive dashboard. By leveraging structural findings and educational distribution data, the system identifies key demographics and sectors most affected by joblessness. The goal is to provide actionable insights for policymakers and recruitment strategists to bridge the gap between skill development and market demand.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-UnemplymentRate.jpeg\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Students from IT department participated in the <strong data-start=\"401\" data-end=\"441\">Avishkar Research Convention 2024-25 organised by University of Mumbai</strong>, where they presented innovative and well-researched posters on following topics:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Early Detection to Parkinson - Shaking Palsy</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Shraddha Malewadkar, Swarangi Sawant (MSc DS Part II)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Sumedha Barve</strong></p>\n<p>The research focuses on the early detection of Parkinson&rsquo;s Disease by analyzing MRI images and clinical tabular data. A classification model was developed to identify Parkinson&rsquo;s at different stages (Control, Prodromal, and PD) using advanced deep learning techniques like EfficientNetB0 for image classification and CatBoost for tabular data. The project aims to enhance early diagnosis by detecting subtle patterns in MRI scans that are often difficult to differentiate visually.<br />The developed model achieved 95% training accuracy and 92% testing accuracy on MRI data, and 97% training accuracy and 93% testing accuracy on clinical tabular data, demonstrating high reliability across both modalities.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-Parkinson.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"794\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Monitoring Coral Health using Image Processing and Deep Learning Techniques</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Vaibhavi Ghadage, Akshata Patankar (MSc DS Part II)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Sumedha Barve</strong></p>\n<p>Coral reefs often termed the &ldquo;rainforests of the sea&rdquo; face severe threats from climate change, ocean acidification, and disease outbreaks, which undermine their ecological and socioeconomic roles. This research develops an a coral reef health monitoring framework that classifies coral images into healthy, bleached, and diseased categories using image processing and deep learning. Traditional manual monitoring methods are labor-intensive and inconsistent, so the study uses enhanced datasets (with Sea-Thru, CLAHE, edge detection) and deep models like ConvNeXt-Base and a VGG16+XGBoost hybrid, achieving around 81&ndash;83% accuracy. The system successfully detects coral health conditions and estimates bleaching and disease severity, providing faster, scalable, and more reliable reef monitoring. The study suggests future improvements like integrating environmental data, real-time drone-based deployment, and predictive risk assessment to further support coral conservation efforts.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Research-Poster-Coral.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Other research work done by students:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Retrieval Augmentation (RAG) of Library Resources by Deploying Searchable PDF of Scanned Content Pages and Keywords Matrix for Online Search Engines&nbsp;</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Student Name: Vinita Chowkekar (MSc DS Part II)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Mentor: Smt. Swapna Gawde</strong></p>\n<p>The paper explores enhancing library resource accessibility through the digitization of printed books using Optical Character Recognition (OCR) to create searchable PDFs. This method allows users to easily locate specific topics via keyword-based searches, improving discoverability both within library portals and on external search engines. The study addresses challenges like OCR accuracy, metadata standardization, and search engine optimization (SEO). It proposes benefits such as preservation of rare books, improved accessibility for visually challenged users (via text-to-speech), and better alignment with academic curricula. The research concludes that searchable PDFs and structured metadata can modernize libraries, making them dynamic, inclusive knowledge hubs. Future suggestions include AI-based metadata tagging, multilingual OCR support, and blockchain for digital preservation.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 330, '2026-04-25', 0),
(2059, 94, 46, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2060, 94, 48, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Education and research are complementary to each other. Research-oriented teaching-learning helps higher education institutes achieve global competency. Research keeps teachers updated and makes teaching more interesting to students. It fosters application-oriented studies in students.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In view of this, the research committee has introduced two programmes to nurture the research environment in our college. The first is \"The Fledgling Researchers&rsquo; Programme,\" where students will explore their new research ideas under the guidance of their research advisors. Surely, this programme will engender the next generation of researchers.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">\"The Reminiscences of a Research Journey\" is the second programme. The senior faculty members share experiences and difficulties faced during their research journey. This encourages young teachers to conduct research and forecast potential future problems.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To facilitate the research environment, this year the college started the central research and instrumentation laboratory. It provides major basic instruments used in scientific research and different advanced software for research in languages, commerce, and the humanities.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Of 64 permanent faculty members, one has a D.Litt, 27 have PhD degrees, and eight are pursuing the doctoral programme. A total of 222 research papers have been published in national and international journals. 65 books and 9 chapters have been published in the last five years. The college has received a research grant of Rs. 40, 46,970 and 15 research projects have been completed by the faculty members.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 0, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2061, 94, 49, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<table border=\"1\" height=\"43\" cellpadding=\",5\" cellspacing=\".5\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 101.894%; height: 98px; float: left;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 41px;\">\n<td width=\"85\" style=\"width: 13.4449%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 10pt;\">&nbsp;Academic Year</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"113\" style=\"width: 12.0703%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 10pt;\">Name of the &nbsp;staff</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"76\" style=\"width: 10.3555%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 10pt;\">No of Papers</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"418\" style=\"width: 62.7148%; height: 10px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 10pt;\">Title of the Publication</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 13.4449%; height: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt;\">2023--24&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 12.0703%; height: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt;\">Leela Chauhan</span></td>\n<td width=\"106\" style=\"width: 10.3555%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n<p style=\"line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;1</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"586\" style=\"width: 62.7148%; height: 10px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 10pt;\">Analysis of cultivale soil from various regions of Maharashtra</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 10pt;\">The Journal of Oriental Research Madras, Vol. XCV - I</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 10pt;\">Year of Publication 2024</span></p>\n<p style=\"t