(2351, 97, 261, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ethics of women in the Indian context, Universal Publishing House Publication&nbsp; K.T. College. 2015</li>\n<li>Ethics in Buddhism, Social Existence, 2016</li>\n<li>Dhammapada: A Guide to Right Living, Social Existence 2321-6069</li>\n<li>भूमंडलीकरण कि चुनौतिया, भूमंडलीकरण के परिप्रेक्ष्य में साहित्य, समाज संस्कृति और भाषा International Conferences<strong>, </strong>Sathaye college, 2016</li>\n<li>Kabir Ka Darshan, Saraswati Prakashan, 2017</li>\n<li>बौद्ध धम्मातील बोधिसत्व संकल्पना paper presented in, महाराष्ट्र तत्त्वज्ञान परिषद, Mumbai, 2018</li>\n<li>Application of Buddhist environmental ethics in contemporary society, National conference, Upayojit Nitishatra, Akhil Bhartiya tatvdnyan Parishad, Maitri Publication, 2019</li>\n<li>Gandhian Philosophy: views on truth and nonviolence, Significance of Mahatma, paper presented in national conference, Gandhi\'s Methodology in 21st Century, 2020</li>\n<li>Influence of Buddhism on Mahatma Gandhi&rsquo;s Concept of Nonviolence, Studies in Indian Place Names (UGC CARE Journal) ISSN: 2394-3114 Vol-40, Special Issue-24</li>\n<li>The Buddhist concept of Brahma Viharas and its application in our daily life for healthy living.International Journal of Humanities, Law and Social Sciences Published biannually by New. Archaeological, &amp; Genological Society, Kanpur India</li>\n<li>Buddhist Realistic Approach Towards The Concept Of Happiness 2022</li>\n<li>Buddhist Psychology: Roll and Importance of Mind into Removing Suffering 2023</li>\n<li>Buddhist Ethics For Environmental Protection And Sustainable Development In Contemporary Society</li>\n<li>Ethical application of Nagarjuna\'s Sunyata (emptiness)</li>\n<li>Narayan Guru</li>\n<li>S. N. Goenka, Marathi Vishvkosh, 2019</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <a href=\"https://marathivishwakosh.org/4259/\">https://marathivishwakosh.org/4259/</a></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 261, '2025-09-23', 0),
