(2832, 97, 298, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>STUDY OF PROBABLE POTENCY OF DOXYCYCLINE ANALOGS AS POTENTIAL ONCHOCERA VOLVORUS PROTEASE INHIBITOR USING CB DOCK AS WEBSERVER.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 298, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2833, 71, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Dr. Sandeep P. Shinde has made significant contributions to the field of chemistry and education, with a remarkable academic and professional record.</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\"><strong>A. Academic Milestones:</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\"><strong>Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)</strong></span>: Dr. Shinde earned his Ph.D. in April 2015 with a thesis on \"Thermodynamic Studies of Molecular Interactions in Aqueous Solutions Containing Ionic Liquids and Polyethylene Glycols,\" under the guidance of Dr. D. H. Dagade at Shivaji University, Kolhapur.</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\"><strong>State Eligibility Test (SET)</strong>: </span>Qualified in September 2015, conducted by UGC and Savitribai Phule University, Pune.</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\"><strong>Master of Science (M.Sc.)</strong>:</span> Graduated in Physical Chemistry from Shivaji University, Kolhapur, in May 2009.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">B. Research Contributions:</span></h4>\n<p>Dr. Shinde\'s research focuses on several cutting-edge areas, including the synthesis of amino acid ionic liquids, kosmotropic and chaotropic effects of solutes, solute-solvent interactions, protein folding, phase equilibrium, nanomaterials, and spectroscopic studies of dyes.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">C. Teaching and Development Programs:&nbsp;</span></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Orientation and Refresher Courses</strong>: Participated in multiple professional development programs, including a four-week orientation program at Ramanujan College, University of Delhi, and an interdisciplinary refresher course in Chemical Sciences.</li>\n<li><strong>Faculty Development Programs</strong>: Engaged in several faculty development programs focusing on ICT tools, research methods, and analytical instruments, enhancing his teaching methodologies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">D. Teaching Experience:</span></h4>\n<p>Dr. Shinde has a robust teaching portfolio, with roles as an Assistant Professor at various esteemed institutions, including PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College, Shivaji University, and others, since 2009. His experience spans teaching physical chemistry, nanoscience, and biotechnology.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">E. Research Publications:</span></h4>\n<p>He has published 08 research papers in reputable journals, with topics ranging from memristive devices and ionic liquids to volumetric and thermodynamic studies. His work is widely recognized, with publications in journals like Materials Research Express, Journal of Nano and Electronic Physics, Journal of Solution Chemistry, J. Chem. Eng. Data and J. Phys. Chem. B.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">F. Conference Presentations:</span></h4>\n<p>Dr. Shinde has actively participated in national and international conferences, presenting his research on ionic liquids, nanomaterials, and thermodynamic studies. His contributions have been acknowledged with awards for best poster presentations and oral presentations.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">G. Workshops and Webinars:</span></h4>\n<p>He has attended and contributed to various workshops and webinars on topics like nanomaterials, laboratory safety, and educational content development, staying updated with the latest advancements in his field.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">H. Memberships and Lectures:</span></h4>\n<p>Dr. Shinde is a lifetime member of the Indian Thermodynamic Society and the Indian Science Congress. He has delivered numerous guest lectures on Electrochemistry, Molecular Chemistry and Quantum chemistry at various institutions.</p>\n<h4><span style=\"color: #e67e23;\">I. Honors and Recognitions:</span></h4>\n<p>He was awarded the Junior Research Fellowship for meritorious scholars by UGC, New Delhi, from April 2012 to April 2014, highlighting his research capabilities and academic excellence.</p>\n<p>Dr. Sandeep P. Shinde&rsquo;s achievements reflect his dedication to advancing scientific knowledge and education, making significant impacts in both research and teaching domain.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2834, 73, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ol>\n<li>Nodal Officer, Academic Bank Credits (ABC).&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Incharge of Science Association and Gravity from Academic year 2022-2023.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Member of NAAC Criteria II (Teaching-Learning and Evaluation).</li>\n<li>Member of NEP-2020 implimentaion core committee.</li>\n<li>Member of Board of Studies (BOS) in Chemistry.</li>\n<li>Member of Cultural Committee.</li>\n<li>Member of Admission Committee.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Member of Mastersoft Team&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2835, 74, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2836, 75, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ol>\n<li><span>Assistant Professor in Chemistry, PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College, Vile Parle (East), Mumbai,&nbsp; Maharashtra, India<strong>&nbsp;from 13 September 2019 to till date.</strong></span></li>\n<li><span>Assistant Professor, Department of Chemistry, Shivaji University, Kolhapur,&nbsp; Maharashtra, India&nbsp;<strong>from Nov. 2018 to May 2019.</strong></span></li>\n<li>Assistant Professor, School of Nanoscience and Biotechnology, Shivaji University, Kolhapur,&nbsp; Maharashtra, India<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>&nbsp;from July 2016 to May 2018.</strong></li>\n<li>Assistant Professor in Chemistry: Department of Chemistry, Post Graduate Department of Chemistry, Padmabhushan Dr. Vasantrao Dada Patil College, Tasgaon, Sangli, Maharashtra, India<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>from July 2015 to Apr.2016.</strong></li>\n<li>Assistant Professor in Chemistry: Department of Chemistry, Shikashan Maharshi Dr. Bapuji Salunkhe College, Miraj, Sangli, Maharashtra, India<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>from July 2014 to 2015.</strong></li>\n<li>Teaching Assistant in Chemistry: Department of Applied Chemistry, Shivaji University, Kolhapur from<span>&nbsp;</span><strong>July 2011 to April 2013.</strong></li>\n<li>Lecturer in Chemistry: Government Polytechnic, Kolhapur, Maharashtra, India.F<strong>rom Sept.2009 to May 2011.</strong></li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2837, 76, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ol>\n<li><strong>Guest lecture:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>On topic &ldquo;Photochemistry&rdquo; for M. Sc I Industrial Chemistry : from 3<sup>rd</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>June 2021 to 6<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>June 2021 in Department of Industrial Chemistry, Shivaji University, Kolhapur</li>\n<li><strong>Guest lecture:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>On topic &ldquo;Volumetric and Titrimetric Analysis&rdquo; for M. Sc I Inductrial Chemistry : from 14<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>May 2021 to 16<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>May 2021 in Department of Industrial Chemistry, Shivaji University, Kolhapur</li>\n<li><strong>Guest lecture:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>On topic Quantum Chemistry for M. Sc I (Chemistry) : from 28<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>December 2019 to 30<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>December 2019 in P. D. V. P. College, Tasgaon, Sangli</li>\n<li><strong>Guest lecture:</strong><span>&nbsp;</span>On topic Physical Chemistry for M. Sc I (Chemistry) : from 16<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>October 2016 to 17<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>October 2016 in P. D. V. P. College, Tasgaon, Sangli</li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
