(2843, 95, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Books Published:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Future Unfolded: Sciene and Technology Frontiers Volume-I,&nbsp;BHUMI PUBLISHING, Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a> , ISBN:978-81-989981-4-9, July 2025.</li>\r\n<li>&ldquo;Innovative Approaches in Science and Technology Research Volume II, \" BHUMI PUBLISHING, Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a>, ISBN: 978-81-981907-1-0, October 2024.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;\"NEP- 2020: Challenges and Opportunities\" BHUMI PUBLISHING, Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;, ISBN: 978-93-95847-06-3, , February, 2024.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;\"Research and Reviews in Chemical Science Volume I \" BHUMI PUBLISHING, Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;, ISBN: 978-93-95847-58-2, April- 2024.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Book Chapters :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Book Chapter on \" Impact and Frontiers of ICT in Higher Education: Teaching learning and Evaluation\" in Book \"Impact of ICT in Teaching, Learning and Evaluation Process\" Published by Harshwardhan Publication Pvt.Ltd. Limbaganesh, Dist. Beed (Maharashtra) Pin-431126,&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:vidyawarta@gmail.com\">vidyawarta@gmail.com</a>, ISBN 978-93-85882-33-3, Chapter -11, Page number 89-99, Dec. 2021.</li>\r\n<li>Book Chapter on \" Impact of ICT on Teaching &amp; Learning in the Modern Era of 21st Century\" in Book \"Impact of ICT in Teaching, Learning and Evaluation Process\" Published by Harshwardhan Publication Pvt.Ltd. Limbaganesh, Dist. Beed (Maharashtra) Pin-431126,&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:vidyawarta@gmail.com\">vidyawarta@gmail.com</a>, ISBN 978-93-85882-33-3, Chapter -10, Page number 100-109, Dec. 2021.</li>\r\n<li>Book Chaper on\"REVITALIZING PEDAGOGY: CHALLENGES AND OPPORTUNITIES IN IMPLEMENTING NEP-2020\" in Book \"NEP- 2020: Challenges and Opportunities\" BHUMI PUBLISHING,&nbsp;Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;, ISBN: 978-93-95847-06-3, Chapter -09, Page number 75-93, February, 2024.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Book Chaper on\" EXPLORING THE VERSATILE APPLICATIONS OF IONIC LIQUIDS: FROM ELECTROCHEMISTRY TO GREEN CHEMISTRY \" in Book \"Research and Reviews in Chemical Science Volume II\" BHUMI PUBLISHING, Nigave Khalasa, Tal &ndash; Karveer, Dist &ndash; Kolhapur, Maharashtra, INDIA 416 207,&nbsp; E-mail:&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:bhumipublishing@gmail.com\">bhumipublishing@gmail.com</a>&nbsp;, ISBN: 978-93-95847-31-5, Chapter -08, Page number 87-102, April- 2024.</li>\r\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2844, 96, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ol>\n<li>National level webinar on &ldquo; Feedback, SSS, Best and Distinctive Practices&rdquo; organised by PGK Mandals Haribhai V. Desai Arts, Science and Commerce, college, Pune from 19<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>May 2021 to 21th May 2021</li>\n<li>National level Webinar on &ldquo; Revised Guidelines on NAAC&rdquo; organised by University of Mumbai, Department of Commerce in association with Swami Hansumani Maharaj Degree college of Commerce, Mumbai. 22<sup>nd</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>Feb. 2021</li>\n<li>National Level Webinar on &ldquo;Teaching-Learning Process: Learning the Unlearned&rdquo; organised by University of Mumbai on 24<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>April 2021</li>\n<li>National webinar on &ldquo;Marketing Insights&rdquo; organised by PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College, Vile Parle, Mumbai on 4<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>July 2020.</li>\n<li>National Level Seminar on &ldquo;Advances in Material Science&rdquo; organised by department of Chemistry, Maharshi Dayanand College of Arts, Science and Conference, Parel, Mumbai on 20<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>July 2020.</li>\n<li>National Webinar on &ldquo;Bioremediation- A tool for environment clean-up&rdquo; organised by Shri Raosaheb Ranrao Patil Mahavidyalaya, Savlaj on 21<sup>st</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>July 2020.</li>\n<li>National Webinar on &ldquo; Covid-19 Cure Precausions Through Naturopathy, Yoga, Stress Management and Diet&rdquo; organised by P. D. V. P. College, Tasgaon, Sangli, on 11<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>July 2020.</li>\n<li>International Webinar on &ldquo; The Reflections of Pandemics on Literature, Culture and Society&rdquo; organised by PTVA&rsquo;s Sathaye College, Vile Parle, Mumbai on 10<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>July 2020.</li>\n<li>National Webinar on &ldquo; Laboratory Safety Practices&rdquo; organised by SIES College of Arts, Science and Commerce, Sion West, Mumbai on 31<sup>st</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>May 2020</li>\n<li>Workshop on &ldquo; Solution from Synthesis to Characterisation of Nanomaterials&rdquo; organised by School of Nanoscience and Technology, Shivaji University, Kolhapur and Anton Paar PVT limited, on 26-27<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>March, 2018.</li>\n<li>GAIN programme on &ldquo;Cancer and Neurological Nanotechnology from Basic to Translational and clinical sciences&rdquo; organised by School of Nanoscience and Technology, Shivaji University, Kolhapur and Ministry og Human Resource Development, 14<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>-18<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>Nov. 2016.</li>\n<li>Designing laboratory sessions for Meaningful Learning in Undergraduate Chemistry under Savitribai Phule University, Pune, State level Workshop, Jan 4<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>-5<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>2016, Sir Parshurambhau, college, Pune.</li>\n<li>Workshop on Revised syllabus of B.Sc. III in Physical Chemistry subject Paper No. IX and XIII under Shivaji University, Kolhapur organised by &ldquo;Dr. Pantangrao Kadam Mahavidhyalaya, Sangli, on 20<sup>th</sup><span>&nbsp;</span>Aug. 2015</li>\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2845, 97, 299, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>A. PATENTS: </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>1. DESIGN Indian Patents NO. : 446670-001 DATE: 04/02/2025 </strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>NAME:&nbsp; IOT ENABLED WATER LEVEL INDICATION DEVICE</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>2.&nbsp;</strong><strong>DESIGN UK Patents Design NO. : 6509389 Grant DATE:8 March 2026</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>NAME: Quantum Chemistry and Spectroscopic Analysis Device</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>B. Research Publications:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Frugal discrete Memristive device based on potassium permanganate solution,&nbsp;<strong>Materials Research Express</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>2021</strong>; 8 (7),&nbsp;076304 (1-13), 572-892. ISSN:&nbsp;2053-1591.</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Resistive Switching property of Bmim Br Ionic liquid under the influence of ZnO nanorods, Journal of Nano and&nbsp;electronic&nbsp;Physics,<strong>2020</strong>; 12 (2);02003-1-02003-4. ISSN:&nbsp;2077-6772</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Memristive Switching in Ionic liquid- based two terminal discrete devices, Ionics,&nbsp;<strong>2019</strong>; 25: 5575-5583. ISSN:1862-0760 (Impact factor=2.29)</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Volumetric and Compressibility studies and Phase equilibria of aqueous biphasic systems of alcohols using Phase diagram,&nbsp;<strong>SN Applied Sciences</strong>, 1:671,&nbsp;<strong>2019</strong>.</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Apparent and transfer molar volumes for aqueous solutions containing Polyethylene Glycols and Amino Acid Ionic Liquids at 298.15 K.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>J.&nbsp;<strong>Solution Chemistry</strong>, 47, 1060-1078,&nbsp;<strong>2018</strong>. (Impact factor = 1.4)</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al.&nbsp;Osmotic and Activity Coefficients for Binary Aqueous Solutions of 1‑Butyl-3-methylimidazolium Based Amino Acid Ionic Liquids at 298.15 K and at 0.1 MPa,&nbsp;<strong>J. Chem. Eng. Data</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>2015</strong>,&nbsp;60, 635&ndash;642 (Impact factor=2.045)</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Density and sound speed study of hydration of 1-butyl-3-methylimidazolium based amino acid ionic liquids in aqueous solutions&nbsp;<strong>J. Chem. Thermodynamics</strong>&nbsp;79,&nbsp;<strong>2014</strong>, 192&ndash;204 (Impact factor = 2.432)</li>\r\n<li>S. P. Shinde et.al. Thermodynamic Studies of Ionic Hydration and Interactions for Amino Acid Ionic Liquids in Aqueous Solutions at 298.15 K,&nbsp;<strong>J. Phys. Chem. B</strong>&nbsp;<strong>2013</strong>, 117, 1031&minus;1043 (Impact factor = 3.377)</li>\r\n</ol>', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
