(2931, 79, 306, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Highlights:</strong></span></p>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1. Isolation of Lipase Producers from the Environment and Standardization of Lipase Detection Method</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Screening:</strong> Isolated lipase-producing bacteria from different environmental samples.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Taxonomical Identification:</strong> Utilized BLAST search analysis for the identification of bacterial species.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Lipase Study:</strong> Investigated lipase enzymes from <em>Candida rugosa</em> and <em>Candida antarctica</em>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Standardization Methods:</strong> Standardized titrimetric and spectrophotometric methods, including phenyl acetate and p-nitrophenyl dodecanoate methods for lipase activity detection.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2. Optimization Studies of Lipase Enzyme and Its Purification</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Optimization for Production:</strong> Enhanced lipase production through submerged fermentation techniques.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Enzyme Extraction:</strong> Extracted lipase from chicken pancreas.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Purification:</strong> Performed purification and characterization of lipase enzymes.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3. Immobilization of Lipases and Its Application in Bio Flavor Synthesis</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Esterification:</strong> Used lipase for esterification reactions involving acids and alcohols.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Transesterification:</strong> Catalyzed esterification and transesterification of coconut and palm oils with alcohols.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Detection Methods:</strong> Employed GC-HRMS, TLC, and microfluidics for ester detection.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Optimization Studies:</strong> Improved immobilization methods for lipase and bio flavor production.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Ester Production:</strong> Synthesized a variety of esters, including butyl acetate, ethyl acetate, and isoamyl acetate, as well as transesters like isobutyl stearate.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Oil Esterification:</strong> Esterified coconut and palm oils with alcohols to produce various esters and transesters such as ethyl laurate and butyl palmitate.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4. Use of Low-Cost Microfluidics for Detection of Microbial Lipase Activity and Esters</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Microfluidics Systems:</strong> Developed paper, cotton, and PDMS-based microfluidic devices for detecting lipase activity and ester production.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Onsite Detection:</strong> Enabled rapid onsite detection of lipase activity and esters.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Smartphone Integration:</strong> Integrated smartphone technology with microfluidics, allowing mobile cameras to capture reaction color changes, and used software for analysis, eliminating the need for colorimeters or spectrophotometers.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5. Detection of Cysts from Water Bodies</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Cyst Detection:</strong> Utilized fluorescent microscopy to detect <em>Cryptosporidium parvum</em> and <em>Giardia lamblia</em> cysts.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Microfluidic Biosensor:</strong> Developed a self-made microfluidic biosensor for rapid detection of protozoan cysts.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6. Microbial and Algal Pigment Enhancement and Extraction</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Pigment Enhancement:</strong> Improved phycoerythrin production from <em>Spirulina platensis</em> by optimizing media composition for enhanced pigment concentration.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>7. Phylogeny Studies of Microorganisms</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Phylogeny:</strong> Conducted phylogenetic studies using <em>Bergey&rsquo;s Manual</em> and 16S rRNA sequencing.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>8. Lipid Extraction from Animal Sources</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Lipid Extraction:</strong> Extracted lipids from chicken pancreas for further biochemical analysis.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>9. Bioinformatics Expertise</strong></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Tools:</strong> Proficient in using bioinformatics tools like BLAST and FASTA for sequence analysis.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h1><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">RESEARCH GRANTS OBTAINED:</span></h1>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">UGC Minor Research Project entitled &ldquo;Production of flavoring compounds-esters using lipase from <em>Staphylococcus pasteuri</em>.&rdquo; Received 4,95,000 /- from UGC. 2014-2016.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research guide: </strong>Dr.Mrs.Meenal Dukhande.</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Minor Research Project entitled &ldquo;A study on synthesis and analysis of flavoring compounds produced by <em>Candida rugosa</em>.&rdquo; Received 35,000/- from University of Mumbai. 2016-2017.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research guide: </strong>Dr.Mrs.Meenal Dukhande.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 306, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2932, 80, 306, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Guidance</strong>:</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"76\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"73\">2024</strong>:</span></p>\n<ol data-start=\"77\" data-end=\"350\">\n<li data-start=\"77\" data-end=\"350\" class=\"\">\n<p data-start=\"80\" data-end=\"350\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong data-start=\"80\" data-end=\"106\">Guided Ms. Gargee Rane</strong> and <strong data-start=\"111\" data-end=\"133\">Ms. Alethea Dsouza</strong> for the research project titled:</span><br data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"169\" /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"190\">Research Title</strong>: <em data-start=\"192\" data-end=\"348\">A Study on Enhancing Crop Growth Rate Using Biofertilizers Made with Species of Rhizobium, Azotobacter, Phosphate Solubilizers, and Potassium Solubilizers</em></span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2023</strong>:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Guided Ms. Brahmi Shenoy</strong> for the Science Research Contest 2022 organized by Marathi Vidyan Parishad on 28th February 2023.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Title</strong>: <em>Rapid and Low-Cost Estimation of Ketonuria Using Paper-Based Microfluidics</em></span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The project stood among the top ten out of forty projects.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2022</strong>:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Guided Ms. Brahmi Shenoy</strong> for <em>Aavishkar - Inter-Collegiate Research Convention</em> organized by the University of Mumbai, December 2022.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Title</strong>: <em>Rapid and Low-Cost Assessment of Urological Health Using Biodegradable Lab-On-Chip</em></span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">The research was selected among the top nine posters for a podium presentation from 50 pure science UG participants.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Guided Ms. Brahmi Shenoy</strong> and <strong>Ms. Jai Jadhav</strong> for the National Level Research Paper Competition \"SODH\" organized by Mulund College of Commerce, August 2022.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Titles</strong>:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><em>Ms. Jai Jadhav</em>: <em>Detection of Bilirubin in Urine Using Microfluidic Paper-Based Device</em></span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><em>Ms. Brahmi Shenoy</em>: <em>Analysis of Human Health Using Ketones as Biomarkers</em></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2021</strong>:</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Guided Ms. Brahmi Shenoy</strong> and <strong>Ms. Jai Jadhav</strong> for the Fledging Research Competition organized by the Research Cell of Sathaye College under the aegis of <em>Vigyan Sarvatra Pujyate</em>, which won the <strong>First Prize</strong> in February 2022.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research Title</strong>: <em>Urinary Health Analysis Using Lab-On-Chip</em></span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 306, '2025-09-23', 0),
(2933, 81, 306, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Oral presentation on &ldquo;A Study on Optimization of Enzyme Lipase from <em>Candida rugosa</em> and Synthesis of Flavoring Compounds&rdquo; at the Bi-yearly In-House Research Scholar Seminar, Guru Nanak Khalsa College, Matunga, on 23rd June 2017.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Poster presentation on &ldquo;Lipase Mediated Ester Synthesis and Its Rapid Detection by Microfluidics&rdquo; at the National Level Research Meet &ndash; The Sajjan Gupta Konark Memorial Award 2017, Vivekananda Education Society College, Chembur, Mumbai, on 18th January 2017.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Oral presentation on &ldquo;Estimation of Lipase Activity Using Different Colorimetric and Titrimetric Methods&rdquo; at the Bi-yearly In-House Research Scholar Seminar, Guru Nanak Khalsa College, Matunga, on 11th November 2016.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Poster presentation on &ldquo;A Comparative Study of Lipase Activity by Colorimetric and Titrimetric Methods&rdquo; at PICASA III, an International Paper and Poster Competition, and seminar on 360 Degree Cosmetics, KET\'s VG Vaze Kelkar College, Mumbai, on 2nd September 2016.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Presentation of my first research article &ldquo;Microfluidics System for the Entrapment and Detection of Oocysts of <em>Cryptosporidium</em>&rdquo; at the National Conference on Recent Trends and Innovations in the Microbial World, Smt. C.H.M. College, Ulhasnagar, in January 2015.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Presentation on &ldquo;Rapid Detection of Carbohydrates on Paper Microfluidics&rdquo; at a workshop on MICROFLUIDICS, Department of Microbiology, Ramnarain Ruia College, in January 2012.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Oral presentation on &ldquo;Isolation and Cultivated Algae from Extreme Environments&rdquo; at &lsquo;MICROBES,&rsquo; a research festival organized by the Department of Microbiology, Ramnarain Ruia College, in collaboration with the Institute of Chemical Technology, Mumbai, in December 2011.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Oral presentation on &ldquo;Carbohydrate Estimation Using Paper Microfluidics&rdquo; at a UGC-sponsored Research Scholar&rsquo;s Meet &ldquo;Jigyaasa&rdquo; at Kishanchand Chellaram College in July 2011.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Oral presentation on &ldquo;Cultivation and Quantification of Microorganisms Using Lab-On-Paper Principles&rdquo; at a UGC-sponsored Research Scholar&rsquo;s Meet &ldquo;Jigyaasa&rdquo; at Kishanchand Chellaram College in July 2011.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Poster presentation on &ldquo;Medicinal Plants and Their Uses&rdquo; at the Botany Festival &ldquo;KINGDOM PLANTAE,&rdquo; organized by the Department of Botany, Ramnarain Ruia College, in June 2009.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 306, '2025-09-23', 0),
