(4094, 108, 239, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>I\'m a dedicated teacher inspiring young minds. Creating engaging lessons for growth and guiding students to success.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 239, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4096, 108, 243, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prof. Dr. Suraj A. Pandit</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">is a</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">trained archaeologist and professor in the Department of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaelogy. He earned his Masters Degree from Deccan College, Pune in Ancient Indian History, Culture and Archaeology and went on to complete his Ph.D. on &lsquo;Kanheri Caves&rsquo; from the University of Mumbai under the guidance of Dr. A. P. Jamkhedkar. He has also obtained a second Masters Degree in Buddhist Studies from the University of Mumbai. Dr. Pandit is identified as a remarkable archaeologist and art historian famous for his work in the fields of Buddhist culture, urban archaeology, art history, heritage tourism and heritage management. Some of his books include &lsquo;Mumbai Beyond Bombay&rsquo;, &lsquo;Stories in Stone - Historic Caves Of Mumbai&rsquo;, &lsquo;Age of Traikutakas: Coins, Inscription And Art &rsquo; and many more.</span></p>', '1', 0, 0, '', 243, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4097, 108, 245, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Smt. Radha Sabnis is the Head of the Department of Ancient Indian Culture &amp; Archaeology and works as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology, and she has been teaching this subject for last 19 years. She has completed her graduation in the subject of History from Sathaye College. She holds a master&rsquo;s degree in the subject of History as well as in the subject of Buddhist Studies. She hold the degree of M.Phil the subject of History. Her interest areas concern Indian culture and archaeology with her area of research largely dealing with the history and culture of Mumbai.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 245, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4098, 108, 246, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ms. Nishigandha Parulekar is the course coordinator and assistant professor at Sathaye College (Autonomous), The Departments of Ancient Indian Culture &amp; Archaeology, Buddhist Studies. She has completed her BA in Ancient Indian Culture from Sathaye College (2014-15) itself and her MA in Buddhist Studies (2016-17) and MA in Archaeology (2021-22) from Sathaye College (Autonomous) and&nbsp; University of Mumbai, respectively. She Completed One year Diploma in &lsquo;Archiving and Museology&rsquo; from K J Somaiya Institute of Dharma Studies, Mumbai (2022). She has also co-authored numerous research papers and is part of/was part of numerous research projects in the field of Archaeology.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 246, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4099, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 247, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4100, 108, 248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Pratibha Kamble is an accomplished academician and researcher with over a decade of teaching experience in Economics. She has been serving as a full-time Head and Assistant Professor at Sathaye College, Mumbai, since December 2013.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Kamble completed her Ph.D. in Economics from SNDT Women&rsquo;s University, Mumbai, under the guidance of Dr. Vibhuti Patel. Her doctoral research was titled &ldquo;The Role of Dalit Indian Chamber of Commerce and Industries (DICCI) in the Development of Dalit Entrepreneurs.&rdquo; She has also successfully qualified the UGC-NET Examination multiple times and holds postgraduate degrees from Savitribai Phule Pune University and the University of Mumbai.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Prior to joining Sathaye College, Dr. Kamble gained valuable teaching experience at renowned institutions including Chetana College, R.A. Podar College, Joshi Bedekar College, Ambedkar College, Vikas College, and Kelkar College. She has participated in various prestigious orientation and refresher programs organized by institutions such as Jawaharlal Nehru University, IIT Delhi, Kumaun University, and Himachal Pradesh University.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to her teaching, Dr. Kamble has contributed significantly to research. She was awarded a Minor Research Project by the Babasaheb Ambedkar Research and Training Institute (BARTI), Pune. She has also been associated with important research projects at Tata Institute of Social Sciences and the University of Mumbai. Her areas of research interest include Dalit Entrepreneurship, Agricultural Economics, Gender Studies, and Inclusive Economic Development.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Kamble has presented papers at several national and international conferences and has published research articles on subjects like Women Entrepreneurship, Unpaid Labor of Dalit Women, and Dr. B.R. Ambedkar&rsquo;s Thoughts on Collective Farming. She has also served as a panel expert for student selection interviews at Tata Institute of Social Sciences (TISS) over multiple years.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beyond academics, Dr. Kamble has been actively involved in co-curricular and extra-curricular activities. She has completed the NSS program, holds NCC \'B\' and \'C\' certificates, and has worked as a Radio Jockey for the University of Mumbai&rsquo;s MUST Radio (107.8 FM). Her hobbies include swimming, reading, singing, and traveling.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Pratibha Kamble&rsquo;s passion for teaching, dedication to research, and commitment to social development make her a valuable member of the Sathaye College faculty.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Courses taught Micro Economics, Macro Economics, Labour Economics, Public Finance, Rural Development, Indian Economy, Research Methodology, Basic Econometrics, Advanced Macroeconomics, Economics of Growth and Development, Economics of Agriculture and Co-operation, History of Economics Thought, Quantitative Economics, Mathematics and Statistics for Economic &nbsp;Analysis and International Economics, Entrepreneurship and Small Scale Industries, Indian Economy.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 248, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4101, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 249, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4102, 108, 251, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Mr. Olya I. Vasave is an accomplished academic with over eleven years of experience in undergraduate teaching. He specializes in the field of Economics and holds a Master of Arts degree with a specialization in Economics. He is currently pursuing his Ph.D. at the Kavayitri Bahinabai Chaudhari North Maharashtra University, Jalgaon.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Throughout his academic career, Mr. Vasave has made significant contributions to research, publishing papers on topics such as agriculture, tourism, the socio-economic conditions of marginalized communities, poverty, and sustainability. His research has been presented at national/International conferences and published in reputed journals, reflecting his active engagement with contemporary socio-economic issues.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to his teaching and research responsibilities, Mr. Vasave plays a vital role in college administration. He has actively contributed to student development through his service on various key committees, including the Member of CAP Committee, Member of Association of Fine Arts, Member of&nbsp; Alumni Outreach Committee, Member of Media Outreach Committee, Member of Library Committee, Member of Mentor-Mentee Scheme, BoS. Secretary (Economics, Sathaye College, Autonomous) Member of IQAC, Member of Skill Enhancement Course Monitoring Committee, Member of Attendance Committee, Member of Discipline Committee, Member of Gymkhana Management Committee, Member of Admission Committee.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 251, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4103, 108, 252, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dimple Mehta is an Assistant Professor in Economics with extensive experience in teaching undergraduate courses, including Business Economics, Macroeconomics, and Econometrics. She holds a Master\'s degree in Economics from the Mumbai School of Economics and a Diploma in Big Data Analytics, equipping her with both academic depth and technical proficiency in Python, R, SQL, and Tableau. Passionate about interdisciplinary learning and research, she actively contributes to curriculum development, student mentorship, and workshops in data science. Her academic journey is marked by excellence, with several top-rank honors and active involvement in college committees, seminars, and social initiatives.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 252, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4104, 108, 253, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Passionate about teaching. Loves doing activities with students. Motivates the students for self learning. Guide them for their future career.</strong></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 253, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4105, 108, 254, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I am a committed and dedicated instructor with a strong background in human physiology, psychology, and education. I try to explain concepts in a simple and clear way so that all students can understand easily.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I support and guide my students and always encourage them to do their best. I manage my teaching along with my personal responsibilities with commitment.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I also try to improve myself by learning new methods and exploring new opportunities in education, as teaching is not just a job for me but an important part of my life.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 254, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4106, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 255, '2025-09-23', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(4107, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 257, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4108, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 258, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4110, 108, 260, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Mr. Awhad Abhijit Ashok</p>\r\n<p>Assistant Professor</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Awhad is dedicated educator with a passion for Geography, he strives to create engaging learning environments that foster growth, curiosity, and critical thinking. With 8 years of experience in teaching Geography at Under-graduate level, he has developed a commitment to helping students achieve their academic goals.</p>\r\n<p>His Teaching Philosophy:</p>\r\n<p>- He believies in student-centered learning, he encourages active participation, creativity, and collaboration.<br />- He fosters a supportive and inclusive classroom environment, aims to meet the diverse needs of his students.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 260, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4111, 108, 261, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>He is currently working as an Associate Professor and Head of the Department of Philosophy at Sathaye College (Autonomous), Mumbai, the institution he joined in 2004. He is the head of the Department of Philosophy. He is a postgraduate with a doctorate in Philosophy. Apart from his regular academic duties, he has been working and actively participating in various co-curricular activities. He was an NSS program officer from 2006 to 2015.</p>\n<p>He is currently the IQAC Coordinator and a Member of CDC Sathaye College (Autonomous). He is also a Member of the Board of Studies (BOS), Department of Philosophy, University of Mumbai, a visiting faculty member at the Department of Philosophy, University of Mumbai, and an M.A. in Buddhist studies at Sathaye College. He has published over 15 research articles and papers, completed one minor research project (MRP) under the University of Mumbai, and published one book.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 261, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4112, 108, 262, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Sampada V. Chawan is an Assistant Professor in Philosophy and is working in Sathaye College (autonomous) from 2019 onwards. She has cleared UGC NET-JRF and SET exams and has worked as a Junior Research Fellow in University of Mumbai in the year 2018-19. She has completed her Bachelor of Arts degree in Philosophy with a University of Mumbai Gold Medal and completed her Master&rsquo;s degree in Philosophy from the same institution. Her research interests lie at the intersection of philosophy and gender studies with a special focus on the philosophy of masculinity, feminist ethics, and alternate masculinities.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 262, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4113, 108, 263, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul>\n<li>Associate Professor &amp; Head of the Department of Political Science, Joined Sathaye Degree College in 1990.</li>\n<li>Teaching experience: 34 years in Sathaye College.</li>\n<li>Academic Qualifications: MA, M.Phil., Mumbai University.</li>\n<li>Associated with Mumbai University as VC nominee on various Autonomous College Board of Studies such as Mithibai Autonomous College, St Xavier\'s Autonomous College, Patkar-Varde Autonomous College, Mumbai. Also worked as member of Ad hoc BOS of Elphinston Government College, Mumbai.</li>\n<li>Presently working as College nominee on BOS of Chetna College, Mumbai.</li>\n<li>Member of Governing Body of Sathaye College, Autonomous.</li>\n<li>Chairperson of ICC Sathaye College, Autonomous.</li>\n<li>Treasurer &amp; Managing Committee Member of Sathaye College Cooperative Stores, welfare activity run for Sathaye students.</li>\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 263, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4114, 108, 264, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong data-start=\"32\" data-end=\"46\">Dr. Ketan Bhosale</strong> is a passionate political science professor whose academic interests are matched by a deep love for reading, writing, and cinema. With a keen appreciation for art and culture, he brings a humanistic lens to the study of politics, often drawing connections between political theory and cultural expression. Whether immersed in classic literature, crafting insightful essays, or exploring films from around the world, he finds inspiration in the stories that shape societies and the ideas that influence change.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 264, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4115, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 265, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4116, 108, 266, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div class=\"conatiner-fluid page-back py-4 ng-scope\">\n<div class=\"container main-whitePanel\">\n<div class=\"vtabs\">\n<div class=\"row faculty-Tab-Info\">\n<div class=\"col-md-9 col-custom-80 tabsContent-holder\">\n<div id=\"accordion-left-tabs\" class=\"tab-content accordion\">\n<div id=\"TabMenu0\" class=\"tab-pane fade accordion-item ng-scope active show\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n<article id=\"TabMenu0\" class=\"accordion-body accordion-collapse collapse\" data-bs-parent=\"#accordion-left-tabs\" aria-labelledby=\"TabMenu0\">\n<section class=\"ng-binding\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Swati Belsare is the Head of the Department of Sanskrit and works as an Associate Professor in the Department of Sanskrit, and she has been teaching this subject for the last 35 years. She has completed her graduation in the subject of Sanskrit from Sathaye College. She holds a master&rsquo;s degree in the subject of Sanskrit. She has done her PhD. in the subject of Sanskrit (अभिजात संस्कृत साहित्यातील \'प्रमुख\' मानवी भावभावनांचे सखोल अध्ययन (ई.स. पूर्व ४ थे शतक ते ई.स. चे ८ वे शतक).&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She is a dedicated academic professional with a strong interest in Sanskrit studies and education. She is passionate about teaching, research, and promoting the richness of Indian knowledge systems. She actively engages in organizing academic activities, guiding students, and contributing to curriculum development.</p>\n</section>\n</article>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"container-fluid footer-section footer pt-5 pb-4 wow fadeIn animated animated\" data-wow-delay=\"0.1s\">\n<div class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row g-5\">\n<div class=\"col-lg-3 col-md-6 col-sm-12 footer-col-1\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 266, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4118, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 268, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4120, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 270, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4121, 108, 271, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 2, 'r', 271, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4122, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 272, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4123, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 273, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4125, 108, 275, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul>\n<li><strong>२००९ पासून साठये महाविद्यालयात अध्यापनाचे कार्य</strong></li>\n<li><strong>सदस्य</strong><strong>, </strong><strong>संचालक मंडळ</strong><strong> , </strong><strong>मराठी संशोधन मंडळ</strong><strong> , </strong><strong>मुंबई</strong><strong>. </strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ph.D. </strong><strong>: </strong><strong>तंजावर येथील मराठी नाटकांचा चिकित्सक अभ्यास</strong><strong> , </strong><strong>मुंबई विद्यापीठ </strong></li>\n<li><strong>M.Phil</strong><strong>&nbsp;: </strong><strong>रंगनाथ पठारे यांच्या कादंबरीचा चिकित्सक अभ्यास</strong><strong>, </strong><strong>मुंबई विद्यापीठ </strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 275, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4126, 108, 276, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Professor Dr. Sanjay D. Sonawane ( <strong class=\"ng-binding\">M.COM;LL.M;FCMA;FCA,DISA(ICAI),SET,PhD</strong>) is the Head of the Department. He is also a Practising Chartered Accountant for over 36 years and a Research guide for Ph.D students in the University of Mumbai and ShriJagdishprasad Jhabarmal Tibrewala University (JJTU). He is also a Member of the Board of Studies in Accountancy at the University of Mumbai. He is also a Member of the Board of Studies in Accountancy at the University of Mumbai. He is a Vice-Chancellor nominee in an Academic Council Body of R.A.Podar College of Commerce &amp; Economics, Patkar Varde College. He is a Vice-Chancellor Nominee on the Board of Studies-Accountancy &amp; Self Financing Courses of DTSS College of Commerce and MMK College.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 276, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4127, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 277, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4128, 108, 278, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Priya Ramesh Yeole (M.Com., SET, Ph.D.) is a dedicated and passionate teacher who brings a wealth of knowledge and infectious enthusiasm to the classroom. With a student-first approach, Dr. Priya skillfully blends academic rigor with real-world insights, ensuring that her lessons are not just taught but deeply understood. Whether guiding research projects, mentoring students, or leading engaging discussions, she is committed to fostering a dynamic learning environment that nurtures curiosity, sharpens critical thinking, and inspires every student to reach their full potential. She is also actively involved in teaching and research, with several noteworthy publications in UGC Care Listed and Scopus Indexed Journals, along with authored books. Additionally, she serves as a member of the Board of Studies in various autonomous colleges across Maharashtra, contributing her expertise to the academic&nbsp;community.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 278, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4129, 108, 279, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span>Dr. Monika Prakash Bhosale&nbsp;</span></p>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Lecturer</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Sathaye College (Autonomous)&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Vile Parle East, Mumbai, Maharashtra.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Mcom, SET, M.Phil, MBA (Finance), PhD (Commerce and Management) from University of Mumbai.&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">I have total 7 Years of Teaching Experience to understand graduate and post graduate students.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Published 13 Research Papers in various National and international Journals.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">Awarded with 3 times the Best Research Paper award. Holding 2 published Patents.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">I am an Author of 2 textbooks in the subject of Accountancy and Research Methodology.</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 279, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4130, 108, 280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Sanchita S. Humane [M.Com (Advanced Accountancy), NET ( Commerce)] is working as Lecturer at PTVA\'s Sathaye College (Autonomous), Vile Parle. She has 3 years of teaching experience. She is a member of BoS in Sathaye College (Autonomous). Her areas of interest are Accountancy &amp; Financial Management, Management Accounting, Corporate Finance etc.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 280, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4131, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 281, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4132, 108, 282, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Mr. Gautam Dilip Maske is an esteemed academic with over seventeen years of teaching experience at the undergraduate level and four years at the postgraduate level. He specializes in various subjects related to commerce and management, including business, entrepreneurship, business management, marketing, human resource management, and research methodology. He holds a Master of Commerce degree in Banking and Finance, as well as Accountancy, and is currently pursuing a Ph.D. from the University of Mumbai.</p>\n<p>Mr. Maske has a strong record of research publications covering diverse topics such as Foreign Direct Investment, the performance of MSMEs in India, the impact of GST on micro, small, and medium enterprises, and government schemes for marginalized communities, among others. His research has been presented and published at various national conferences, reflecting his active engagement with contemporary research issues. He has also published textbooks include <em data-start=\"1526\" data-end=\"1545\">Retail Management</em> and <em data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1597\">Introduction to Business and Entrepreneurship</em>, and also contributed chapters to edited volumes on topics such as Intorudction to financial literacy and A Comprehensive Study of Trade and Commerce in the Ancient India.</p>\n<p>Since 2021, Mr. Maske has served as the Head of Department, contributing significantly to student development through his roles on various college committees, including NSS, the Commerce Association, Discipline, and as Gymkhana Chairman. His commitment extends beyond the classroom, as demonstrated by his involvement in organizing workshops, seminars, and social initiatives aimed at fostering entrepreneurship and social responsibility among students.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>In addition to his academic achievements, Mr. Maske is deeply involved in social work. He serves as the Vice Treasurer of Bahujan Samata Prabodhini, an NGO dedicated to uplifting Dalit, Adivasi, and other marginalized communities. His efforts in conducting social activities and empowering the youth underscore his passion for creating a positive societal impact.</p>\n<p></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 282, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4133, 108, 283, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Dr. Poonam Vibhute is a passionate academician and researcher dedicated to shaping the future of education. With a strong commitment to leadership, teaching, and research, she has made notable contributions in the field of commerce. Dr. Poonam holds a Ph.D. in Accountancy from C. K. Thakur Arts, Commerce, and Science College, New Panvel, affiliated with the University of Mumbai. She also holds two Master\'s degrees: M.Com. in Accountancy and M.Com. in E-Commerce, both from esteemed institutions under the University of Mumbai.</p>\n<p>Currently serving as an Assistant Professor at Sathaye College (Autonomous), Vile Parle, Dr. Poonam focuses on creating an engaging and supportive learning environment that encourages her students to thrive academically and personally. She teaches a diverse range of subjects in business, finance, marketing, advertising, export marketing, banking system and tourism management and management at the undergraduate level, with a particular emphasis on practical knowledge, ethical decision-making, and fostering critical thinking.</p>\n<p>Beyond her teaching responsibilities, Dr. Poonam has made significant contributions to the academic community through her research. She has published papers on various important topics, such as the financial performance of municipal corporations, the role of solar technology in mobile devices to reduce e-waste and energy consumption, and a study on municipal finance, focusing on Kalyan-Dombivli Municipal Corporation. Her research also explores the evolution of taxation systems in India from the Vedic period to contemporary times, the financial impact of Maharashtra\'s Majhi Ladki Bahin scheme, and how digital narratives and artificial intelligence are reshaping India&rsquo;s creative industries. Additionally, she has explored the historical context of accounting records in ancient India, shedding light on indigenous knowledge systems in financial documentation.</p>\n<p>Dr. Poonam is also the author of academic books such as \"Advertising &ndash; I\" and \"Tourism Management,\" as well as a non-academic book titled \"काहण्या कोरोनाच्या काहीशा अशाही.\" Her active participation in national and international webinars, workshops, and faculty development programs further reflects her commitment to continuous learning and professional growth.</p>\n<p>Driven by a passion for research and a dedication to her students&rsquo; success, Dr. Poonam is a valuable asset to the academic community. She continues to shape the future of education with her contributions in both teaching and research.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 283, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4134, 108, 285, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 285, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4136, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 288, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4137, 108, 292, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 292, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4138, 108, 293, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Shri K.S.Waghmode teaches Inorganic Chemistry</p>\n<p>PhD: Registered for Ph.D. in Inorganic Chemistry ( JJT University, Rajasthan)<br />Research Guide: Dr. A. Venkatachalam<br />Thesis Title: Studies in Spinel Compounds<br />M.Sc. in Inorganic Chemistry (1993), Shivaji University Kolhapur<br />B.Sc. in Chemistry (1991), Shivaji University Kolhapur</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 293, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4139, 108, 294, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Dear viewer, I am a teacher of Organic Chemistry for B,Sc and M.Sc. students, teaching since last 23 years. The topics that I teach include Stereochemistry, Spectroscopy, Natural products, Polymers, Aromaticity. I believe, Education is empowerment of individual to think and make decisions that are good for entire society. We need others for our progress and happiness. I am grateful being part of Sathaye College.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 294, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4140, 108, 295, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>I am working as an associate professor of chemistry in Sathaye College (Autonomous).</p>\n<p>I have completed&nbsp; my Ph.D. in 2004 in the subject of Analytical Chemistry from Institute of Science , University of Mumbai under the guidance of Dr. D.P.Dave.</p>\n<p></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 295, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4141, 108, 296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Dr. Santosh Waghu Zote is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Chemistry, with a focus on Organic Chemistry. With a Ph.D. from the University of Mumbai, his research specializes in organofluorine liquid crystals, material science, and the designing of novel chemical compounds for various applications. He has published numerous research papers and book chapters, and his work is widely recognized in the scientific community. He is also an active participant in academic development, having served as a resource person for various workshops and contributed to syllabus revisions.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 296, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4142, 108, 297, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Educational Qualification:</strong> M.Sc.,<strong>Ph.D</strong>.</p>\r\n<strong>Subject specialization: </strong>&nbsp;Analytical Chemistry&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Working as an Assistant Professor in Department of Chemistry, Sathaye College (Autonomous) since 21st December 2013.</li>\r\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 297, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4143, 108, 298, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Currently working as Assistant&nbsp; Professor at Sathaye College(Autonomous) since 2019. Total 6+ years of teaching experience in the subject of chemistry at UG and PG level.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 298, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4144, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 299, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4147, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 302, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4148, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 303, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4149, 108, 304, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Currently working as Assistant Professor, Department of Mathematics, PTVA\'s Sathaye College(Autonomous) , &nbsp;Mumbai , Maharashtra . I did my M.Sc. from University of Mumbai. I Love and enjoy Teaching as we get chance to interact with young minds. Some of my teachers played a crucial role in shaping my career and I always try to do that as a teacher and motivate students to think independently. I have learned many things as a teacher and try to learn new things whenever possible.</p>\n<p><span>I also promote Open Source Software in education through workshops and training programs. You can reach me at&nbsp; rmpathakmaths@gmail.com</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 304, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4150, 108, 305, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p data-start=\"45\" data-end=\"113\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><em data-start=\"69\" data-end=\"111\">Microbiologist, Educator, and Researcher</em></span></p>\n<p data-start=\"115\" data-end=\"433\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">I am Dr. Shilpa Jadhav, an ardent microbiologist passionate about teaching and shaping society through education. With over 12 years of experience in teaching <strong data-start=\"274\" data-end=\"300\">Microbial Biochemistry</strong> at the undergraduate level, I have dedicated myself to nurturing young minds and cultivating a deeper understanding of microbiology.</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"435\" data-end=\"939\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">I am a recognized teacher for <strong data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"474\">M.Sc.</strong> in Microbiology at the University of Mumbai and have been appointed as a <strong data-start=\"548\" data-end=\"572\">Ph.D. research guide</strong> in the same subject. My involvement with the <strong data-start=\"618\" data-end=\"642\">University of Mumbai</strong> extends to being a member of the <strong data-start=\"676\" data-end=\"706\">syllabus framing committee</strong> for <strong data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"740\">M.Sc. Part I Microbiology</strong>, where I contribute to shaping the academic curriculum. Additionally, I serve as a <strong data-start=\"824\" data-end=\"857\">theory and practical examiner</strong> for <strong data-start=\"862\" data-end=\"875\">T.Y.B.Sc.</strong> and <strong data-start=\"880\" data-end=\"910\">M.Sc. Part II Microbiology</strong> at the University of Mumbai.</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"941\" data-end=\"1214\" class=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">My research interests lie in <strong data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"994\">applied microbiology</strong>, particularly in <strong data-start=\"1012\" data-end=\"1048\">plant growth-promoting molecules</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1071\">bioremediation</strong>. I strive to bridge the gap between theoretical knowledge and real-world applications, aiming to use microbiology to tackle global challenges.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 305, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4151, 108, 306, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><em>Shaping Future Scientists!</em></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">I am Dr. Amita Kocharekar, an Assistant Professor in the Department of Microbiology at Sathaye College, Mumbai. I hold a B.Sc, M.Sc, and Ph.D. in Microbiology, and I am passionate about both teaching and research. My research interests are primarily focused on <strong>Microfluidics</strong> and its applications in <strong>biomolecule detection</strong>, along with the study of <strong>lipase enzymes</strong> in the field of biotechnology. I have contributed to several publications in reputed journals and continue to engage in projects that advance knowledge in these areas.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Beyond my academic and research responsibilities, I am deeply involved in the administrative activities of the college. I serve as a member of the <strong>Exam Committee</strong>, the <strong>Research and Innovation Criterion of IQAC</strong>, the <strong>NSS Advisory Committee</strong>, the <strong>Acharya Chanakya Samiti</strong>, the <strong>Science Association</strong>, and the <strong>Green Club Committee</strong>. Through these roles, I strive to enhance the academic environment, foster innovation, and contribute to the overall growth and development of our institution.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">I am committed to fostering a conducive learning environment, encouraging innovation, and shaping the future of the next generation of microbiologists.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 306, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4152, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 309, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4155, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 312, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4156, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong data-start=\"123\" data-end=\"156\">Shri. Suryakant Eknath Jaware</strong> is an <strong data-start=\"163\" data-end=\"242\">Assistant Professor in the Department of Physics at Sathaye College, Mumbai</strong>, with over <strong data-start=\"254\" data-end=\"303\">29 years of undergraduate teaching experience</strong>. He holds an <strong data-start=\"317\" data-end=\"337\">M.Sc. in Physics</strong> and an <strong data-start=\"345\" data-end=\"367\" data-is-only-node=\"\">M.Phil. in Physics</strong>, with research interests in <strong data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"474\">conducting polymer composites, nanocomposites, thin films, and gas sensors</strong>. He has published research papers in national and international journals and has presented research work at international conferences, receiving <strong data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"655\">Best Poster Presentation awards</strong>. He has also completed an <strong data-start=\"682\" data-end=\"722\">Orientation Course at Goa University</strong> and a <strong data-start=\"729\" data-end=\"775\">Refresher Course at the University of Pune</strong>. In addition to teaching and research, he has contributed to college administration through responsibilities as a member of the <strong data-start=\"904\" data-end=\"995\">Discipline Committee, Admission Committee, Gymkhana Committee, and Attendance Committee</strong>.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 313, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4157, 108, 314, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Smt. Sukruta Pethe is a versatile but modest individual with a diverse range of skills and experiences with a strong educational background and a passion for teaching, &nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She completed her schooling at Sou. Vimalabai Garware High School in Pune, followed by her Higher Secondary at S. P. College, Pune. She then pursued B.Sc. in Electronics from Abasaheb Garware College and later shifted her career to physics by completing M.Sc. in the subject from the Department of Physics, University of Pune.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Smt. Sukruta is working as an Assistant Professor in Physics in Sathaye College for over two decades since 2002.<br />She has taught a wide range of physics subjects to undergraduate students which includes Solid State Physics, Optics, Mechanics, Electrodynamics, Special Theory of Relativity, Microprocessor, Applied Physics and Digital Electronics.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She launched the MSc Physics programme at Sathaye College in the academic year 2024-25, single-handedly developing its syllabus. She also established collaborations with SPPU and TIFR to provide MSc Nuclear Technique practicals, enhancing the programme\'s academic rigor.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She is pursuing her PhD in Non Linear Dynamics under Dr. Kiran Kolwankar from R. J. College, Ghatkopar.&nbsp;She was invited for <strong>विज्ञान व्याख्यानमाला</strong>&nbsp; by Phatak Granthalaya of Tilak Mandir to give a speech on \"<strong>Fractals, Chaos and Synchronisation</strong>\" in Marathi in October 2018.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The walls of the Physics laboratories, enriched by her efforts, display curated profiles of eminent physicists highlighting their contributions, journeys, and honors alongside information on premier institutes in India for higher studies, inspiring students to dream bigger and pursue excellence in Physics.&nbsp;TYBSc Physics Batch of 2021-22 initiated an outreach activity namely <strong>SciPhy</strong> under her guidance in which undergraduate students demonstrate various experiments to School Children from the vicinity schools.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She actively takes the initiative in all departmental activities aimed at student development and often undertakes major events single-handedly. Her contributions include organizing the departmental library, Cafe physics-based treasure hunts, Vidnyan Katha Din celebration, Talk about LGBTQ community, visits to various research institutes, visits sociatl organisaations for social sensitisation, expert talks, workshops, and a variety of other innovative programs that enrich the academic and co-curricular experience of students.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to her teaching responsibilities, she has been actively involved in co-curricular and extra-curricular activities, contributing to initiatives such as the Music Association, Science Association, Research Committee, and others. She took the initiative in establishing the <strong>Entrepreneurship Development Cell</strong> (EDC) at Sathaye College, nurturing a spirit of innovation and enterprise among students.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She has also been a part of key administrative committees like the Admission Committee, Examination Committee, IQAC, and the NEP Core Committee, where she left a positive mark through her dedicated work. She is currently working as an On Job Training (OJT) in-charge and secretary for Acharya Chanakya Koushalya Vikas Kendra (ACKVK) of Sathaye College.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sukruta Pethe is recently nominated by VC of University of Mumbai as a <span>Member of Internship/OJT Guidelines Draft Committee for Mumbai University Undergraduate Programme.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She pioneered the <strong>annual E-waste drives</strong> at her college in 2015, single-handedly organizing them for the first five years before they were formalized by a committee. In 2017, she launched the <strong>Zero Garbage Project </strong>at Sathaye College under the guidance of then Principal, introducing composting of canteen waste, waste disposal systems, incinerators, e-waste bin, and green audits.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 314, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4159, 108, 316, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Shri Sanjay Karande is currently serving as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Statistics. He has been a part of this esteemed institution since 2013 and has contributed significantly to the academic and overall development of the department.&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"409\" data-end=\"628\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">He is currently pursuing a Ph.D. in Applied Statistics, with research focused on practical applications of statistical methods. His areas of interest include data analysis, statistical modeling, and applied probability.</p>\n<p data-start=\"630\" data-end=\"891\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Throughout his tenure, Shri Karande has actively contributed to curriculum development, student mentorship, and departmental activities. He regularly participates in academic seminars and workshops to stay updated with current trends in statistics and research.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 316, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4160, 108, 317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ms. Vasanti Todakar is an Assistant Professor of Statistics at Sathaye College with over five years of teaching experience (as of 2024). She is currently pursuing a Ph.D. in Statistics and is passionate about teaching and applying statistical concepts to real-world problems. Her research interests include Reliability, Operations Research Techniques, Lean Six Sigma, Sampling Techniques, and Biostatistics.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She is actively involved in college-level committees such as examinations and NAAC, regularly participates in conferences, and enjoys mentoring students in research and academic development.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 317, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4161, 108, 318, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Qualification: M.Sc in Statistics (Mumbai University)</p>\n<p>Subject Taught: Statistical Methods, Sampling Theory, Analysis of Variance and Designs of Experiment, Theory of Estimation, Regression Analysis using R software, Mathematical and Statistical Techniques, Operation Research Techniques, Acturial Science.</p>\n<p>Total experience: 4 years.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 318, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4163, 108, 320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Teaching is my passion and research is my prime interest. I particularly enjoy teaching subjects like Biotechnology, Cell biology, Molecular biology and Genetics. In my research journey, I have worked on model organisms like Hydra, Drosophila, Giant Wood Spider (<em>Nephila pilipes</em>), Indian bats, Giant African Snail (<em>Achatina fulica</em>) and Zebrafish (<em>Danio rerio</em>).</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4164, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 322, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4165, 108, 323, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>I am Amruta Daulat pharande, an ardent Zoologist by heart. I have a strong belief that education should be used to shape society, which is why I adore teaching. In 2017, I secured my master\'s degree from Shivaji University in Kolhapur. In 2018, I achieved my MH-SET and CSIR-NET(JRF) qualifications. For the past seven years, I have been an undergraduate zoology professor.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 323, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4166, 108, 324, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Dr. Ravindra Harsing Pawara is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Zoology with strong academic qualifications including M.Sc., Ph.D., and SET at Sathaye College (Autonomous) since 6th September 2019. He completed his Ph.D. in Zoology in 2018 from KBC North Maharashtra University, Jalgaon.</p>\r\n<p>He has contributed significantly to academic research, with 11 research publications in reputed journals and authorship of 4 books. He has a keen interest in diverse areas of biological sciences such as ornithology, entomology, ecology, taxonomy, and toxicology. He is dedicated to teaching, research, and fostering scientific curiosity among students.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 324, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4167, 108, 325, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Teaching is my passion and <em><strong>Educational management</strong> </em>is my prime interest.</li>\r\n<li>Engaged in the Teaching profession for the past <strong><em>sixteen years.</em></strong></li>\r\n<li><strong><em>Click on the link for the supporting documents:&nbsp; </em></strong><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mxPY18KkDd8kNBu1DoXvgiPlXM3bUkrH?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mxPY18KkDd8kNBu1DoXvgiPlXM3bUkrH?usp=sharing</a></li>\r\n<li>\r\n<table style=\"width: 951px; height: 890px;\" width=\"933\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 119px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; text-align: center; height: 119px;\">\r\n<p><strong>Sr. No.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; text-align: center; height: 119px;\">\r\n<p><strong>Degree</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; text-align: center; height: 119px;\">\r\n<p><strong>University/Board</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; text-align: center; height: 119px;\">\r\n<p><strong>College/School</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 119px;\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Year Of Passing</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 103px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p><strong>1. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>Ph.D.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>University of Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>Bhavan&rsquo;s Hazarimal Somani College,</p>\r\n<p>Chowpatty - Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>Thesis submitted</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 121px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p><strong>2. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">DSM</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">(Diploma in School Management)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p>Yeshwantrao Chavan Maharashtra Open University</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Chembur Sarvankash Shikshanshastra Mahavidyalaya,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Chembur &ndash; Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p>May 2019</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 103px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p><strong>3. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>M.Ed.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>University Of Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>Shri.Bapusaheb D.D. Vispute college of Education, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>New Panvel - Raigad</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>April 2017</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 121px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p><strong>4. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p>B.Ed.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p>University Of Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Chembur Sarvankash Shikshanshastra Mahavidyalaya.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Chembur &ndash; Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 121px;\">\r\n<p>May 2012</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 103px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p><strong>5. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">M.Sc. (Zoology)</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Specialization: -Animal Physiology</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>University Of Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The D.G. Ruparel College,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Mahim &ndash; Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 103px;\">\r\n<p>April 2013</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 84px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 84px;\">\r\n<p><strong>6.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 84px;\">\r\n<p>B.Sc. (Zoology)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 84px;\">\r\n<p>University Of Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 84px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Sathaye College,&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Vile-Parle - Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 84px;\">\r\n<p>April 2009</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p><strong>7. </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>H.S.C.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>Maharashtra Board</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Sathaye College&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Vile-Parle - Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>Oct. 2005</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 60px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p><strong>8.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 234px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>S.S.C.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>Maharashtra Board</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 226px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Parle Tilak Vidyalaya</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Vile-Parle - Mumbai</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 138px; height: 68px;\">\r\n<p>March 2003</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 325, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4168, 108, 326, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>&nbsp;Accomplished Assistant Professor at PTVA\'s Sathaye College (Autonomous) Affiliated to University of Mumbai, adept in technology implementation and mentoring, enhanced student success through innovative course design and effective classroom management. Spearheaded the development of \"Result Generation Software,\" showcasing leadership and a commitment to educational excellence. Expert in fostering faculty collaboration and student counseling, significantly contributing to curriculum development and academic advisement.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 326, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4169, 108, 327, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">The faculty has <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"qbe-widget\" href=\"http://M.Sc\">M.Sc</a>. in Physics from the Shivaji University, Kolhapur. He has been working at Sathaye College since 2008 in the Department of IT. He has since then proved to be an asset to the institute. Before 2008, he had 4 years of teaching experience at B.N. Bandodkar College of Science, Thane.<br />He worked as visiting faculty for the master\'s course in Physics at the Institute of Science, Mumbai, and K.J. Somaiya College of Commerce &amp; Science, Vidyavihar. He also worked as moderator for the M.Sc. Physics theory examination at K.J. Somaiya College of Science &amp; Commerce and moderator for <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"qbe-widget\" href=\"http://B.Sc\">B.Sc</a>. IT theory examinations at various colleges.<br />As a college asset, he is handling the Training and Placement Cell efficiently. He has done notable work as a member of the examination committee and a member of the core committee for the implementation of NEP 2020.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 327, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4170, 108, 328, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ms. Larissa Pegado has been working at Sathaye College(Autonomous) since 2012. She has a Master\'s degree in Computer Science and has qualified the National Eligibility Test(NET). Her keen interest lies in the core Computing subjects like Software Engineering and Programming as well as applied fields like Data analytics and visualization. Ms. Larissa is serving&nbsp; as the Secretary, Board of Studies in Information Technology at the college. She has also been actively mentoring projects for TYBSc IT students. She has also worked with the Placement committee which was instrumental in placing a sizable number of students across several prominent IT companies. She has also been a member of the Examination Committee since 2023-2024.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 328, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4171, 108, 329, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<p>Ms. Tanvi Nerurkar has been working at Sathaye College (Autonomous) since 2019. She has completed her MCA and MBA (IT). Her specialization is in the core computing subjects like Database Management Systems, Cyber Laws, Android Programming, Research Methodology, Tools for Data Science.</p>\r\n<p>She is a member of Board of Studies in Information Technology in our college. She is working as a member of the Training and&nbsp; Placement Committee since the academic year 2022-23, placing a sizable number of students across several prominent IT companies. She is a member of&nbsp; Entrepreneurship Development Cell Commitee where we promote entrepreneurship development for our students.</p>', '<p>Ms. Tanvi Nerurkar has been working at Sathaye College (Autonomous) since 2019. She has completed her MCA and MBA (IT). Her specialization is in the core computing subjects like Database Management Systems, Cyber Laws, Programming, Research Methodology, Tools for Data Science.</p>\n<p>She is a member of Board of Studies in Information Technology in our college. She is working as a member of the Training and&nbsp; Placement Committee since the academic year 2022-23, placing a sizable number of students across several prominent IT companies. She is a member of&nbsp; Entrepreneurship Development Cell Commitee where we promote entrepreneurship development for our students.</p>', '1', 0, 0, '', 329, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4172, 108, 330, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Ms. Chetna Suthar has been working with Sathaye College since 2019. She has completed her graduation and post-graduation from the same institution and have qualified the UGC&ndash;NET. Her teaching experience includes subjects such as Artificial Intelligence, Database Management Systems (DBMS), Computer Graphics, Geographic Information Systems (GIS), Apache Kafka, WordPress and WebServices.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 330, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4174, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 332, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4175, 108, 333, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Dr. Jayashree Gaikwad</strong> is the Head and Associate Professor in the Department of Botany with over 35 years of teaching experience. Her specialization includes Bryophytes and Pteridophytes, with research interests in sustainable horticulture, ethnobotany, plant taxonomy, and phytochemistry.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">She provides strong academic and administrative leadership, overseeing curriculum development, faculty coordination, research activities, and student mentoring. She has served as Chairperson and Member of several institutional committees, including BoS (Curriculum Development), IQAC (Criterion V &ndash; NAAC Cycles I, II &amp; III), Internal Complaints Committee (ICC), Women Development Cell, Anti-Ragging Committee, Student Grievance Redressal Cell, Admission Committee, Prospectus Committee, Cultural Committee, Garden Committee, Governing Body, and Finance Committee.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">She actively contributes to academic excellence, sustainable campus initiatives, and student development. She has published research papers in reputed journals and regularly guides student research projects.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 333, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4176, 108, 334, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Leela Chauhan, Associate Professor, has teaching experience of more than 30 years, with both undergraduate and Post graduate students. She is an active member of various committes and Chaiperson of Garden Committee. Dedicated to teaching and inculcating basic research methodologies, she also shares an excellent rapport with students. She has been a paper setter and moderator for TYBSc at the University level.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 334, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4178, 108, 336, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<p>Working as assistant Professor in Botany Since 2013. I have 13 year experience in Teaching for UG as well as PG students. Area of specialization is plant Physiology. Currently PhD is going on.&nbsp;</p>', '<p>Working as assistant Professor in Botany Since 2013. Teaching for UG as well as PG students. Area of specialization is plant Physiology. Currently PhD is going on.&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 0, '', 336, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4179, 108, 337, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p class=\"\" data-start=\"105\" data-end=\"396\">Dr. Deepali Mhapsekar has been serving as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Botany since 2019. She holds a Ph.D. in Botany and has qualified the State Eligibility Test (SET). Her areas of interest include Phytochemistry, Pharmacognosy, and Medicinal Botany. She has made significant academic contributions through research papers published in reputed national and international journals. She has also presented her work at numerous national and international conferences. In addition to her research pursuits, she has edited three academic books, published by recognized national publisher. Beyond academics, she actively contributes to institutional development as a member of various college committees. Her commitment to teaching, research, and academic leadership underscores her dedication to the advancement of botanical sciences and higher education.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 337, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4180, 108, 338, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Ms. Chaitali Pujare has been serving as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Botany since year 2019. She is pursuing her Ph.D in Botany (Taxonomy of Angiosperms)&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 338, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4181, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 339, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4182, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 1, '', 340, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4183, 108, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '1', 0, 0, '', 341, '2025-09-23', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(4184, 108, 343, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\">Mr. Rutam Mulay is currently pursuing a PhD in Science &amp; Technology (Microbiology) at Bhavan&rsquo;s College, University of Mumbai, under the guidance of Prof. Dr. Zarine Bhathena. He earned a Master of Science in Microbiology from the University of Mumbai, achieving an outstanding CGPA of 9.84 out of 10, which secured him the top rank in the Mumbai University 2017-2018 graduating class. Since 2018, he has served as Assistant Professor in Microbiology and has a teaching experience of 6 years. He has qualified the Maharashtra State Eligibility Test [MH-SET] in Life Sciences in 2019. He has undertaken significant research initiatives, including his ongoing investigation into the antiviral properties of medicinal plant extracts for dairy industry applications under Dr. Zarine Bhathena\'s guidance since August 2021. He previously did a study from 2017 to 2019 on developing a cost-effective method to assess <i>Cryptosporidium spp.</i> prevalence in coriander leaves, supervised by Dr. Sandhya Shrivastava. In 2015, he conducted research on isolating and purifying heterotrophic microalgae from Mumbai\'s mangrove ecosystems, also supervised by Dr. Zarine Bhathena. He has presented his research at prominent conferences, earning recognition such as the Best Poster Award at the 8<sup>th</sup> International Conference on Indian Network for Soil Contamination and Research in April 2024 and a Consolation Prize for an oral presentation at The Blue Voyage in March 2024. He has published two papers, including one accepted in Pharmacognosy Research, a Web of Science indexed journal. Complementing his academic achievements, he has administrative experience of working in the Centralized Assessment Program (CAP Committee), Library Committee and has specialized training in DNA sequencing using NGS and data analysis, Gas Chromatography and GC-MS. He has actively guided UG students in small projects under the DBT Star Scheme and MSc 1 students under the NEP curriculum. <o:p></o:p></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 343, '2025-09-23', 0),
(4186, 108, 345, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"593\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assistant Professor</span></em></p>\n<p data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"593\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">My name is Ms. Rashmi Sunil Patil, and I am passionate about the field of Microbiology and its allied disciplines. I hold an M.Sc. in Microbiology from Ruia College (2017&ndash;2019) and a B.Sc. in Microbiology from Sathaye College (2014&ndash;2017). Additionally, I have successfully cleared the Maharashtra State Eligibility Test (M-SET) and the Ph.D. Entrance Test (PET) conducted by Mumbai University, underscoring my strong academic background and dedication to scholarly excellence.</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"595\" data-end=\"1109\" class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">I bring five years of teaching experience at K.C. College and Sathaye College, where I have had the privilege of instructing B.Sc. and M.Sc. students. The subjects I have taught include Microbiology, Biochemistry, Medical Microbiology, Genetics, Cell Biology, Plant Physiology, Environmental Microbiology, Food Microbiology, and Industrial Biotechnology. Through my teaching journey, I have focused on creating an engaging, student-centered learning environment that fosters critical thinking, scientific inquiry, and academic growth.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 345, '2025-09-23', 0),
