(4464, 113, 15, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"https://www.sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/copy-1745559418-Classroom-Museum.jpg\" alt=\"Classroom Museum\" width=\"353\" height=\"265\" /></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Classroom Museum of the Department of Ancient Indian Culture &amp; Archaeology was set up in the academic year 2008-09 with a few antiquities donated by acquaintances and brought by students of the department during Explorations. When the department was shifted to Room No. 14, the concept of Museum classroom was introduced with minimal infrastructure available.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This Museum is a treasure house of various antiquities which consists of some rare antiquities which includes Fossils, Stone Tools including a few Hand Axes, Hammer Stones, Choppers of the Lower Paleolithic Period, a collection of Crystallized Rock formations, Terracotta Pottery fragments from distinctive cultures, Chinese porcelain ware fragments of the Portuguese period, antiquities of the Harappan period including a few bangle pieces of the same period, Architectural Fragments, rare collection of coins including punch marked Coins, Ancient, Medieval, Maratha and British period Coins, Manuscripts, Replicas of Harappan Seals, Buddhist&nbsp; Sculptures and most noteworthy a replica of the foot impression of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj from the fort of Sindhudurga. There are some new additions to the department museum which includes stone sculptures of Vishnu, Varaha, Ganpati, Nandi, Yakshini, Bodhisattva and few Temple Fragments.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '0', 0, 1, '', 246, '2026-04-18', 0),
