(4978, 122, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>1) Shreyash S. Chavan from SYBSc (Roll no. 301), Anshita R. Singh from SYBSc (Roll no. 310), Sneha G. Yadav from FYBSc (Roll no. 177) completed a research project in Fledgling Research Competition 2024 of the college under the guidance of Smt. Sukruta Pethe, Assistant Professor Head, Department of Physics. The topic of their research was \"DETERMINING NON-LINEAR STIFFNESS CONSTANTS OF TULSI PLANT (OCIMUM TENUIFLORUM)\"</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Determining-Non=linear-stiffness-constants-of-Tulsi-plant-Poster-(1).pdf\">Link for the Poster.</a></p>\n<p>2) Aditya Yadav from FYBSc (Roll no. 181), Keerti Pandey from FYBSc (Roll no. 195), Deeya Umbarje from SYBSc (Roll no. 311) completed a research project in Fledgling Research Competition 2024 of the college under the guidance of Smt. Malvika A. Naik from the Department of Physics. The topic of their research was \"PRECESSION OF EQUINOX.\"</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Precession-of-Equinox-Poster.pdf\">Link for the Poster.</a></p>\n<p>3) MSc Physics Semester III and IV Research Projects:</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">1. Marufa Khan; <strong>Photocatalytic degradation of drug molecules using V-N-TiO2 at Sathaye College&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">2. Shubham Santosh More: <strong>Study of radioactive decay of 124Sn(n, &gamma;) 125Sn populated through neutron Irradiation and determination of reaction cross section of 126Sn at TIFR</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">3. SAIRAJ NAIDU : &nbsp;<strong>Study of fission dynamic using charge particle evaporation as probes. Role of nuclear dissipation in fission dynamic at BARC</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">4. Tej Patil : <strong>Arduino-Based QRNG for Secure Autonomous Robotics, Enhancing Robotic Security with Quantum-Inspired Entropy</strong> <strong>at Viva College</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">6. Aryan Sawant : <strong>Study of Ion-beam Measurement Techniques</strong> <strong>at AMS facility, University of Mumbai</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">7. Moinuddin Shaikh: <strong>Dynamics simulations of HSA Protein followed by its trajectory analysis</strong> <strong>at TIFR</strong></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">5 and 8. &nbsp;Vivek Yadav and Soham Pimple: <strong>IoT-Based Smart Room Temperature Control and &nbsp;Monitoring System using ESP32</strong> <strong>at TIFR</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4) </strong>Shreyas Chavan and Anshita Singh from TYBSc Physics <strong>won Second Prize in Research Poster Presentation Competition in 32nd Raman Memorial Conference held in Department of Physics, SPPU </strong>at the hands of Prof. Sunil Bhagwat, Director of IISER, Pune. These students are working for a part of a Project for which Sukruta A. Pethe and Chaitali Pujare received the Institutional Research Grant 2025-26 from the College.</p>\n<p><strong>Topic of their project:</strong> Determining Linear and Nonlinear Stiffness constants in Tulsi (Oscimum tenuiflorum) &amp; Hibiscus (Hibiscus rosa-sinensis) and correlaing them with their Anatomical adaptations</p>\n<p>5) Ms. Marupha Khan from MSc Part II won 2nd Prize in Fledgling Research Competition at Sathaye College in March 2026&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Topic of the Poster: Photocatalytic Degradation of Pharmaceutical Molecules Using V&ndash;N&ndash;TiO₂</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 314, '2026-04-15', 0),
