(5452, 1, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Welcome to the Department of Zoology, Sathaye College (Autonomous)</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Established in 1982, the Department of Zoology at Sathaye College has built a strong legacy of academic excellence and innovation in the biological sciences. We offer comprehensive undergraduate programs and a postgraduate program (M.Sc. in Molecular Biology) that integrate theoretical foundations with extensive practical training through laboratory sessions, fieldwork, and research-based learning.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our department is dedicated to the scientific study of animal life, encompassing a wide spectrum of disciplines such as anatomy, physiology, behavior, genetics, ecology, evolution, and conservation. Students gain in-depth insights into both invertebrate and vertebrate biology, biodiversity, and the ecological roles animals play in natural systems.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our esteemed faculty includes Dr. Vishal Kadu, Dr. Ravindra Pawara, Ms. Amruta Pharande, Dr. Soni Ghumnani, Mr. Nikhil Yadav, Mr. Jitendra Shedge, Ms. Rasika Palsamkar and Ms. Shruti Dalvi&mdash;who are not only passionate educators but also active researchers mentoring students toward academic and professional excellence.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The department is equipped with cutting-edge laboratory infrastructure, a dedicated departmental library, and facilities that support innovative research and hands-on experimentation. Research is a core focus, with ongoing faculty- and student-led projects in areas such as molecular biology, marine biology and toxicology.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In alignment with the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020, our curriculum emphasizes experiential learning through field visits, internships, interdisciplinary workshops, and training in advanced topics such as bioinformatics and molecular biology techniques.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates of our department are well-prepared for diverse careers in Molecular biology, Taxonomy, Haematology, Animal physiology, environmental Science, wildlife conservation and scientific research.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the Department of Zoology, we believe in blending academic rigor with real-world application to empower the next generation of zoologists and life science professionals. Whether you&rsquo;re beginning your academic journey or pursuing advanced research, we invite you to explore, discover, and grow with us.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-04-20', 0),
(5454, 3, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>1. Dr. Vishal S. Kadu (HOD)<br />2. Dr. Ravindra H. Pawara<br />3. Smt. Amruta D. Pharande<br />4. Dr. Soni H. Ghumnani<br />5. Shri. Nikhil D. Yadav<br />6. Shri. Jitendra R. Shedge<br />7. Dr. Juliya C. Palande</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 444, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5455, 4, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Programs offered</strong></p>\n<p><strong>1. BSc Zoology</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An undergraduate program that covers topics such as animal physiology, cell biology, genetics, ecology, evolutionary biology, genetic engineering, molecular biology and comparative anatomy. Students also engage in practical lab work and field studies.</span></p>\n<p><strong>2. MSc Zoology (Molecular Biology)</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A postgraduate program offering specialized knowledge in area of molecular biology. It includes coursework, field studies and research-based dissertation work.</span></p>\n<ol>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> In trend Curriculum: The curriculum is designed to enable learners to get in depth knowledge of the subject by syllabi based on competitive exams like NTA CSIR-UGC NET, MH-SET, GATE, DBT-JRF etc.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Practical based learning: For each theory course there is associated practical course which allows leaners to apply the theoretical learning into praticals.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Industrial exposure through on job training. In semester II, learners will be given hands on training in various industries like healthcare, Biotechnology, Chemical etc.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Research exposure through research project. Learners will have to take up a research project in the semester III and IV. The research project to be carried out across various research institutes across Mumbai.</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>3. Zoology Minor subject for BA students with Psychology Major:</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"68\" data-end=\"416\">Aligned with the <span class=\"hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline\"><span class=\"whitespace-normal\">National Education Policy 2020</span></span>, this interdisciplinary program integrates Psychology (Major) with Zoology (Minor) to provide a holistic understanding of human behaviour through both social and biological lenses. It equips students with the ability to connect mental processes with physiological and evolutionary foundations.</p>\n<p data-start=\"418\" data-end=\"449\">This unique combination offers:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"790\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1u1w5xp\" data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"536\"><strong data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"482\">Interdisciplinary Insight:</strong> Understanding the interaction between mind and body</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1fy7jsn\" data-start=\"537\" data-end=\"621\"><strong data-start=\"539\" data-end=\"565\">Scientific Foundation:</strong> Exposure to laboratory sciences and analytical skills</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1cvupn5\" data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"708\"><strong data-start=\"624\" data-end=\"645\">Career Relevance:</strong> Useful for clinical psychology, rehabilitation, and research</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1fp5vy6\" data-start=\"709\" data-end=\"790\"><strong data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"733\">Holistic Approach:</strong> Behaviour studied as both psychological and biological</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"792\" data-end=\"994\">The Zoology minor strengthens core knowledge in areas such as physiology, genetics, immunology, endocrinology, and neurobiology, enabling students to approach behavioural sciences with scientific depth.</p>\n<p data-start=\"996\" data-end=\"1208\"><strong data-start=\"996\" data-end=\"1028\">Key Zoology Courses (Minor): </strong>Human Physiology, Behavioural Biology, Immunology, Human Genetics, Human Endocrinology, and Neurobiology (with corresponding practicals).</p>\n<p data-start=\"1210\" data-end=\"1348\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">This program prepares students for emerging careers that demand interdisciplinary expertise in health, research, and behavioural sciences.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1210\" data-end=\"1348\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><strong>List of Courses Offered under Zoology Minor</strong><br />1. Human Physiology<br />2. Behavioural Biology<br />3. Immunology<br />4. Human Genetics<br />5. Human Endocrinology<br />6. Neurobiology</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-04-20', 0);
