g\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click here</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">TYBSc</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">2024-25</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db;\">Click here</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>University Syllabi</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 90px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">Year of Syllabus first implemented&nbsp;</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\">Download</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">FYBSc</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">2015-16</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a style=\"color: #3598db;\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10dDBim2mEOnoU0KXLVt7RzStFh2CUjWu/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click here</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">SYBSc</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">2018-19</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a style=\"color: #3598db;\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kv9rxx2_DXVYP2wlq03KF29isy6yzIqN/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click here</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">TYBSc (Paper I-IV)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">2018-19</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a style=\"color: #3598db;\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1E9hRWhhqWi9qZt6z7nkixG3HyI0Qh658/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click here</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">TYBSc (Applied component; Paper V)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.058%; height: 18px;\">2018-19</td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.0591%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a style=\"color: #3598db;\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q2GARo63u9SsawcqRZSDMKfV3A3ABWWF/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click here</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-10-04', 0),
(5457, 57, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Zoology Association:</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 180, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5458, 59, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Guest Lectures:</strong></p>\n<p>1. Importance of Mangrove Forest in Biodiversity Brochure (24-25)<br />2. PCR Workshop Brochure February (24-25)</p>\n<p><strong>Outreach Activities</strong><br />1. Amazing World of Animals Brochure (24-25)</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 180, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5459, 86, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/14k15-0L8dyLjt-oHsUEJ1rhxVwayOIUm?usp=sharing\" style=\"color: #3598db;\">DBT Outreach Program</a></span></p>\n<p>Zoology Excursion</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 180, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5460, 94, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One of our primary research areas explores the impact of ethanol on fin regeneration in zebrafish (Danio rerio), a widely used model organism in developmental biology and toxicology. Zebrafish possess a remarkable regenerative ability, primarily driven by the formation of a blastema composed of proliferating and differentiating cells. Our study investigates ethanol&rsquo;s teratogenic potential and its broader ecological implications on aquatic health, aiming to inform future conservation strategies and environmental policies.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In parallel, our lab also studies regeneration in Planaria in response to teratogenic substances, expanding our understanding of fundamental regenerative mechanisms across species.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Another line of research investigates adaptive physiology in Cyclopes, focusing on their unique capability to process urea molecules providing insights into metabolic adaptations in aquatic invertebrates.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In the realm of food safety and public health, our lab assesses heavy metal contamination in commonly consumed dairy products. Given the nutritional importance of ice cream and its popularity especially among children this research aims to assess potential health risks and identify contamination sources across the production and supply chain, including environmental, packaging, and processing factors.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Additionally, our lab examines the protein content in different prawn species under wet and preserved conditions. This research aims to evaluate the most effective preservation methods for maintaining high protein levels and to assess the overall protein quality of prawn species commonly available in Mumbai.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Through these diverse projects, our goal is to contribute valuable insights to the fields of developmental biology, environmental science, public health, and food safety, while also offering undergraduate and postgraduate student&rsquo;s opportunities to engage in hands-on, impactful research.</span></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 180, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5461, 105, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Zoology has well equiped labs with notable equipments, like:</p>\n<p>Thermocycler machine</p>\n<p>Automated bioanalyzer</p>\n<p>CO2 Incubator</p>\n<p>Laminar Airflow</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-04-20', 0),
(5463, 126, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><b>ADD-ON COURSE &ndash; FISH REARING AND CARE (For syllabus, click here) <span style=\"color: #3598db;\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15OPFRL1sGpTU7CVevx_Xp4rS4dy3uHYp/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #3598db;\">(for syllabus, click here)</a></span></b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While presenting the add on course - Fish rearing and care for the under graduate students, we are happy to state that efforts has been made to take inputs from all the teachers in Zoology subject to make it more relevant, by keeping in view the demand of the students and to nurture the interest amongst the students. It is necessary to update the pupils in this current era of exponential information and knowledge due to the quick growth in technology, new ideas and concepts, and an ocean of information being generated every day. With this intention, the teachers in Zoology took decision to put this add on course fish rearing and care for the undergraduate students, so that they can study topics of their interest. The add on course that includes fish rearing and care is made more interesting with and innovative topic. It has been made discovery oriented, learner centered, flexible and enjoyable in order to prepare the students for gainful knowledge. The course content has been framed to emphasize creativity and innovation and the ability to assimilate new information. Along with the theory part, availability of Hands-on training will become a crucial component of the course. Practical experience in aquarium design, construction and maintenance for a long period of time will give student an insight for the fish rearing and care. The success of this course will totally depend on the enthusiasm of the teachers and obviously students, and their expertise will be strengthened by developing skills and information.</span></p>\n<p><b>Course Objective:&nbsp;</b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To introduce participants with scientific aspects of </span>Aquarium setting and maintaining</p>\n<p><b></b></p>\n<p><b>Course Content:</b></p>\n<p><b>Setting and Maintenance of Aquarium&nbsp;</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Light and aeriation for Aquarium</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cleaning and water recycling/replacing</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best Aquarium fishes</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fish infection and fish diseases</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to maintain Aquarium when you are on long vacation?</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fish food&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to choose location for aquarium in your home/office?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p></p>\n<p><b>Learning Outcomes: Participants will be able to&nbsp;</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Experience better fish survival in his/her aquarium after this course.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Understand Aquarium setting, maintaining and rearing of fishes with scientific approach. </span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Enhance their interest towards the Aquarium, Aquarium fishes, Cats and Dogs.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Decipher that how owning of pet makes them more empathic.&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse causes, symptoms and preventions of diseases.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><b></b></p>\n<p><b>Course duration and Credits:&nbsp;</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">30 Hours</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2 Credits</span></li>\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 180, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5464, 127, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Zoology on Social media:<br /><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/department.of.zoology?igsh=MTRrZnR5cnZ1cnVqZQ==\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram Page:</a></p>\n<p>https://www.instagram.com/department.of.zoology?igsh=MTRrZnR5cnZ1cnVqZQ==</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-04-20', 0),
