(5844, 78, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong><u>Paper presentation in conferences:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>1) Soni Ghumnani</strong>, Arjun Shahu, Neeraj Adkar, Yogesh Shouche, Saroj Ghaskadbi, Richa Ashma. &lsquo;Polyalanine polymorphism in the signal peptide of Glutathione peroxidase 1 gene and its association with osteoporosis&rsquo;, at National Research Scholars Meet organised by ACTREC, Navi&nbsp;Mumbai&nbsp;from 16-18 November 2018. <strong><u>Poster presentation.</u></strong><strong><u></u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>2) Soni Ghumnani</strong> and Richa Ashma. Plumbagin suppresses RANKL-induced Osteoclast differentiation via inhibiting NFATc1 translocation at the International Conference on Fundamental and Applied Sciences organised by the Faculty of Science in collaboration with IQAC, Mumbai from 24th March to 26th March 2021.&nbsp;<strong><u>Won First Prize for Best Poster presentation.</u></strong></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5845, 79, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Completed two research projects:</p>\r\n<p>1) Project fellow, UGC-funded project, Department of Zoology, Savitribai Phule Pune University, Pune (January 2016 to June 2018).</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;2) Research staff, ISRO-SPPU funded project, Department of Zoology, Savitribai Phule Pune University, Pune (November 2019 to March 2024).</p>\r\n<p>3) Co-Principal Investigator, Institutional Research Project, Sathaye College, Vile Parle (East), Mumbai (January 2025 to January 2026).</p>\r\n<p>Ongoing Research Project</p>\r\n<p>1) Co-Principal Investigator, Institutional Research Project, Sathaye College, Vile Parle (East), Mumbai (December 2025).</p>', '0', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5846, 80, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Nil</p>', '0', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5847, 81, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong><u>Paper presentation in conferences:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>1) Soni Ghumnani</strong>, Arjun Shahu, Neeraj Adkar, Yogesh Shouche, Saroj Ghaskadbi, Richa Ashma. &lsquo;Polyalanine polymorphism in the signal peptide of Glutathione peroxidase 1 gene and its association with osteoporosis&rsquo;, at National Research Scholars Meet organised by ACTREC, Navi&nbsp;Mumbai&nbsp;from 16-18 November 2018. <strong><u>Poster presentation.</u></strong><strong><u></u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>2) Soni Ghumnani</strong> and Richa Ashma. Plumbagin suppresses RANKL-induced Osteoclast differentiation via inhibiting NFATc1 translocation at the International Conference on Fundamental and Applied Sciences organised by the Faculty of Science in collaboration with IQAC, Mumbai from 24th March to 26th March 2021.&nbsp;<strong><u>Won First Prize for Best Poster presentation.</u></strong></p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5848, 95, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>1)Kazi, M., Jaiswar, A., <strong>Ghumnani, S.&nbsp;</strong>Detection of Lead in different Ice-cream samples across Mumbai City. <em>Journal of Emerging Technologies and Innovative Research</em>, 13(1), 297-302.</p>\r\n<p>1) <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Barvkar, V. T., Mhaske, S. T., Saha, B., &amp; Ashma, R. (2023). Plumbagin modulates RANKL-induced osteoclast and osteoblast differentiation.&nbsp;<em>Phytomedicine Plus</em>,&nbsp;<em>3</em>(2), 100429.</p>\r\n<p>2) Yadav, A. M., Bagade, M. M., <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Raman, S., Saha, B., Kubatzky, K. F., &amp; Ashma, R. (2022). The phytochemical plumbagin reciprocally modulates osteoblasts and osteoclasts.&nbsp;<em>Biological Chemistry</em>,&nbsp;<em>403</em>(2), 211-229.</p>\r\n<p>3) <strong>Ahuja, S. G., </strong>Shahu, A., Rath, S., Adkar, N., Shouche, Y., Ghaskadbi, S., &amp; Ashma, R. (2022). Polyalanine polymorphism in the signal peptide of Glutathione peroxidase 1 (GPX1) gene &amp; its association with osteoporosis. <em>Indian Journal of Medical Research</em>,&nbsp;<em>156</em>(4&amp;5), 640-647.</p>\r\n<p>4) Sultanli, S., <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Ashma, R., &amp; Kubatzky, K. F. (2021). Plumbagin, a biomolecule with (anti) osteoclastic properties.&nbsp;<em>International Journal of Molecular Sciences</em>,&nbsp;<em>22</em>(5), 2779.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5849, 96, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>&nbsp;1) Symposium on &lsquo;Accelerating Biology 2016: Decoding the Deluge&rsquo; organised by Bioinformatics Group, C-DAC, Pune at Yashada, Pune, 19<sup>th</sup>-21<sup>st</sup> January 2016.</p>\n<p>2) Online Workshop on &lsquo;Molecular Docking&rsquo; organised by Qstatix Ltd, Hyderabad from 29<sup>th</sup> to 31<sup>st</sup> October, 2020</p>\n<p>3) Indo-Finnish Workshop on &lsquo;Tools and techniques for analysis of skin Microbiome and metabolome&rsquo; organised by Department of Zoology, Savitribai Phule Pune University, Pune, from 4<sup>th</sup> and 5<sup>th</sup> January, 2021.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5850, 97, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>1)Kazi, M., Jaiswar, A., <strong>Ghumnani, S.&nbsp;</strong>Detection of Lead in different Ice-cream samples across Mumbai City. <em>Journal of Emerging Technologies and Innovative Research</em>, 13(1), 297-302.</p>\r\n<p>1) <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Barvkar, V. T., Mhaske, S. T., Saha, B., &amp; Ashma, R. (2023). Plumbagin modulates RANKL-induced osteoclast and osteoblast differentiation.&nbsp;<em>Phytomedicine Plus</em>,&nbsp;<em>3</em>(2), 100429.</p>\r\n<p>2) Yadav, A. M., Bagade, M. M., <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Raman, S., Saha, B., Kubatzky, K. F., &amp; Ashma, R. (2022). The phytochemical plumbagin reciprocally modulates osteoblasts and osteoclasts.&nbsp;<em>Biological Chemistry</em>,&nbsp;<em>403</em>(2), 211-229.</p>\r\n<p>3) <strong>Ahuja, S. G., </strong>Shahu, A., Rath, S., Adkar, N., Shouche, Y., Ghaskadbi, S., &amp; Ashma, R. (2022). Polyalanine polymorphism in the signal peptide of Glutathione peroxidase 1 (GPX1) gene &amp; its association with osteoporosis. <em>Indian Journal of Medical Research</em>,&nbsp;<em>156</em>(4&amp;5), 640-647.</p>\r\n<p>4) Sultanli, S., <strong>Ghumnani, S.,</strong> Ashma, R., &amp; Kubatzky, K. F. (2021). Plumbagin, a biomolecule with (anti) osteoclastic properties.&nbsp;<em>International Journal of Molecular Sciences</em>,&nbsp;<em>22</em>(5), 2779.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5851, 98, 448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p>Faculty Development Programs:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Faculty Development Programme on \"<strong>Flipped Learning\"</strong>&nbsp;organised by&nbsp;<strong>PTVA\'s Sathaye College</strong>&nbsp;from 16th January 2025 to 6th March 2025.</li>\r\n</ol>', '0', 0, 1, '', 448, '2025-09-23', 0),
