(5922, 129, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h3 class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"70\">Department of Physics &ndash; Academic &amp; Administrative Responsibilities</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"644\">\r\n<li data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"195\"><strong data-start=\"74\" data-end=\"94\">FYBSc In-Charge:</strong> Coordinating academic activities, student records, and departmental requirements for FYBSc students.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"196\" data-end=\"339\"><strong data-start=\"198\" data-end=\"218\">TYBSc In-Charge:</strong> Managing academic coordination, student-related activities, and examination-related responsibilities for TYBSc students.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"473\"><strong data-start=\"342\" data-end=\"367\">Department Timetable:</strong> Preparing and coordinating the departmental timetable to ensure smooth and effective academic scheduling.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"474\" data-end=\"644\"><strong data-start=\"476\" data-end=\"506\">Mentor&ndash;Mentee Coordinator:</strong> Providing academic guidance, monitoring student progress, addressing student concerns, and maintaining regular mentor&ndash;mentee interaction.</li>\r\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 313, '2025-09-23', 0),
(5923, 129, 314, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Smt. Sukruta is working as an Assistant Professor in Physics in Sathaye College for over two decades since 2002.<br />She has taught a wide range of physics subjects to undergraduate students which includes Solid State Physics, Optics, Mechanics, Electrodynamics, Special Theory of Relativity, Microprocessor, Applied Physics and Digital Electronics.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She launched the MSc Physics programme at Sathaye College in the academic year 2024-25, single-handedly developing its syllabus. She also established collaborations with SPPU and TIFR to provide MSc Nuclear Technique practicals, enhancing the programme\'s academic rigor.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The walls of the Physics laboratories, enriched by her efforts, display curated profiles of eminent physicists highlighting their contributions, journeys, and honors alongside information on premier institutes in India for higher studies, inspiring students to dream bigger and pursue excellence in Physics. TYBSc Physics Batch of 2021-22 initiated an outreach activity namely <strong>SciPhy</strong> under her guidance in which undergraduate students demonstrate various experiments to School Children from the vicinity schools.&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">She actively takes the initiative in all departmental activities aimed at student development and often undertakes major events single-handedly. Her contributions include organizing the departmental library, Cafe physics-based treasure hunts, Vidnyan Katha Din celebration, Talk about LGBTQ community, visits to various research institutes, visits sociatl organisaations for social sensitisation, expert talks, workshops, and a variety of other innovative programs that enrich the academic and co-curricular experience of students.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 314, '2025-09-23', 0),
