(5939, 129, 333, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h3 data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"44\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">As a Teacher in the Botany Department</span></h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"46\" data-end=\"339\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">As a teacher in the Botany Department, my role extends beyond classroom instruction to mentoring, research guidance, and academic administration. I am committed to nurturing scientific curiosity and environmental responsibility among students through effective teaching and practical exposure.</span></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"341\" data-end=\"840\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">In teaching, I focus on delivering clear conceptual understanding in subjects such as Plant Taxonomy, Anatomy, Physiology, Ecology, Genetics, and specialized areas like Bryophytes and Pteridophytes. I adopt student-centric methods including experiential learning, participative discussions, field visits, herbarium preparation, and project-based assignments to enhance learning outcomes. ICT-enabled tools and innovative teaching strategies are incorporated to make lessons interactive and engaging.</span></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"842\" data-end=\"1160\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">In laboratory sessions, I guide students in developing observational, analytical, and technical skills through experiments, slide preparation, specimen identification, and research projects. I also encourage students to undertake small research studies and biodiversity surveys to strengthen their scientific aptitude.</span></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1477\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apart from academics, I actively participate in curriculum development, evaluation processes, examination work, and various institutional committees. I support environmental initiatives such as tree plantation drives, maintenance of the botanical garden, and awareness programmes on conservation and sustainability.</span></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1479\" data-end=\"1863\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">As a mentor, I guide students in career opportunities in botany, higher education, competitive examinations, entrepreneurship in mushroom cultivation and horticulture, and research fields. My aim as a teacher is to inspire students to appreciate plant diversity, develop critical thinking skills, and contribute positively to environmental conservation and sustainable development</span>.</p>', '1', 0, 1, '', 333, '2025-09-23', 0),
