(6155, 131, 314, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<ul>\n<li>She works in the editorial boards of a 25 year old Marathi Periodical namely घरकुल which is privately circulated.</li>\n<li>She founded Dholpathak of more than 75 participants and performed for 6 years. Creative writing in Marathi is her passion.</li>\n<li>She has written various articles, Science Fictions, written, directed and performed skits for cultural programmes.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Taken initiative in launching &ldquo;Zero Garbage Project&rdquo; in her residential complex namely Vijaynagar Society located in Andheri East. The colony consists of 515 members with more than 2000 residents. With consistent efforts the project is sustained and got acceptance from all residents of the society. In December 2016, Vijaynagar Society received Mega Gold Award in ICICI Swachh Society Competition, at the hands of then <strong>Honorable Chief Minister of Maharashtra, Mr. Devendra Phadanvis </strong>and Mrs. Chanda Kochher, MD, ICICI form amongst the 7000 plus residential societies from Brihan Mumbai, Kalyan Dombiwali, Thane, Navi Mumbai. Being one of the leading volunteers, I got an opportunity to attend the prize distribution function to receive the award. The prize consists of a Gold Trophy and Rs. 15 Lakh.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Visits different societies in Mumbai to spread awareness about Cleanliness and promote the need of Zero Garbage Projects voluntary. Given presentation about zero garbage project in more than 60 societies and in more than ten Colleges and school.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Attended and explained Zero Garbage Project to more than 2500 visitors to our Society from different locations across Mumbai and outside Mumbai. It also includes NIRRH and Sarpanch Training Programme at Murbad.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>', '1', 0, 1, '', 314, '2025-09-23', 0),
