(7871, 54, 52, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<div dir=\"auto\">Green Club and Green Audit Committee of PTVA\'s Sathaye College (Autonomous) represents a progressive institutional initiative dedicated to fostering environmental stewardship, ecological literacy, and sustainable development within the academic community. The Committee reflects the institution&rsquo;s enduring commitment to nurturing socially responsible and environmentally conscious citizens. It actively integrates principles of conservation biology, environmental governance, and climate science into campus culture through structured programs and action-oriented campaigns. By promoting biodiversity conservation, resource efficiency, and carbon footprint reduction, the Committee ensures that sustainability remains a lived practice rather than a theoretical discourse. Regular environmental audits, afforestation drives, cleanliness drives, waste segregation systems, and water conservation initiatives exemplify its systematic approach to ecological management. The Club also emphasizes climate resilience and sustainable urban living, aligning its initiatives with global sustainable development frameworks. Through workshops, seminars, and interdisciplinary dialogues, it cultivates scientific temper and environmental ethics among students. In doing so, it transforms awareness into measurable ecological impact.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">The legacy of environmental advocacy at Sathaye College is deeply rooted in student leadership and collective responsibility. Successive generations of dedicated volunteers have strengthened the green movement on campus through ecosystem restoration projects, waste recyling drives and collaborations with civic bodies and non-governmental organizations. Their efforts demonstrate an informed understanding of ecological interdependence and the urgency of sustainable practices in the current period. The Committee functions as a catalyst for experiential learning, enabling students to engage in field-based research, sustainability assessments, and community outreach programs. By integrating perspectives from environmental science, public policy, and sustainable economics, it encourages analytical thinking and solution-oriented action. The Committee not only safeguards natural resources but also inspires behavioral transformation toward responsible consumption and environmental accountability. Its initiatives contribute to building a resilient and environmentally literate campus community. Ultimately, the Committee stands as a testament to the dedication, integrity, and forward-thinking vision of Sathaye College students in preserving and protecting nature for future generations.</div>', '1', 0, 1, '', 2, '2025-10-28', 0),
