(9564, 108, 553, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Shrishti Tripathi is an economist, researcher and educator with a strong commitment to academic excellence, evidence-based research and student-centric learning. Her academic journey has been shaped by a deep interest in understanding developmental challenges through the lens of economics, with particular emphasis on financial inclusion, public policy, entrepreneurship and sustainable development. Her doctoral research focuses on the role of financial inclusion in reducing multidimensional poverty in India, employing quantitative research methods and primary field-based data to generate meaningful policy insights.</p>\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">As an educator, she has taught diverse branches of Economics, including Microeconomics, Macroeconomics, Public Finance, International Economics, Econometrics, and Statistics. She has also mentored students preparing for competitive examinations such as UPSC, Indian Economic Services (IES), RBI DEPR, and UGC-NET, where the emphasis was on conceptual clarity, analytical thinking, and practical application of economic theory. Her teaching philosophy revolves around making economics engaging, relatable, and relevant by integrating real-world examples, data-driven analysis, and interactive classroom discussions.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Dr. Tripathi&rsquo;s research interests encompass Applied Economics, Financial Inclusion, Development Economics, Gender Studies, Entrepreneurship, and Public Policy. She has presented and published research papers in national and international conferences and journals on topics including digital banking, women&rsquo;s entrepreneurship, self-help groups, corporate social responsibility, and the JAM Trinity framework. These scholarly engagements have strengthened her commitment to producing research that contributes to both academic discourse and policy formulation.</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Beyond teaching and research, she has actively contributed to academic administration through curriculum support, mentoring, workshops, seminars, examination responsibilities, and institutional activities. She believes that higher education should not only impart knowledge but also cultivate critical thinking, ethical values and a spirit of inquiry among students. As an academic, she aspires to create an inclusive learning environment that inspires curiosity, encourages research, and prepares students to address contemporary economic and societal challenges with confidence and integrity.</div>', '', '1', 0, 0, '', 553, '0000-00-00', 0),
