(9750, 203, 15, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>For UG:</strong></p>\n<p>The course of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology under NEP has been designed to have a progressive and innovative curriculum in order to equip learners to face the future challenges in the field of higher education. In this program learners are introduced to the various facets of archaeology, art and culture of Ancient India.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>For PG:</strong></p>\n<p>The Master&rsquo;s programme in Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology under the National Education Policy (NEP) aims to provide an advanced, interdisciplinary, and research-oriented education that develops critical understanding of the archaeology, art, culture, and heritage of India. The programme seeks to equip learners with theoretical, methodological, practical, and research skills necessary for higher studies, professional careers, heritage management, and meaningful contributions to the preservation and interpretation of India&rsquo;s cultural heritage.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>For UG:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>To provide education which includes theoretical and practical knowledge according to international standards.</li>\n<li>To contribute to the protection of cultural heritage by aiming towards sustainable growth and development in the field.</li>\n<li>To apply the knowledge from the fields of art, archaeology and cultural history which will aid in understanding various phases in and the process of the evolution of Archaeology and Indian Culture.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>For PG:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>To provide advanced theoretical, practical, and research-oriented education in Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>To develop critical, analytical, and interdisciplinary skills through archaeological methods, fieldwork, and research.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>To promote the documentation, conservation, preservation, and sustainable management of cultural heritage.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>To prepare learners for higher education, research, and professional careers in archaeology, heritage, museums, and allied fields.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>To foster ethical and innovative approaches to the study and interpretation of India&rsquo;s cultural heritage.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge:</strong> Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behavior and social life.</p>\n<p><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking:</strong> Critically evaluate texts, cultural artefacts, historical evidence, media content, and scholarly arguments; and apply reflective and analytical thinking to interpret and understand complex human experiences.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Research Skills: </strong>Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social; national and global community level issues.</p>\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning: </strong>Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning:</strong> Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes.</p>\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical awareness:</strong> Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n<p><strong>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities:</strong> Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership.</p>\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning:</strong> Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>For UG:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PSO1 - </strong>To recall and recognize key concepts, theories, methods and principles from the field of Archaeology.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO2 -</strong> To enable learners to demonstrate comprehensive and critical understanding of methods, and theories, apply theoretical knowledge of archaeological theories to plan and conduct fieldwork, analyse the data collected.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO3 -</strong> To develop learners&rsquo; ability to critically examine, compare, and interpret collected data, identifying patterns, cultural sequences, material remains.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO4 - </strong>To enable learners to critically assess research findings, and scientific literature, and to apply this evaluation in designing and executing original research projects by formulating hypotheses and developing innovative solutions to complex problems in the field of Ancient Indian Culture and Archaeology.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>For PG:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PSO1 -</strong> Demonstrate advanced and critical understanding of concepts, theories, methods, and principles of Archaeology and Ancient Indian Culture.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO2 -</strong> Apply archaeological theories, methodologies, and interdisciplinary approaches to undertake fieldwork and critically analyse, interpret, and evaluate archaeological evidence and material remains.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO3 -</strong> Formulate research questions and hypotheses, critically evaluate scholarly literature and research findings, and undertake independent research using appropriate archaeological and scientific methods.</p>\n<p><strong>PSO4 -</strong> Apply knowledge and skills in the documentation, interpretation, conservation, preservation, and sustainable management of archaeological and cultural heritage.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>For UG:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PEO1 - </strong>Equip graduates with a strong foundation in archaeological concepts, theories, methods, and scientific approaches, enabling them to conduct archaeological exploration, excavation, documentation, analysis, and interpretation effectively.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO2 -</strong> Enable graduates to apply analytical and critical thinking skills in examining archaeological data, interpreting material culture, evaluating research findings, and contributing to innovative research in archaeology and heritage studies.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO3 - </strong>Prepare graduates to preserve, protect, and manage archaeological and cultural heritage by applying ethical principles, conservation practices, documentation techniques, and relevant legal frameworks in professional practice.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO4 - </strong>Inspire graduates to engage in continuous learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and the adoption of emerging technologies and scientific methods to address contemporary challenges in archaeology, cultural resource management, and heritage conservation.</p>\n<p><strong>For PG:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>PEO1 -</strong> Equip graduates with advanced knowledge of archaeological concepts, theories, methodologies, and scientific approaches to undertake archaeological exploration, excavation, documentation, analysis, and interpretation.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO2 -</strong> Develop critical, analytical, and research skills to evaluate archaeological evidence, material culture, scholarly research, and contribute to original and innovative research in Archaeology and Heritage Studies.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO3 -</strong> Prepare graduates to professionally document, conserve, preserve, interpret, and manage archaeological and cultural heritage in accordance with ethical principles, conservation practices, and relevant legal frameworks.</p>\n<p><strong>PEO4 -</strong> Foster lifelong learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and the use of emerging technologies and scientific techniques to address contemporary challenges in archaeology, heritage management, and cultural resource conservation.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 516, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9751, 203, 18, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9752, 203, 19, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp; </strong></h4>\n<p>To empower students with economic knowledge, research competence, ethical values and social responsibility to become responsible professionals and lifelong learners.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>To facilitate academic excellence through innovative and learner-centric</li>\n<li>To promote critical thinking, research aptitude and issue-based problem</li>\n<li>To develop socially responsible citizens committed to sustainable</li>\n<li>To encourage interdisciplinary learning, digital literacy and experiential</li>\n<li>To enhance employability, entrepreneurship and leadership through continuous learning</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 97.8768%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 38.7432%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"229\">\n<p><strong>Program</strong><strong> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; B.A&nbsp; &nbsp; in Economics</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 60.7973%;\" width=\"366\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 99.5405%;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"595\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge: </strong>Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Communication Skills: </strong>Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of</p>\n<p>expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking</strong>: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple</p>\n<p>perspectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Research Skills</strong>: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social;</p>\n<p>national and global community level issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.38538%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.1552%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning: </strong>Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyse multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table style=\"width: 98.0137%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 8.80399%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0332%;\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning: </strong>Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 8.80399%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0332%;\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical awareness</strong>: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 8.80399%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0332%;\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: </strong>Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 8.80399%;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO9</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0332%;\" width=\"542\">\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning: </strong>Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 97.7397%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 77.9557%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"468\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B.A in Economics</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 21.8391%;\" width=\"133\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG/PG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 99.7948%;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.44171%;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.3531%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.44171%;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.3531%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Demonstrate fundamental knowledge of microeconomic concepts, basic economic problems, price mechanism and market functioning, and relate them to resource allocation and contemporary economic issues</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.44171%;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.3531%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Apply mathematical, graphical and analytical tools to interpret economic relationships and</p>\n<p>solve basic numerical problems.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.44171%;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.3531%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Develop basic research and data analysis competencies by applying appropriate sampling techniques, determining suitable sample sizes, collecting and processing data, analysing research findings, and assessing the quality of research data.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.44171%;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.3531%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Communicate and evaluate economic and research findings responsibly by interpreting evidence, critically assessing research practices, and adhering to ethical standards, scientific integrity, data privacy and responsible reporting.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 98.2191%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 76.6756%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"461\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B.A.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 23.0263%;\" width=\"140\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG/PG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 99.7019%;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.62171%;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0802%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.62171%;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0802%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Pursue postgraduate education, doctoral research, academic careers, and teaching professions in Economics and related disciplines.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.62171%;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0802%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Serve in civil services, public administration, banking, finance, government departments, economic planning, and public-service organisations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.62171%;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0802%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Work in banking, financial services, business, management, consulting, market research, data analysis, and corporate sectors.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 9.62171%;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.0802%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Engage in interdisciplinary and emerging career fields such as econometrics, data analytics, public policy, development research, environmental economics, behavioural economics, and economic research</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp; </strong><strong>Microeconomics&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 96.7808%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO1: Explain the fundamental concepts of microeconomics, basic economic problems, price mechanism and market functioning and communicate their relevance in resource allocation and contemporary economic issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO2: Apply economic principles, mathematical functions, equations, graphs and diagrams to interpret economic relationships and solve basic numerical problems.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO3: Analyse consumer behaviour using utility analysis, indifference curve approach and consumer equilibrium to explain demand</p>\n<p>behaviour.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO4: Examine/ Critically examine the market equilibrium, elasticity of demand and demand forecasting techniques to evaluate changes in market conditions and consumer decision-making.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp; </strong><strong>Research Methodology</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 97.6027%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome </strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO1: Apply appropriate sampling techniques, determine suitable sample sizes, and employ data collection methods to conduct basic research studies.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO2: Analyse research data by selecting appropriate sampling methods, identifying sampling complications, interpreting research findings, and</p>\n<p>assessing the quality of processed data.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.9289%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 86.2944%;\" width=\"340\">\n<p>CO3: Critically evaluate research practices based on ethical standards, scientific integrity, data privacy, and responsible reporting to ensure credible and socially</p>\n<p>responsible research outcomes.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 248, '2026-10-14', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9753, 203, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department : </strong></h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To be a centre of excellence in Education that nurtures competent, ethical, innovative, and socially responsible educators and lifelong learners through quality education, research, critical inquiry, inclusive practices, interdisciplinary knowledge, leadership, and human values, fostering national development, global citizenship, lifelong learning, and educational excellence.</span></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1. To provide learner-centred, inclusive, and interdisciplinary education that develops pedagogical competence, critical thinking, communication skills, and professional ethics.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">2. To promote research, innovation, analytical and scientific reasoning through experiential learning, field engagement, and technology-enabled educational practices.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">3. To cultivate leadership, social responsibility, constitutional values, teamwork, and community engagement for addressing local, national, and global educational challenges.</span><br /><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">4. To encourage lifelong learning, employability, entrepreneurship, and continuous professional development by fostering creativity, collaboration, and reflective practice.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO1 Disciplinary Knowledge: Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO2 Communication Skills: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO3 Critical Thinking: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO4 Research Skills: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social, national and global community level issues.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO5 Analytical Reasoning: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO6 Scientific Reasoning: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO7 Moral and Ethical awareness: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO8 Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PO9 Lifelong Learning: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PSO1<br />Demonstrate comprehensive knowledge of the philosophical, psychological, sociological, and historical foundations of education and apply these concepts to understand contemporary educational issues.<br /></span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PSO2<br />Design, implement, and evaluate learner-centred, inclusive, and technology- enabled teaching-learning processes using appropriate pedagogical strategies and assessment techniques.<br /></span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PSO3<br />Apply research methods, analytical thinking, and scientific reasoning to investigate educational problems and propose evidence-based solutions for improving educational practices.<br /></span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PSO4<br />Exhibit ethical values, leadership qualities, teamwork, and social responsibility by actively participating in educational institutions, community development, and lifelong learning initiatives.<br /></span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PSO5<br />Integrate interdisciplinary knowledge, digital literacy, communication skills, and reflective practices to pursue higher education, educational entrepreneurship, research, counselling, curriculum development, educational administration, and other professional careers in the field of education.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">PEO1</span><br /><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Develop strong knowledge of educational theories, pedagogy, interdisciplinary perspectives, and emerging educational technologies.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">PEO2</span><br /><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply critical thinking, research, and problem-solving skills to address educational and societal challenges effectively.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">PEO3</span><br /><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Demonstrate effective communication, teamwork, leadership, ethical values, social responsibility, inclusivity, and constitutional principles in educational and professional settings.</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">PEO4</span><br /><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Engage in lifelong learning, professional development, and innovation to contribute to educational excellence, national development, and global citizenship.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><u>SEMESTER-I</u></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Education Paper I</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Course code: </strong><strong>GBA1EDUMJ0124</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Title: - </strong><strong>INTRODUCTION TO EDUCATION</strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Course Objectives:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Credits: 04</strong></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To acquire knowledge about the meaning, characteristics, and functions of education.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To be acquainted with different types of education.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To understand the role of different agencies in education.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To explain the factors of education and their interrelationship.</span></li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Course Title: Introduction to Education</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Course Code: GBA1EDUMJ0124</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Academic Year: 2026-27</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"227\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">No. of total contact Hours: 60</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"148\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Course credits: 4</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Class: FYBA</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"227\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Semester: I</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"148\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO Statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>BTL</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>L</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>P</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO</strong></span></p>\n</td