opment.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K1</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1,9</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Explain the meaning of life skills and the role of school in life skill development.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K2</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">8,9</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">4,5</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply life skills and principles of balanced nutrition to promote healthy growth and development during childhood.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K3</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">5,9</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">3,5</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Evaluate the role of nutrition, balanced diet, multimedia, and ICT tools in promoting children&rsquo;s health, development, and effective learning.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K4</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">10</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">3,6</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1,3</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Analyze and evaluate the causes of malnutrition and the effectiveness of ICT-enabled multimedia activities in addressing health and learning needs of children.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">10</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">4,5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1,2</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>CO6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Design and develop ICT-supported multimedia activities and child-health initiatives that promote balanced nutrition, prevent malnutrition, and enhance activity-based learning.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">K6</span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">10</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">3,4</span></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">2,5</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 253, '2026-10-14', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9754, 203, 21, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Vision of the Department:</strong></p>\n<p>To be a dynamic centre for English Studies that nurtures literary competence, critical and creative thinking, effective communication, translation skills, cultural awareness and lifelong learning, enabling learners to engage meaningfully with diverse texts, languages, cultures and contemporary modes of communication.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p>The Department of English strives to:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Develop strong foundations in English literature including prose, fiction and translation through a progressive and learner-centered curriculum.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Foster critical, analytical and creative thinking through close reading, interpretation, analysis and engagement with literary, non-literary and translated texts.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Develop effective communication skills in listening, speaking, reading, writing, viewing and presentation across academic, professional and social contexts.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Develop practical translation competence by introducing learners to translation processes, theories, approaches, strategies, linguistic skills and varied translation contexts.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Cultivate independent learning, intellectual curiosity and lifelong engagement with reading, language, literature, translation and knowledge.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Prepare learners for higher education, professional life and responsible social participation by developing transferable, communication, analytical and creative skills.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Program Outcomes (POs) details: </strong>Developed by the faculty of BA using Graduate attributes (GAS)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;PO1 Disciplinary Knowledge: Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</p>\n<p>PO2 Communication Skills: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n<p>PO3 Critical Thinking: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</p>\n<p>PO4 Research Skills: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social; national and global community level issues.</p>\n<p>PO5 Analytical Reasoning: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n<p>PO6 Scientific Reasoning: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n<p>PO7 Moral and Ethical awareness: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n<p>PO8 Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership.</p>\n<p>PO9 Lifelong Learning: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSO):</strong> Developed by the Department of English</p>\n<p><br />PSO1 Demonstrate foundational knowledge of English language, literature, literary genres, prose and fiction, and translation studies.</p>\n<p>PSO2 Interpret, appreciate and critically analyse literary and non-literary texts through close reading and from diverse perspectives, with attention to form, language, context, values and meaning.</p>\n<p>PSO3 Demonstrate effective listening, speaking, reading, writing, viewing and presentation skills for academic, professional and social communication.</p>\n<p>PSO4 Apply critical, analytical and creative thinking to interpret texts, examine ideas, formulate reasoned responses and engage with language, literature and translation.</p>\n<p>PSO5 Demonstrate an understanding of translation processes, theories, types and strategies and apply appropriate linguistic and contextual skills to translate texts for different purposes and audiences.</p>\n<p>PSO6 Engage sensitively with diverse linguistic, literary, historical and cultural perspectives and recognize the relationship between language, literature, translation and society.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEO):</strong> Developed by the Department of English</p>\n<p><br />PEO1 Literary, Linguistic and Translation Application<br />Graduates will apply their literary, linguistic, analytical and translation skills to interpret texts, communicate ideas and address language-related tasks in diverse contexts.</p>\n<p>PEO2 Communication and Professional Competence<br />Graduates will demonstrate effective oral, written and digital communication, along with critical and creative thinking, in academic, professional and social contexts.</p>\n<p>PEO3 Cultural and Social Awareness<br />Graduates will engage responsibly with diverse linguistic, literary and cultural perspectives and demonstrate sensitivity to the relationship between language, literature, translation and society.</p>\n<p>PEO4 Career and Professional Development<br />Graduates will pursue diverse career opportunities in translation, editing, publishing, content writing, media, communication, language services and other literary and language-based professions.</p>\n<p>PEO5 Creative and Critical Thinking<br />Graduates will employ critical, analytical and creative thinking skills to interpret literary and non-literary texts, develop original ideas and address complex language and communication tasks.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) : </strong></h4>\n<h4>CO1 &nbsp; &nbsp;Explain the characteristics and forms of short story, prose, fiction, essay and non-fiction.</h4>\n<h4>CO2 &nbsp; &nbsp;Sketch the characters/features for the given literary text.</h4>\n<h4>CO3 &nbsp; &nbsp;Analyse selected prose and fictional texts through close reading with reference to their language, form, style, themes and context.</h4>\n<h4>CO4 &nbsp; &nbsp;Present an argument for the <span style=\"color: #000000;\">human</span> experiences, values and universal concerns in selected literary texts.</h4>\n<h4>CO5 &nbsp; &nbsp;Evaluate the human values, social concerns and universal truths reflected in selected literary works.<strong><br /></strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 257, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9755, 203, 22, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Vision of Department : </strong></h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">The department envisions fostering a research-oriented, analytical, and environmentally conscious academic environment. It aims to shape students into efficient, empathetic, and socially responsible individuals who possess the critical thinking skills to address the complex relationship between human activities and the natural environment in a spatio-temporal context.</h4>\n<hr />\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Mission of Department : </strong></h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">To empower students through academic excellence, ethical grounding, and holistic field-based learning in geography. We integrate contemporary spatial technologies like GIS and Remote Sensing with environmental sensitization to foster critical thinking, sustainable resource management, and real-world problem-solving.</h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 180px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PO</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PO Statements</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge:</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behavior and social life.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Communication Skills: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Research Skills: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social, national and global community level issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence- based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO7</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical awareness: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO8</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.90508%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>PO9</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.3223%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning: </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 198px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PSO</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PSO Statements</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PSO1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; text-align: justify; height: 36px; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Demonstrate comprehensive knowledge of physical, human, economic, regional and environmental geography and explain spatial patterns and geographical processes at local, regional, national and global scales.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PSO2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Apply geographical concepts, theories, maps, spatial data and geospatial techniques to interpret locations, distributions, patterns, relationships and regional variations.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PSO3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Analyse geographical phenomena using critical, scientific and analytical reasoning to understand interactions among physical environment, resources, population and economic activities.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PSO4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Conduct geographical inquiry through fieldwork, observation, data collection, mapping, interpretation and basic research methods to investigate spatial and environmental issues.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PSO5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 18px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Evaluate environmental, resource, developmental and socio-spatial challenges and propose sustainable, ethical and regionally appropriate geographical solutions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PSO6</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 18px; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">&nbsp;Develop practical and professional competencies in data science, cartography, thematic mapping, geospatial communication, teamwork and independent learning for higher education, research, employment and public services.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 180px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PEO</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PEO Statements</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PEO1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify;\">Graduates have a strong multidisciplinary academic foundation of various social, economic, political, environmental issues.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PEO2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify;\">Graduates integrate theory and scientific research through deliberations on practical applications of concepts.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PEO3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify;\">Graduates have a sharpened ability to converse critically and innovatively about real life issues.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\"><strong>PEO4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 36px; text-align: justify;\">Graduates are able to demonstrate skill sets as per industry requirements in respective fields.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.68434%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>PEO5</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.5431%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Graduates are able to synthesize aesthetic, social and cultural domains of knowledge.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>CO Summary:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; text-align: center;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; text-align: center;\">Download</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; text-align: center;\">FYBA (NEP 1.1)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; text-align: center;\"><a title=\"Course Outcomes\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QATJEEOeiJPNVJxkIk0zA9qhERNDjxX_/view?usp=drive_link\">Course Outcomes</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 260, '2026-10-15', 0),
(9756, 203, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<h3><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To be a centre of excellence in philosophical education that nurtures critical thinking, ethical leadership, and reflective inquiry by integrating Indian and Western philosophical traditions with contemporary knowledge, interdisciplinary learning, and social responsibility for the holistic development of individuals and society.</p>\n<hr />\n<h3><strong>Mission of Department :&nbsp;<br /></strong></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">1. To provide a strong foundation in Indian and Western philosophical traditions, major branches of philosophy, and diverse philosophical methods through quality teaching and experiential learning.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">2. To cultivate logical reasoning, critical thinking, ethical awareness, and reflective inquiry for informed decision-making in academic, professional, and social life.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">3. To promote interdisciplinary learning, research, community engagement, internships, and field-based applications of philosophy in areas such as management, human resources, media, film, counselling, public administration, and emerging technologies.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">4. To nurture responsible, socially conscious, and lifelong learners who demonstrate leadership, effective communication, professional ethics, and commitment to democratic and constitutional values.</p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>P</strong>rogram Outcomes (PO) :</h3>\n<table style=\"width: 92.4391%; height: 899px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 78.6118%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"472\">\n<h3>Program Name: Bachelor of Arts</h3>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 21.2521%; height: 50px;\" width=\"129\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 99.8639%; height: 28px;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 50px;\" width=\"53\">\n<h3>PO</h3>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<h3>PO statements</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 106px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 106px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 106px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Disciplinary Knowledge: Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Communication Skills: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Critical Thinking: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Research Skills: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social; national and global community level issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 106px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 106px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO5</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 106px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Analytical Reasoning: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO6</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Scientific Reasoning: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO7</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Moral and Ethical awareness: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO8</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO9</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Lifelong Learning: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"468\">\n<h3>Program Name: BA in Philosophy</h3>\n</td>\n<td width=\"133\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<h4>PSO</h4>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<h4>PSO statements</h4>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of Indian and Western philosophical traditions, major branches of philosophy and diverse philosophical methods to interpret philosophical ideas and contemporary issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apply logical reasoning, critical thinking and ethical frameworks to analyse philosophical arguments, evaluate diverse viewpoints and make reasoned judgments in personal, professional and social contexts.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Employ philosophical inquiry, research methods and interdisciplinary perspectives to investigate contemporary issues through field projects, community engagement, internships and applications in areas such as management, human resources, media, film, counselling and public administration.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Demonstrate ethical leadership, effective communication, teamwork, social responsibility and reflective practice while contributing responsibly to organisations, communities and lifelong professional development.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"461\">\n<h3>Program Name: BA in Philosophy</h3>\n</td>\n<td width=\"140\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<h3>PEO</h3>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<h3>PEO statements</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pursue postgraduate education, doctoral research, academic careers, and teaching professions in Philosophy and related disciplines.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Serve in civil services, public administration, education, governance, and public-service organisations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Work in management, human resources, counselling, media, communication, content development, social organisations, and corporate sectors.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Engage in interdisciplinary and emerging career fields such as ethics and technology, policy research, cultural organisations, social research, and related professional domains.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Moral Philosophy&nbsp; (Credits: 4)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: I&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA1PHIMJ0124 / GBA1PHIMJ0224</h4>\n<table style=\"width: 750px;\" width=\"841\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Explain the fundamental concepts, approaches, and ethical traditions of Indian, Western, and contemporary moral philosophy.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Apply ethical concepts and theories to interpret moral dilemmas, human conduct, and contemporary ethical issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Analyze classical and contemporary philosophies and ethical theories in individual, social, and technological contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Evaluate philosophical approaches and ethical arguments to make reasoned judgments on issues of human values, social responsibility, and Artificial Intelligence and other contemporary issues.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SYLLABUS: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JFYoJNfgeRS0UYdA8xxeNSotH3TZ6yRY/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JFYoJNfgeRS0UYdA8xxeNSotH3TZ6yRY/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Professional Ethics&nbsp; (Credits: 4)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: II&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA2PHIMJ0124 / GBA2PHIMJ0224<br /><br /></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 754px;\" width=\"850\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Explain the concepts, principles, and significance of professional ethics, ethical decision-making, and ethical practices across diverse professions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Apply ethical principles, professional standards, and codes of conduct to address ethical issues in human resource management and other professional contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Analyze ethical challenges and professional responsibilities in business, administration, law, media, medicine, engineering, and information technology.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Evaluate professional practices and emerging ethical issues to make responsible, value-based, and socially accountable decisions in professional and technological environments.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SYLLABUS: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CX_AEsokFlgdg6nKvPO3Y1jsoBSefXrJ/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CX_AEsokFlgdg6nKvPO3Y1jsoBSefXrJ/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Foundation of Film Philosophy- (VSC) (Credits: 2)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: II&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA1PHIVSC124 / GBA2PHIVSC124</h4>\n<table style=\"width: 786px;\" width=\"907\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<h4>CO</h4>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<h4>CO Statements</h4>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Explain the historical development of cinema, film genres, cinematic styles, and the emergence of Philosophy of Film as a discipline, along with the evolution of cinema and its major forms and platforms</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Apply philosophical concepts and methods to interpret film scripts, characters, narratives, cinematic perspectives, and films in relation to philosophical and cultural contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Analyze films through critical, ethical, and interdisciplinary perspectives by examining film criticism, review writing, journalism, filmmaking practices, censorship, and contemporary cinematic practices including the transition from theatres to OTT platforms.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>SYLLABUS: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TfqPa3I-pBeDK9UuV4jEnsjCr3X6YLVA/view?usp=sharing\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TfqPa3I-pBeDK9UuV4jEnsjCr3X6YLVA/view?usp=sharing</a></p>\n<hr />', '<h3><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To be a centre of excellence in philosophical education that nurtures critical thinking, ethical leadership, and reflective inquiry by integrating Indian and Western philosophical traditions with contemporary knowledge, interdisciplinary learning, and social responsibility for the holistic development of individuals and society.</p>\n<hr />\n<h3><strong>Mission of Department :&nbsp;<br /></strong></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">1. To provide a strong foundation in Indian and Western philosophical traditions, major branches of philosophy, and diverse philosophical methods through quality teaching and experiential learning.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">2. To cultivate logical reasoning, critical thinking, ethical awareness, and reflective inquiry for informed decision-making in academic, professional, and social life.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">3. To promote interdisciplinary learning, research, community engagement, internships, and field-based applications of philosophy in areas such as management, human resources, media, film, counselling, public administration, and emerging technologies.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">4. To nurture responsible, socially conscious, and lifelong learners who demonstrate leadership, effective communication, professional ethics, and commitment to democratic and constitutional values.</p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>P</strong>rogram Outcomes (PO) :</h3>\n<table style=\"width: 92.4391%; height: 899px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 78.6118%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"472\">\n<h3>Program Name: Bachelor of Arts</h3>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 21.2521%; height: 50px;\" width=\"129\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 99.8639%; height: 28px;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 50px;\" width=\"53\">\n<h3>PO</h3>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<h3>PO statements</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 106px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 106px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 106px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Disciplinary Knowledge: Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Communication Skills: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Critical Thinking: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Research Skills: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social; national and global community level issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 106px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 106px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO5</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 106px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Analytical Reasoning: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO6</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Scientific Reasoning: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO7</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Moral and Ethical awareness: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 88px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO8</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 88px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.2257%; height: 69px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p>PO9</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.6382%; height: 69px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Lifelong Learning: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"468\">\n<h3>Program Name: BA in Philosophy</h3>\n</td>\n<td width=\"133\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<h4>PSO</h4>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<h4>PSO statements</h4>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of Indian and Western philosophical traditions, major branches of philosophy and diverse philosophical methods to interpret philosophical ideas and contemporary issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apply logical reasoning, critical thinking and ethical frameworks to analyse philosophical arguments, evaluate diverse viewpoints and make reasoned judgments in personal, professional and social contexts.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Employ philosophical inquiry, research methods and interdisciplinary perspectives to investigate contemporary issues through field projects, community engagement, internships and applications in areas such as management, human resources, media, film, counselling and public administration.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>PSO4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Demonstrate ethical leadership, effective communication, teamwork, social responsibility and reflective practice while contributing responsibly to organisations, communities and lifelong professional development.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"461\">\n<h3>Program Name: BA in Philosophy</h3>\n</td>\n<td width=\"140\">\n<h3>Degree: <u>UG</u></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<h3>PEO</h3>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<h3>PEO statements</h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pursue postgraduate education, doctoral research, academic careers, and teaching professions in Philosophy and related disciplines.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Serve in civil services, public administration, education, governance, and public-service organisations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Work in management, human resources, counselling, media, communication, content development, social organisations, and corporate sectors.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p>PEO4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Engage in interdisciplinary and emerging career fields such as ethics and technology, policy research, cultural organisations, social research, and related professional domains.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Moral Philosophy&nbsp; (Credits: 4)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: I&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA1PHIMJ0124 / GBA1PHIMJ0224</h4>\n<table style=\"width: 750px;\" width=\"841\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Explain the fundamental concepts, approaches, and ethical traditions of Indian, Western, and contemporary moral philosophy.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Apply ethical concepts and theories to interpret moral dilemmas, human conduct, and contemporary ethical issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Analyze classical and contemporary philosophies and ethical theories in individual, social, and technological contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8854px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 693.115px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Evaluate philosophical approaches and ethical arguments to make reasoned judgments on issues of human values, social responsibility, and Artificial Intelligence and other contemporary issues.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Professional Ethics&nbsp; (Credits: 4)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: II&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA2PHIMJ0124 / GBA2PHIMJ0224<br /><br /></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 754px;\" width=\"850\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Explain the concepts, principles, and significance of professional ethics, ethical decision-making, and ethical practices across diverse professions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Apply ethical principles, professional standards, and codes of conduct to address ethical issues in human resource management and other professional contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Analyze ethical challenges and professional responsibilities in business, administration, law, media, medicine, engineering, and information technology.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 87.5px;\" width=\"66\">\n<p>CO4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 659.5px;\" width=\"350\">\n<p>Evaluate professional practices and emerging ethical issues to make responsible, value-based, and socially accountable decisions in professional and technological environments.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Course Title: Foundation of Film Philosophy- (VSC) (Credits: 2)</h4>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Semester: II&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Course Code : GBA1PHIVSC124 / GBA2PHIVSC124</h4>\n<table style=\"width: 786px;\" width=\"907\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<h4>CO</h4>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<h4>CO Statements</h4>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Explain the historical development of cinema, film genres, cinematic styles, and the emergence of Philosophy of Film as a discipline, along with the evolution of cinema and its major forms and platforms</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Apply philosophical concepts and methods to interpret film scripts, characters, narratives, cinematic perspectives, and films in relation to philosophical and cultural contexts.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 43.5px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p>CO3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 735.5px;\" width=\"369\">\n<p>Analyze films through critical, ethical, and interdisciplinary perspectives by examining film criticism, review writing, journalism, filmmaking practices, censorship, and contemporary cinematic practices including the transition from theatres to OTT platforms.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 0, '', 262, '2026-10-21', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9757, 203, 27, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p>To be a centre of excellence in undergraduate political science education that nurtures critically aware, ethically grounded, and socially responsible citizens, who advance democratic values, informed public discourse, and just governance in India and the world.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p>The Department of Political Science is committed to providing a rigorous contemporary undergraduate education that equips students with deep conceptual understanding, analytical skills, and practical insights into politics, governance, and public affairs.</p>\n<p><strong>We strive to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Foster intellectual curiosity and critical engagement with political ideas, institutions, processes, and power relations at local, national, and global levels.</li>\n<li>Develop research aptitude, effective communication, and problem-solving abilities through innovative pedagogy, experiential learning, and curriculum autonomy.</li>\n<li>Prepare students for meaningful careers in public service, civil services, law, media, policy research, academia, civil society, and related fields.</li>\n<li>Promote democratic citizenship, ethical leadership, social justice, and inclusive public participation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Through these efforts, the department aspires to contribute to the creation of informed, reflective, and engaged individuals who strengthen democratic institutions and public life.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 92.4515%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 89.677%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"464\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: </strong>BA in Political Science</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 10.2622%;\" width=\"137\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge: </strong>Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Communication Skills</strong>: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking</strong>: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Research Skills</strong>: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social; national and global community level issues</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong>: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong>: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical awareness</strong>: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Social Interactive Skills</strong>, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 4.45693%;\" width=\"56\">\n<p><strong>PO9</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 95.4822%;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning</strong>: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"468\">\n<p><strong>Program Name:</strong> BA in Political Science</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"133\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Students will be able to demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of major political theories, ideologies, institutions, and processes at the local, national, and international levels.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Students will be able to critically analyse political issues, policies, and power structures using appropriate theoretical frameworks and empirical evidence.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Students will be able to apply research methods and analytical skills to examine contemporary political problems and communicate findings effectively in both written and oral forms.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Students will be able to evaluate the role of citizenship, governance, and democratic values in society and engage thoughtfully with issues of rights, justice, and public policy.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4><strong>&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"461\">\n<p><strong>Program Name:</strong> BA in Political Science</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"140\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Graduates will uphold excellence in higher education preparing them for successful careers in academia and research.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Graduates will develop strong analytical, research, and critical-thinking skills to evaluate political phenomena, preparing them for successful careers in Law, public policy arena.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Graduates will be able to communicate political ideas effectively&mdash;both orally and in writing, preparing them for successful careers in public discourse, Media and Journalism.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Graduates will uphold ethical values, civic responsibility, and a commitment to social justice, preparing them for successful careers in competitive examinations, non-governmental organisations, and public administration, International Relationsor for further higher studies.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p>Understand an evolution of the Indian Constitution, decode values enshrined in Preamble and explain the features of the Indian Constitution</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K2</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,3,7,9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p>Explain fundamental rights and importance of directive principles of state policy</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3/K4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,3, 5, 6, 7,9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p>Assess the functions and interrelationships between political institutions and structures.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3/K4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1, 3, 4, 5,6,7,8, 9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1.2.3.4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p>Critical analysis of political structures</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K4/K5</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>25</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"340\">\n<p>Orientation for civil services and other government examinations.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"38\">\n<p>05</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,2, 9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p>Course Title: Introduction to Psephology</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p>Course Code: GB1POLVSC124</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p>Academic Year: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"227\">\n<p>No. of total contact Hours: 45</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"148\">\n<p>Course credits:02</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p>Class: FYBA</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"227\">\n<p>Semester: I/ II</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"148\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Assess basic tools and techniques of Psephology</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Demonstrate basic skills of election analyst, political surveyor</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,2, 8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>3</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Analyse electoral data, voting patterns, and public opinion trends using basic statistical and interpretive methods to identify factors influencing voter behaviour and election outcomes.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K5</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"38\">\n<p>25</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"19\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 264, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9758, 203, 28, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9759, 203, 29, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To be a centre of excellence in Sanskrit education by nurturing academically proficient, ethically grounded, research-oriented, and socially responsible individuals through the preservation and promotion of Sanskrit language, literature, and Indian Knowledge Systems, while fostering critical thinking, environmental consciousness, and lifelong learning.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Mission 1:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Provide quality education in Sanskrit language, literature, and Indian Knowledge Systems to achieve academic excellence and intellectual growth.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Mission 2:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Develop critical thinking, communication, research, and problem-solving skills through interdisciplinary learning.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Mission 3:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Preserve and promote India\'s linguistic, literary, philosophical, and cultural heritage while nurturing national values and social commitment.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Mission 4:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Inculcate ethical values, independent thinking, leadership, and social responsibility for responsible citizenship.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Mission 5:</strong><strong><br /></strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Promote holistic development, lifelong learning, environmental awareness, sustainable living, and active participation in curricular, co-curricular, extension, and community engagement activities.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 12.2146%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B.A.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 90.28%;\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">UG</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 102.495%;\" colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Communication Skills: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Research Skills: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social, national and global community level issues.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Logical Reasoning: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical awareness: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos and ethical and constitutional principles.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Leadership readiness / qualities: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Develop leadership, teamwork and social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement and social work.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability, and good citizenship, preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 11.4123%;\">\n<p><strong>PO9</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.0823%;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Sustainable Living: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Develop sensitivity towards the environment and evaluate the use of the environment and natural resources ethically proposing lifelong sustainable living.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B.A.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">UG</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Understanding of the cultural, philosophical, and literary heritage reflected in Sanskrit literature.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Proficiency in Sanskrit grammar for the translation and interpretation of classical Sanskrit texts.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Critical understanding of Sanskrit texts in relation to contemporary social and ethical issues.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Knowledge of basic research methods in Sanskrit studies and competence in original Sanskrit composition based on the principles of Sanskrit language and literature.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B.A.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Knowledge and professional competence in Sanskrit for careers in academia, education, research, translation, and interpretation.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Communication, writing, and analytical skills for opportunities in media, publishing, content development, scriptwriting, and digital platforms.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Application of Sanskrit knowledge and Indian cultural heritage in government services, tourism, cultural promotion, and related professional domains.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Foundational understanding of Sanskrit-based traditional knowledge systems, including Ayurveda and traditional medicine, with readiness for higher education, research, and lifelong professional development.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>CO Summary for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 36px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7483%; height: 18px;\"><strong>Class</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7483%; height: 18px;\"><strong>Download</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7483%; height: 18px;\">FYBA (NEP 1.1)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7483%; height: 18px;\"><a title=\"FYBA (NEP 1.1) COs\" href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Department-of-Sanskrit---COs-26-27.pdf\">https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/Department-of-Sanskrit---COs-26-27.pdf</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 266, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9760, 203, 30, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<p><strong>Vision of Department : </strong></p>\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">Vision of the Department for UG</h5>\n<h5 style=\"text-align: left;\">The Department of Sociology strives for academic and research excellence while fostering social responsibility, critical thinking, and community engagement. It aims to empower students with sociological knowledge, leadership, and democratic values to address contemporary social challenges and contribute to an inclusive, equitable, and sustainable society.</h5>\n<hr />\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mission of Department : &nbsp;</strong>Mission of the Department for UG</li>\n<li>● To provide quality education in Sociology by integrating theoretical knowledge with<br />experiential learning, fieldwork, and research.<br />● To develop critical thinking, scientific temper, analytical skills, and ethical values for<br />understanding complex social realities.<br />● To promote research, innovation, community outreach, and interdisciplinary collaboration<br />in addressing local, national, and global social issues.<br />● To inculcate constitutional values, social justice, gender sensitivity, environmental<br />responsibility, and respect for diversity through teaching and extension activities.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PO for UG:</strong></p>\n<table width=\"640\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p><strong>PO No.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p><strong>PO Statement</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Disciplinary Knowledge: Demonstrate an understanding of social, political, economic, cultural, historical and geographical aspects of society and appreciate diverse civilizations and cultures by considering individual and collective human perspectives that influence individual behaviour and social life.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO2</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Communication Skills: Communicate effectively using appropriate language and style, present ideas clearly in academic, creative, and professional contexts; and engage with diverse audiences through oral, written, and digital modes of expression.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO3</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Critical Thinking: Possess intellectual inquiry and innovation enabling analysis and synthesis of social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues from multiple perspectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Research Skills: Develop interdisciplinary learning and research to address various social, national and global community level issues.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO5</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Analytical Reasoning: Apply empirical knowledge and develop scientific temperament to address social, political, economic, historical, geographical issues. Compare, classify, and analyze multiple perspectives, recognize underlying assumptions, and interpret data or arguments using logical reasoning.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO6</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Scientific Reasoning: Demonstrate scientific reasoning by applying logical, evidence-based, and systematic methods of inquiry to analyse complex human phenomena, texts, cultural practices, and socio-historical processes</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Moral and Ethical awareness: Demonstrate sensitivity towards issues of national security, social justice, human rights, gender equality, diversity and inclusion, and make informed judgments grounded in democratic ethos, ethical, constitutional principles and good citizenship.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Social Interactive Skills, team work and Leadership qualities: Stimulate constructive social Interactions, inculcate social responsibility through fieldwork, community engagement, social work and develop leadership.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"89\">\n<p>PO9</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"471\">\n<p>Lifelong Learning: Cultivate attitudes of lifelong learning, adaptability and preparing for higher studies, employment, public service, and on larger scale social engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) : &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table dir=\"ltr\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-baot=\"1\"><colgroup><col width=\"102\" /><col width=\"319\" /></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>PSO1</td>\n<td>Apply Sociological Knowledge: Graduates will apply comprehensive sociological knowledge, theories, concepts, and perspectives to critically understand and address contemporary social issues at local, national, and global levels.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PSO2</td>\n<td>Research, Analytical and Professional Competence: Graduates will demonstrate research, fieldwork, analytical, communication, digital, and professional skills to pursue higher education, research, public service, and careers in social development and related sectors.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PSO3</td>\n<td>Social Responsibility and Ethical Leadership: Graduates will demonstrate ethical leadership and commitment to social justice, gender equality, human rights, constitutional values, democratic principles, diversity, and sustainable development through responsible citizenship and community engagement.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PSO4</td>\n<td>Lifelong Learning and Social Transformation: Graduates will pursue lifelong learning, innovation, and continuous professional development while contributing to inclusive communities, social harmony, nation-building, and positive social transformation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PEOs for UG</strong></p>\n<table width=\"655\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"97\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"466\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"97\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"466\">\n<p>Apply Sociological Knowledge: Graduates will apply comprehensive sociological knowledge, theories, concepts, and perspectives to critically understand and address contemporary social issues at local, national, and global levels.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"97\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"466\">\n<p>Research, Analytical and Professional Competence: Graduates will demonstrate research, fieldwork, analytical, communication, digital, and professional skills to pursue higher education, research, public service, and careers in social development and related sectors.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"97\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"466\">\n<p>Social Responsibility and Ethical Leadership: Graduates will demonstrate ethical leadership and commitment to social justice, gender equality, human rights, constitutional values, democratic principles, diversity, and sustainable development through responsible citizenship and community engagement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"97\">\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"466\">\n<p>Lifelong Learning and Social Transformation: Graduates will pursue lifelong learning, innovation, and continuous professional development while contributing to inclusive communities, social harmony, nation-building, and positive social transformation.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 36px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7603%; height: 18px;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7603%; height: 18px;\">Download</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7603%; height: 18px;\">FYBA (NEP 1.1)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7603%; height: 18px;\"><a title=\"Course Outcome\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12TlNK7nekKzkgSKFJIDbYyf3ejA62jIY/edit\">Click Here</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 384, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9761, 203, 31, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9762, 203, 32, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;<br /></strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To educate and train the student to be efficient, empathetic and socially responsible individuals and foster a research-oriented academic environment through applying an issue-based problem-solving method for both students and teachers.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :<br /></strong></h4>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.5;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To facilitate pursuit of academic excellence.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.5;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To harness students\' potential for extra-curricular and co-curricular activities.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.5;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To foster in students a commitment towards society and nation.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.5;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To sensitize students towards environmental issues.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"734\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"660\">\n<p>Academic Batch: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"74\">\n<p>Program:&nbsp;<br />B.Com</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>PO No.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p>PO Statement</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"74\">\n<p>Target % Students</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO1: Disciplinary Knowledge</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>65%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Apply</strong> integrated knowledge of Business Management, Production Management, Financial Management, Marketing, Human Resource Management, Marketing Research, Tourism Management, Business Economics, Financial Accounting, Cost Accounting, Management Accounting, Auditing, Financial Reporting, Taxation, Business Law, Accounting Software, IKS in Commerce &amp; Accountancy and related disciplines to address organizational challenges within the legal and regulatory environment.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO2: Communication skills</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>65%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Analyze </strong>- Communication skills including ability to express ideas, thoughts, and information clearly, effectively, and appropriately through verbal, non-verbal, written, and digital communication, which improves speaking, listening and work place messaging.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO3: Critical Thinking</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>60%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Analyze and evaluate</strong> business situations using critical thinking to identify issues, assess alternatives, and develop innovative, sustainable, and evidence-based solutions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO4: Problem Solving</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>65%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Identify, analyze, and formulate</strong> effective solutions to business and financial accounting problems by applying systematic, logical, and research-oriented problem-solving approaches and use of technology.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>5</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO5: Analytical Reasoning</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>50%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Apply</strong> analytical and quantitative reasoning skills to interpret business data, evaluate, analyze and interpret financial reports, conduct research, and draw meaningful conclusions for informed managerial decision-making.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>6</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO6: Cooperation and Teamwork</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>50%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Demonstrate</strong> effective teamwork and interpersonal skills by collaborating with diverse groups, managing tasks responsibly, and guiding teams with integrity, accountability, and social responsibility to achieve organizational goals.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO7: Scientific reasoning</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>60%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Ability </strong>to apply, analyze, and evaluate financial statements using logical and evidence-based thinking to make informed business decisions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO8: Information and Digital Literacy</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>60%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Utilize and evaluate</strong> digital technologies, accounting software, information systems, and emerging information technology tools to access, manage, analyze, and communicate information effectively while ensuring ethical, secure, and responsible practices in a digital business environment.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"42\">\n<p>9</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO9: Moral and Ethical Awareness</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"74\">\n<p>65%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>Evaluate</strong> ethical issues and <strong>apply</strong> professional values, legal principles, and moral reasoning to make responsible, fair, and ethical decisions in academic, professional, and business environments.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>10</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p><strong>PO10: Leadership</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"74\">\n<p>60%</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"42\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"618\">\n<p>Demonstrate leadership by applying concepts of Management, Business Ethics and Corporate Governance, Human Resource Management, Business communication and Accountancy to solve business problems, lead teams ethically, and achieve organizational goals.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 74px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"74\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :<br /></strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"671\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>Academic&nbsp;&nbsp; Batch:</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>Program:</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">\n<p>BCom</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>PSO No.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>PSO Statement</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>Target % Students</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">\n<p>Note</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>Apply the principles of financial accounting, cost accounting, taxation, and auditing to analyze organizational financial problems and recommend appropriate solutions.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>70</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">\n<p>More than 55% of Accountancy students during their graduation will be able achieve PSO1.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>Analyze and evaluate financial statements using analytical and critical thinking skills to support effective financial planning and strategic decision-making.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>60</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>Apply and integrate modern accounting software and information technology like tally to manage financial records, analyze financial data, and enhance organizational efficiency in a digital business environment.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>55</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"89\">\n<p>4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\" width=\"358\">\n<p>Evaluate financial statements through systematic auditing procedures by demonstrating ethical responsibility, professional judgment, and compliance with accounting standards.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"80\">\n<p>55</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"144\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4><strong>&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :<br /></strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 623px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"623\">\n<p><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs)</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 623px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"623\">\n<p>Program: B.Com. (Accountancy)</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 623px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"623\">\n<p>Academic Batch: 2026&ndash;27</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 623px; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"623\">\n<p>Department: Accountancy</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4><strong>&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"75\">\n<p>PEO No.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Program Educational Objective</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"75\">\n<p>PEO 1</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify;\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Pursue higher education and advanced studies</strong> in Accountancy, Commerce, and allied professional fields (such as CA, CMA, CS, or M. Com), contributing to financial research and knowledge advancement.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"75\">\n<p>PEO 2</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify;\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Build entrepreneurial ventures</strong> in financial consulting, tax advisory, business management, and commerce-based enterprises.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"75\">\n<p>PEO 3</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify;\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Establish careers in accounting and finance</strong>, including roles in corporate accounting, banking, taxation, auditing firms, and financial institutions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: center;\" width=\"75\">\n<p>PEO 4</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify;\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Develop professional careers in financial reporting and auditing services</strong> by applying their knowledge and practical skills in accounting standards, taxation laws, and regulatory compliance.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /></strong></h4>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER I &ndash; Accountancy &amp; Financial Management &ndash; I&nbsp;<br /></strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the concepts and conventions of accounting, Capital and Revenue&nbsp; Expenditure and Receipts, AS, Ind-AS and IFRS, Accounting Standards,&nbsp; Inventory Valuation, Final Accounts, Departmental Accounts and Accounting in&nbsp; a Computerized Environment.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply appropriate accounting principles and procedures to determine inventory&nbsp; valuation under FIFO and Weighted Average Method, prepare Final Accounts of&nbsp; Manufacturing Concerns, allocate departmental expenses and incomes, and&nbsp; record accounting transactions in computerized accounting software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse accounting transactions, adjustments, inventory valuation methods,&nbsp; inter-departmental transfers, stock reserves and accounting data to determine&nbsp; their appropriate treatment in financial statements and accounting records.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting policies, inventory valuation methods, revenue recognition,&nbsp; allocation of expenses and incomes, inter-departmental transfers and&nbsp; accounting information for appropriate treatment, accuracy and consistency.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare inventory valuation statements, Final Accounts of Manufacturing&nbsp; Concerns, Departmental Trading and Profit &amp; Loss Accounts, General Profit &amp;&nbsp; Loss Account and Balance Sheet, and generate accounting reports using&nbsp; computerized accounting software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER II &ndash; Accountancy &amp; Financial Management &ndash; II<br /></strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the concepts, principles and accounting procedures relating to&nbsp; Incomplete Records, Redemption of Preference Shares and Debentures,&nbsp; Branch Accounts and Hire Purchase.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply appropriate accounting principles and procedures to prepare Final&nbsp; Accounts under the Conversion Method, account for redemption of preference&nbsp; shares and debentures, prepare branch accounts and record hire purchase&nbsp; transactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse incomplete accounting records, redemption transactions, branch&nbsp; transactions and hire purchase transactions to determine the appropriate&nbsp; accounting treatment and financial impact.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting procedures and treatments relating to incomplete records,&nbsp; redemption of preference shares and debentures, branch accounting and hire&nbsp; purchase for accuracy and appropriate presentation in accounting records.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare Final Accounts under the Conversion Method, accounting entries,&nbsp; ledger accounts and Balance Sheet relating to redemption of debentures,&nbsp; branch accounts, and journal and ledger accounts in the books of Hire Vendor&nbsp; and Hire Purchaser.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER I &ndash; Accounting in Commerce<br /></strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the concepts, benefits and procedures for issue of Accounting&nbsp; Standards, AS-1 Disclosure of Accounting Policies, AS-2 Valuation of&nbsp; Inventories, inventory valuation, Final Accounts and Accounting in a&nbsp; Computerised Environment.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply accounting principles and procedures to classify capital and revenue&nbsp; expenditure and receipts, determine inventory valuation using FIFO, prepare&nbsp; Final Accounts of Manufacturing Concerns and record Sales, Purchase,&nbsp; Receipt, Payment and other vouchers using accounting software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse accounting policies, inventory systems, inventory valuation, capital and&nbsp; revenue items, adjustments and closing entries to determine their appropriate&nbsp; treatment in accounting records and financial statements.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting policies, inventory valuation methods, accounting&nbsp; adjustments and financial information for accuracy, consistency and appropriate&nbsp; financial reporting.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare inventory valuation statements, Final Accounts of Manufacturing&nbsp; Concerns and generate Trial Balance, Profit &amp; Loss Account and Balance Sheet&nbsp; using appropriate accounting procedures and accounting software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER II &ndash; Accounting in Commerce<br /></strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the concepts, principles and accounting procedures relating to&nbsp; Accounting from Incomplete Records, Branch Accounts, Hire Purchase and&nbsp; Instalment Sales Transactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply accounting principles and procedures to prepare Final Accounts of a&nbsp; Proprietary Trading Concern under the Conversion Method, prepare accounts of&nbsp; dependent branches and account for Hire Purchase transactions under the&nbsp; Asset Purchase Method based on Full Cash Price.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse incomplete accounting records, branch transactions under Debtors&nbsp; Method and Stock and Debtors Method, and Hire Purchase and Instalment&nbsp; Sales transactions to determine their appropriate accounting treatment.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting methods and procedures relating to incomplete records,&nbsp; dependent branch accounting, Hire Purchase and Instalment Sales for&nbsp; accuracy, suitability and appropriate presentation.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare Final Accounts under the Conversion Method, Branch Accounts using&nbsp; Debtors Method and Stock and Debtors Method, and accounting records under&nbsp; the Asset Purchase Method for Hire Purchase transactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>FYBCOM NEP (1.1) &ndash; Vocational Skill Courses&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER I &ndash; VSC&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Book Keeping and Basic Accounting&nbsp;<br /></strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the fundamentals of Double Entry Book-Keeping, subsidiary books,&nbsp; accounting documents and the basic structure of Trading Account,&nbsp; Manufacturing Account, Profit &amp; Loss Account and Balance Sheet.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply Double Entry Book-Keeping principles to record transactions in Sales&nbsp; Book, Purchases Book, Cash Book with Cash and Bank Columns and Journal&nbsp; Proper, and to prepare Ledger and Trial Balance.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse business transactions and source documents such as Sales Invoice,&nbsp; Credit Note, Debit Note, Receipt, Payment Voucher, Purchase Order and Sales&nbsp; Order to determine their appropriate accounting treatment.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting records, subsidiary books and accounting documents for&nbsp; accuracy, completeness and consistency in recording business transactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: justify; border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare Ledger, Trial Balance, Trading Account, Manufacturing Account, Profit&nbsp; &amp; Loss Account and Balance Sheet using appropriate bookkeeping and&nbsp; accounting procedures.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>SEMESTER II &ndash; VSC&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Introduction to Accounting Software&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>CO&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><strong>Course Outcome&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO1&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explain the concept, advantages and use of Accounting Software with reference&nbsp; to Tally Software, including company creation, masters, ledgers, vouchers,&nbsp; books of accounts and accounting reports.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply accounting software to create a company, masters and ledgers and&nbsp; record Sales, Purchase, Payment, Receipt, Contra, Journal, Credit Note and&nbsp; Debit Note vouchers.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO3&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyse accounting transactions to select appropriate voucher types and&nbsp; generate Subsidiary Books, Ledger and Trial Balance using manual procedures&nbsp; and Tally Software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO4&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate accounting records, adjustment and closing entries and reports&nbsp; generated through Tally Software for accuracy, completeness and consistency.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO5&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-color: #000000; border-style: solid; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prepare and generate Subsidiary Books, Ledger, Trial Balance, Profit &amp; Loss&nbsp; Account, Balance Sheet and Cash Flow Statement using appropriate accounting&nbsp; procedures and Tally Software.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h4>&nbsp;</h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 278, '2026-10-21', 0),
(9763, 203, 33, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9764, 203, 34, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9765, 203, 35, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<p><strong>Vision of the Department:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To develop competent, ethical, innovative and socially responsible management professionals equipped with the knowledge, skills and values required to excel in a dynamic and competitive business environment.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong>Mission of the Department:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To provide quality and industry-relevant management education through innovative teaching-learning practices.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To develop managerial, entrepreneurial, analytical, communication and leadership skills among students.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To encourage critical thinking, creativity, research orientation and lifelong learning.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To promote ethical values, social responsibility and professional integrity.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To facilitate industry interaction, experiential learning and career development opportunities for students.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Program Outcomes (POs) :</strong></span></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: BCOM (MANAGEMENT STUDIES)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Demonstrate comprehensive knowledge and conceptual understanding of core management disciplines including Principles of Management, Marketing, Human Resource Management, Finance, Operations, Business Analytics, Entrepreneurship, Logistics, and Strategic Management that form the foundation of the undergraduate B.Com. (Management Studies) programme.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Communication Skills: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Communicate management concepts, business strategies, and organizational information effectively through written, oral, and digital modes. Present ideas confidently, prepare professional reports, and interact effectively with diverse stakeholders in business environments.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Analyze organizational issues, evaluate business alternatives, and make informed managerial decisions using logical reasoning, evidence-based approaches, and ethical considerations in dynamic business situations.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Apply management theories, analytical tools, and decision-making techniques to identify, evaluate, and solve complex organizational and business problems across functional domains.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Identify business research problems, formulate research objectives, collect and analyze data using appropriate methodologies, and generate meaningful insights for managerial decision-making and business improvement.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Reflective Thinking:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Demonstrate self-awareness by critically evaluating managerial practices, organizational behavior, and personal leadership capabilities for continuous professional and personal improvement.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Self-Directed Learning:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Demonstrate initiative in acquiring new managerial knowledge and professional competencies independently, adapting to changing business environments through continuous learning and skill development.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Multicultural Competence:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Develop an understanding of global business environments, cross-cultural management practices, international trade, and diversity in organizations while working effectively in multicultural settings.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO9</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Uphold professional ethics, corporate governance, social responsibility, sustainability, and legal compliance while demonstrating integrity, transparency, accountability, and respect for intellectual property in business practices.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO10</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Leadership Readiness: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstrate leadership potential by planning, organizing, motivating, coordinating, and guiding teams to achieve organizational goals through strategic thinking, innovation, and effective decision-making.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSO):</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: BCOM (MANAGEMENT STUDIES)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">UG</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Management Knowledge and Functional Competence:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Apply fundamental and contemporary concepts of management across functional areas such as Marketing, Human Resource Management, Finance, Operations, Logistics, Business Analytics and Strategic Management to address business requirements effectively.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Business Research and Analytical Decision-Making:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Apply research methodologies, quantitative and analytical tools to identify business problems, interpret data, evaluate alternatives and generate evidence-based solutions for managerial decision-making.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Entrepreneurship, Innovation and Business Leadership:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Demonstrate entrepreneurial thinking, innovation, leadership and strategic capabilities to identify business opportunities, develop sustainable business solutions and contribute effectively to organizational growth.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Ethical, Sustainable and Global Business Practices:</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Apply ethical, socially responsible and sustainable management practices while demonstrating awareness of legal, cultural, technological and global business environments in professional decision-making.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEO):</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: BCOM (MANAGEMENT STUDIES)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">UG</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates establish themselves as competent management professionals by applying multidisciplinary business knowledge, managerial skills and functional expertise to effectively perform in diverse organizational and business environments.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates demonstrate critical thinking, analytical, problem-solving, entrepreneurial and leadership capabilities to make informed decisions, manage challenges, pursue business opportunities and contribute to organizational growth.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates engage in lifelong learning, research and professional development to adapt to emerging technologies, changing business practices and evolving economic, social and global environments.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates demonstrate professional integrity, ethical conduct, social responsibility and commitment to sustainability while contributing positively to organizations, communities and society.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></p>\n<p>https://docs.google.com/document/d/14yVKL0VxQTvuWhFqbqL8KmEul1MGw9nH/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=103000682144841514656&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true</p>', '', '1', 0, 0, '', 524, '2026-10-15', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9766, 203, 37, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Vision of Department</strong></span></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To be a centre of excellence in chemical education, research, and innovation, producing skilled and socially responsible citizens.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Mission of Department</strong></span></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">To provide quality education in chemical sciences through innovative teaching and experiential learning.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">To promote research, innovation, and critical thinking for scientific and professional excellence.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">To develop skilled, ethical, and socially responsible graduates committed to lifelong learning.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></span></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 154px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>POs</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Undergraduate</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Postgraduate</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">1</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 10px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge:</strong> Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena. <strong>(70%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 10px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge:</strong> Apply advanced theoretical concepts, recent developments, and interdisciplinary knowledge in the respective scientific discipline to analyse complex scientific problems. <strong>(65%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">2</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Critical Thinking: </strong>Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions. <strong>(55%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Critical Thinking and Problem Solving:</strong> Evaluate scientific literature critically and design appropriate strategies to solve complex and unfamiliar problems using logical and evidence-based approaches. <strong>(70%)</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">3</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Problem Solving: </strong>Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques. <strong>(65%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analytical Reasoning: Analyse, interpret, and validate complex experimental data using advanced analytical, mathematical, and statistical tools to draw scientifically sound conclusions. <strong>(55%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">4</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong>: Analyse and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences. <strong>(55%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research-Related Skills: </strong>Design and conduct independent research, apply appropriate methodologies, analyze results, and communicate findings through dissertations, reports, or <strong>publications.(60%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">5</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Research-Related Skills:</strong> Design and perform basic experiments, analyse data, and present findings using standard scientific methods. <strong>(45%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Cooperation / Team Work: </strong>Collaborate effectively in multidisciplinary research teams, demonstrating leadership, accountability, and professional communication skills. <strong>(60%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">6</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Cooperation / Team Work:</strong> Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives. <strong>(70%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong>: Formulate original hypotheses or models, test those using rigorous scientific methods, and justify outcomes based on empirical evidence and theory. <strong>(65%)</strong>&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">7</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Scientific Reasoning:</strong> Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations. <strong>(45%)</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Information / Digital Literacy: </strong>Use advanced digital tools, databases, computational software, and research platforms to retrieve, analyze, manage, and present scientific information ethically.(55%)&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 6.37544%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">8</span></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; height: 18px;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness/ Reasoning:</strong> Practise ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities. (70%)</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning:</strong> Apply ethical principles, biosafety norms, research integrity, and environmental responsibility in advanced scientific research and professional practice. <strong>(65%)</strong> &nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs):</strong></span></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 277px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.44607%; text-align: center; height: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>PSOs</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: center; height: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Undergraduate</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Postgraduate</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 64px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.44607%; text-align: center; height: 64px;\"><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Understand the fundamental concepts of organic, inorganic, physical, and analytical chemistry and apply them to solve basic chemical problems.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 64px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Demonstrate in-depth knowledge of organic, inorganic, physical, analytical, and interdisciplinary areas of chemistry to understand and solve advanced chemical problems.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 64px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.44607%; text-align: center; height: 64px;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Develop practical laboratory skills through performing experiments, handling instruments, and interpreting experimental results accurately and safely.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 64px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Plan and perform advanced laboratory experiments using modern analytical techniques and instruments, and interpret experimental results with accuracy.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 64px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.44607%; text-align: center; height: 64px;\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply scientific knowledge, critical thinking, and analytical skills to understand chemical processes and carry out basic research activities.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 64px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design and carry out independent research, analyze scientific data, and communicate research findings effectively through dissertations, reports, and presentations.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 64px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 5.44607%; text-align: center; height: 64px;\"><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Demonstrate ethical practices, environmental awareness, teamwork, and lifelong learning skills for higher studies and careers in chemistry and allied fields.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 64px; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply ethical practices, digital tools, and environmental awareness while working individually or in multidisciplinary teams for higher studies, research, and professional careers.</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Programme Educational Objectives (PEOs):</strong></span></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.63194%;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">PEOs</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: center; height: 21px;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Undergraduate</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; height: 21px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Postgraduate</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.63194%; text-align: center;\"><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Acquire fundamental knowledge and practical skills in chemistry to pursue further higher education, research, and career opportunities in chemistry and allied fields.</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply advanced knowledge and practical skills in chemistry to pursue successful careers in academia, research, industry, and allied fields.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.63194%; text-align: center;\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply scientific knowledge, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills to address basic scientific challenges.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Carry out independent research by applying scientific reasoning, analytical thinking, and modern research methodologies to solve complex chemical problems.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.63194%; text-align: center;\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Demonstrate ethical practices, teamwork, environmental awareness, and social responsibility in academic and professional activities.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Demonstrate professional ethics, environmental responsibility, leadership, and effective teamwork in research and professional practice.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.63194%; text-align: center;\"><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 41.8773%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Develop lifelong learning habits and adapt to emerging developments in chemical sciences through continuous skill enhancement.&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50.8922%; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Engage in lifelong learning and adapt to emerging developments in chemical sciences through continuous professional and academic growth.&nbsp;</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>Course Outcomes (COs):</strong></span></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 18pt;\"><strong>FYBSC (2026-27)</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>BASICS IN PHYSICAL AND ANALYTICAL CHEMISTRY-1 THEORY</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1061px; height: 392px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 29px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 29px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 29px; text-align: center;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 29px; text-align: center;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 100px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 100px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 100px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, laws, terminology, and principles of chemical thermodynamics, chemical kinetics, calibration of volumetric apparatus, methods of expressing solution concentration, and ionic equilibrium, including buffers and pH.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 100px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, laws, terminology, and principles of the second law of thermodynamics, entropy, free energy, gaseous and liquid states, chemical equilibrium, electrochemistry, and molecular spectroscopy.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 17px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 17px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 17px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Explain the principles of chemical thermodynamics, thermochemistry, chemical kinetics, calibration techniques, concentration expressions, ionic equilibrium, buffers, and pH.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 17px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Explain the principles of entropy, free energy, gaseous and liquid states, chemical equilibrium, electro-chemistry, and molecular spectro-scopy to describe the behaviour of chemical systems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 10px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 10px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Determine and analyse thermodynamic properties, thermochemical parameters, reaction kinetics, calibration data, different concentration units, and ionic equilibrium using mathematical relationships and experimental observations.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 10px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply the principles of thermodynamics, gaseous and liquid states, chemical equilibrium, electrochemistry, and molecular spectroscopy to solve qualitative and quantitative chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 105px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 105px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyse the influence of thermodynamic variables, reaction conditions, concentration units, calibration accuracy, and ionic equilibrium on the behaviour of chemical systems and experimental results.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 105px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyse thermodynamic parameters, gas and liquid-state properties, equilibrium systems, electrochemical behaviour, and spectroscopic data to interpret chemical phenomena and experimental observations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 10px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 10px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate appropriate thermodynamic principles, kinetic methods, calibration procedures, concentration expressions, and buffer systems for interpreting experimental data and solving analytical chemistry problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 10px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate thermodynamic criteria, equilibrium conditions, electrochemical&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">methods, gaseous and liquid-state models, and spectroscopic techniques for&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">interpreting chemical and spectroscopic data and solving analytical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 121px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 58px; height: 121px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; height: 121px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Integrate the principles of chemical thermodynamics, chemical kinetics, concentration expressions, ionic equilibrium, and calibration techniques to&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">formulate solutions for complex chemical and analytical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 510px; height: 121px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Integrate the principles of thermodynamics, gaseous and liquid states, chemical equilibrium, electrochemistry, and molecular spectroscopy to formulate solutions for complex chemical and spectroscopic problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>BASIC INORGANIC &amp; ORGANIC CHEMISTRY &ndash; 1 PAPER II THEORY</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1057px; height: 860px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 53px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; height: 53px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 53px; text-align: center;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 53px; text-align: center;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 118px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; text-align: center; height: 118px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 118px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recollect the basic concepts of atomic structures, quantum mechanical concepts, the hydrogen atom, periodic table classification and properties of main group elements, IUPAC nomenclature, bonding and structure, the reaction mechanism of organic compounds and stereochemistry.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 118px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the concepts of qualitative analysis, acid-base theories, types of chemical bonds, gaseous evolutes, precipitation reactions, and the principles of VSEPR theory. Aliphatic hydrocarbons.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 161px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; text-align: center; height: 161px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 161px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Discuss the concept of atomic orbitals, quantum numbers, electronic configuration rules, periodic trends, comparative properties of main group elements, bonding and structure, reaction mechanism of organic compounds and stereochemistry.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 161px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Describe the concepts of the common ion effect, aromaticity, preparation and reactions of aliphatic hydrocarbons, different systems of naming stereoisomers, the role of reagent-impregnated papers in qualitative analysis, precipitation equilibria, acid-base theories, Fajan\'s rule, and molecular geometry based on VSEPR theory.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 91px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; text-align: center; height: 91px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 91px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Calculate the effective nuclear charge according to Slater&rsquo;s Rule, and apply quantum mechanical principles, the Aufbau principle, Hund&rsquo;s rule, the Pauli exclusion principle, ionisation enthalpy, electron gain enthalpy and electronegativity using Pauling and Mulliken methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 91px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Compare the ionic and covalent bonds, aliphatic and aromatic compounds, and aromatic and anti-aromatic compounds. Apply the principles of precipitation equilibria, balanced chemical equations, the HSAB concept, and VSEPR theory to solve problems related to qualitative analysis and chemical bonding.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 183px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; height: 183px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 183px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Predict the oxidation states of main group elements, electronic configurations, periodic trends, and compare the metallic, nonmetallic, oxidation state, carbide and nitride forming behavior of group-I and group-II elements, the correct interconversion of projection formulas.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 183px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Classify compounds into aromatic, non&ndash;aromatic and anti-aromatic, functional groups into activating, deactivating or ortho-para directing and meta directing. Analyze the effects of common ions, uncommon ions, oxidation states, buffer action, and complexing agents on precipitation reactions, and compare different acid-base theories and types of chemical bonds.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 139px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; height: 139px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 139px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assign the correct IUPAC name to the organic compounds and the structure from their IUPAC name. Evaluate the merits and limitations of different atomic models and justify periodic variations of main group elements.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 139px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assign the correct stereo descriptors to stereoisomers. Evaluate the suitability of different acid-base theories, HSAB applications, and bonding concepts in explaining chemical reactivity and predicting the outcomes of qualitative analysis.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 115px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 56px; height: 115px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 483px; height: 115px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assess the hybridization of carbon in the given molecule, comparative chemistry to predict properties and behaviour of elements and compounds.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; height: 115px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Justify the aromatic or non-aromatic behavior of different cyclic hydrocarbons using Hueckel&rsquo;s rule. Design systematic schemes for qualitative analysis of inorganic ions using precipitation equilibria, reagent papers, acid-base concepts.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>PRACTICAL </strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1059px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px; text-align: center;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px; text-align: center;\" width=\"301\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Demonstrate understanding and application of basic laboratory techniques, including calibration of apparatus and preparation of standard solutions with accuracy and precision.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Demonstrate understanding of fundamental laboratory techniques, including preparation and standardization of solutions, proper handling of reagents, and interpretation of Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS).</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply thermodynamic principles to determine enthalpy changes and understand the concept of energy transformations in chemical reactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply principles of physical chemistry to study relationships among concentration, absorbance, viscosity, and dissociation using colorimetric, viscometric, conductometric, and polarimetric methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze the kinetics of chemical reactions using appropriate experimental methods and calculate rate constants for various reaction systems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze and interpret experimental data to determine physical constants and kinetic parameters, reinforcing theoretical concepts of thermodynamics and chemical kinetics.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Perform gravimetric and volumetric analyses to determine the purity, concentration, and composition of inorganic and commercial chemical samples.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Perform qualitative inorganic analysis systematically to identify cations and anions in mixtures using semi-micro techniques and safe laboratory practices.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Execute purification and separation techniques for organic compounds using recrystallization and chromatography, and interpret results based on physical constants and separation behavior.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Carry out volumetric redox titrations accurately to determine the percentage composition or oxidation state of metal ions in inorganic samples.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 478px;\" width=\"254\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Develop skills in data recording, error analysis, and result interpretation while adhering to safety protocols and good laboratory practices.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 509px;\" width=\"301\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Identify and characterize unknown organic compounds through elemental analysis and functional group tests, developing skills in systematic organic qualitative analysis.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>Post Graduate ( MSC-I and 4th Year Honours)[2026-27</strong></span></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>PG-I ADVANCED &nbsp;PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY THEORY</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1054px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px; text-align: center;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: center;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: center;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall and explain the fundamental principles of thermodynamics, chemical kinetics, and electrochemistry.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, terminology, principles, equations, and postulates related to fugacity, real solutions, surface thermodynamics, bioenergetics, quantum chemistry, solid-state chemistry, and phase equilibria.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px; text-align: center;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply thermodynamic, kinetic, and 5 concepts to derive Maxwell&rsquo;s relations, exact and inexact differentials, entropy changes, steady-state approximations, enzyme-catalysed reactions, and Debye&ndash;Huckel and Onsager equations.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, terminology, principles, equations, and postulates related to fugacity, real solutions, surface thermodynamics, bioenergetics, quantum chemistry, solid-state chemistry, and phase equilibria.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px; text-align: center;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Use theoretical models to evaluate thermodynamic parameters and solve numerical problems based on thermodynamics, electrochemistry, and chemical kinetics.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply thermodynamic equations, quantum mechanical operators and mathematical relationships to determine fugacity, partial molar properties, surface parameters, quantum-mechanical energy levels, defect concentrations, and phase-equilibrium parameters.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px;\" width=\"47\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Compare and differentiate the working principles, materials, and performance of various fuel cells; analyze enzyme activities; and apply experimental knowledge from the Joule&ndash;Thomson experiment to interpret real gas behaviours.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze thermodynamic, quantum-mechanical, solid-state, and phase-equilibrium systems to interpret molecular behaviour, non-ideal solution properties, quantum states, defects in solids, and phase diagrams using appropriate mathematical and theoretical approaches.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px; text-align: center;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assess and justify mechanisms, effects, and theoretical models based on experimental</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate theoretical models, mathematical derivations, thermo- dynamic relationships, quantum-mechanical solutions, defect models, and phase-equilibrium systems to assess their validity, limitations, and applicability to advanced chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 59px; text-align: center;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 489px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"255\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Formulate steady-state approximations for composite reactions and evaluate the effects of applied voltage and current on electrolytic interactions and ionic conductance behaviour.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 496px; text-align: justify;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>ADVANCED PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY PRACTICAL</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 97.7695%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.88623%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.2273%;\" width=\"284\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental principles, terminology, equations, experi- mental procedures, and safety practices related to thermo-dynamics, solubility equilibria, chemical kinetics, ionic activity, conductometry, potentiometry, pH-metry, and enzyme kinetics.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.4135%;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Create integrated experimental approaches and scientifically justified solutions by combining thermodynamic, kinetic, equilibrium, electrochemical, and enzyme-kinetic principles for investigating advanced chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.88623%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.2273%;\" width=\"284\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental principles, terminology, equations, experi-mental procedures, and safety practices related to thermo-dynamics, solubility equilibria, chemical kinetics, ionic activity, conductometry, potentiometry, pH-metry, and enzyme kinetics.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.4135%;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply mathematical equations, wave functions, kinetic models, phase-rule concepts and electrochemical relationships to perform experiments and determine kinetic, equilibrium, structural and physicochemical parameters.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.88623%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.2273%;\" width=\"284\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze experimental observations and numerical data to determine the effects of temperature, ionic strength, concentration, subs-tituents, pH, and experimental uncertainty on thermodynamic, kinetic, equilibrium, and electro chemical parameters.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.4135%;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze experimental data, graphs, polar plots, phase diagrams, X-ray diffraction patterns and kinetic/ electrochemical measurements to interpret reaction behaviour, molecular structure, phase equilibria, complex formation and substituent effects.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.88623%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.2273%;\" width=\"284\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate experimental methods, calculated parameters, uncertain -nties, theoretical models, and experimental results to assess their accuracy, validity, limitations, and&nbsp;suitability for solving chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.4135%;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate experimental methods, calculated parameters, graphical representations, structural interpretations and experimental uncertainties to assess the accuracy, validity, limitations and suitability of different physical chemistry techniques.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 5.88623%;\" width=\"47\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">5</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.2273%;\" width=\"284\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Create integrated experimental approaches and scientifically justified solutions by combining thermodynamic, kinetic, equili -brium, electrochemical, and enzyme-kinetic principles for investigating advanced chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 46.4135%;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Create integrated experimental approaches and scientifically justified solutions by combining mathematical, thermodynamic, kinetic, quantum-mechanical, structural and electrochemical principles to investigate advanced physical.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>PG-I : ADVANCED ORGANIC CHEMISTRY</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1051px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px; text-align: center;\" width=\"271\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px; text-align: center;\" width=\"283\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Define fundamental concepts, terminology, and classifications related to nucleophilic substitution reactions, aromaticity, chirality, stereochemical descriptors, and oxidation&ndash;reduction reagents.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Define fundamental concepts, terminology, reagents, and classifications related to organic reactions, rearrangements, alkylation processes, and spectroscopic techniques.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Explain reaction mechanisms, principles, and criteria governing nucleophilic substitution reactions, aromaticity, stereo -chemical features, and oxidation and reduction processes.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">: Explain reaction mechanisms, rearrangement pathways, regio- and stereochemical principles, and the theoretical basis of UV, IR, NMR, and mass spectrometric techniques.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply mechanistic principles, stereochemical rules, and reagent selectivity to predict products, assign configurations, interconvert projections, and solve numerical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply mechanistic rules, selectivity principles, and spectroscopic correlations to predict products, calculate spectral parameters, and interpret experimental data.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Differentiate between competing mechanisms, stereo-chemical relationships, aromatic vs antiaromatic systems, and oxidation -reduction pathways based on structure, symmetry, and experimental evidence.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Differentiate between related reactions, rearrangement mechanisms, alkylation pathways, and spectral features based on structure, conditions, and observed data.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assess aromaticity, chirality, optical activity, and reaction feasibility by interpreting symmetry elements, spectral data, thermodynamic criteria, and experimental outcomes.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Assess reaction feasibility, mechanistic validity, regio-stereochemical outcomes, and structural assignments using combined chemical and spectroscopic evidence.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 492px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design reaction pathways, stereochemical representations, and redox strategies for important organic conversions,</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 486px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design synthetic sequences, alkylation strategies, and complete structure elucidation schemes using integrated reaction chemistry and spectroscopic techniques.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;ADVANCED ORGANIC CHEMISTRY PRACTICAL</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1046px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 499px; text-align: center;\" width=\"271\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 474px; text-align: center;\" width=\"283\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 499px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply stoichiometric calculations, reaction requirements, and safety measures including MSDS for organic synthesis.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 474px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply suitable physical and chemical methods and microscale techniques for the separation of binary organic mixtures.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 499px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze one-step organic synthesis with respect to reaction conditions, purification, and TLC</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">monitoring.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 474px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyse the principles, criteria and experimental observations involved in the separation and purification of binary organic mixtures.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 499px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate synthesized products using TLC, mass/yield, melting point, and purity criteria.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 474px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate the identity and purity of separated components using chemical tests, derivative preparation, mass and physical constants.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 62px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 499px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Generate the desired organic product by integrating prescribed reaction conditions, purification, and characterization techniques.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 474px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design appropriate separation, purification and characterization strategies for different binary organic mixtures using microscale techniques<strong>.</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>ADVANCED INORGANIC CHEMISTRY THEORY </strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1042px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center; width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts of hybridisation, resonance, formal charge, molecular orbital theory, weak forces of attraction, transition metal carbonyls, coordination chemistry, solid-state chemistry and nanomaterials.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, terminology, mechanisms and characteristic features of inorganic reaction mechanisms, organometallic compounds, non-aqueous solvents, f-block elements, bioinorganic systems and environmental toxicants.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Explain the principles of hybridisation, molecular orbital theory, metal carbonyl bonding, coordination chemistry, band theory, solid-state structures and nanomaterial preparation methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Explain the principles governing reaction rates, ligand substitution, redox reactions, stereochemical changes, electron counting, organometallic bonding, non-aqueous solvent chemistry, f-block chemistry and metal&ndash;biomolecule interactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply concepts of chemical bonding, molecular orbital theory, Orgel and Tanabe&ndash; Sugano diagrams, electronic parameters, solid-state structures and nanomaterial synthesis to solve chemical problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply appropriate theoretical models and chemical principles to determine reaction rates, interpret ligand-substitution and redox mechanisms, perform electron counting, explain f-block properties, and interpret metal&ndash;biomolecule interactions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze molecular and electronic structures, spectral information, bonding characteristics, solid-state structures and preparation methods of inorganic materials and nanomaterials.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze inorganic reaction mechanisms and stereochemical outcomes by interpreting kinetic data, isotopic-labelling evidence, trans-effect behaviour, inner- and outer-sphere pathways, electron-counting schemes, spectral/ magnetic properties and biochemical data.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate different bonding models, transition-metal compounds, electronic structures, solid-state preparation methods and nanomaterial synthesis routes based on their principles, properties, advantages and limitations.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate competing reaction mechanisms, organometallic and nonaqueous solvent systems, f-block properties, metal-based medicinal compounds and heavy-metal toxicity by comparing their mechanisms, properties, advantages, limitations and biological or environmental implications.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 70px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 503px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design appropriate approaches for the preparation and application of advanced inorganic materials and nanomaterials by integrating concepts of bonding, electronic structure, synthesis and material properties.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 458px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design scientifically appropriate approaches for predicting and controlling inorganic reaction pathways, developing applications of metal complexes and f-block compounds, and proposing strategies for the safe, ethical and environmentally responsible use and remediation of metal-containing systems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>ADVANCED INORGANIC CHEMISTRY PRACTICAL</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1040px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 66px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px; text-align: center;\" width=\"252\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 455px; text-align: center;\" width=\"302\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>SEM-II</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 66px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px;\" width=\"252\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Explain the principles, reactions and procedures involved in the analysis of ores, alloys, limestone and instrumental methods such as potentiometry, conductometry and pH-metry.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 455px;\" width=\"302\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply appropriate synthetic, instrumental and analytical procedures to prepare inorganic coordination compounds and determine equilibrium constants, electrolytic nature, stoichiometry and stability constants.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 66px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px;\" width=\"252\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Apply appropriate analytical principles and experimental procedures to estimate constituents in ores, alloys, limestone and given samples using classical and instrumental methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 455px;\" width=\"302\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze experimental observations, instrumental data, graphical relationships and characterization results to determine equilibrium, stoichiometric and stability parameters.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 66px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px;\" width=\"252\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Analyze experimental observations and instrumental data obtained from potentiometric, conductometric and pH-metric titrations to determine the composition or strength of unknown samples.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 455px;\" width=\"302\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate the purity, yield, accuracy, precision and reliability of experimental results by assessing sources of error and the suitability of experimental methods.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 66px; text-align: center;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 508px;\" width=\"252\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Evaluate the accuracy, precision, reliability and suitability of classical and instrumental analytical methods for the quantitative determination of analytes in different samples.</span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 455px;\" width=\"302\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">Design appropriate experimental strategies for the synthesis, characterization and instrumental investigation of inorganic compounds by selecting suitable techniques, optimizing experimental conditions and incorporating safety and environmental considerations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\">A<strong>nalytical Chemistry THEORY( ELECTIVE)</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1030px; height: 648px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 53px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: justify; height: 53px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif;\"><strong>COs</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 53px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>SEM-I</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; text-align: center; height: 53px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p><strong>SEM-II</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 105px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 105px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, terminology, standards, classify-cations and instrumentation associated with laboratory quality, safety, accreditation, GLP, spectroscopy and thermal analysis.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 105px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Recall the fundamental concepts, classifications, principles, instru-menttation and applications of chromatographic, spectroscopic, radioanalytical, surface and atomic analytical techniques.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 105px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 105px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Explain the principles and significance of quality management, laboratory safety,GLP, Fourier Transform techniques, molecular spectro-scopy and thermal analytical methods.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 105px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Explain the theories, working principles, instrumentation and analytical applications of chromatography, X-ray spectro-scopy, mass spectrometry, radioanalytical, surface and atomic spectroscopy.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 54px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Apply chemical principles, mathematical relationships and instrumental concepts to solve numerical and quantitative analytical problems.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 54px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Apply chromatographic and spectroscopic principles for optimization of analytical conditions, selection of instrumental components and qualitative and quantitative analysis.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 121px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 121px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 121px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Analyze chemical, spectral and thermal data to identify analytical characteristics, sources of variation and factors affecting measurement results.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 121px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Analyze chromatographic, spectral and instrumental data to determine separation efficiency, identify analytes and interpret chemical, structural and compositional information.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 105px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 105px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Evaluate the quality, safety, reliability, advantages, limitations and suitability of laboratory practices and analytical techniques for specific chemical-analysis applications.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 105px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Evaluate the performance, advantages, limitations and suitability of chromatographic and spectroscopic techniques, detectors and instrumental configurations for specific analytical applications.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 69px; text-align: center; height: 105px;\" width=\"50\">6</td>\n<td style=\"width: 497px; height: 105px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Design appropriate quality, safety and instrumental analytical strategies by integrating spectroscopy, thermal analysis, GLP and laboratory quality- management principles.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 453px; height: 105px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Design appropriate analytical strategies by integrating chromatographic, spectroscopic, radioanalytical, surface and atomic techniques to solve complex chemical-analysis problems.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>ANALYTICAL CHEMISTRY PRACTICAL</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 1020px; height: 446px;\" width=\"604\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 55px; text-align: center; height: 50px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>COs</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 449px; text-align: center; height: 50px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p><strong>SEM-I</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 505px; text-align: center; height: 50px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p><strong>SEM-II</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 87px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 55px; text-align: center; height: 87px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 449px; text-align: justify; height: 87px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p>Explain the principles and analytical concepts involved in precipitation titration, ion-exchange processes, complex-metric titration, and redox estimation used in the given practicals.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 505px; text-align: justify; height: 87px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p>Explain the principles and working of potentiometric, pH-metric, conductometric, colorimetric, spectrophotometric, and flame photometric methods used for quantitative chemical analysis.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 105px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 55px; text-align: center; height: 105px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 449px; text-align: justify; height: 105px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p>Perform analytical experiments to determine assay values, ion-exchange capacity and efficiency, breakthrough capacity, and the concentration of metal ions usingappropriate titrimetric methods.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 505px; text-align: justify; height: 105px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p>Apply appropriate instrumental and titrimetric analytical techniques to determine the purity and concentration of inorganic and organic substances in given samples and mixtures.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 140px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 55px; text-align: center; height: 140px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 449px; text-align: justify; height: 140px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p>Analyze experimental observations and titration data to calculate the quantities of NaCl, Cr(III), Fe(II), Pb, Sn, Cu(II), and nitro groups, including appropriate statistical treatment of results.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 505px; text-align: justify; height: 140px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p>Analyze experimental data and calibration/titration curves to quantitatively determine analytes such as sodium carbonate, Ti(III), Fe(II)/Fe(III), nitrite, Cr(VI), Mn(VII), HCl, H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>, and potassium.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 64px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 55px; text-align: center; height: 64px;\" width=\"50\">\n<p><strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 449px; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\" width=\"271\">\n<p>Evaluate the accuracy, precision, and reliability of experimental results by interpreting deviations, identifying possible sources of error, and justify the suitability of the analytical method used.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 505px; text-align: justify; height: 64px;\" width=\"283\">\n<p>Evaluate the accuracy, precision, and reliability of analytical results by interpreting experimental observations, identifying sources of error, and assessing the suitability of the selected analytical method for a given sample.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 292, '2026-10-17', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9767, 203, 38, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department : </strong></h4>\n<h4><strong>To cultivate a dynamic mathematical community, developing strong mathematical<br />knowledge and curiosity among students and faculty, while fostering research and<br />innovation.</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department : </strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>To encourage and nurture the students with an interest and aptitude in mathematics by<br />providing a supportive environment that promotes intellectual growth.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>To deliver quality education through effective teaching practices enabling students to<br />develop a strong understanding of mathematical concepts.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Program Outcomes (POs) details: </strong>Developed by the faculty of Science using Graduate attributes (GAS)</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"472\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B. Sc.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"128\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge</strong><br />Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking</strong><br />Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving</strong><br />Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong><br />Analyze and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills</strong><br />Design and perform basic experiments, analyze data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Cooperation / Team Work</strong><br />Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong><br />Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning</strong><br />Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSO):</strong>&nbsp;After completion of the Bachelor&rsquo;s degree in Mathematics</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"467\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B. Sc.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"133\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"547\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"547\">\n<p>The learner will be able to explain and apply&nbsp;fundamental principles, methods, and concepts in algebra, analysis, differential equations, and other branches of mathematics.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"547\">\n<p>Students will be able to analyze and evaluate&nbsp;mathematical problems using analytical reasoning and critical thinking, and apply&nbsp;mathematical concepts to solve real-life problems.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"547\">\n<p>The program enables students to develop and demonstrate&nbsp;mathematical modelling abilities, problem-solving skills, and communication skills required for various kinds of employment.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"547\">\n<p>Students will be able to apply and solve&nbsp;numerical and interdisciplinary problems, and analyze<strong>&nbsp;</strong>number-theoretic contexts relevant to project and field work.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p>Department of Mathematics Within a few years of graduation, the graduates will be able to:</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"461\">\n<p><strong>Program Name: B. Sc.</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"140\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"601\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p>Apply logical reasoning, critical thinking, technological skills and mathematical knowledge in professional roles such as educators, quantitative analysts, data analysts, and computing professionals.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p>Pursue higher studies, research and diverse career opportunities through mathematical competence, programming skills, and a commitment to lifelong learning, as academicians, teachers, lecturers, researchers, statisticians, and data scientists.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"545\">\n<p>Apply quantitative and computing skills effectively in professional roles such as financial analysts, risk analysts, banking professionals, government analysts, cryptographers and IT and software professionals.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Calculus- I</strong></p>\n<p><strong>COURSE OUTCOMES: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>On completion of this course, the learners would be able to:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"663\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: Calculus- I</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"663\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS1MATMJ0124</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"249\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"250\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 30</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"163\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>:2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"249\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: F.Y.B.Sc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"250\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: I</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"163\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"69\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"357\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"62\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"31\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"31\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"69\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"357\">\n<p>State the basic concepts of differential equations, fundamental properties of real numbers and sequences.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"62\">\n<p>K1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"31\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"31\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,6</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"69\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"357\">\n<p>Explain the core principles of first-order differential equations and its applications, inequalities, intervals in R and advanced properties of real numbers and convergent, bounded sequences.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"62\">\n<p>K2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"31\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"31\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>1,2,5</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"69\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"357\">\n<p>Apply appropriate methods to solve differential equations, evaluate neighbourhoods, bounds for subsets of real numbers, and detect convergence of monotone sequences.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"62\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"31\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"31\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"69\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"357\">\n<p>Analyze mathematical conditions to classify exact differential equations, monotone sequences, and characteristics of various subsets of real numbers.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"62\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"31\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"31\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"57\">\n<p>3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>BTL:</strong>Bloom&rsquo;s Taxonomy Level <strong>[</strong>K1 (Remember), K2(Understand), K3(Apply), K4(Analyze)<strong>]</strong></p>\n<p><strong>No. of contact hours:</strong>&nbsp;Lectures (L), Practicals (P)</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"659\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: Algebra - I</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"659\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS1MATMJ0224</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 30</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"206\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>: 2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: FYBSc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: I</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"206\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Recall the definitions, properties, and fundamental results of integers, divisibility, congruence, relations, functions, binary operations, and polynomials.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Explain the concepts and properties of divisibility, equivalence relations, functions, binary operations, congruence, and polynomial operations with suitable examples.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Apply mathematical techniques to solve problems involving divisibility, gcd, Euclidean algorithm, congruence, functions, equivalence classes, binary operations, and polynomial operations.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Analyze the mathematical relationships and properties of integers, residue classes, equivalence relations, functions, and polynomials to justify results and solve unfamiliar problems.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"52\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3,4,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"665\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: <strong>Mathematics Major Practical I</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"665\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS1MATMJP124</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 60</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"212\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>: 2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: FYBSc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: I</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"212\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Apply appropriate methods and formulas to solve differential equations and detect convergence of&nbsp; sequences of real numbers, and solve problems related to properties of real numbers and&nbsp;mathematical techniques to solve problems involving divisibility, gcd, Euclidean algorithm, congruence, functions, binary operations, and polynomial operations.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>15</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,3</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Analyze the behavior and structure of sequences, sets of real numbers in view of convergence, subsets of R in view of boundedness, neighbourhoods, intervals and the exactness of first order first degree equations, solutions of first order first degree differential equations and&nbsp;mathematical relationships among integers, residue classes, functions, equivalence relations, binary operations, and polynomials to determine valid results.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>16</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Evaluate the validity of mathematical properties related to real numbers, inequalities, and the convergence or divergence of various standard and Cauchy sequences and mathematical arguments and solutions involving divisibility, congruence, functions, equivalence relations, polynomial properties, roots, and algebraic structures.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K5</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>14</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Formulate mathematical models for applied real-world scenarios by constructing and solving exact and non-exact first-order differential equations. and solutions for unfamiliar problems involving integers, functions, equivalence relations, congruence, and polynomials.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K6</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>15</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>2,3,4,5,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"650\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: <strong>Calculus -II </strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"650\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS2MATMJ0124</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"245\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"245\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 30</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"160\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>:2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"245\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: F.Y.B.Sc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"245\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: II</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"160\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"650\">\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"71\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"326\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"81\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"58\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"71\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"326\">\n<p>State the core definitions and theorems concerning limits, continuous functions, differentiability, and critical points.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"81\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"58\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"71\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"326\">\n<p>Explain the underlying principles of limits, derivative, and their theoretical applications such as mean value theorems and optimization.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p>2</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"81\">\n<p>1,2</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"58\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"71\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"326\">\n<p>Apply mathematical rules to evaluate indeterminate limits, compute higher-order derivatives, and utilize Taylor\'s theorem for polynomial approximation.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p>3</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"81\">\n<p>3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"58\">\n<p>3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"71\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"326\">\n<p>Analyze real-valued functions to classify discontinuities, determine rates of change, and deduce intervals of increase, decrease, and concavity.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p>4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"81\">\n<p>2,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"58\">\n<p>2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"659\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: Discrete Mathematics</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"659\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS2MATMJ0224</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"248\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"248\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 30</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"162\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>:2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"248\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: F.Y.B.Sc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"248\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: II</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"162\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"398\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"42\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"398\">\n<p>Recall fundamental concepts, definitions, principles, and formulas related to finite, infinite, countable and uncountable sets, counting principles, Stirling numbers, permutations, combinations, and recurrence relations.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"42\">\n<p>K1</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"398\">\n<p>Explain counting principles, pigeonhole principle, permutations and combinations of sets and multisets, binomial and multinomial theorems, inclusion-exclusion principle, permutations, and recurrence relations with suitable examples.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"42\">\n<p>K2</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>1,2,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"398\">\n<p>Apply counting techniques, Stirling numbers, pigeonhole principle, permutations and combinations, non-negative integer solutions, inclusion-exclusion, derangements, Euler&rsquo;s function, permutation operations, and recurrence methods to solve mathematical problems.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"42\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>8</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>1,2,3,4,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2,3</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"51\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"398\">\n<p>Analyze combinatorial structures, permutation cycles and transpositions, signatures of permutations, and homogeneous and non-homogeneous recurrence relations to select appropriate methods and justify mathematical results.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"42\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n<p>7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"30\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"54\">\n<p>1,2,3,4,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"53\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"665\">\n<p><strong>Course Title</strong>: <strong>Mathematics Major Practical I</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"9\" width=\"665\">\n<p><strong>Course Code</strong>: GBS1MATMJP124</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Academic Year</strong>: 2026-27</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>No. of total contact Hours</strong>: 60</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"212\">\n<p><strong>Course credits</strong>: 2</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Class</strong>: FYBSc</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"226\">\n<p><strong>Semester</strong>: I</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"212\">\n<p><strong>Degree: </strong><u>UG</u></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p><strong>CO Statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p><strong>BTL</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p><strong>L</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p><strong>P</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Apply the concepts of limits, continuity and differentiability of functions, to solve problems involving functions and their properties and&nbsp;counting principles, permutations, combinations, and recurrence techniques to solve mathematical problems.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K3</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>16</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,3</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Examine<strong>&nbsp;</strong>functions using derivatives for applying Leibnitz rule, Mean Value Theorems, L&rsquo;Hospital Rule, and conditions for increasing and decreasing functions and combinatorial structures, counting arguments, permutation properties, and recurrence relations to determine appropriate mathematical methods.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K4</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>16</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Evaluate the behaviour of limits, continuity, and differentiability of real-valued functions by applying core analytical theorems such as the Sandwich theorem, Intermediate Value theorem, Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem, and L\'Hospital\'s Rule and solutions involving counting techniques, combinatorial identities, permutations, inclusion&ndash;exclusion, and recurrence relations for mathematical validity.</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K5</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>14</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"46\">\n<p><strong>CO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"340\">\n<p>Construct detailed graphical representations (curve sketching) and mathematical approximations of functions by integrating higher-order derivatives, Leibnitz Rule, mean value theorems, and Taylor\'s theorem and mathematical solutions and computational activities involving counting techniques, permutations, combinatorial structures, and recurrence relations.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"47\">\n<p>K6</p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"28\">\n<p>0</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"37\">\n<p>14</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"93\">\n<p>2,3,4,5,7</p>\n</td>\n<td width=\"72\">\n<p>1,2,3,4</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 303, '2026-10-14', 0),
(9768, 203, 39, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Departmental Vision for UG Education: </strong></p>\n<p>To develop scientifically competent, intellectually empowered and socially responsible graduates with a strong foundation and comprehensive knowledge in Microbiology, enabling them to contribute meaningfully to scientific advancement, human welfare and sustainable development</p>\n<p><strong>Departmental Vision for PG Education:</strong></p>\n<p>To develop scientifically competent, intellectually empowered and socially responsible postgraduate students with advanced knowledge and research-oriented skills in Microbiology, enabling them to contribute to scientific advancement, human welfare, environmental sustainability and technological development.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Departmental Mission for UG Education:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>To impart strong foundational and applied knowledge in Microbiology through effective, innovative and student-centric teaching-learning practices.</li>\n<li>To develop scientific aptitude and critical-thinking skills among students through practical training, experimentation, research-oriented activities and problem-solving approaches.</li>\n<li>To inculcate scientific responsibility, ethical values and social commitment by highlighting the applications of Microbiology in human health, food, agriculture, biotechnology and industry.</li>\n<li>To promote environmental awareness and sustainable practices by developing an understanding of the role of microorganisms in ecosystems, environmental conservation and sustainable development.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Departmental Mission for PG Education:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>To impart advanced and comprehensive knowledge of Microbiology through innovative, interdisciplinary and research-oriented teaching-learning practices.</li>\n<li>To develop advanced laboratory, analytical and research competencies through hands-on training in modern microbiological, molecular, genomic, bioinformatics and analytical techniques.</li>\n<li>To foster critical thinking, scientific reasoning and innovation by engaging students in experimental investigations, research projects, scientific literature analysis and problem-solving activities.</li>\n<li>To inculcate scientific responsibility, ethical values, social commitment and environmental awareness by highlighting the applications of Microbiology in healthcare, biotechnology, agriculture, food, industry and environmental sustainability.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PO for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 871px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge: </strong></p>\n<p>Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving: </strong></p>\n<p>Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;Analyse and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;Design and perform basic experiments, analyse data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Cooperation / Team Work: </strong></p>\n<p>Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 142.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 724.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p>Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>PO for PG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 876px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge: </strong></p>\n<p>Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking: </strong></p>\n<p>Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p>Analyse and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills: </strong></p>\n<p>Design and perform basic experiments, analyse data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Cooperation / Team Work: </strong></p>\n<p>Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p>Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 138.333px;\" width=\"53\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 733.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning: </strong></p>\n<p>Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PSOs for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 894px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151.667px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 738.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151.667px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 738.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Explain the diversity, structure, physiology, and ecological significance of microorganisms, and understand their roles in health, environment, agriculture and industry.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151.667px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 738.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Apply theoretical knowledge of microbiological concepts to perform experiments and identify microorganisms, analyze results, and address biological problems in laboratory and research settings</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151.667px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 738.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Analyze, compare and interpret microbiological and molecular data to identify relationships and underlying mechanisms associated with microbial growth, metabolism, genetics and cellular processes.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151.667px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 738.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Demonstrate proficiency in microbiological techniques, aseptic practices, microscopy, microbial culture, staining, biochemical testing, instrumentation and basic molecular biology techniques, while evaluating data generated through laboratory investigations.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>PSOs for PG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 881px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.333px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 729.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.333px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 729.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Integrate advanced concepts of Microbiology, microbial diversity, microbial physiology, microbiome biology and microbial ecology, with emphasis on their significance in human health, environmental sustainability and ecosystem management.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.333px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 729.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Apply advanced microbiological, molecular, genomic, bioinformatics and analytical techniques to investigate microorganisms and microbial communities, conduct laboratory research, analyse experimental data and address complex biological problems.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.333px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 729.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Critically evaluate experimental findings, scientific literature and emerging developments in Microbiology and integrate interdisciplinary applications in biotechnology, nanotechnology, pharmaceutical sciences and allied biosciences to make evidence-based scientific decisions.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 147.333px;\" width=\"54\">\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 729.667px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"548\">\n<p>Design, develop and evaluate innovative and sustainable microbial technologies, research projects, industrial processes and entrepreneurial ventures by integrating advanced microbiological knowledge, research skills and professional competencies to address societal, industrial and environmental challenges.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PEOs for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"height: 466px; width: 897px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 50px; width: 153.667px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 50px; width: 739.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 104px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 153.667px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 739.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Pursue higher education and advanced studies in Microbiology, Biotechnology, Life Sciences, Molecular Biology, Medical Microbiology and allied disciplines, contributing to scientific research and knowledge advancement</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 104px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 153.667px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 739.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Develop entrepreneurial ventures and professional opportunities in areas such as food and dairy microbiology, industrial microbiology, biotechnology, fermentation, environmental microbiology and microbiological testing services.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 104px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 153.667px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 739.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Establish professional careers in clinical, pharmaceutical, food, agricultural, environmental and industrial microbiology laboratories by applying their knowledge of microorganisms, microbial processes and laboratory techniques.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 104px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 153.667px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 104px; width: 739.333px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Apply microbiological and biotechnological knowledge to address challenges related to human health, food safety, environmental sustainability, public health and industrial processes while demonstrating ethical and socially responsible professional practices.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>PEOs for PG:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"width: 889px;\" width=\"601\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 734px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 734px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Establish successful professional careers in academia, research organizations, healthcare, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, food, environmental and allied industries by applying advanced microbiological knowledge, technical expertise and problem-solving skills.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 734px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Pursue doctoral studies, advanced research and lifelong learning by critically analysing scientific problems, evaluating emerging technologies and contributing to the advancement of Microbiology and allied sciences.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 734px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Contribute to interdisciplinary research, innovation, entrepreneurship and technology development by designing sustainable microbial products, processes and solutions addressing societal, industrial, healthcare and environmental needs.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 151px;\" width=\"55\">\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 734px;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"546\">\n<p>Demonstrate scientific integrity, professional ethics, leadership, effective communication, teamwork and environmental responsibility while applying microbiological knowledge for sustainable development and global well-being.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>CO Summary for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 38.9624%; height: 36px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.1052%; height: 18px;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.1222%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;Download here</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.1052%; height: 18px;\">F.Y.B.Sc (NEP 1.1)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.1222%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp; Click here</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>CO Summary for PG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 38.9624%; height: 36px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.1052%; height: 18px;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.1222%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;Download here</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 47.1052%; height: 18px;\">M.Sc Part I / Honours</td>\n<td style=\"width: 52.1222%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp; Click here</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 305, '2026-10-08', 0),
(9769, 203, 40, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9770, 203, 41, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of the Department :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To become a centre of excellence in statistical education and research by developing graduates with strong analytical skills, scientific thinking, ethical values, and a commitment to contributing to higher education, industry, and society.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">To provide sound education and practical training in statistics through a well-structured curriculum covering descriptive statistics, probability, statistical inference, sampling techniques, and experimental design.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">To develop analytical, computational, and problem-solving skills through the use of statistical software, programming tools, and real-world data.</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">To encourage critical thinking, research interest, and responsible use of data in accordance with Outcome-Based Education (OBE) and the National Education Policy (NEP-2020).</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">To promote continuous learning, professional skills, teamwork, and social responsibility among students.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PO1: Disciplinary Knowledge <br /></strong>Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</p>\n<p><strong>PO2: Critical Thinking <br /></strong>Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</p>\n<p><strong>PO3: Problem Solving <br /></strong>Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</p>\n<p><strong>PO4: Analytical Reasoning <br /></strong>Analyze and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</p>\n<p><strong>PO5: Research-Related Skills <br /></strong>Design and perform basic experiments, analyze data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</p>\n<p><strong>PO6: Cooperation / Team Work <br /></strong>Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</p>\n<p><strong>PO7: Scientific Reasoning <br /></strong>Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</p>\n<p><strong>PO8: Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning <br /></strong>Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Statistical Knowledge and Analytical Competence&nbsp;</strong><br />Demonstrate a strong foundation in statistical concepts, probability, statistical inference, sampling, regression, stochastic processes, operations research, and experimental design to analyze, interpret, and solve quantitative problems.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Analytics and Computational Skills&nbsp;</strong><br />Apply statistical methods, mathematical models, and computational tools such as R, Python, and data visualization software to analyze real-world datasets, draw meaningful conclusions, and support evidence-based decision-making.</li>\n<li><strong>Research, Professional Ethics and Lifelong Learning </strong>&nbsp;<br />Design statistical investigations, surveys, and experiments; communicate findings effectively; and demonstrate ethical practices, professional responsibility, teamwork, and lifelong learning in research and professional environments.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>PEO1: Academic and Professional Excellence</strong><br />Graduates will pursue higher education or successful careers in statistics, data science, research, education, government, industry, and other allied fields by applying sound statistical knowledge and professional competence.<br /><strong>PEO2: Analytical, Computational and Research Competence</strong><br />Graduates will apply statistical reasoning, computational tools, and research skills to analyze data, solve real-world problems, and support evidence-based decision- making.<br /><strong>PEO3: Ethics, Leadership and Lifelong Learning</strong><br />Graduates will demonstrate ethical and responsible professional practices, effective communication, teamwork, leadership, and a commitment to lifelong learning in a rapidly evolving data-driven environment.</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 42.8439%; height: 55px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\"><strong>Class</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\"><strong>Download</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">FYBSC NEP 1.1 COs</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;<a title=\"FYBSC COs\" href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1lcMVCJYvDqo-MbahtCt_6Z1T1FlmGYru/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CLICK HERE</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">SYBSC NEP 1.1 COs</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">TYBSC NEP 1.1 COs</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.7026%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 316, '2026-10-13', 0),
(9771, 203, 42, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Vision of the Department: For UG</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To develop scientifically competent, critical-thinking and socially responsible graduates with strong foundational to advanced knowledge in Zoology, proficient laboratory skills, and a deep understanding of wildlife, biodiversity and nature conservation, enabling them to contribute meaningfully to science and society.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Vision of the Department: For PG</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To establish the Department as a distinguished Post Graduate centre recognized for excellence in academics and molecular biology research, strengthen scientific aptitude, and a progressive scientific mindset among learners</span><strong>.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Mission of the Department: For UG</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To impart comprehensive knowledge of Zoology</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> from fundamental concepts to advanced areas through innovative, experiential and interdisciplinary teaching-learning practices.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To develop strong practical and laboratory competencies</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> through hands-on training, field studies, research-oriented activities and modern laboratory techniques.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To inculcate critical thinking and environmental responsibility</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> by creating awareness and appreciation of wildlife, biodiversity and nature conservation, empowering students to become responsible citizens.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Mission of the Department: For PG</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To provide advanced and comprehensive education in Zoology</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> through contemporary, interdisciplinary and research-oriented teaching-learning practices.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To promote excellence in Molecular Biology </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">through hands-on laboratory training, research exposure and application of modern scientific techniques.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To develop scientific aptitude, critical thinking and innovation</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> through inquiry-based learning, problem-solving and independent research.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><strong>To prepare scientifically competent and professionally skilled post-graduates</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> for advanced research, higher education and diverse career opportunities in Zoology and Life Sciences.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PO for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; height: 612px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 50px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 50px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 86px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 86px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 86px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Critical Thinking</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyze and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Design and perform basic experiments, analyze data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Cooperation / Team Work</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 68px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 3.53373%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\">\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 96.0265%; height: 68px; text-align: left;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>PO for PG:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply advanced theoretical concepts, recent developments, and interdisciplinary knowledge in the respective science discipline to analyze complex scientific problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Problem Solving</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evaluate scientific literature critically and design appropriate strategies to solve complex and unfamiliar problems using logical and evidence-based approaches.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analyze, interpret, and validate complex experimental data using advanced analytical, mathematical, and statistical tools to draw scientifically sound conclusions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Research-Related Skills</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Design and conduct independent research, apply appropriate methodologies, analyze results, and communicate findings through dissertations, reports, or publications.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Cooperation / Team Work</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Collaborate effectively in multidisciplinary research teams, demonstrating leadership, accountability, and professional communication skills.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Formulate original hypotheses or models, test those using rigorous scientific methods, and justify outcomes based on empirical evidence and theory.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Information / Digital Literacy</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use advanced digital tools, databases, computational software, and research platforms to retrieve, analyze, manage, and present scientific information ethically.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply ethical principles, biosafety norms, research integrity, and environmental responsibility in advanced scientific research and professional practice.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PSOs for UG:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Conceptual insights&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;Explain living systems by analyzing the physiological, genetic, and ecological frameworks that define the animal kingdom.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Practical Application&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply theoretical knowledge of Zoological concepts to design and execute experiments, interpret results, and solve biological problems in laboratory and research settings.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Thinking&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Examine, compare, and interpret experimental data, identifying patterns, relationships, and underlying principles of Zoology and cellular processes.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Laboratory and Field Expertise</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Standardise laboratory procedures, instrumentation, field techniques and evaluate data generated from the laboratory and field visits.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>PSOs for PG:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PSO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Foundational Knowledge&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Describe key concepts, terminologies, and principles in molecular biology and allied life science disciplines, forming a strong theoretical foundation.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Practical Application&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply theoretical knowledge of molecular biology to interpret results, and solve biological problems in laboratory and research settings.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Analytical Thinking&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Develop ability to critically examine, compare, and interpret experimental data, identifying patterns, relationships, and underlying principles in molecular and cellular processes.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Critical Evaluation &amp; Research</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Design and execute original research projects by formulating hypotheses and developing innovative solutions to complex problems in the field of life sciences.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>PEOs for UG:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Pursue higher education and advanced studies</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in Zoology, Life Sciences and allied disciplines, contributing to scientific research and knowledge advancement.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Build entrepreneurial ventures</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> in wildlife conservation, ecotourism, biodiversity management and nature-based enterprises.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Establish careers in wildlife conservation</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, including zoological parks, wildlife sanctuaries, zoos and other conservation organisations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Develop professional careers in laboratory and diagnostic services</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> by applying their knowledge and practical skills in biological, biomedical and diagnostic laboratories.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>PEOS for PG:</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>PEO statements</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Achieve Academic and Competitive Success: Demonstrate the comprehensive knowledge and specialized skills necessary to qualify for competitive national examinations (such as NET/SET) and successfully pursue higher academic degrees (Ph.D.).</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Conduct Independent Research and Innovate: Utilize advanced research skills and analytical thinking to design, execute, and interpret laboratory research, leading to new knowledge and innovative contributions in the fields of zoology and molecular biotechnology.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Excel in industrial careers: Apply a strong foundation in Molecular Biology/Zoology to secure and thrive in professional roles within the Biotechnology, Pharmaceutical, and Life Science industries.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pursue Entrepreneurial Ventures: Develop and launch entrepreneurial initiatives in applied biological sciences, focusing on creating value in areas such as biotechnology, diagnostics, and related life science solutions</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>CO Summary for UG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%;\">Download</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%;\">FYBSc (NEP 1.1)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/FY-UG-CO-ZOOLOGY.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>CO Summary for PG:</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 36px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; height: 18px;\">Class</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; height: 18px;\">Download</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; height: 18px;\">MSc Part I/Honours</td>\n<td style=\"width: 49.6137%; height: 18px;\"><a href=\"https://sathayecollege.edu.in/uploads/COs-PG-1-MSc-Zoology.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Click Here</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 320, '2026-09-30', 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_section_info` (`dsi_id`, `dsi_dsm_id`, `dsi_dsl_id`, `dsi_asl_id`, `dsi_ayl_id`, `dsi_assl_id`, `dsi_lib_id`, `dsi_res_id`, `dsi_new_content`, `dsi_content`, `dsi_is_display_on_website`, `dsm_order`, `approve_bit`, `rejected_reason`, `dsi_user_id`, `dsi_time`, `delete_bit`) VALUES
(9772, 203, 43, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Vision of Department :&nbsp;</strong></span></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Vision(UG)</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To develop competent, innovative, ethical, and socially responsible IT professionals with strong technical, analytical, and problem-solving skills who contribute effectively to technological advancement and societal development.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Vision(PG)</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To develop skilled, innovative, ethical, and research-oriented data science professionals with advanced analytical, statistical, computational, and AI capabilities to address complex real-world challenges and contribute responsibly to industry, research, and society.</span></p>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></span></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Mission(UG)</strong></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To impart strong foundational and advanced knowledge in Information Technology and emerging technologies.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To develop problem-solving, analytical, critical-thinking, and scientific reasoning abilities through practical and project-based learning.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To provide industry-oriented exposure to modern programming, data, networking, cloud, IoT, security, and emerging technologies.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To nurture communication, teamwork, leadership, professional ethics, and social responsibility.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To promote lifelong learning, innovation, research, higher education, and professional development.</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Mission(PG)</strong></span></p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To impart advanced knowledge in data science, statistics, mathematics, data engineering, machine learning, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To develop analytical, critical-thinking, scientific reasoning, and problem-solving skills through practical, project-based, and research-oriented learning.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To provide hands-on exposure to modern data science tools, big data, cloud technologies, visualization, machine learning, deep learning, NLP, and generative AI.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To nurture research aptitude, innovation, teamwork, communication, professional ethics, and responsible data and AI practices.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">To promote self-directed and lifelong learning for continuous professional development, higher education, research, and career advancement.</span></li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></span></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>BSc IT</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Disciplinary Knowledge &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply strong foundations of computer science principles including data structures, operating systems, computer networks, software engineering, electronics, mathematics, and statistics to analyze and solve computing problems</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Communication Skills</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Prepare and deliver clear technical documentation, code reports, and presentations for programming, allied fields and field projects that meet defined academic and professional standards</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Critical Thinking</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Analyze and evaluate problems in Data Structures, Operating Systems, Computer Networks, Security domain, IoT, and Kafka-based systems to design efficient, reliable, and scalable IT solutions</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Problem Solving</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Design, develop, test, and deploy efficient software solutions using modern programming languages and technologies such as Python, Core Java, Web Programming, Full Stack Development, and object-oriented concepts</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Analytical Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Use analytical, statistical, and computational techniques to interpret data, optimize systems, support business intelligence, and provide technology-driven solutions to real-world problems</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Cooperation and Teamwork&nbsp; </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Exhibit professional ethics, teamwork and an understanding of societal impacts of IT solutions, while engaging in continuous learning to adapt to emerging technologies and industry needs</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO7</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Scientific Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Formulate hypotheses, analyze quantitative data, and draw validated conclusions using concepts from mathematics, statistics, electronics, and computing in project work.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO8</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Self directed learning&nbsp; </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply industry tools like Docker, Kafka, databases, BI tools and development frameworks to design and develop scalable applications, demonstrating evaluation and synthesis of emerging technologies for continuous learning, develop skills required for technical support and system maintenance</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO9</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Identify, analyze, and apply ethical principles, professional standards, and legal guidelines in decision-making related to programming, data handling, cybersecurity, AI, IoT, and community-oriented IT projects</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO10</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> </span><strong>Lifelong Learning</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Demonstrate the ability to independently acquire, adapt to emerging technologies, tools, and professional practices in information technology</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>MSc DS</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Disciplinary Knowledge - Apply strong foundations of data structures, mathematics, probability, and statistics to analyze, model, and solve complex data-driven problems in real-world domains.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Critical Thinking - Develop, evaluate, and deploy machine learning, deep learning, NLP, and generative AI models to solve analytics problems ethically and effectively.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Problem Solving - Design and implement efficient solutions for structured and unstructured data management, including big data ecosystems, data engineering pipelines, and scalable storage systems, ensuring data quality and reliability.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Analytical Reasoning - Analyze large and diverse datasets using advanced analytics, time series techniques, and visualization tools to extract meaningful insights and support data-driven decision-making.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO5</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Research related skills - Apply research methodologies, experimental design, and analytical techniques to investigate data science problems and produce scientifically valid conclusions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO6</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Cooperation and Teamwork - Demonstrate professional skills, including the use of advanced Excel, modern data science tools, teamwork, communication, and ethical practices, and engage in continuous learning to adapt to emerging technologies in data science and AI.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO7</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Scientific reasoning - Apply scientific reasoning, mathematical and statistical principles to formulate hypotheses, analyze structured and unstructured data, evaluate machine learning and deep learning models, and derive valid conclusions for data science problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO8</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Reflective Thinking - Critically reflect on data analysis approaches, model performance, ethical implications, and learning experiences to improve decision-making, problem-solving effectiveness, and professional practice in data science.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO9</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Self directed learning - Demonstrate the ability to independently identify learning needs, acquire new technical skills, and apply modern data science tools and frameworks to solve analytical and computational problems.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PO10</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Lifelong learning - Recognize the need for and engage in continuous learning to keep pace with emerging tools, technologies, and methodologies in data science, artificial intelligence, big data, and generative AI.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></span></h4>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; height: 526px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.52055%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 91.739%; height: 50px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>BSc IT</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 101.26%; height: 18px;\" colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.02119%; height: 50px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.2384%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 122px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.02119%; height: 122px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.2384%; height: 122px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Software Development &amp; Programming</strong></span></h3>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Develop, test, and deploy robust software applications using modern programming languages, object-oriented concepts, web technologies, and full-stack development frameworks to solve real-world IT problems.</span></h3>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.02119%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.2384%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Systems, Networking &amp; Infrastructure</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Design and manage operating systems concepts, computer networks, security mechanisms, IoT systems, and distributed platforms to ensure efficient, secure, and scalable IT solutions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.02119%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.2384%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Data, Analytics &amp; Emerging Technologies</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply databases, data analytics, BI tools, Kafka-based streaming systems, and cloud-native technologies to process, analyze, and visualize data for informed decision-making.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 100px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.02119%; height: 100px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 93.2384%; height: 100px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Professional Practice &amp; Industry Readiness</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Demonstrate professional ethics, teamwork, communication skills, and industry readiness through projects, internships, and use of modern IT tools, while adapting to emerging technologies.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table style=\"width: 96.3699%; height: 490px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 9.08293%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.203%; height: 50px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>MSc Data Science</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 101.286%; height: 18px;\" colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.37442%; height: 50px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.9115%; height: 50px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.37442%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.9115%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Data Analytics &amp; Statistical Modeling</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Apply statistical, mathematical, and analytical techniques to explore, model, and interpret complex datasets, including time series data, to support data-driven decision-making across domains.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.37442%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.9115%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Data Engineering &amp; Big Data Systems</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Design and implement scalable data engineering solutions, including structured and unstructured data pipelines, big data ecosystems, and cloud-based storage and processing frameworks.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.37442%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.9115%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Machine Learning, AI &amp; Intelligent Systems</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Develop, evaluate, and deploy machine learning, deep learning, NLP, and generative AI models to solve real-world analytical problems ethically and efficiently.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 93px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 8.37442%; height: 93px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PSO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width: 92.9115%; height: 93px;\" colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Research, Professional Practice &amp; Ethics</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Conduct independent research and industry-oriented projects, demonstrating scientific reasoning, teamwork, communication skills, ethical awareness, and professional use of modern data science tools.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></span></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>BSc IT</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Professional Competence</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will establish successful careers as software developers, system administrators, data analysts, or IT professionals by applying strong technical foundations and problem-solving skills.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong> Industry &amp; Societal Impact</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will design and implement technology-driven solutions that address business, industrial, and societal challenges ethically and responsibly.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Lifelong Learning &amp; Career Advancement</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will engage in continuous learning, professional development, higher education, certifications, or research to adapt to rapidly evolving IT technologies.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Leadership, Ethics &amp; Teamwork</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will demonstrate leadership qualities, effective communication, teamwork, and ethical reasoning while contributing positively to multidisciplinary and multicultural work environments.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Program Name:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>MSc Data Science</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO statements</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO1</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Professional Competence in Data Science</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will establish careers as data scientists, data engineers, machine learning engineers, analysts, or AI professionals by applying advanced knowledge and problem-solving skills.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO2</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Industry, Research &amp; Societal Impact</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will design and implement data-driven and AI-based solutions that address industry, research, and societal challenges responsibly and ethically.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO3</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Lifelong Learning &amp; Career Advancement</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will pursue continuous learning, advanced certifications, higher studies, or research to adapt to rapidly evolving technologies in data science and artificial intelligence.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>PEO4</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<h3><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Leadership, Collaboration &amp; Professional Growth</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Graduates will demonstrate leadership qualities, effective communication, teamwork, and reflective thinking while contributing to multidisciplinary and global work environments.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><span style=\"font-family: \'times new roman\', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></span></h4>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 326, '2026-10-16', 0),
(9773, 203, 46, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9774, 203, 48, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9775, 203, 49, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department : <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To create scientifically competent, socially responsible, and environmentally conscious graduates through quality education, experiential learning, research, innovation, and sustainable practices in plant sciences. </span></strong></h4>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">M1: Provide quality, outcome-based education in plant sciences through innovative teaching and experiential learning.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">M2: Develop scientific temper, critical thinking, and research skills through laboratory and field-based education.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">M3:&nbsp; Promote biodiversity conservation, environmental awareness, and sustainable use of plant resources.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">M4: Encourage innovation, entrepreneurship, and the application of modern biological techniques to address societal and environmental challenges.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">M5: Prepare competent, ethical, and socially responsible graduates for higher education, research, and diverse career opportunities.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Disciplinary Knowledge: Apply fundamental concepts and principles of Chemistry, Botany, Zoology, Microbiology, Mathematics, Statistics, and Physics to explain scientific phenomena.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Critical Thinking: Evaluate scientific information and experimental data critically to draw evidence-based conclusions.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Problem Solving: Solve scientific and quantitative problems using appropriate mathematical, statistical, and scientific techniques.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Analytical Reasoning: Analyze and interpret experimental results, datasets, and graphical information to derive valid inferences.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Research-Related Skills: Design and perform basic experiments, analyze data, and present findings using standard scientific methods.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cooperation / Team Work: Collaborate effectively in laboratory, field, and academic activities to achieve shared scientific objectives.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scientific Reasoning: Formulate hypotheses and apply scientific methods to test, validate, and explain observations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PO8</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Moral and Ethical Awareness / Reasoning: Practice ethical conduct, academic integrity, and environmental responsibility in scientific activities.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Plant Diversity and Biological Principles</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply knowledge of plant diversity, taxonomy, morphology, anatomy, physiology, genetics, ecology, and evolution to understand the structure, function, classification, adaptation, and significance of plants.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Practical and Research Competence</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstrate proficiency in laboratory experiments, microscopy, herbarium techniques, field surveys, plant identification, data analysis, scientific documentation, and research methodologies to investigate biological problems.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Modern Biological Tools and Sustainable Applications</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Apply concepts of plant biotechnology, microbiology, molecular biology, bioinformatics, and modern analytical techniques to solve biological, agricultural, environmental, and industrial challenges while promoting biodiversity conservation and sustainable utilization of plant resources.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PSO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Professional Skills and Employability</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Demonstrate scientific temperament, ethical values, effective communication, leadership, teamwork, entrepreneurship, and lifelong learning skills for higher education, research, and careers in academia, agriculture, horticulture, forestry, biotechnology, industry, and environmental organizations.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong> Academic Excellence: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates will possess a strong foundation in plant sciences and apply botanical knowledge for higher education, research, and professional advancement.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong> Scientific Inquiry and Research; </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates will demonstrate scientific reasoning, analytical thinking, laboratory and field skills, and research aptitude to address biological and environmental challenges.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Professional Competence and Employability: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates will develop technical competency, communication, leadership, teamwork, digital literacy, and ethical values for successful careers in academia, industry, agriculture, horticulture, forestry, biotechnology, and environmental organizations.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Environmental Stewardship and Social Responsibility: </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates will contribute to biodiversity conservation, sustainable resource management, environmental protection, and community development through responsible scientific practices</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>PEO5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><strong>Lifelong Learning and Innovation; </strong><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Graduates will engage in lifelong learning, entrepreneurship, innovation, and interdisciplinary collaboration to adapt to emerging developments in plant sciences and meet global societal needs.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :&nbsp;</strong></h4>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1CZAXHKaW_bk28hjV4btyQ6ZRKeL8dxJt?usp=drive_link\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1CZAXHKaW_bk28hjV4btyQ6ZRKeL8dxJt?usp=drive_link</a></strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 336, '2026-10-30', 0),
(9776, 203, 50, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
(9777, 203, 51, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '<h4><strong>Vision of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Mission of Department :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Outcomes (PO) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Specific Outcomes (PSOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Program Educational Objectives (PEOs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />\n<h4><strong>Course Outcomes (COs) :</strong></h4>\n<hr />', '1', 0, 1, '', 562, '2026-09-29', 0),
